window.AKK_TRANSMIGRATED_INTO_A_SISTER_FORTUNE_ON_THE_FARM_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_TRANSMIGRATED_INTO_A_SISTER_FORTUNE_ON_THE_FARM_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":301,"title":"Chapter 301: The Birth of the Third Prince","paragraphs":["\"It has been half a year since we last met. The Prince seems to have lost quite a bit of weight. It seems this inspection tour out of the capital must have been quite arduous.\"","Facing Song Jinzhao's sarcastic remarks, Xiao Rongyan did not back down.","\"It is all thanks to you, County Princess. During the half year I was away from the capital, I thought of you often. Now that I have returned and finally seen you, let's wait and see.\"","The clattering sound of hooves approached from a distance.","Seeing Song Jinzhao, Qingshuang shouted at the top of her lungs, \"County Princess, news has come from the palace that Low-Rank Concubine Yan is about to give birth! They need you to enter the palace immediately.\"","Everyone in the convoy froze for a moment, instinctively turning their gazes toward Xiao Rongyan, who was sitting in the carriage.","Song Jinzhao furrowed her brows.","Low-Rank Concubine Yan was still half a month away from her due date. Why was she giving birth now?","\"The palace summons me. I shall take my leave first.\"","Song Qiming and the others immediately mounted their horses and followed Song Jinzhao as she rode away.","Watching the receding figures of Song Jinzhao and her group galloping away, Xiao Rongyan's face darkened, and he angrily slammed his fist against the carriage.","A guard riding beside him said, \"Your Highness, do not worry. It might be a princess.\"","As he gritted his back teeth tightly, the muscles in his jaw bulged and twisted.","\"There is no way all thirteen will be princesses. This is all Song Jinzhao's fault.\"","By the time Song Jinzhao rushed to the palace on horseback, several imperial physicians were already standing in the Bamboo Leaf Pavilion.","\"I pay my respects to Your Majesties the Emperor and Empress, and to all the consorts.\"","Standing beneath the eaves, Noble Consort Rong and Concubine Jin rolled their eyes at Song Jinzhao.","Xiao Chengjing's brows were tightly knitted, and two sharp glares shot from his dark eyes, landing on Song Jinzhao's face.","\"No matter what, save the child first. Nothing must happen to the child.\"","Inside the room was a woman's heart-wrenching screams, while outside was Xiao Chengjing's cold and ruthless command.","Song Jinzhao found it incredibly grating to her ears.","It served him right to be impotent for so many years; he should have just been a eunuch.","With a cold face, she stepped over the threshold. Several imperial physicians stood inside, and Gu Jupu had also arrived.","\"What is the situation?\"","Imperial Physician Xu, who was responsible for caring for Low-Rank Concubine Yan, was sweating profusely from anxiety. Seeing Song Jinzhao enter, he hurriedly scrambled up from the floor.","\"An hour ago, Low-Rank Concubine Yan accidentally slipped in the courtyard. Her stomach hit a rock, and she started bleeding immediately.\"","\"She is bleeding more and more, and she is feeling dizzy. I have already prescribed medication and had Low-Rank Concubine Yan take it, but the child just won't come out.\"","Song Jinzhao took the prescription from Imperial Physician Xu and skimmed it quickly.","The prescription was fine.","She decisively took off her outer coat and bypassed the folding screen separating the inner and outer rooms to walk inside.","The three midwives squatting at the foot of the bed were momentarily stunned to see Song Jinzhao enter, but then hurriedly made way for her.","Song Jinzhao picked up a hot towel from the tray and wiped her hands clean.","The cervix was contracting too slowly, and the mother was almost out of strength.","\"Bring a bowl of ginseng soup,\" she ordered while opening her medical box to prepare for acupuncture.","\"Bite on this, save your strength to deliver the child.\"","She stuffed a silk handkerchief into Low-Rank Concubine Yan's mouth. If this continued, the concubine would bite right through her own teeth.","The commotion inside gradually quieted down. The concubines waiting outside whispered with a hint of worry, \"Why is there no sound?\"","Another concubine, over forty years old, clutched her handkerchief over her racing heart.","\"County Princess Linghui is inside; everything should be fine.\"","Many concubines stood in the courtyard, but aside from Noble Consort Rong and Concubine Jin, none of the others had ever even been pregnant, let alone given birth.","Having listened to an hour of agonizing wails, many of them were feeling a bit panicked, as if they too would face this one day.","Stimulated by the silver needles, the semi-conscious Low-Rank Concubine Yan gasped and widened her eyes.","Her pupils cleared up, and the pain in her lower body became even more pronounced, feeling as if she were being torn in half.","Song Jinzhao held her hand and comforted her, \"Stay awake. Now, take a deep breath, hold it, and push all your strength downwards from your chest.\"","Sweat poured down Low-Rank Concubine Yan's forehead like heavy rain, and the pain brought tears to her eyes.","She bit down hard on the silk handkerchief in her mouth. As a muffled groan sounded, all the veins on her forehead bulged.","\"Hold it, don't lose your breath. Good. Now exhale slowly, and let's do it again.\"","Another half hour passed. The woman's constantly straining hands left a row of nail marks on the back of Song Jinzhao's hand.","The silk handkerchief slipped from her mouth. With a near-collapsing scream, something slipped out from her body below.","The midwife squatting at the foot of the bed caught the wet child with both hands and cried out in pleasant surprise.","\"It is a little prince.\"","The child's cries rang out in the room. With a faint smile on her lips, Low-Rank Concubine Yan fainted from exhaustion.","Song Jinzhao performed a check and only felt relieved after confirming she was fine.","Outside the door, hearing the baby's cry, Xiao Chengjing stood up excitedly.","The midwife who ran out to report knelt on the ground and said with a smile, \"Congratulations, Your Majesty. The young mistress has given birth to a little prince.\"","Hearing that it was a prince, Xiao Chengjing finally breathed a sigh of relief.","Remembering that Low-Rank Concubine Yan had given birth prematurely, the Empress asked nervously, \"How is the Third Prince's health?\"","The midwife replied, \"Rest assured, Your Majesty the Empress. The Third Prince has a loud cry, strong limbs, and is very healthy.\"","Hearing that the prince was healthy, Noble Consort Rong and Concubine Jin, standing under the eaves, disappointedly tightened their grip on their handkerchiefs.","The news of the Third Prince's birth spread quickly. The restless Xiao Rongyan closed his eyes with a heavy heart upon receiving the news, feeling utterly exhausted.","This was only the first. From now on, his imperial father would have more princes than just him and Xiao Rongche.","By the time Song Jinzhao returned from the palace, it was already night.","Walking through the courtyard gate, bright firelight greeted her eyes.","The flames illuminated the faces of Song Qiming and the others, the warmth making her feel very at peace.","\"Eldest Sister, why are you only back now? My rabbit is almost burnt.\"","Song Jinzhao reached out and wiped the corner of her younger brother's mouth. \"Your mouth is full of oil. Is it good?\"","Song Anhao guiltily pinched his fingers together.","\"Eldest Brother and Second Sister said we had to wait for you, but I really couldn't resist, so I just had a tiny bite.\"","Song Jinzhao took his hand and walked to the fire. \"You don't have to wait for me next time. Eat when you are hungry.\"","Today's delivery had actually been quite fast; longer ones could drag on until midnight.","A spicy roasted rabbit leg was handed to her by Song Shixue. Song Jinzhao took it and took a bite.","The tenderness was just right, and the spiciness was exactly how she liked it.","Song Qiming placed a few roasted rabbits from a nearby rack back over the fire to reheat them.","\"Sister, did Low-Rank Concubine Yan deliver safely?\"","Song Jinzhao nodded. \"It is a prince. Both mother and child are safe.\"","Song Qiming made two slices on a rabbit leg with a small knife.","\"Our teacher will definitely be very happy when he finds out. He has been longing for princes to be born, even saying the more the better.\"","Song Jinzhao stopped chewing, thinking of the nine princes fighting for the throne.","Emperor Kangxi was at least a wise ruler; Xiao Chengjing fell short of him by a hundred thousand miles.","With the moral character of Xiao Rongche and Xiao Rongyan laid bare, what would happen in the future was truly uncertain."]},{"number":302,"title":"Chapter 302: Six Princes and Seven Princesses Return Home in Glory","paragraphs":["Ten days later, Xiao Rongche, who had been inspecting the southern waterways, also returned to the capital.","Upon learning of the birth of the Third Prince, his expression became just as awful as Xiao Rongyan's.","What disappointed both of them the most was the Emperor's promise before they left the capital: that they would be rewarded for their achievements.","They originally thought this meant the restoration of their titles as Princes of the First Rank. Instead, what Xiao Chengjing bestowed upon them were mere silks, satins, antiques, and jade artifacts—things that could not compare to actual power and status.","Twenty days after the Third Prince's birth, the third pregnant concubine in the palace gave birth to the Second Princess.","Before Xiao Rongche and Xiao Rongyan even had a chance to catch their breath, the Fourth Prince was born five days later.","During the New Year period, joyous news poured out from the imperial palace one after another.","From the end of the eleventh lunar month to the Lantern Festival of the following year, a total of six princes and seven princesses were born in the palace.","Xiao Chengjing, whose lineage had previously been thin, instantly found his family tree flourishing.","Looking at the rewards the Imperial Household Department had just delivered to the front hall, Song Jinzhao let out a heavy sigh. \"They're finally done giving birth.\"","Six princes were enough to satisfy Xiao Chengjing's appetite. In his joy, the leave of absence he had previously promised to grant Song Qiming arrived right alongside the imperial edict.","It was a four-month leave to visit family in their hometown. Upon his return, he would be immediately promoted to an Imperial Academy Compiler of the secondary sixth rank, a promotion speed far exceeding that of others.","The court officials knew clearly in their hearts that the Emperor's favor toward Song Qiming was due to the Linghui County Princess, Song Jinzhao, so no one raised any objections.","After all, imperial heirs were also a matter of state, and of the utmost importance at that.","Song Gaoli, who had come to the door carrying gifts, looked at Song Qiming as he packed his belongings and sighed helplessly.","\"Your official rank is higher than mine, yet I didn't expect that in the end, I'd be the one unable to go back.\"","Ever since entering the Ministry of War, Song Gaoli hadn't had a single peaceful night's sleep.","The Ministry of War had previously been the Prince of Ying's sphere of influence. After Xiao Rongyan left the capital, Wu Jianzheng did not hesitate to raise his broadsword and start slashing.","They say a new official lights three fires upon taking office; his fire burned for three whole months.","Within half a year, the number of people transferred out or demoted in the Ministry of War exceeded half of its personnel.","From when he first entered the Ministry of War as an observer to learn the ropes, to now firmly sitting in the position of Secretary of the Bureau of Armaments, Song Gaoli's hairline had receded by more than just a little bit.","Song Qiming smiled and said, \"I'm just basking in my sister's reflected glory. Otherwise, how could I get such a long leave and still have my position kept for me?\"","\"But are you sure you don't want us to conveniently bring Uncle Dazhuang and the others over to see you along the way?\"","Unlike Song Jinzhao and her brother, Song Gaoli's parents were still alive and healthy, and he was the only grandson whom the whole family fully supported.","Not seeing each other for such a long time, it wouldn't be an exaggeration to say they missed him madly, and there would surely be plenty of idle gossip in the village.","Song Gaoli sighed and shook his head. \"Better not. It's convenient when you bring them over, but on the way back, they'd need a merchant caravan to escort them. The journey is too far; I wouldn't feel at ease.\"","He had originally thought that being an official in the capital would allow him to bring his family over to live together, but after taking office, Song Gaoli discovered the truth.","As long as one stuck to their principles, the salary of a low-ranking official was very meager.","Especially in the capital, everything was expensive. Housing and land prices were outrageously high. After half a year, he could still only afford to rent a house.","He genuinely couldn't quite afford to support his family if he brought them over.","It was better to use the salary he had saved up to let his parents buy more farmland in their hometown to rent out.","Living off collected rent would always be more comfortable than living a penny-pinching life in the capital.","Compared to a journey of over a thousand miles, a four-month vacation really wasn't considered long.","With the white tiger leading the way, four-year-old Song Anhao took turns sitting on the backs of three different horses. When he came, he had been sleeping soundly in the carriage; this time, riding on a tall horse, he found everything novel.","Although they only traveled during the day, riding horses was faster than driving a carriage, so Song Jinzhao and her group smoothly arrived at Xining City in a month and a half.","With the warm sunlight shining on her, looking up at the familiar city gates, Song Jinzhao, who hadn't returned in two years, unexpectedly felt a sense of trepidation upon nearing home.","Seeing a group of people approaching on horseback, the city guards had just braced themselves when they spotted a tiger wearing red clothes sandwiched between the horses.","He rubbed his eyes uncertainly.","\"Am I seeing things? Why is there a tiger?\"","Another guard, eating a flatbread in his hand, turned to look at him. \"How could there be a tiger? I think your eyes are playing tricks on you. It's definitely a dog.\"","After saying that, he followed the other's gaze. A white tiger face, previously hidden by a red hat, was exposed. The flatbread in his hand fell to the ground with a smack.","Both of them widened their eyes in terror. It really was a tiger!","\"There's a tiger!\" With a scream, the surrounding guards rushed over with their weapons.","Song Shixue looked down and realized that the hat worn on Xuetuan's head had gone askew at some point, revealing half of a tiger face.","She quickly dismounted, hugged Xuetuan's neck, and shook her head at the guards. \"Don't be afraid. This is my family's pet. It doesn't bite.\"","The guard holding his sword had hands that wouldn't stop shaking. Hearing the little girl say the tiger was her pet, he found it simply unbelievable.","How could anyone raise a tiger as a pet? That was way too bold.","The guard who had dropped his flatbread shook his head frantically. \"A tiger is a fierce beast! You cannot enter. Leave immediately.\"","Sensing their hostility, Xuetuan wanted to open its mouth and roar, but Song Shixue, who had her arms around its neck, pinched its jaws shut.","\"No, your disguise failed. You can't make a sound now.\"","Having been scolded, Xuetuan aggrievedly buried its head in Song Shixue's chest.","I wasn't even being fierce. Master is speaking so loudly.","Seeing the white tiger acting spoiled in the little girl's arms like a dog, the guards looked at each other in dismay.","Was this actually a tiger or a dog?","\"What's going on?\" Seeing the city guards pointing swords at people, Constable Zhao, who had come to patrol, ran over with his men while shouting.","\"Miss Song!\" Looking up and seeing a familiar face on horseback, Constable Zhao widened his eyes in pleasant surprise.","Remembering Song Jinzhao's current status, he quickly dropped to one knee, cupped his fists, and lowered his head.","\"Greetings to the Linghui County Princess. Greetings, Lord Song.\"","The city guards holding their swords froze, looking up at Song Jinzhao. She was a County Princess?","The swords in their hands fell to the ground. Their knees went weak, and they hurriedly knelt down to beg for mercy.","\"Greetings to the County Princess. This lowly one had eyes but failed to recognize Mount Tai. Please forgive us, County Princess.\"","Constable Zhao raised his head and glanced at his trembling subordinates. Noticing the white tiger being held by Song Shixue, he was surprised but also guessed most of what had happened.","He pleaded on their behalf, \"County Princess, these men were all recently transferred here and are unaware of your abilities. If they have offended you in any way, please forgive them.\"","Song Jinzhao didn't mind the minor incident that had just occurred. She said gently, \"It is a small matter. The pet we brought looks a bit fierce, so it's normal for them to be cautious. Rise, all of you.\"","\"Thank you, County Princess.\" The guards kowtowed on the ground. After getting up, they carefully retreated to stand by the base of the wall.","After standing up, Constable Zhao wore a smile on his face.","\"Has the County Princess just returned from the capital?\"","Song Jinzhao nodded. \"We haven't returned to the village yet. We wanted to stroll through the city first.\"","Constable Zhao reached out and cleared the way. \"Please, County Princess. Please, Lord Song.\"","Song Shixue put Xuetuan's hat back on properly, tying the strings to ensure its head and face would remain covered."]},{"number":303,"title":"Chapter 303: Returning to Songjia Village, Taking the Imperial Examination","paragraphs":["Watching the group slowly depart, the guards who had just tried to stop them gaped, panting heavily.","\"Headman Zhao, our Xining City actually produced a County Princess? Why does she raise a tiger? Isn't she afraid?\"","Head Constable Zhao looked at this group of newcomers and decided to give them a thorough lesson on Song Jinzhao's history of rising to power.","He put his hands on his hips. \"What's raising a tiger? She's even killed one.\"","\"Back when I first met the Linghui County Princess, she was just a...\"","He recounted everything from how she lost her parents and hunted for a living, to selling tea and cold noodles on the streets to make money, and then moving on to how she captured the traitors from the Northern Shuo Kingdom alive.","Head Constable Zhao talked until his mouth was dry, while his listeners stood with their mouths wide open, finding it all utterly unbelievable.","Were these really things a teenage girl could accomplish?","In just four short years, she went from a simple peasant girl to a County Princess. Even her younger brother scored third place in the imperial examinations and entered the Hanlin Academy. The rise of the Song family's third branch was simply too fast.","Towards the end of his story, Head Constable Zhao suddenly remembered something and slapped his forehead.","\"I almost forgot! I need to hurry and report such an important matter to the magistrate.\"","\"Knowing the County Princess has returned, His Honor will definitely want to pay a visit to the Song family.\"","After buying provisions in the city, Song Jinzhao and her group left the city and headed straight for Song Family Village.","It took an hour to walk from Xining City to Song Family Village, but riding a horse took only about thirty minutes.","When the villagers saw over a dozen horses passing by their doors, they all looked astonished.","The timid ones thought bandits had invaded the village and hid in fear.","Zhou Yagu, who was squatting by the well washing vegetables, heard the sound of hooves and looked up. At a glance, she saw the fine horses stopped at the courtyard gate.","It wasn't until she clearly saw the people riding the horses that she cried out in pleasant surprise.","\"The County Princess has returned!\" Her voice echoed through the courtyard.","The sound reached the small room to the right of the main hall. Old Man Song, who was taking a nap on the heated brick bed, snapped his eyes open. \"Old woman, is that Jinzhao and the others coming back?\"","He scrambled out of bed as he spoke, and Old Madam Song also set down the clothes she was sewing and hurried outside.","\"Grandpa, Grandma.\"","The moment Song Shixue saw the two elders, she immediately broke into a wide smile and called out to them.","Old Madam Song happily hurried over and took her hands.","\"Shixue is back. You've grown so tall, Grandma almost didn't recognize you.\"","She wore a long red dress embroidered with beautiful patterns, a jade pendant hanging at her waist, and hairpins adorning her head.","Although she didn't wear many accessories, one could tell at a glance that they were exquisite and expensive.","The old woman's rough palms were warm. Looking at her gray-haired grandparents, Song Shixue suddenly felt that they had aged quite a bit more.","\"Grandpa, Grandma.\"","Old Man Song's moist eyes looked Song Jinzhao and Song Qiming up and down. When he saw little Song Anhao, whose hand was being held, his chest swelled with overwhelming joy.","\"The wind is strong outside, hurry and come in.\" He reached out, grabbed Song Jinzhao's hand, and led her to a chair to sit down.","Zhou Yagu, who had hastily washed her hands clean, walked in carrying hot tea.","Outside, Hu Sanluo was directing the guards to lead the horses into the stable; those that couldn't fit had to be tied near the corners of the wall.","After sitting down, the two elders never took their eyes off Song Jinzhao and the others.","They looked from one to the other, from the oldest to the youngest, their hearts filled with nothing but comfort and pride.","Old Madam Song asked, \"Have you eaten lunch yet? You must be starving after traveling for so long.\"","\"Yagu, go cook right away. We'll have an early dinner today.\"","Song Jinzhao smiled and said, \"We ate lunch on the way back. We're not hungry yet, so there's no need to eat too early.\"","Seeing this, Old Man Song and Old Madam Song began asking how they had been doing in the capital.","The three siblings patiently answered, chiming in one after another. Only the youngest, Song Anhao, had taken off his outer coat and was leaning against the bedding on the kang, yawning.","The members of the first and second branches of the family, who had rushed over, saw the horses tied in the courtyard. Their first thought was that the third branch had truly returned.","After taking just two steps, Song Dalang stared wide-eyed at Xuetuan, who was lying by the woodshed door. His lips trembled as he spoke.","He gripped Aunt Song's arm tightly and said, \"Is that a tiger?\"","These words drew everyone's attention. Xuetuan, who was being held by Lanxi, noticed strangers looking at him and opened his tiger maw to let out a roar.","Hearing the sound, Song Shixue ran out of the main hall and scolded it.","\"Xuetuan, be quiet. Stay obediently by the woodshed. Lanxi, watch him.\"","Looking at the gorgeously dressed, lively, and beautiful Song Shixue, Song Qiaoniang, who was two years younger, and the others stared blankly.","Second Aunt Song stared at the clothes and jewelry on Song Shixue, her mind already calculating how much silver these things were worth.","\"Eldest Uncle, Second Uncle, Eldest Aunt, Second Aunt.\"","Eldest Aunt Song nodded kindly in response, looking at Song Shixue with a gaze that was both familiar and unfamiliar.","Walking into the main hall, everyone immediately began greeting each other.","The youngest, Song Anhao, looked at the child held in Eldest Aunt Song's arms and sat up with interest to get a better look.","This was the first time he had seen a child younger than himself.","Song Jinzhao introduced them, \"This is your cousin Yongshi. He is two years younger than you.\"","Song Anhao nodded in understanding. \"I know. Second Sister told me on the way back.\"","Before dinner, Song Qiming first made a trip to the village chief's house to deliver the money and goods that Song Gaoli had entrusted him to bring back to the chief's family.","Song Mancang handed the bank notes to Song Dazhuang, his eyes filled with uncontrollable worry.","\"Qiming, how is our Gaoli doing in the capital? Every time he writes, he says he's doing well, but we are truly worried about him being all alone in the capital.\"","Song Qiming held the elderly village chief's hands and said, \"Gaoli is doing very well in the capital. He is now a Principal in the Armory Bureau of the Ministry of War and is highly valued by his superiors. It's just that he is too busy with his official duties and has no time to come back.\"","Song Gaoli's mother wiped her tears and sighed. \"The capital is so far away. If we had known, it would have been better for him to return to Anyang Prefecture to be an official. At least it would be closer, and we could see him.\"","Having not seen her son for two years, she worried that he wasn't eating or sleeping well, and that he had no one to take care of him.","And the capital was so far away that even if they wanted to visit, it was inconvenient.","Song Qiming stayed at the village chief's house for a while before leaving. Over a couple of cups of tea, he talked entirely about Song Gaoli's situation in the capital.","For dinner, the first and second branches of the family all ate together at the third branch's house.","Two tables were pushed together, and everyone sat packed tightly around them.","Afterward, Song Qiming tested the knowledge of his two younger cousins. Song Yongnian was able to answer a few questions, but Song Yaozu hemmed and hawed.","As the difficulty was lowered, when asked about the simplest poem, it was actually the usually silent Song Laidi who beat Song Yaozu to the punch and answered it.","For a moment, Song Qiming felt a bit surprised. \"How did little sister Laidi know that?\"","Seeing this, Old Man Song smiled and explained.","\"I saw that Hu Sanluo knew how to read, and there wasn't that much work to do around the house. So, I simply dug out the books you and Shixue left at home and let Sanluo teach the girls. I figured knowing how to read couldn't hurt.\"","Song Jinzhao raised her eyebrows in surprise. She hadn't expected Old Man Song to take the initiative to let his two granddaughters study. It was truly a bit unexpected.","Sitting in her chair eating peanuts, Second Aunt Song rolled her eyes and muttered quietly to herself.","\"What's the point of learning so many words? It's not like they can take the imperial exams and become officials.\"","\"If you ask me, it would be better to have Zhou Yagu teach them how to cook so it'll be easier to find them a good husband's family later on.\"","With her sharp hearing, Song Jinzhao looked at Second Aunt Song speechlessly. She wanted to say something but felt it would be useless to speak up.","Once a person's mindset is fixed, it is very difficult to change in a short amount of time, not to mention her deep-rooted preference for boys over girls.","Seeing Song Jinzhao suddenly look her way, Second Aunt Song guiltily turned her head away.","I hadn't even made a sound. Did she hear me?"]},{"number":304,"title":"Chapter 304: Worship and Plans for Renovating the Ancestral Grave","paragraphs":["Early in the morning, Song Jinzhao was awakened by the crowing of roosters. Looking through the window at the distant, mist-shrouded mountain peaks, she couldn't help but think back to the first time she went up the mountain to hunt.","Over four years had passed, and everything had changed.","After breakfast, everyone took incense, paper money, food, and wine, and walked toward the foot of the back mountain.","Upon arriving, all that could be seen were burial mounds. Big and small, they were all surrounded by withered yellow shrubs and tall grass.","Only the graves of Third Song and his wife, along with a few mounds around them, were free of dead grass. Furthermore, the characters on their tombstones were crystal clear, suggesting someone frequently came to trace over them.","Standing before the tombstone, Song Jinzhao held a copied imperial decree conferring her the title of County Princess, read it aloud to the grave, and then tossed it into the fire to burn.","Song Qiming followed suit, reading aloud a copied edict granting him the status of a Jinshi scholar.","The white paper, now turned to ash, spiraled upward in the gentle breeze, as if Third Song and his wife had come to take them away.","The cool, chilly wind blew the rabbit fur on Song Anhao's hat, making it sway from side to side.","He knelt properly before the tombstone, his milky, soft voice like freshly steamed rice cakes—soft and sweet.","\"Father, Mother, I now study and practice martial arts every day. Grandpa Dongfang, who teaches me at the academy, says I am very smart. My brother and sisters treat me incredibly well, and I live happily every single day.\"","After speaking, he bit his lip and silently muttered in his heart: It's just that sometimes older brother bullies me, please remember to visit him in a dream and teach him a lesson.","The three older siblings looked at Song Anhao with eyes full of doting affection, unable to stop themselves from recalling how he had wailed in his swaddling clothes right after he was born.","It felt as if it had all just happened not long ago.","Watching the fire on the ground gradually die out, Song Qiming turned to Old Man Song and said, \"Grandpa, aside from paying our respects to our parents and visiting you all, my sister and I also want to renovate the ancestral tombs this time we're back.\"","Old Man Song looked around at the clustered burial mounds. \"It is time to repair them. Now that you and Jinzhao have different statuses, the ancestral tombs should be made more presentable.\"","\"I will go find some craftsmen later. Before breaking ground, we must also find someone to read the feng shui. We cannot be careless about this.\"","Song Jinzhao smiled faintly. \"Rest assured, Grandpa. I will definitely find the best feng shui master in Xining City to come take a look. The craftsmen will also be properly arranged, ensuring the ancestral tombs are rebuilt to be both grand and prosperous for our descendants.\"","Old Man Song nodded in satisfaction. \"I am at ease with you handling things.\"","\"After finding out you were conferred the title of County Princess, the village chief led people to erect a stele for you at the entrance of the village shrine. Let me take you to see it.\"","Seeing them settle the matter of renovating the ancestral tombs in just a few words, Oldest Song, who was following behind, felt a complex mix of emotions in his heart.","There was a sense of loss from being ignored and unable to intervene.","Walking beside him, Second Song nudged Oldest Song's arm with his hand.","\"Big brother, a major event like repairing the ancestral tombs should be left to us two sons. You are the eldest, why don't you go talk to Dad about it?\"","Oldest Song thought about it and felt it made sense. Just as he was about to nod and go speak to Old Man Song, Second Song added another sentence.","\"Tell Jinzhao to hand over the silver for the tomb renovations to the two of us, and we'll handle it.\"","Oldest Song's feet instantly skidded to a halt. He blinked and blew his nose.","\"I think we should let Jinzhao and Qiming handle it. They are successful and have broad horizons; the ancestors will definitely be more satisfied.\"","Saying this, he quickened his pace and quickly distanced himself.","Since he wasn't the one paying, it was better to speak less. When the time came to repair the tombs, helping out would count as participation.","Watching Oldest Song walk away briskly, Second Song stomped his foot in displeasure.","Old Man Song pulled Song Jinzhao to the entrance of the village shrine.","A rectangular stone stele, six or seven feet tall, stood surrounded by stones in the middle. Engraved prominently upon it were Song Jinzhao's name, birth, the reason for her ennoblement, the date, and a series of praises for her character and merits.","Old Man Song spoke with a face full of pride, \"The village chief said that once you returned, they would open the inner shrine. Once the ancestral tombs are repaired, I'll go talk to him.\"","Looking at the stone stele before her, Song Jinzhao felt a bit conflicted.","Besides feeling honored, it also felt as if a heavy weight had been pressed onto her shoulders.","Song Shixue walked a circle around the stele. Having only her sister's monument standing here felt a bit bare.","\"Brother, when your official rank grows higher and higher in the future, you should also erect a stele next to our sister's. That would look much better.\"","Song Qiming curled his lips into a helpless smile. \"You certainly think highly of me.\"","\"County Princess, Magistrate Zhang of Xining City has arrived,\" Hu Sanluo reported as he ran over.","Barely stepping through the courtyard gate upon returning home, Zhang Yuanzong rushed over from the main hall and bowed deeply with a long salute.","\"This humble official, Magistrate Zhang Yuanzong of Xining City, pays his respects to the Linghui County Princess.\"","Song Jinzhao said, \"We are old acquaintances, Lord Zhang. There is no need for such formalities.\"","Zhang Yuanzong straightened his posture and cupped his hands in greeting upon seeing Song Qiming.","\"Lord Song.\"","Song Qiming nodded in response, \"Lord Zhang.\"","As they sat down to exchange pleasantries, Zhang Yuanzong asked, \"How long will the County Princess be able to stay at home for this visit?\"","Song Jinzhao replied, \"About ten days to half a month. I plan to renovate our family's ancestral tombs this time, and since Qiming placed third in the imperial examination, we also need to host a banquet to celebrate with the villagers. You must definitely come when the time arrives, my lord.\"","The smile faded from Zhang Yuanzong's face as he regretfully said, \"To be honest with you, Princess, this humble official will be departing in three days to take up a new post in Anyang Prefecture, so I'm afraid I won't be able to attend the banquet.\"","\"Oh? Has Lord Zhang been promoted?\" Moving from Xining City to Anyang Prefecture was undoubtedly a promotion.","Zhang Yuanzong smiled calmly and cupped his hands toward Song Jinzhao once more.","\"Thanks to the County Princess's blessings, the transfer order came down before the new year. I have been promoted to Co-Prefect of Anyang Prefecture. If it weren't for the delay in the new magistrate's arrival, I would have already left to take up my post.\"","Song Qiming interjected, \"May I ask who the new magistrate is? Has he arrived yet?\"","Zhang Yuanzong replied, \"It is Xiang Guangnian, a newly minted Jinshi. Speaking of which, he is from the same batch of graduates as Lord Song. He will arrive the day after tomorrow.\"","Song Qiming frowned in confusion and began to recall. \"I feel like I've seen that name somewhere before.\"","But he didn't know the person.","Song Jinzhao arched her brow and reminded him, \"He was the top scorer in the final metropolitan examination. His name was right next to Gao Li's.\"","Song Qiming suddenly understood. \"Right, that's him.\"","\"I was wondering why it looked so familiar. It was on the metropolitan examination roll.\"","If one did not perform well in the metropolitan exam and ranked low in the court exam, without any official vacancies, some new Jinshi often had to wait three to five months, and waiting a year or half a year was also a common occurrence.","The next day, when Song Jinzhao took people into the city to find a feng shui master, Song Qiming took the opportunity to visit Scholar Zheng's home.","Upon entering, the familiar sound of reciting texts reached his ears. As Song Qiming looked at the students studying in the private school, for a brief, dazed moment, he saw his past self."]},{"number":305,"title":"Chapter 305: Renovating the Ancestral Hall, Urging Marriage","paragraphs":["Hearing from the servants that Song Qiming had come to visit, Scholar Zheng, who was drinking tea to soothe his throat, hurried out of the room to welcome him.","\"Qiming.\"","Dressed in a long green scholar's robe, he looked exactly the same as he did back then.","Song Qiming quickly stepped forward and bowed deeply to Scholar Zheng. \"Your student greets you, sir.\"","Scholar Zheng reached out to support Song Qiming's hands. \"I haven't seen you in over two years, and you've grown so much. Did Gaoli not come back?\"","Song Qiming shook his head. \"The Ministry of War is busy, so he didn't have time to return. I was only able to come back this time thanks to my eldest sister.\"","The commotion outside attracted the attention of the students studying in the elementary and classics halls.","\"Who is that? A new student?\"","Sitting by the window, Song Yaozu quietly turned his head to the person behind him and whispered, \"That's my older cousin. He was the second runner-up in last year's imperial palace examination, and now he's a high-ranking official in the capital.\"","His classmate craned his neck. \"Your cousin is back? Then did your cousin who became a County Princess come back too?\"","Just as Song Yaozu was about to speak, someone rapped on his desk.","He shrank his neck and turned back around to see his teacher glaring at him fiercely with a disciplinary ruler in hand.","\"You were distracted and talking during morning class. I order you to copy the article we are currently reading ten times and hand it in before morning class tomorrow.\"","Song Yaozu lowered his head bitterly. \"Yes.\"","If he had known, he would have waited until after class to talk. How could he possibly finish copying something ten times?","Inside the room, the more Scholar Zheng looked at Song Qiming, the more satisfied he felt. This was his most successful student.","Song Qiming took a sip of tea. \"It seems there are a lot more students in the private school.\"","With a glance, he could see the numbers had at least doubled, and the lecture hall was completely full.","Scholar Zheng replied, \"Thanks to your success in the imperial exams, people from all the surrounding villages heard about it and sent their children to me to teach. There were too many people, so I had to hire two more teachers. It allows me to steal a little leisure amidst the busyness.\"","As the two chatted, the topic shifted to Song Yongnian and Song Yaozu, who were currently attending class in the classics hall.","Scholar Zheng's tone became slightly subdued.","\"Yongnian is now a child scholar. The boy lacks natural talent, but he is quite hardworking. It's not impossible for him to pass the county exams and become a full scholar if he studies for a few more years, though it will ultimately take him a longer time.\"","\"Yaozu falls a bit short. He talks a lot and has many friends, but he doesn't use his cleverness for studying. I've caught him climbing the wall to sneak out at noon several times. He is still young now, but if he gets a few years older and still can't pass the child scholar exams, it would be better for him to find another path. That would be better than wasting time and money.\"","Song Qiming glanced at the students running out the door after class.","\"My second uncle will naturally worry about my younger cousin's affairs. I imagine he won't give up on him, so just let him study for a few more years. He's too young to do any real work outside anyway.\"","Scholar Zheng nodded slowly and sighed with emotion.","\"That's true. I suppose I will likely never meet another student as brilliant as you.\"","Song Qiming picked up the teapot and refilled Scholar Zheng's cup.","\"What are you saying, sir? You are not old at all. Perhaps you will meet one someday.\"","Scholar Zheng picked up his teacup and shook his head with a smile.","Even though Song Jinzhao was a firm believer in science, the fact that she had managed to transmigrate here made her adopt an attitude of \"better to believe it than not.\" Thus, she still sought out the most famous feng shui master in Xining City.","Hearing that the County Princess wanted to repair her ancestral tombs, the white-bearded feng shui master grabbed his tools and came to the back mountain of Song Family Village.","He first wandered around the graves of Third Song and his wife, and then began to point out various things about the surrounding environment.","Old Man Song, who took this very seriously, immediately arranged for Oldest Song and Second Song to move trees and shift rocks. He didn't even allow the servants Song Jinzhao brought back to help, using the beautiful excuse that these tasks should be done by the men of the family to better show their filial piety, which would please their ancestors.","Knowing that Song Jinzhao and Song Qiming were going to repair the ancestral tombs, Village Head Song Mancang ran over that afternoon.","\"Jinzhao, the village ancestral shrine has been built for quite a few years now. The roof tiles and beams are old, and some of the ancestral tablets in the inner shrine are cracking.\"","\"After Qiming and Gaoli passed their imperial exams, I wanted to renovate the village shrine. Do you think our two families could pool some money together to refurbish it? We could have Qiming, our top scholar, personally write the words on the tablets, so people from other villages will know how successful the children of our Song Family Village are.\"","Hearing that Song Qiming would be asked to write the tablets, Old Man Song excitedly slapped his thigh.","\"I think that's a great idea. Our Qiming's handwriting is the most beautiful.\"","The siblings exchanged a look. The money to renovate the village shrine was a drop in the bucket for them, but it would earn them a good reputation. This was something they could do.","Song Jinzhao said, \"That's fine. If everyone in the village agrees, we will have to trouble the Village Head to handle the renovation matters. We can take care of the money.\"","Song Mancang waved his hand. \"I will go talk to every household in the village. As for the money, our two families will split it in half, and Gaoli has to chip in too.\"","Gaoli hadn't scored as high as Song Qiming on the exams, nor was his official rank as high. If he didn't contribute any money, his presence would be even less felt.","Song Jinzhao hired craftsmen from the city to repair the ancestral tombs. With the help of the servants she brought back, the work was completed in just two and a half days.","Knowing that Song Jinzhao and her family wouldn't stay in the village for long, Song Mancang hurried to persuade the villagers.","Since Song Jinzhao and the Village Head's family were providing the money, the others had to provide the labor. Every household had to participate in the renovation of the village shrine.","Hearing that they didn't have to spend their own money, the villagers essentially had no objections.","The wooden beams used for the renovation and the wood for the plaques were all cut from the mountains by the villagers together.","On the day the renovation was completed, Song Jinzhao and Song Qiming led the villagers of Song Family Village in a grand sacrificial ceremony. Song Mancang even hosted a ten-table continuous banquet.","After the ceremony ended, Old Man Song and Song Jinzhao began to busy themselves with organizing a celebratory banquet for Song Qiming's success in the imperial exams.","Many prominent families in Xining City heard the news, and one by one, they showed up uninvited with gifts in hand.","The number of guests on the day of the banquet exceeded the total number of households in the entire Song Family Village.","At the main table, Song Qiming and the newly appointed magistrate of Xining City, Xiang Guangnian, chatted for a long time.","After all the official business was concluded, Song Jinzhao only had three days left of her planned stay in the village.","In the main hall, Old Man Song was reluctant to see them go, while at the same time, he began to worry about Song Jinzhao's marriage.","\"There must be many talented young men in the capital. Now that Qiming has entered the court as an official, you should also consider the major events of your own life. Pick a good one, whether you marry into his family or take a live-in husband, you have to start making arrangements.\"","Song Jinzhao, who had been specifically called over to sit down, paused her expression for a moment.","Then she spoke, \"Qiming isn't married yet, and Anhao is still young. Marriage can wait until later.\"","Watching Song Jinzhao walk away after speaking, Old Lady Song reached out and stopped Song Qiming, who was trying to follow her.","\"Qiming, you are the eldest son of the third branch. Your older sister is already nineteen years old this year. You need to pay attention to her marriage.\"","Song Qiming awkwardly looked away at the wall.","\"Grandson understands what Grandfather and Grandmother mean, but my sister is a very independent person. It's very difficult for me to interfere in her marriage; it has to be someone she likes herself.\"","Old Man Song glared. \"I didn't tell you to force her! There are so many talented young men and sons of officials in the capital. Just bring a few more around her to show their faces. She's bound to find one she likes.\"","Old Lady Song nodded in agreement.","\"In the past, our family was poor, and Jinzhao had to take care of the three of you. But now that we have so many servants, we absolutely cannot delay your sister any longer. If we wait a few more years, it will be truly difficult to find a good match.\""]},{"number":306,"title":"Chapter 306: Planning to Open a School in the Village","paragraphs":["Dongfang Yukun and Cui Zhengyang automatically appeared in Song Qiming's mind.","Whether in terms of looks, talent, or family background, these two were considered the cream of the crop, but his older sister hadn't taken a fancy to them either.","At the thought of his sister getting married, he truly couldn't imagine who would be worthy of her.","He just felt like no one was good enough.","Song Shixue, returning from outside, saw Song Jinzhao. Her eyes lit up as she grabbed her hand and led her out.","\"Sister, I'm taking you to see something.\"","Song Shixue held Song Jinzhao's hand all the way to the riverside.","Pointing to a group of children squatting together on the riverbank not far away, she asked, \"Sister, what do you think they are doing?\"","Looking up, there were eight children in total. Upon closer inspection, Song Laidi and Song Pandi from the second branch of the family were among them.","The eight of them squatted in a circle, with buckets of clothes placed behind them.","Song Laidi was holding a wooden stick, writing stroke by stroke in the sand.","\"This is how you write Song Erhua,\" she said, looking up at the little girl squatting beside her after she finished writing.","Song Erhua stared at the incomprehensible strokes and characters on the ground, unable to resist touching them a couple of times.","\"So this is how my name is written. It looks quite nice. Laidi, can you teach me how to write it?\"","A little boy kneeling on the ground, his chest covered in sand, immediately grew anxious.","\"No, my name hasn't been written yet. We agreed it was my turn next.\"","Listening to the noisy chatter of the children, Song Jinzhao had already guessed what they were doing.","Noticing someone approaching, the children turned their heads one after another to look.","Seeing that it was Song Jinzhao and Song Shixue, Song Laidi and Song Pandi quickly stood up to greet them.","\"Sister Jinzhao, Sister Shixue.\"","Several names were written on the sandy ground, some crooked and some straight. One character was replaced by an 'X', and a small, muddy wooden stick lay nearby.","Song Jinzhao pointed to it and asked, \"Do you not know how to write this character?\"","Song Laidi glanced down and nodded.","\"Song Yuchan's name was given by a wandering Taoist priest. Uncle Sanluo never taught us the character 'chan', so I don't know how to write it.\"","A boy with a small braid raised his hand. \"Sister Jinzhao, they say you are a County Princess, a high official. Do you know how to write my name?\"","\"I do.\" Song Jinzhao lifted her skirt and squatted down.","She picked up the wooden stick from the ground, smoothed over the sand where the 'X' was drawn, and then wrote the character 'chan'.","Song Laidi looked at the character in the sand and bit her lip.","\"This character is so hard to write, it has so many strokes. No wonder Uncle Sanluo didn't teach it.\"","\"Erhua!\" A woman's call echoed from the village. Song Erhua, squatting on the ground, nimbly scrambled up, grabbed her bucket, and left.","\"My mother is calling me. I have to go back. See you tomorrow.\"","Thirteen-year-old Song Pandi glanced at the sun, which was almost directly overhead, and said to Song Laidi, \"Sister, we should go back too.\"","Song Laidi dropped the wooden stick, politely picked up her bucket full of clothes, and waved.","\"Sister Jinzhao, my sister and I will head home first. We'll come find Song Shixue to play this afternoon.\"","Seeing them leave, the other children also said their goodbyes and departed one by one.","Song Shixue looked down, gazing at the names written in the sand.","\"If only everyone could afford to go to school.\"","Song Jinzhao looked toward the distant village, her eyes thoughtful.","The cost of education in this era was too high, especially for the poorest people at the bottom of society.","For most, even basic food, clothing, and shelter were luxuries. How could they send their children to school? They didn't have the money, nor did they dare to dream of it.","Upon returning home, Song Jinzhao called Hu Sanluo over and asked him how he had been teaching Song Laidi and the others to read.","Hu Sanluo ran back to the side room and brought a few old books to Song Jinzhao.","\"This servant just teaches them to read and write according to the book. I skip the ones I don't know.\"","\"The lines of poetry Miss Laidi recited last time were just memorized by rote. This servant doesn't know what they actually mean either.\"","Song Jinzhao opened the poetry collection. These were the books she had bought for Qiming and Shixue when they first started their education.","\"Why didn't you let them take the books back with them? With three people learning, do they all share them during class?\"","Hu Sanluo shook his head. \"Miss Qiaoniang uses the old books that Young Master Yongnian no longer needs. These are the ones Miss Laidi and Miss Pandi use.\"","\"At first, they took them back a few times, but later Miss Laidi said to just leave them here and read them when they come over to study every day.\"","Recalling what Second Aunt Song had said the other day, Song Jinzhao had a guess in her heart.","\"Open a school?\" Song Qiming's eyes widened, his eyebrows raised high.","Song Jinzhao nodded slightly. \"Today, Shixue saw Laidi on the riverbank teaching the village children how to write their own names.\"","\"Children from poor families can't afford an education, and girls have even less of a chance to enter a school. I want to open a school in the village where both boys and girls can study. By teaching the village children to read and write, they will have more options in the future.\"","Song Qiming looked up in thought. \"I support whatever you want to do, Sister. But are we going to open the school in our house? Grandpa doesn't know how to read, and we won't be at home. Who will manage it?\"","Song Jinzhao shook her head; she had already figured it out before bringing it up.","\"There is an empty room in the renovated village ancestral hall. We can open the school there.\"","\"We will hire the teacher and let the village children attend without paying tuition fees. The village chief will definitely agree, and we can leave the management of the school to him.\"","Song Qiming asked, \"Do you have any requirements for the teacher's qualifications, Sister? It's relatively hard to hire a Xiucai in Xining City. If a Tongsheng is acceptable, it shouldn't be a big problem. I can go ask Teacher Zheng.\"","Song Jinzhao replied, \"A Tongsheng will do. I just want to provide them with an opportunity to learn to read. A Tongsheng's knowledge is enough.\"","Hearing this, Song Qiming thought for a moment and then nodded.","\"I understand what you mean, Sister. Let's go find the village chief then.\"","At Song Gaoli's house.","A short exclamation erupted inside the house, startling the spring swallows resting on the thatched roof into a hasty flight.","\"Jinzhao, say that again. Did you just say you want to open a school?\"","Song Mancang stood up abruptly, his eyes wide as he sought confirmation from Song Jinzhao once more.","A clear and affirmative voice rang out in the room, striking the minds of everyone present.","\"Yes, I was thinking that since the room in the ancestral hall is sitting empty anyway, we might as well open a school to let the village children learn to read and write. I will hire the teacher, and the children can attend tuition-free. What do you think?\"","Song Mancang paced around the room in ecstasy, looking at Song Jinzhao as if she were a lifesaver.","\"This is a great deed of charity and virtue. If we can produce a few more promising children like Qiming and Gaoli, our Song family village will surely become famous far and wide.\"","Meeting Song Jinzhao's eyes with a fervent gaze, he grabbed her arm and said with deep sincerity, \"Jinzhao, on behalf of the 136 households in the Song family village, I thank you. I thank you on behalf of all the children in the village.\"","Song Jinzhao clasped Song Mancang's hand in return, stopping him from kneeling.","\"There's no need for this, Village Chief. Qiming and I both came from the Song family village, so of course we want to see the people here do better and better.\"","\"Qiming and I will be departing for the capital in a few days, so we will have to trouble you to take care of the school's affairs.\""]},{"number":307,"title":"Chapter 307: Fourteen and Getting Married, Can I Stop Going to School","paragraphs":["Song Mancang nodded continuously, \"That is natural. Jinzhao, if you have any requirements, just say them. I will definitely do as you say.\"","After everyone sat down, Song Jinzhao began to speak.","\"First, the school will waive tuition and miscellaneous fees.\"","\"Second, children studying at the school must be at least six years old, and the maximum age cannot exceed sixteen.\"","\"Third, both boys and girls will be accepted. If a family has both boys and girls, but does not send the girls to school, the boys will not be accepted either.\"","\"Finally, everyone can only study at the school for three years. After three years, they will automatically graduate.\"","Song Mancang hesitated, \"Isn't three years too short?\"","Song Jinzhao shook her head, \"If things that don't cost money are not restricted by time, there will always be people who won't cherish them.\"","\"My goal is to let them learn to read and write.\"","\"As long as they study seriously, basic books like the Three Character Classic, Hundred Family Surnames, and Thousand Character Classic can be finished in three years. If they don't study seriously, staying a few more years would just be a waste.\"","Sitting to the side, Song Qiming said, \"We will hire a Tongsheng scholar to be the teacher, and the teaching will be more practical. If anyone wants to take the imperial examinations, they can go to another private school after their elementary education.\"","After hearing this, Song Mancang already understood Song Jinzhao and Song Qiming's thoughts.","What was being given was an opportunity; which path they wanted to take in the future would depend on themselves.","But this opportunity was already hard to come by for the children of Songjia Village.","There wasn't much time left for Song Jinzhao and the others. Since they decided to do it, they had to move fast.","After all matters were discussed and settled, the village head immediately picked up a gong, ran to the entrance of the village ancestral hall, and started beating it.","Hearing the sound, the villagers walked out one by one.","\"It's not time to pay the grain tax, so why is the village head beating the gong?\"","Song Ada, who lived next to the old house, walked out and said with a look of horror, \"Could it be that the imperial court is conscripting soldiers again?\"","The villagers who heard this shrank their necks in fear.","\"How is that possible? The imperial court isn't fighting a war, why would they suddenly conscript soldiers!\"","Whether curious, doubtful, or afraid, the villagers still hurried toward the ancestral hall.","Old Man Song guessed that it was about opening the school. With the mindset of watching the excitement, he still pulled Old Lady Song along to the ancestral hall.","Seeing that almost everyone had arrived, the village head began to shout at the top of his lungs, announcing the matter of Song Jinzhao funding the opening of a school.","The crowd of over a hundred people instantly exploded into an uproar.","Everyone discussed animatedly, shouting in disbelief, \"Village Head, is tuition really waived?\"","Song Mancang nodded vigorously, \"Not only is tuition waived, but you don't even have to spend money on the brushes, ink, paper, and inkstones needed at the school.\"","The villagers cast fervent gazes at Song Jinzhao and Song Qiming, who sat unmoving on the chairs behind the village head.","Ever since Song Jinzhao was titled a County Princess, and Song Qiming and Song Gaoli became officials, Songjia Village had gained a good reputation, and they were all looked up to by others when they went out.","But now, free education—this was a tangible benefit.","\"Village Head, how do we sign up? Is there a limit on the number of people? My Yuchan will sign up first.\"","\"Village Head, why six years old? Can my five-year-old son go to the school to study?\"","\"...\"","Over a hundred people chattered non-stop, making people's eardrums ache from the noise.","Second Song grabbed Old Man Song's arm.","\"Dad, since it doesn't cost money, can I have Yaozu come back to the village to study?\"","Old Man Song looked at him. \"The teacher Jinzhao and the others are hiring is a Tongsheng, while Teacher Zheng is a Xiucai. Think about it carefully yourself.\"","Second Song closed his mouth in conflict, his mind swaying back and forth between academic excellence and free education.","Upon seeing Oldest Song, he couldn't help but complain to him, \"Why do you think Jinzhao didn't hire a Xiucai to be the teacher? It's not like she lacks the money.\"","Oldest Song couldn't help but roll his eyes at him.","\"There aren't many Xiucai in Xining City. Those willing to teach have opened their own private schools at home. Who would be willing to come to a village!\"","Second Song thought about it and felt it made sense, but he still felt uncomfortable in his heart.","A woman ran up to Song Jinzhao, trying to curry favor. \"Jinzhao girl, the village head said that if the girls don't go to school, the boys can't go either. But my Chunnu is fourteen this year and is about to discuss marriage. Does she not count?\"","Song Jinzhao raised her eyes and stared at her. \"Then wait until she has gone to school for two years before discussing marriage.\"","The woman's smile froze, her face looking as if it had cracked in several places.","\"Jinzhao girl, girls will marry sooner or later. It doesn't matter whether they study or not. You see, the private schools in the city only accept boys.\"","Song Jinzhao's face darkened. She stood up and raised her voice, \"I am a woman. Since I am paying the silver, girls must be accepted.\"","\"They have to marry anyway, so what does it matter if it's two years later? If you find it difficult, Auntie, you can send your son to study in the city.\"","The villagers who were gathered around the village head talking suddenly fell silent. Seeing that Song Jinzhao was unhappy, no one dared to speak for a moment.","Old Man Song squeezed in and said to the woman, \"Who says it's useless for girls to study? Wasn't my Jinzhao titled a County Princess by the Emperor?\"","The village head stepped forward, \"Mazi's wife, many girls in the village marry at sixteen. Isn't fourteen too early for your family?\"","\"If you've really picked a good person, you can get engaged now and marry in two years; it won't be too late. Only our Songjia Village has this opportunity for free education. Don't think about it the wrong way.\"","After the village head spoke, many people began to echo his sentiments.","Seeing that no one was on her side, the woman smiled awkwardly and backed down.","\"I was just asking. Since it's not allowed, I will definitely send her.\"","Song Jinzhao knew that the thinking of ancient people was hard to change, but since she was the one paying, things had to be done according to her words.","She said to Song Mancang, \"The villagers probably have many more questions to ask. I'll leave this place to you.\"","\"I only have one point: the school's enrollment must strictly follow the requirements I stated, otherwise I won't pay the silver.\"","Song Mancang quickly patted his chest and guaranteed, \"Don't worry, with me guarding the gate, it will definitely be done according to your requirements. If any family has objections, their children won't be accepted.\"","That very night, the village head compiled the enrollment list for the school and handed it to Song Jinzhao overnight.","There were a total of one hundred and thirty-six households in Songjia Village, and there were one hundred and three people on the list.","Almost all the eligible children had signed up: forty-three boys and sixty girls. The three girls from the first and second branches were all included.","Holding the list, Song Qiming said, \"With so many people, one teacher won't be able to teach them all.\"","Song Jinzhao: \"The ancestral hall also can't fit so many desks.\"","Song Mancang had thought of this problem before coming.","\"We can open up the outer hall and have the boys and girls study separately.\"","\"The empty room is large; it can be used for the girls, and the boys can be in the outer hall.\"","Tapping her fingertips on the table, Song Jinzhao felt there was no problem.","\"Then we will hire two teachers. Tomorrow, Qiming and I will go to Xiucai Zheng's house to finalize the candidates.\""]},{"number":308,"title":"Chapter 308: Zheng Jiangyue: Aspiring to Be a Female Teacher","paragraphs":["In the early morning, the sun rose, bathing the entire courtyard in the rosy light of dawn.","Knowing that the third branch of the family was heading to Xining City today, Song Yongnian and Song Yaozu were sent over after breakfast to hitch a ride.","Second Aunt Song whispered in Song Yaozu's ear, \"Make sure you talk more with your cousins in the carriage and try to get on their good side.\"","Song Yaozu reluctantly bit his lip.","He also wanted to maintain a good relationship, but every time they spoke, Brother Qiming would always ask about his studies, which was so annoying to hear.","Seeing him stay silent, Second Aunt Song frowned and gave his back a hard pinch.","\"Did you hear me?\"","Song Yaozu grimaced in pain, instinctively shrinking his shoulders to brush her off.","\"I know.\"","After getting into the carriage, Song Yongnian occasionally asked Song Qiming about things from his school days.","Song Yaozu watched this, feeling a bit awkward in his heart, so he simply closed his eyes and pretended to catch up on sleep.","In the main hall, Scholar Zheng couldn't help but nod after learning the purpose of their visit.","\"Given the current power and status of the County Princess and Qiming, opening a school in the village is a good thing for your reputation.\"","\"Hiring two young scholars as teachers is not difficult. I have a few old classmates and friends in Xining City I can go and ask.\"","Being able to teach at a school opened by the County Princess was something ordinary people could only dream of, it was just...","\"It's just that none of them have ever taught female students. Does the County Princess plan to teach them according to the same standards as the boys?\"","Song Jinzhao replied, \"I would like it to be a bit different, but there are no female teachers in Xining City, so as long as they can learn to read, that will be enough. We will follow the same standards for both boys and girls.\"","Scholar Zheng stroked his beard and said, \"I understand. Please sit here for a moment. I will go out, and if they agree, I will bring them back to meet the County Princess.\"","Song Jinzhao stood up and nodded, \"Then I must thank Teacher Zheng.\"","Scholar Zheng was just about to instruct the porter to prepare the carriage when Zheng Jiangyue, who had just brought tea into the room, chased after him and grabbed his sleeve.","\"Father, your daughter has something to discuss with you.\"","Scholar Zheng looked at his daughter in confusion.","\"What is it? If it's not urgent, wait until I get back. The County Princess and Qiming are still waiting in the room.\"","Zheng Jiangyue gripped his arm tightly, her brows furrowed together, and dragged out her words in a coquettish tone.","\"It's very urgent. If I wait until you come back, it'll be too late.\"","Under Zheng Jiangyue's persistent pulling and tugging, Scholar Zheng was dragged into her room.","Sitting in the main hall drinking tea, Song Jinzhao turned her head and saw Zheng Jiangyue taking Scholar Zheng away, but she didn't think much of it.","In the room, looking at his slightly anxious daughter, Scholar Zheng asked her.","\"What exactly is so urgent?\"","Zheng Jiangyue brought over a stool for Scholar Zheng to sit on. She was a little nervous in her heart, but also excited.","\"Father, I want to go to Songjia Village to be a female teacher. Can you recommend me to the County Princess?\"","Scholar Zheng's expression froze, and his mind went completely blank.","After he reacted, he stood up abruptly, his hands leaning on the round table almost pulling the tablecloth down.","\"Nonsense! You've never taught before. How can you go to a school and lead students?\"","The anticipation on Zheng Jiangyue's face was as if it had been slapped away, instantly turning into displeasure.","\"Watching you give lectures in the classroom every day, I've learned just by watching.\"","\"I've even helped you grade the assignments of the elementary students before. Why can't I go teach at the school?\"","\"The County Princess also just said that if there were a female teacher in Xining City, she would definitely prefer to hire a female teacher to teach those girls. I think I'm very suitable.\"","\"Not only can I teach them to read and write, but I can also teach them to play chess and the lute. I am much more suitable than a male teacher~\"","Scholar Zheng still shook his head in disagreement. \"If you go to Songjia Village to teach, what about Yunzhi? He's only three years old. He can't be without his parents by his side.\"","Zheng Jiangyue grabbed his sleeve and swung it. \"Mother and the maids are at home; they can take care of Yunzhi.\"","\"The village school finishes classes right at the beginning of the Shen hour. There are five days of classes and two days off. There will be plenty of free time left to accompany Yunzhi.\"","\"Father, please let me go.\"","Scholar Zheng pulled his sleeve back. \"No. Ah Rao doesn't know about this, and he won't agree to it.\"","Zheng Jiangyue blocked Scholar Zheng's path, raising three fingers to guarantee, \"As long as I speak to him, Ah Rao will definitely agree. Father, please just mention it for me. If the County Princess doesn't agree, I absolutely won't force it.\"","Scholar Zheng raised a hand and pinched the bridge of his nose.","\"I can support you, and Ah Rao can support you too. Waking up early every day to go to Songjia Village to teach is so tiring. It's not worth it for that little bit of tuition money.\"","The pleading in Zheng Jiangyue's eyes disappeared, and her tone became serious and firm.","\"It's not entirely for the tuition money. I ask myself, and my talents and learning are no less than a man's.\"","\"But as a woman, I am shackled at every turn. After marrying, I can only stay at home to assist my husband and raise my children. But isn't the County Princess also a woman?\"","\"I can't be as amazing as she is, but I also want to do something within my power. With such a good opportunity right in front of me, I definitely have to try. If you won't mention it to the County Princess, I will go and tell her myself.\"","Saying this, Zheng Jiangyue was about to turn around and rush out.","Scholar Zheng hurriedly stopped her.","Seeing her feeling both wronged and resolute, he was caught in a dilemma for a moment, not knowing how to persuade her.","\"Master, just let her go,\" Madam Zheng walked in from outside.","Seeing his wife enter, Scholar Zheng breathed a sigh of relief but also couldn't believe it.","\"Madam, you agree?\"","Madam Zheng nodded. \"In the past, when you were teaching in the classroom, she often hid outside to watch.\"","\"The assignments you handed over to her, she graded more seriously than anyone else. I think she can handle this matter of being a female teacher.\"","Zheng Jiangyue joyfully hugged Madam Zheng's arm, her eyes sparkling.","\"Mother, I knew you understood me the best.\"","Looking at his precious daughter acting coquettishly toward his wife, these words sounded a bit grating to Scholar Zheng.","What did she mean her mother understood her the best? It was as if he didn't understand her.","\"Father, Mother has already agreed. Will you just say yes?\"","Scholar Zheng let out a long sigh, having no choice but to compromise.","\"I will take you to see the County Princess. Whether it works out or not is up to you.\"","Zheng Jiangyue happily agreed, \"Thank you, Father. I definitely won't make you lose face.\"","Seeing Scholar Zheng return, Song Qiming and Song Jinzhao, who were sitting in the main hall, stood up to greet him.","Seeing the confusion on their faces, Scholar Zheng stepped aside and signaled his daughter to step forward.","He cupped his hands in greeting toward Song Jinzhao.","\"County Princess, although my little daughter Jiangyue is somewhat dull in aptitude, she is well-read in poetry and literature and has some understanding of the classics. I would like to recommend her to become a female teacher in the school you are opening, and I invite the County Princess to test her.\"","Song Jinzhao's eyes widened slightly, and she shifted her gaze to Zheng Jiangyue.","She met the other woman's gaze, which was filled with four parts nervousness and six parts anticipation.","She didn't know much about Zheng Jiangyue, only that she was Teacher Zheng's only daughter, was already married, and her husband had married into her family.","\"Miss Zheng, do you want to be a female teacher yourself, or does Teacher Zheng want you to be one?\"","With so many students in the private school, the Zheng family shouldn't be lacking money right now.","Scholar Zheng was just about to speak when Zheng Jiangyue's voice rang out.","\"To answer the County Princess, I want to do it myself, which is why I asked my father to recommend me.\"","\"Compared to my father's former classmates, I feel I am much more suitable.\"","Seeing that Song Jinzhao was looking at her quietly and listening very seriously, Zheng Jiangyue gathered her courage and continued speaking."]},{"number":309,"title":"Chapter 309: Selecting the Candidate and Returning to the Capital","paragraphs":["\"First of all, there is the strict boundary between men and women, so having a female teacher means there is no need to worry about any damage to one's reputation.\"","\"Secondly, the teaching methods of the teachers recommended by my father are all geared toward the imperial examinations, but women do not need to take these exams.\"","\"Not only can I teach them how to read and write, but I can also teach them accounting, playing the zither, and embroidery—things that men cannot teach.\"","\"Furthermore, compared to men, women can more easily build a close relationship with young girls. For instance, guiding their hands to teach them how to write is something men cannot do.\"","\"If the County Princess is worried about my knowledge, you may test me with any questions you like. I will absolutely not fall short compared to them.\"","Looking at Zheng Jiangyue, who was speaking with such confidence and fighting hard for the opportunity, the admiration in Song Jinzhao's eyes grew stronger.","She saw a hint of a modern woman in Zheng Jiangyue.","Song Qiming said, \"Sister, Miss Zheng's knowledge was personally taught by the teacher, and her skills in the zither, chess, calligraphy, and painting were passed down directly from the teacher's wife. There will definitely be no problem with her teaching.\"","Song Jinzhao's eyes curved in a smile. \"In that case, there is no need for a test. I could not ask for anything more than to hire a female teacher.\"","Zheng Jiangyue took a sharp breath, her eyebrows shooting up in surprise.","\"Thank you, County Princess. I will definitely teach them well.\"","Seeing that his daughter's matter was settled, Scholar Zheng finally went out.","An hour later, he brought back a white-haired old man who looked to be twenty years older than Teacher Zheng.","After they sat down and introductions were made, Song Jinzhao learned that they were indeed former classmates.","However, the other man had been relatively old when he passed the county-level exams, and the two had been classmates at the academy for three years.","Later, this Teacher Wen found a private school to teach at while continuing to study for the provincial exams, but he never managed to pass.","Song Qiming tested his knowledge on the spot, and after confirming there were no issues, they hired him.","After finalizing the annual salary and various benefits, the two signed the employment contracts right then and there.","After leaving the Zheng residence, Song Jinzhao and Song Qiming took their people to the streets to purchase tables, chairs, benches, brushes, ink, paper, inkstones, and books.","When several handcarts were pulled into the village, the village chief had already led people to clean the house thoroughly.","Song Mancang pointed at the blank plaque and asked Song Jinzhao.","\"Jinzhao, my girl, what do you think we should name this school? How about calling it Zhaoming School?\"","Song Jinzhao pursed her lips. \"Let's just call it Song Family School. It sounds nice.\"","Hearing this, Song Mancang grinned from ear to ear.","\"Alright, Song Family School it is. I also think this name sounds wonderful.\"","The name he had originally wanted was Song Family School, but he had been too embarrassed to say it, considering that all the school's future expenses would be covered by Song Jinzhao.","He had thought that naming it Zhaoming School would make the Song siblings happier.","Song Jinzhao handed the two employment contracts to Song Mancang.","\"The teachers have been decided. We hired a female teacher to teach the girls in the village. She is the daughter of Scholar Zheng.\"","Song Mancang opened the contracts and, upon seeing the names of Teacher Wen and Zheng Jiangyue, said good three times in a row.","\"A female teacher is great. The daughter of Scholar Zheng must have considerable talent. Having her teach the village girls is even more suitable than a male scholar.\"","To attend the school's opening ceremony, Song Jinzhao and her group stayed in Song Family Village for an extra two days.","The night before their departure, Song Jinzhao spoke with Old Man Song and Hu Sanluo for nearly an hour, ensuring that everything would run smoothly after she left.","When they left Song Family Village the next day, the sunlight was perfect, shining warmly upon them.","Compared to the past when only the two elders and the first and second branches of the family came to see them off, this time the village chief led many villagers to watch them leave from the village entrance, not dispersing until they were far away.","Song Jinzhao and her group also made a detour to Anyang Prefecture on their way.","Besides instructing them to regularly send silver to the school in Song Family Village, they also went to meet Steward Lu, who had taken over Chunxing's position.","Song Jinzhao also audited the accounts once over.","Song Qiming, meanwhile, went to the Mu residence to visit Mu Hongyue, the headmaster of Anyang Academy.","By the time they finished these tasks and returned to the capital, it was already early June.","In the front hall, Song Qiming placed the letters and bundles on the table.","\"These are the letters your grandfather asked us to bring you. The clothes and shoes were made by your aunt herself. They miss you very much.\"","Song Gaoli picked up the letter, looking at the familiar handwriting and subconsciously rubbing it with his thumb.","\"Are my parents, grandfather, and grandmother doing well?\"","His deep voice could not hide his concern. Being alone in the capital, he felt lonely amidst his longing for them.","Song Qiming sat down and comforted him, \"Do not worry, the village chief and Uncle Dazhuang are in robust health. During this trip back, my sister funded the opening of a school in the village. The village chief will be quite busy from now on.\"","This sudden news pulled Song Gaoli out of his nostalgic mood.","\"Opened a school?\"","Song Qiming took a bite of a rose pastry and nodded.","\"Song Family School. It has over a hundred students and accepts both boys and girls. The teachers we hired are Teacher Zheng's former classmate and his daughter.\"","Song Gaoli blinked in surprise, the image of Zheng Jiangyue appearing in his mind.","\"Teacher Zheng's daughter, Zheng Jiangyue?\"","Song Qiming said, \"Yes, there are no female teachers in Xining City, so she is the perfect fit.\"","In the backyard study, Qingshuang stood tall and straight in front of Song Jinzhao, reporting on what had happened in the capital during this period.","\"Prince Qi'an of the Second Rank and Prince Yingcheng of the Second Rank tried to repeat their old tricks to win over the court officials, but the officials with any standing in the court no longer buy into their influence. Therefore, the officials they contacted are of relatively low ranks and cannot make any waves.\"","\"After the princes in the palace successively reached their one-month milestones, the Emperor arranged adoptive mothers for them. They are all concubines of the Pin rank or higher, and the Fifth Prince was given to the Empress to raise.\"","Song Jinzhao's fingers resting on the table paused slightly, and a cold sneer appeared at the corners of her mouth.","Xiao Rongche and Xiao Rongyan were completely out of hope now.","Originally, the six princes had low statuses, but now their worth depended on their mothers, not to mention the Fifth Prince who was being raised by the Empress.","The court officials all had a scale in their hearts; naturally, they would not place bets when the odds of winning were slim.","In the front hall, after chatting about family matters, Song Gaoli brought up Duan Yanhua.","\"Two months ago, I discovered that the Second Prince wanted to bring Duan Yanhua under his wing. Worried that something might happen, I asked Lord Ye and Yukun to transfer him out of the capital. He is already on his way to Mingzhou.\"","Song Qiming frowned in curiosity.","\"Prince Yingcheng of the Second Rank actually took a fancy to Duan Yanhua?\"","A seventh-rank compiler in the Hanlin Academy, old and incompetent—Xiao Rongyan should not have even bothered trying to recruit him.","Song Gaoli said, \"You were not in the capital, so you do not know. The Emperor arranged high-status adoptive mothers for the six recently born princes, and the Fifth Prince is even being raised personally by the Empress.\"","\"Many officials feel that the Emperor favors making the Fifth Prince the Crown Prince. It is no longer as easy for the First Prince and Second Prince to recruit people to their factions as it used to be. Taking an interest in Duan Yanhua is just them casting a wide net without being picky.\"","Letting out a deep sigh, Song Gaoli felt nothing but regret in his heart for having so easily taken him as his teacher back then.","\"After I became the Director of the Armory Bureau, Duan Yanhua tried several times to drag me to restaurants to drink with other court officials. I used the excuse that the Ministry of War was too busy to reject them all. On top of that, I was unwilling to help him maneuver for a promotion. Seeing that I was of no use to him, he was more than eager to accept the Second Prince's overtures.\"","\"Everyone knows that Duan Yanhua is my teacher. Tearing up our relationship would be bad for my reputation, and if something happened to him, it would drag me down too. It was better to just transfer him away early and be done with it once and for all.\"","Without the need to enter the palace every day, Song Jinzhao suddenly had a lot more free time after returning to the capital.","After taking stock of her current businesses, she began to set her sights on other ventures.","The businesses in the capital were all out in the open. Not wanting to draw too much attention, Song Jinzhao simply arranged for her people to open shops in neighboring cities under the guise of being competitors. This way, she could avoid inciting jealousy over her wealth and keep her fortune from being targeted."]},{"number":310,"title":"Chapter 310: Turmoil in the Southwest, Envoys from the Northern Frontier","paragraphs":["Today, Song Jinzhao had just returned from outside when the Minister of Works, Ou Shinian, arrived at her door requesting an audience with a brisk look on his face.","\"The hull assembly of the ocean-going sailing ship is currently underway in Mingzhou. The Emperor has ordered me to go to Mingzhou to oversee the construction and complete a seven-day and seven-night sea trial. Would the County Princess like to go together?\"","Song Jinzhao was somewhat surprised. \"So fast? Did they only build one, or several?\"","Ou Shinian replied, \"We are building one first. If there are no issues, we can officially begin mass production.\"","\"The maritime information along the coast has been mostly gathered. Once completed, we can sail across the ocean to find new territories. We might even find crops with a higher yield than potatoes.\"","\"Mingzhou is too far. I have just returned to my hometown and do not wish to travel far again. I will pass on the sea trial.\"","Ou Shinian thought about it and agreed. The round trip would take three months, and the weather was hot. If it hadn't been for the Emperor's decree, he originally planned to send his subordinates over.","\"The County Princess deserves the most credit for the creation of this ship. It is truly a pity that you cannot be the first to step onto the deck and sail the seas.\"","Song Jinzhao curled her lips into a faint smile.","\"It doesn't matter. There will always be opportunities in the future.\"","The day after returning from the County Princess's estate, Ou Shinian packed his bags and prepared to head to Mingzhou.","As he was exiting the city gates, two fast horses brushed past him one after another.","The curtains of his carriage were not drawn, and the kicked-up dust blew right into Ou Shinian's face, making it uncomfortably difficult to open his eyes.","\"Who was that? Riding so fast at the city gates.\"","He complainingly lifted the carriage curtain, but his expression slightly changed when he saw the soldiers on horseback wearing rattan armor.","Red belts, southwestern rattan armor—they were soldiers from the southwest.","Seeing that Ou Shinian hesitated to drop the curtain, his accompanying attendant asked, \"Master, are we still leaving today?\"","Ou Shinian nodded with a worried look. \"We leave.\"","Not long after dropping the curtain, Ou Shinian poked his head out the window.","\"Come here.\"","A soldier following behind the carriage rode closer and leaned in.","\"What are your orders, My Lord?\"","Ou Shinian instructed, \"Go back to the city and find out if the soldiers who just entered are from the southwest. If something has happened, catch up with me immediately and report back.\"","The soldier nodded in compliance. \"Yes, your subordinate will return at once.\"","Watching his subordinate turn around and leave, Ou Shinian took a deep breath to suppress the worry in his heart.","Perhaps it was nothing. Maybe he was just overthinking.","On the official path leading to the Imperial Study, the Minister of War, Wu Jianzheng, furrowed his brows deeply, hurrying forward with hasty steps.","Beads of sweat slid down his neck into his collar, and his back and chest were already soaked.","On another path, the Minister of Rites continuously touched the document placed in his sleeve with his right hand, his heart panicking, his hands trembling, and his chest feeling tight.","The two men, coming from the east and west, bumped into each other at the entrance of the Imperial Study. Seeing that the other's complexion was poor, their own moods worsened.","A young eunuch bent his waist and scurried into the inner chamber of the Imperial Study.","\"Reporting to Your Majesty, Lord Wu, the Minister of War, and Lord Kang, the Minister of Rites, are requesting an audience outside. They are already waiting at the door of the Imperial Study.\"","Xiao Chengjing, who was reviewing memorials, raised his head, a trace of doubt appearing on his face.","\"Why would the two of them come together? Send them in.\"","Wu Jianzheng and Kang Zhibo walked in side by side, and the urgency with which they knelt down was identical.","\"Reporting to Your Majesty,\" they spoke in unison, then glanced at each other.","\"Your Majesty!\" their voices rang out again.","Xiao Chengjing frowned in displeasure. \"Beloved Subject Wu, you speak first.\"","Wu Jianzheng offered up the newly received memorial with both hands. \"To reply to Your Majesty, a military report has arrived from the southwest. Salt fields have been discovered in Binzhou. The Yang clan of Panzhou and the Mu clan of Ningzhou have gone to war at Ningyuan City to fight over the salt fields.\"","\"The Mu clan was outmatched and retreated, but the Yang clan pursued them relentlessly, capturing three cities in a row. The Mu clan sent someone to ask the Southwest Provincial Administration Commissioner, Gu Zhongxun, for help, hoping the imperial court would dispatch troops for support. This is the memorial sent by Gu Zhongxun via eight-hundred-li express, along with the handwritten plea for help from Mu Ji'an, the Pacification Commissioner of Ningzhou.\"","Kang Zhibo, waiting on the side, had his pupils contract sharply. He looked in disbelief at the two memorials stacked in Wu Jianzheng's hands.","Troubles were coming one after another; this was simply adding frost to snow.","Eunuch Zhao hurriedly delivered the two memorials to Xiao Chengjing's side.","Opening the memorial, every word stamped onto Xiao Chengjing's heart, making his chest feel as if it were about to explode.","The Mu clan's handwritten letter even bore bloodstains. The battle must have been fierce, and there was no telling how things were now.","After finishing reading, Xiao Chengjing rubbed his forehead and closed his eyes. He felt mentally exhausted, and his mind was a bit chaotic.","Things had finally been peaceful for a while, but now something had happened in the southwest again. It seemed they did not want him, the Emperor, to sit comfortably on his throne at all.","\"Summon the Secretariat Director Dongfang Shaoting and Chancellor Gu Qishan for an audience.\"","Seeing that the Emperor hadn't remembered him, Kang Zhibo hurriedly knelt and cried out, \"Your Majesty, this humble subject also has an urgent matter to report.\"","Xiao Chengjing turned his dark gaze toward him, his tone deep and somewhat impatient. \"What is it?\"","The Ministry of Rites generally didn't have any major crises.","Kang Zhibo took out the document from his sleeve.","\"To reply to Your Majesty, this is a document just sent from the Kingdom of Shuobei. The Emperor of Shuobei wishes to send envoys to the capital to congratulate Your Majesty on your birthday. The diplomatic mission is already waiting at the border.\"","The air in the Imperial Study suddenly froze. The fly whisk in Eunuch Zhao's hand trembled.","Congratulate him on his birthday! When had the Kingdom of Shuobei ever been this friendly?","It felt somewhat bizarre.","\"He didn't come to congratulate me on my fiftieth birthday, so what is he doing here now?\"","Kang Zhibo kept his head down. \"According to the soldiers escorting the document, the Emperor of Shuobei heard that Your Majesty was blessed with six princes and seven princesses. Coupled with your approaching birthday, it is a double joy. For the sake of harmony between the two nations, he has specially sent envoys for friendly exchanges.\"","Eunuch Zhao placed the document on the desk in front of Xiao Chengjing.","Upon opening it, the document stamped with the national seal of Shuobei brought Xiao Chengjing immense pressure. He couldn't shake the feeling that things weren't this simple.","\"Who is the chief envoy of the mission?\"","Kang Zhibo replied, \"The Prince of Wei, Gong Linjue.\"","Xiao Chengjing was confused. \"Why isn't his surname He?\"","Kang Zhibo raised his head and explained, \"To reply to Your Majesty, Gong Linjue is a prince of a different surname newly ennobled by He Mingyuan, the Emperor of Shuobei. He is not a member of the Shuobei royal family.\"","\"I heard that this man possesses formidable martial arts and is highly favored and trusted by He Mingyuan. He also holds command over a hundred thousand troops of Shuobei. I fear his diplomatic mission this time comes with ill intentions.\"","Sitting on the imperial throne, Xiao Chengjing's hands tightly gripped the dragon-carved armrests. His dark pupils were fixed on the three documents on the desk. After pondering for a long time, he finally spoke.","\"Summon Secretariat Director Dongfang Shaoting, Chancellor Gu Qishan, and Grand Secretary of the Hanlin Academy Fei Yanzhang into the palace for an audience.\"","Wu Jianzheng and Kang Zhibo silently retreated to the side to wait.","Their stiff spines remained slightly bowed. Coupled with the oppressive atmosphere in the Imperial Study and the possibility of Xiao Chengjing losing his temper at any moment, the two men felt even more uncomfortable than standing outside baking in the sun."]},{"number":311,"title":"Chapter 311: Internal Troubles and External Threats","paragraphs":["The four men who had rushed over saw Wu Jianzheng and Kang Zhibo standing to the side, quietly wiping sweat from their faces with their sleeves. They immediately felt that something was wrong.","\"These are the memorials sent from the Southwest and Shuobei. Take a look at them.\"","Eunuch Zhao handed Gu Zhongxun's memorial, the Mu clan's handwritten letter, and the official document from the Shuobei State to three of them respectively.","After taking turns reading them, Fei Yanzhang immediately spoke with a solemn expression.","\"Your Majesty, the Yang clan's actions are clearly an attempt to annex the Mu clan under the guise of the salt field dispute. If the imperial court does not intervene and allows the Yang clan to continue expanding, they will inevitably raise an army in rebellion in the future.\"","Dongfang Shaoting tightened his grip on the letter. \"The foreign tribes in the Southwest revere the Yang and Mu clans. If the Mu clan falls, the situation in the Southwest will surely descend into chaos. We absolutely cannot let them dominate alone.\"","Gu Qishan closed the document sent from the Shuobei State.","\"We do not yet know the true purpose of Shuobei State sending envoys to celebrate the birthday. However, if the imperial court goes to war with the foreign tribes in the Southwest at this time, it is hard to guarantee that the other side won't take advantage of the situation to strike.\"","\"I feel that we should immediately dispatch a prominent court official to the Southwest to mediate the relationship between the two clans, using the majesty of the imperial court to pressure them and strive to make the Yang clan cease hostilities.\"","Dongfang Shaoting and Fei Yanzhang exchanged a glance.","Even though the Dongzhao State had been recovering and building up its strength for three years after the armistice with Shuobei State, the national treasury was still empty. The hearts of the people, which had finally settled down, could not bear even the slightest provocation.","If internal strife and external threats were to occur simultaneously right now, Dongzhao State's current national strength would find it very difficult to endure.","Gu Qishan's suggestion was indeed the best choice at present.","Fei Yanzhang stepped forward and said, \"If we adopt Prime Minister Gu's proposal, I believe the person sent to mediate in the Southwest must have a status sufficient to awe both clans. I propose sending an imperial prince.\"","Gu Qishan furrowed his brows sharply; this was not a good thing.","Dongfang Shaoting cupped his hands and said, \"In addition to this, I believe that while sending someone to mediate, we also need to mobilize troops to prevent any unforeseen events.\"","Gu Qishan immediately retorted, \"This action is unacceptable. It will make the Yang clan think the imperial court intends to go to war.\"","Dongfang Shaoting replied, \"Sending a prince to negotiate peace is enough to show how strongly the imperial court desires peace. Mobilizing troops, on the other hand, can serve to intimidate the Yang clan and force them to compromise and cease fighting. The benefits outweigh the disadvantages.\"","Gu Qishan swallowed hard in fear.","If the Yang clan actually killed the prince sent to mediate, what would they do?","This errand absolutely could not fall on the shoulders of the First Prince. It was too dangerous.","Xiao Chengjing's fingers tapped continuously on the desk.","\"According to what you say, which prince should be sent to the Southwest?\"","Having thought it through, Gu Qishan knelt and said, \"I recommend the Second Prince.\"","\"Prince Yingcheng of the Second Rank once studied under the Duke of Qing for a period of time. Compared to the First Prince, who has never spent time in a military camp, he is more suitable to go to the Southwest.\"","Dongfang Shaoting and Fei Yanzhang stealthily glanced at Gu Qishan at the same time.","This man's blatant ulterior motives were clear for all to see.","However, they did not intend to interfere. To them, it didn't matter which prince went.","Xiao Chengjing's gaze swept darkly over the top of Gu Qishan's head.","He said with a touch of sarcasm, \"Is my beloved Minister Gu unaware of the fine reputation the Second Prince left behind at the western suburbs military camp? I will deliberate further on the choice of candidate.\" He continued, \"Based on your words, who would be the most appropriate person to lead the troops there as a deterrent?\"","Wu Jianzheng stepped forward and said, \"I propose sending the Duke of Qing. With his prestige in the military, the Yang clan will certainly not dare to act rashly.\"","\"No!\" Three resolute voices rang out simultaneously, giving Wu Jianzheng a fright.","Looking up, he saw that Dongfang Shaoting, Gu Qishan, and Fei Yanzhang all disagreed.","Dongfang Shaoting said, \"I have heard that Gong Linjue possesses formidable martial arts skills and is the number one expert in Shuobei State. On his trip to the capital this time, it is hard to guarantee he won't test the strength of Dongzhao State's generals. If no one can withstand him then, wouldn't that boost the enemy's prestige?\"","Gu Qishan added, \"Three years ago, the Duke of Qing led troops to block Shuobei State's great army at the border. Gong Linjue will inevitably be wary of him upon entering the capital this time. If he is not in the capital, it will instead make the other side feel that the situation in the Southwest is dire, which is why His Majesty had to send the Duke of Qing to suppress it.\"","Fei Yanzhang concluded, \"Since the imperial court does not intend to go to war with the Yang clan, sending the Duke of Qing is a bit of a waste of his talents. I recommend General of Xuanwei, Wen Yong.\"","After Gu Qishan and the others emerged from the imperial study, it took no time at all for the news of the unrest in the Southwest and Shuobei sending envoys to celebrate the birthday to spread everywhere.","The first to receive an imperial decree was the Xuanwei General's Manor.","Wen Yong led his entire family to kneel in the front hall.","Everyone listened in silence as the decree-bearing eunuch read the imperial edict.","\"By the grace of Heaven, the Emperor decrees: According to an urgent memorial from the Provincial Administration Commissioner of the Southwest, the Yang clan of Panzhou and the Mu clan of Ningzhou have gone to war at Ningyuan City over a dispute concerning salt fields. The local people are suffering deeply from the ravages of war, and their lives are plunged into misery. I hereby specially order General of Xuanwei, Wen Yong, to lead ten thousand troops to the Southwest to take preventive measures. Respect this!\"","Wen Yong kowtowed solemnly and received the bright yellow silk scroll with both hands.","\"I receive the decree. Long live the Emperor, long live, long, long live!\"","\"Thank you for your hard work, Eunuch. However, the decree does not specify when I should depart. I humbly ask the Eunuch for guidance.\"","Clutching the imperial decree, Wen Yong felt a bit uncertain about the Emperor's intentions.","The decree only ordered him to bring ten thousand troops. Was he only supposed to take preventive measures and not fight? What if the foreign tribes in the Southwest initiated a war?","The eunuch smiled faintly and replied, \"General Wen need not worry. Regarding the unrest in the Southwest, His Majesty intends to dispatch a prince to mediate. The General only needs to wait a few more days.\"","As soon as these words were spoken, Wen Yong understood.","The Emperor did not want to go to war. On this journey, he would definitely be traveling alongside a prince.","But would it be the First Prince or the Second Prince?","This question not only made Wen Yong curious, but all the civil and military officials were curious as well.","If the mediation in the Southwest went well, it would be a great merit. But if it did not go well, and the Yang clan still wanted to go to war with the imperial court after annexing the Mu clan, then the prince, trapped deep in enemy camps, would either be captured alive and turned into a hostage or face certain death.","This errand was not only difficult but also dangerous. The two princes definitely did not want to go. Now it all depended on who the Emperor favored more.","Inside the manor of Prince Yingcheng of the Second Rank, Xiao Rongyan sat in a chair with a gloomy expression, the veins bulging on the hand gripping his teacup.","The next second, the cup was slammed heavily onto the table.","\"Gu Qishan, that old scoundrel, I will kill him sooner or later.\"","The strategist waiting to the side hurriedly spoke up to soothe Xiao Rongyan's temper.","\"Your Highness, please do not be angry. As I see it, Prime Minister Gu's actions are likely dropping a rock on his own foot.\"","\"The more he helps the First Prince target Your Highness, the more likely the Emperor will send the First Prince to the Southwest.\"","Following the assassination attempt on Song Jinzhao, Xiao Rongyan's most trusted servant, guards, and the manor's lieutenant general had all died.","Coupled with the dead assassins, wanting to make a move against anyone was no longer as easy as before.","The six princes who had been born already left them without competitiveness. If anything else happened, the Emperor would truly punish them severely.","Xiao Rongyan took a deep breath, holding it in to suppress his raging fury.","\"The situation in the court has changed drastically now. It truly leaves me at my wits' end.\"","The strategist lowered his head and remained silent.","The courtiers' attitudes toward the First Prince and the Second Prince depended on the Emperor's attitude toward them.","In the past, it was a guaranteed choice between the two of them. Now, they were being suppressed and kept from standing out. Unless they rebelled, they were indeed helpless."]},{"number":312,"title":"Chapter 312: Both Restored to the Rank of Jin Prince, Arriving at the Capital as the Palace Faces Utmost Crisis","paragraphs":["The imperial decree sending Xiao Rongche to the southwest was issued the following evening. The situation was urgent, so the Emperor ordered him and the General of Xuanwei to depart early the next morning. More importantly, Xiao Rongche's title as a Prince of the First Rank was restored.","After receiving the decree, Xiao Rongche entered the palace to bid farewell to the Emperor and Concubine Jin. The Emperor kept him behind alone in the Imperial Study.","\"On this trip to the southwest, aside from making the Yang Clan cease hostilities, I command you to secretly investigate the matter of the Binzhou salt fields.\"","\"What is the yield? Where are they located? How are their defenses? You must find out every single detail.\"","Xiao Rongche widened his eyes in astonishment, yet he did not dare to object and say he was incapable.","The salt fields were in Binzhou and had already been occupied by the Yang Clan. If the other side found out he was scouting the salt fields during the mediation, wouldn't he be courting his own doom?","\"Your subject obeys the decree.\"","Forget it, he would just placate his imperial father for now. At worst, when he returned, he would just say he went and make up some random information to brush it off.","When Song Qiming, who was working in the Hanlin Academy, learned of the decree's contents, he had nowhere to vent his frustration and could only return home to complain.","\"I know the Emperor restored Xiao Rongche's princely title at this time to give him more weight when he goes to the southwest, but I just feel awful. It's suffocating.\"","\"He hasn't achieved any merit at all, and after only a year, the crime of assassination is just wiped away like that?\"","Seeing Song Qiming standing in the room making himself angry, Song Jinzhao, who was playing Gomoku with their younger brother, spoke with a calm expression.","\"I heard that the envoy coming from the Shuobei Kingdom is a prince. When the time comes for the Emperor to have an imperial prince receive him, Xiao Rongyan's princely title might also be restored.\"","Song Qiming opened his mouth, looking blankly at Song Jinzhao who was calmly playing chess.","It was actually quite possible.","Gong Linjue held a princely title, so the person in charge of receiving him could not be of a lower status. An imperial prince was the most likely choice, and it had to be a Prince of the First Rank.","Song Qiming stood frozen in place like a statue for a long time. His expression was crestfallen, and he felt extremely defeated inside.","Looking at her silent brother, Song Jinzhao captured one of the white pieces on the board.","\"Remember what I told you before. Stay calm and just wait.\"","Sitting opposite Song Jinzhao, Song Anhao glanced at the white pieces in his hand and opened his mouth to complain in distress.","\"Eldest sister, you've captured all my white pieces. I only have four left, I can't win~\"","The corners of Song Jinzhao's rosy lips lifted slightly, and she tapped the chess bowl dotingly.","\"You can redeem them with black pieces.\"","Song Anhao looked at the few remaining black pieces in the bowl, feeling that it was meaningless if he couldn't win.","He leaned back, a wave of exhaustion washing over him.","\"So sleepy, I'm going to take a quick nap.\"","Song Jinzhao put down the black piece, shaking her head with a smile. \"Get up, finish the game. We'll be eating soon.\"","Song Anhao rolled over, not wanting to get up, and thought of having someone else play for him.","He immediately scrambled up and shouted to Song Qiming, \"Brother, can you continue playing for me?\"","How could the inwardly frustrated Song Qiming be in the mood to play chess? He strode off, heading to the martial arts arena to practice boxing and vent his anger.","\"You've played until you're a lone king, how am I supposed to continue? Play it yourself.\"","Left with no choice, Song Anhao had to use the black pieces to redeem the white ones.","He looked at the twelve white pieces in his hand, then at the overflowing pieces in Song Jinzhao's bowl, and dejectedly continued on his path to defeat.","After learning that Xiao Rongche had his princely title restored, Xiao Rongyan's heart was filled with mixed feelings.","Did he lose or gain in this calculation?","The next morning, while the sky was still dark, Xiao Rongche headed to the southwest under the escort of the General of Xuanwei and an army of ten thousand.","When he left, his expression was calm; it was impossible to tell if he was happy or unhappy.","The summer heat was so intense it baked the ground dry. The most booming business was undoubtedly the tea shop opened by Song Jinzhao. With two thousand cups sold daily and low costs, she was making a fortune.","Half a month after the autumn harvest, a rainstorm washed away the last traces of summer heat.","The hearts of the civil and military officials, as well as the Emperor, also chilled. The envoy of the Shuobei Kingdom had entered the capital.","At the Yingcheng Commandery Prince's Manor, it was the same decree-reading eunuch.","\"By the grace of Heaven, the Emperor decrees: The Prince of Wei from the Shuobei Kingdom, Gong Linjue, has come to court to offer congratulations and celebrate Our birthday. Given the importance of diplomatic relations, the courtesy shown must be equivalent.\"","\"The Second Prince, Xiao Rongyan, is benevolent, filial, and diligent in his duties. By special decree, he is hereby restored and promoted to the Prince of Ying, to receive the envoy of the Shuobei Kingdom. Respect this!\"","Kneeling on the ground, a smug smile appeared on Xiao Rongyan's lips.","\"Your subject receives the decree and thanks Imperial Father for his immense grace!\"","Three days later, both sides of Vermilion Bird Street were crowded with onlookers. Everyone craned their necks, eager to see who was in the Shuobei Kingdom's diplomatic mission and what they looked like.","A woman carrying a basket chattered to her neighbors, \"The Shuobei Kingdom has never sent an envoy to celebrate our Emperor's birthday before. It seems their newly enthroned emperor is friendly. There definitely won't be any more wars in the future.\"","The neighbor nodded in agreement. \"Who says otherwise? It's the first time in hundreds of years. I heard the Third Prince who ascended the throne is a good-for-nothing, the most useless of all the Shuobei princes. If the Second Prince hadn't died from a severe illness, he would never have had the chance to be emperor.\"","A dark-faced man squeezed beside them said, \"Thank goodness the Second Prince died, or we'd still be fighting.\"","Amidst the anxious waiting of the crowd, the silhouettes of the Shuobei diplomatic mission appeared not far outside the city.","As the distance closed, the appearance of the man riding on a tall, majestic horse became increasingly clear.","The Minister of Rites, Kang Zhibo, wearing a scarlet official robe, stood outside the city gates to welcome them. Behind him were two rows of subordinate officials in dark green robes.","They stood tall with their chests out and eyes firm, wanting to overpower the Shuobei mission with their imposing manner.","Upon clearly seeing Gong Linjue's appearance and build, Kang Zhibo's pupils contracted, and he subconsciously swallowed hard.","His nose, eyes, and mouth all looked normal, but why did they give people the creeps when put together?","Especially those eyes.","Dark and deep, the pupils looked as if they had been dyed in blood, a reddish hue piercing through the black, making one feel uneasy.","\"I am here by the decree of His Majesty the Emperor of Dongzhao to welcome the esteemed envoy. Your Highness has traveled far across mountains and rivers, enduring a wearying journey. You have worked hard.\"","Gong Linjue's gaze fell on Kang Zhibo's face, the slender corners of his eyes curling upward.","\"I have come by imperial command to offer birthday congratulations to your Emperor. Along the way, I have seen the beautiful mountains and rivers of Dongzhao, its vast lands and abundant resources, and its bustling markets. It is truly breathtaking, and I must admit I am somewhat envious.\"","Kang Zhibo grew wary in his heart but maintained a fake smile as he calmly reached out to guide them.","\"Everything has been prepared at the Huitong Guesthouse. Please follow me into the city, esteemed envoy.\"","Praising it so highly, could it be that they want to seize it for themselves again?","\"They're coming, they're coming.\"","The commoners on both sides of the street craned their necks to look toward the city gate entrance.","When they finally got a clear look at the Prince of Wei, many stared blankly and gasped in shock.","\"How is this Prince of Wei from the Shuobei Kingdom so incredibly tall?\"","Riding on his horse, the top of his head almost reached the eaves of the second-story shops on either side of the street.","His robust long legs from the waist down resting in the stirrups suggested that if he stood up, he would easily be over six feet tall.","They had thought the envoy would have a friendly appearance, but upon seeing Gong Linjue's face, many were struck dumb, unable to open their mouths.","Not only was he not kind-looking, but he gave off the aura of a murderous demon, making it impossible for anyone to like him."]},{"number":313,"title":"Chapter 313: Gong Linjue Proposes a Spar with Chu Liuyun","paragraphs":["By the window on the second floor of the hot pot restaurant, Song Jinzhao and the Duke of Qing, Chu Liuyun, stood side by side. Both of their gazes were fixed on the Shuobei State diplomatic mission that was about to pass by downstairs.","Looking at Gong Linjue, Song Jinzhao could tell at first glance that he had killed many people. He gave off the distinct vibe of a ruthless, bloodsucking fiend.","How much does Your Grace know about Gong Linjue?","Chu Liuyun shook his head and replied, I have never seen this person before. Gong Linjue is the youngest son of Gong Huan, the Great General of Shuobei State. He was previously unknown and obscure to the world. He suddenly emerged after He Mingyuan ascended the throne; we have never crossed paths before.","Song Jinzhao raised an eyebrow, finding Shuobei State rather interesting.","Before He Mingyuan ascended the throne, people also called him a good-for-nothing, yet he ended up becoming the emperor.","Gong Linjue was a nobody, yet he was made a prince in such a short period of time. It is truly strange in every aspect.","Chu Liuyun furrowed his brows in deep thought. Put that way, it indeed seemed amiss.","Everyone said He Mingyuan was a good-for-nothing, but in the three years since his ascension, no rumors or gossip had ever leaked from the Shuobei royal court.","Gong Linjue had no military achievements. When He Mingyuan bestowed upon him the title of a prince of a different surname, did no one in the court object?","He could not possibly have been made a prince simply because his martial arts were formidable and no one could defeat him. That defied common sense.","An overpowering, savory aroma drifted into his nose, and Gong Linjue turned his head toward the direction the scent came from.","What caught his eye was a massive red-lacquered signboard, clearly displaying the words Dingfeiju Hot Pot.","What kind of food were they selling? The aroma was so intense.","Shifting his gaze upward, he saw a familiar face.","The hand holding the reins tightened, bringing the warhorse beneath him to a halt.","One face was calm and composed, while the other wore a wicked, charming smirk around the eyes and lips.","Their eyes met, a clash of softness and steel that felt intensely oppressive.","Seeing Gong Linjue stop in his tracks, Kang Zhibo and the others looked up at the second floor in confusion, following his line of sight.","Upon realizing it was the Duke of Qing and County Princess Linghui, they could not help but grow tense.","When military commanders from opposing sides met, they often found each other displeasing to the eye, making it easy for conflicts and disputes to erupt.","They had not even entered the Huitong Guesthouse yet; nothing could be allowed to go wrong now.","Chu Liuyun's straight spine did not bend in the slightest due to the other party's status as a prince. He merely gave Gong Linjue a calm nod.","Prince Wei.","Standing to the side, Song Jinzhao silently offered a slight curtsy.","Gong Linjue cast a brief glance at Song Jinzhao before focusing all his attention on Chu Liuyun's face, as if the two had met before.","During the Battle of Ironclad City, the Duke of Qing burned the granaries and withstood the hundreds of thousands of troops from my Shuobei State. Even while in Yandu, this prince had heard of such a heroic feat. Seeing you today, your presence is indeed extraordinary. You truly live up to the title of Dongzhao State's number one young talent.","Chu Liuyun did not lower his guard because of the other party's flattery. He calmly replied,","Prince Wei was made a prince at such a young age. Your martial arts are formidable, and you are known as the number one expert of Shuobei State. Compared to you, Prince Wei, I fall far short.","Watching Gong Linjue and Chu Liuyun flatter each other, the officials standing below broke out in a cold sweat.","They could not shake the feeling that murderous intent was hidden between their words.","Prince Wei, this evening His Highness Prince Ying will host a banquet at the Huitong Guesthouse to welcome the delegation. The journey has been long and exhausting; it would be best to quickly enter the guesthouse and rest for a while.","Gong Linjue lightly swept his gaze over Kang Zhibo, who had just spoken, completely disregarding him.","He continued speaking to Chu Liuyun, You are mistaken. My princely title relies entirely on the favor of His Majesty the Emperor. How could it possibly compare to the solid military achievements of the Duke of Qing.","After I have an audience with your noble country's emperor, I must definitely spar with you to see who the true young talent is.","Song Jinzhao's gaze darted back and forth between the two men.","Gong Linjue looked a few years older than Chu Liuyun. Calling himself a young talent seemed a bit of a stretch; it sounded like he was shamelessly pretending to be younger than he was.","It would be my honor to spar with Prince Wei. Let us arrange a date another time.","Chu Liuyun did not refuse. He also wanted to test Gong Linjue's true depths to see if the man was really as formidable as the rumors claimed."]},{"number":314,"title":"Chapter 314: Being a Princess in a Weak Nation is a High-Risk Profession","paragraphs":["Seeing Chu Liuyun agree to Gong Linjue's sparring request so quickly, Kang Zhibo was so anxious his heart nearly leaped out of his chest.","He could have at least delayed for a few days. What if he couldn't win?","Watching the diplomatic mission gradually depart, Song Jinzhao spoke up, \"This Prince of Wei comes with ill intentions. Sparring is just an excuse; his true goal is to test our strength. He is preparing for a future war between our two nations.\"","Chu Liuyun stared at the tall figure walking away.","\"I know. Since he came all this way, he wouldn't let me avoid it. That being the case, I might as well accept.\"","\"He wants to test my strength, but I also want to test his.\"","Song Jinzhao withdrew her gaze, lowering her eyes in deep thought.","\"There is something I wonder if I should say.\"","Chu Liuyun turned to look at her, a questioning look in his eyes.","\"Please speak freely, County Princess.\"","Song Jinzhao said, \"Back in Anyang Prefecture, Prince Ying's secondary consort, Li Qinyun, mentioned that Princess Yongjia harbors feelings for you, My Lord Duke.\"","\"Since arriving in the capital, based on my observations, it seems that you and Princess Yongjia share a mutual affection. I presume I haven't misread the situation?\"","\"Uh...\"","Chu Liuyun was momentarily stunned, then let out a short, breathy sound, as if the words were caught in his throat.","He hastily averted his gaze, the tips of his ears growing hot and flushing red. Even his speech became flustered.","\"Why would you ask about this, County Princess?\"","Seeing his face turn red with shyness, Song Jinzhao couldn't help but laugh out loud.","\"It seems my guess was correct. You also have feelings for the Princess.\"","The bashfulness on Chu Liuyun's face faded slightly, replaced by a serious expression.","He lowered his head and murmured to himself, \"I have loved the Princess for many years.\"","Song Jinzhao asked, \"In that case, why don't you petition the Emperor for a marriage decree? Given the prestige of the Duke of Zhenguo's estate, the Emperor surely wouldn't refuse.\"","Chu Liuyun replied, \"I originally intended to ask the Emperor for a marriage decree, but my grandmother passed away, so I had to postpone it for a year.\"","\"Now, Her Majesty the Empress is already selecting a Prince Consort for the Princess. I am on the list of candidates, which is essentially just a formality. The marriage edict will be issued before long.\"","Song Jinzhao understood perfectly.","For the selection of the Prince Consort to be delayed until now, Princess Yongjia must have stalled for a considerable amount of time, all to wait for Chu Liuyun's mourning period to end.","\"Since the affection is mutual, you should marry as quickly as possible. It would be best for you to urge the Emperor.\"","Chu Liuyun couldn't understand why Song Jinzhao was so concerned about his marriage. At her age, she shouldn't have a hobby of playing matchmaker.","\"What do you mean by this, County Princess? The Princess holds a noble status. The process of selecting her Prince Consort must be careful and solemn. How could we rush it and wrong the Princess?\"","Song Jinzhao sighed softly, staring at Chu Liuyun, feeling a bit speechless.","How could his mind be so inflexible? They were already in love, yet he still wasn't hurrying to marry her and bring her home.","Being a princess of a weak nation was a highly dangerous profession.","\"You saw Gong Linjue's attitude. We are bound to have another war with the Shuobei Kingdom. If we lose, ceding territory, paying reparations, or even a political marriage will be inevitable. And in the palace, Princess Yongjia is the only one of marriageable age.\"","\"Just in case, it's better for you two to marry quickly, lest you end up separated by the ends of the earth, regretting it for the rest of your lives.\"","The expression on Chu Liuyun's face completely changed.","\"The Emperor dotes on Princess Yongjia deeply. He probably wouldn't send her away for a political marriage.\"","Song Jinzhao retorted, \"No matter how much he dotes on her, can it outweigh the Dragon Throne?\"","\"When that time comes, the civil and military officials could drown someone with just their spit. If trading one princess can buy peace for the realm, how do you think the Emperor will choose?\"","Chu Liuyun fell into a heavy silence.","Seeing that he had taken her words to heart, Song Jinzhao didn't linger any longer. She turned and walked away."]},{"number":315,"title":"Chapter 315: Preventing Surveillance","paragraphs":["In an alleyway next to Vermilion Bird Street, Lan Xi, wearing a bamboo hat, cast his gaze through the crowded street, landing squarely on Gong Linjue.","His hands, hanging by his sides, were clenched tightly into fists, and his eyes held not only hatred but also fear.","Memories buried deep in his mind were dug up once again. Struggling, he closed his eyes and leaned against the wall, panting heavily.","The diplomatic mission's convoy stopped at the entrance of the Huitong Guesthouse. Gong Linjue dismounted his horse, looked at the dozens of guards standing at the door, gave a cold sneer, and turned to Kang Zhibo.","\"Minister Kang, why are there so many guards outside the Huitong Guesthouse?\"","Kang Zhibo's lips twitched slightly before he curled them into a formal smile. \"They were all sent here to protect and serve Your Highness.\"","\"There is still half a month until His Majesty's birthday. If Your Highness wishes to tour the capital or purchase anything, please feel free to order them around.\"","Gong Linjue's long, narrow eyes stared at Kang Zhibo with a meaningful smile.","\"I see. I had thought these guards were sent by your Emperor to monitor me.\"","Kang Zhibo hastily shook his head in denial.","\"How could that be? His Majesty highly values the diplomatic relations between our two countries, and Your Highness has come to celebrate his birthday. We cannot welcome you enough; how could we possibly spy on you? Your Highness is overthinking this.\"","Gong Linjue forcefully flicked his sleeves, clasped his hands behind his back, and strode into the guesthouse.","\"The guards I brought with me are all exhausted from the long, dusty journey. Since these men were sent to serve me, I'll leave the unloading of the luggage on the carriages to them.\"","Hearing Gong Linjue's words, the members of the Shuobei diplomatic mission, who had been preparing to move the chests, stopped what they were doing.","Seeing Prince Wei's figure disappear behind the doors, the men exchanged glances.","In the blink of an eye, they all jostled each other as they rushed into the guesthouse.","Watching the mission vanish in a rush, Kang Zhibo and the other officials from the Ministry of Rites stood frozen in place.","They just left like that?","\"My Lord, what should we do now?\" Peng Mu, the Vice Director of the Ministry of Rites, asked, at a loss.","These guards were specifically drafted from the Imperial Army by Commander Fan on His Majesty's orders. Are they really going to be treated like lowly servants?","Kang Zhibo pressed his lips into a thin line. After a moment of thought, he blinked in compromise.","\"What else can we do? Have them move the luggage.\"","The words had already been spoken, and there was absolutely no taking them back. Otherwise, wouldn't they become a laughingstock to the Shuobei mission?","The arrangements inside the guesthouse had yet to be introduced to Gong Linjue, and there were still matters to discuss regarding the evening banquet.","After ordering the men to move the luggage, Kang Zhibo quickened his pace to catch up.","By the time he caught sight of Gong Linjue, the man was already seated in the seat of honor in the front hall.","Acting as if he were the master of the place, he slouched casually against the back of the chair.","His dirty boot rested on the seat cushion, and one arm was draped lazily over his knee, looking just as if he were listening to a tune at a tavern.","Kang Zhibo's brow twitched. He hesitated to speak but ultimately chose to endure it.","\"Prince Wei, this is Manager Cao Mo of the Huitong Guesthouse. If the mission needs anything while staying here, you can seek him out.\"","Seeing that Gong Linjue didn't even spare them a glance, Kang Zhibo felt slighted, but he gritted his teeth and swallowed his pride.","Those who accomplish great things do not sweat the small stuff. The visitors were guests, and he couldn't leave them any room for gossip; bearing with it would let it pass.","Seeing this, the deputy envoy seated below Gong Linjue spoke up, \"Minister Kang, you may return first. If anything comes up, we will find Manager Cao ourselves. After traveling for so many days, His Highness is tired, and we need to rest.\"","Kang Zhibo feigned a calm smile. \"In that case, I will let Manager Cao attend to you all.\"","\"At the hour of You, Prince Ying will host a welcoming banquet for the mission in the dining hall, complete with fine wine, delicacies, and singing and dancing for entertainment. We eagerly await your arrival.\""]},{"number":316,"title":"Chapter 316: Inquiring About Song Jinzhao","paragraphs":["After Kang Zhibo left with the officials from the Ministry of Rites, the deputy envoy looked toward Cao Mo.","\"Secretary Cao, where is our Prince's room?\"","For hundreds of years, the Dongzhao Kingdom and the Shuobei Kingdom had clashed in battle so many times that one could not count them all on their fingers and toes.","Gong Linjue looked as though he might murder someone at any given moment. Hosting the Shuobei diplomatic mission for the first time, Cao Mo naturally felt a bit apprehensive.","He extended an arm to lead the way. \"This way, Your Highness. The room arranged for you is the largest and most magnificent in the State Guest House.\"","\"Cotton roses are planted right outside the window. They are currently in full bloom, offering a delightful view the moment you open the window.\"","His words hung in the air for a long time without a response; there was not even a flicker of a reaction in their eyes.","Cao Mo licked his lips, feeling a trace of awkwardness, unsure if he should continue speaking.","Stepping into the courtyard, the cotton roses were in full bloom, with clusters of pink flowers hanging heavily on the branches, filling the air with a faint, elegant fragrance.","Pushing open the door and taking a brief look around, Gong Linjue said to Cao Mo, \"I wish to rest. You may take your leave, Lord Cao. I will attend the evening banquet on my own later.\"","Cao Mo bowed his head and cupped his hands. \"I shall take my leave.\"","As the door closed, Gong Linjue ordered his deputy envoy, \"Go and find out who the woman standing with Chu Liuyun today is, and what their relationship is.\"","The deputy envoy's eyes suddenly sharpened. He nodded in compliance.","\"I will investigate at once.\"","An hour later, the deputy envoy knocked on the door.","\"To answer Your Highness, that woman is named Song Jinzhao. Three years ago, Helan Xiao, the commandant of the military office, and the spies we planted in Xining City were all defeated by her hands.\"","\"Song Jinzhao is now the Princess of Linghui, personally titled by the Emperor of Dongzhao. I heard she has exquisite medical skills and is known as a divine doctor in the capital. She is the one who brought the Duke of Zhenguo back from the brink of death.\"","\"As for her relationship with Chu Liuyun, it is merely that of a life-saving grace; there is nothing else between them.\"","Gong Linjue stood up and walked to the window. The pink cotton roses suddenly looked like an eyesore to him.","\"So it is her. To become a titled princess so quickly, this Song Jinzhao is indeed capable.\"","The deputy envoy lowered his voice, \"I heard Song Jinzhao was granted the title because she presented a type of crop called the potato at the Emperor of Dongzhao's fiftieth birthday banquet.\"","Gong Linjue turned around and asked, \"What is so special about this potato?\"","The deputy envoy replied, \"The commoners in the capital say this potato yields an extremely high harvest, capable of producing thousands of pounds per acre. Furthermore, it has very low soil requirements and can survive anywhere it is planted.\"","Gong Linjue's expression changed abruptly, revealing a trace of surprise.","\"Is this true?\"","The deputy envoy nodded. \"Absolutely true. All the commoners in the capital are talking about it.\"","Gong Linjue's thoughts temporarily shifted from Chu Liuyun to the potatoes.","\"If such a divine crop exists, why have I never heard of it in the Shuobei Kingdom? I haven't seen it in any restaurants or inns along our journey either.\"","The deputy envoy explained, \"The number of potatoes Song Jinzhao presented was not large, and the seeds were not enough to distribute to the commoners of Dongzhao for planting, so it hasn't become widespread yet.\"","Gong Linjue pressed on, \"Then where can this thing be found now?\"","How could such a divine object be enjoyed solely by Dongzhao? He had to bring it back.","\"They are all at the Court of Agricultural Affairs. Judging by the time, the quantity should already be quite abundant. I heard that by next spring, the people of Dongzhao will be able to purchase potato seeds with money.\"","Gong Linjue chuckled softly. Clasping his hands behind his back, he murmured, \"This trip has truly not been in vain.\"","After leaving the State Guest House, Minister of Rites Kang Zhibo headed straight for Prince Ying's manor, reporting Gong Linjue's every word and action to Xiao Rongyan.","\"Your Highness, Gong Linjue is by no means a kind soul. You must be careful at the evening banquet tonight.\"","Xiao Rongyan waved his hand dismissively.","\"No matter how formidable he is, he is currently on our Dongzhao soil. Imperial Father has stationed so many Imperial Guards at the State Guest House; why would I fear his mere two dozen men?\"","A surge of helplessness welled up in Kang Zhibo's heart as he said, \"That is not what I meant. As an envoy, Gong Linjue certainly wouldn't clash with Your Highness at this time.\"","\"It is just that this man is deeply scheming and covets Dongzhao. Your Highness must keep your lips sealed in his presence.\"","\"Especially regarding the matter in the southwest. If he asks about it, you must downplay it.\"","Hearing this, Xiao Rongyan lifted his eyelids and cast a cold glance at Kang Zhibo.","\"I do not need you to teach me how to do things, Minister Kang. Since my return to the capital, you have rarely stepped through the doors of my Prince Ying's manor.\"","\"What, now that Imperial Father has other princes, you no longer take me seriously?\"","Kang Zhibo hurriedly knelt down, feeling a bit panicked inside.","\"I am truly wronged. Your Highness must have also seen the Emperor's intentions. It is not that I do not wish to associate more with Your Highness, but I truly dare not offend the imperial majesty. The Minister of War is a prime example.\"","\"Although I have outwardly reduced my interactions with Your Highness, my heart is still with you. In the future, if Your Highness ever needs me, I will certainly not hesitate to die ten thousand deaths for you.\"","Xiao Rongyan waved his hand with a cold attitude.","\"I certainly hope that is what Lord Kang is thinking.\"","After leaving Prince Ying's manor and getting into his sedan chair, Kang Zhibo sighed. He was not only physically exhausted but mentally drained as well.","Anyone with a discerning eye could see that Prince Qi and Prince Ying no longer enjoyed the Emperor's favor as they once did.","With so many princes in the palace, who would ascend the throne in the future had become a total mystery.","He naturally could no longer openly side with Prince Ying, but he did not want to offend him either.","Kang Zhibo leaned his head back against the sedan carriage and closed his eyes to rest.","As things stood, he could only maneuver and stall, hoping that Prince Ying would not need him in the future, so he would be spared the trouble."]},{"number":317,"title":"Chapter 317: Song Jinzhao Begins to Suspect Lanxi's Identity","paragraphs":["Song Shixue, who was practicing archery in the martial arts field, saw Lanxi returning from outside with a bamboo hat in his hand. She looked up at the sky in confusion.","\"Lanxi, it's cloudy today. Why are you carrying a bamboo hat?\"","\"Ah!\"","Lost in his own thoughts, Lanxi was startled by Song Shixue's sudden voice. He trembled all over, dropping the hat to the ground. When he looked up, the fright in his eyes had not yet faded.","Song Shixue paused slightly, a hint of bewilderment showing on her brows.","\"What's wrong with you? You look like you've done something guilty.\"","Recovering his senses, Lanxi subconsciously lowered his eyelids. His pale blue eyes darted around helplessly as his mind frantically searched for an excuse.","He spoke extremely fast: \"The perfume shop's business has been so good lately that we are almost out of stock. I was wondering if we should buy another estate, and I was so engrossed in my thoughts that I didn't see you, Second Miss.\"","\"I was worried it might rain today, so I brought the hat when I went out. Who knew it wouldn't rain.\"","Seeing him so guilty, Song Shixue narrowed her eyes suspiciously.","Usually, he would refer to himself as \"this servant\" or \"this lowly one\" in front of her. Even when she told him he didn't need to, he never changed. But just now, he used \"I.\"","This showed he was so flustered that his thoughts were in chaos, completely forgetting the rules.","There was definitely something going on.","\"So that's how it is. Be careful when you walk from now on. It's easy to trip when you're too lost in thought.\"","Song Shixue chose not to expose Lanxi's lie.","Since he didn't want to tell her, asking would be useless, and he might just tell another lie.","\"This lowly one will take his leave.\" Lanxi held his breath and bypassed Song Shixue, his figure quickly disappearing around the corner.","Song Shixue raised the bow in her hand and stood sideways, her knuckles turning slightly white from the force.","After aiming, she released her fingers. The sharp feathered arrow shot out like a streak of silver light and hit the bullseye dead center.","How dare he lie to me. When I catch him, he's going to pay for it!","Not long after Song Jinzhao returned from outside, Lanxi walked up to the study and knocked on the door.","\"County Princess, this lowly one has something to report.\"","\"Come in.\"","Standing in front of Song Jinzhao, he was even more nervous than when he had faced Song Shixue earlier.","\"County Princess, more than half of the first batch of perfumes and essential oils produced this year have been sold. As we enter October, the temperature will drop, and greenhouses need to be built in the flower fields immediately. This lowly one plans to stay at the Daohua Estate for the next period of time to keep an eye on things, and return once the work is done.\"","Recalling the impressive account books of the perfume shop, Song Jinzhao nodded in agreement.","\"It's indeed inconvenient to run back and forth frequently when the weather gets cold. There aren't many things to do in the manor, so you can stay at the estate.\"","Lanxi let out a sigh of relief, lowered his head, and said, \"Thank you, County Princess. This lowly one will take his leave.\"","Song Jinzhao watched him walk out of the room and turn to close the door.","He seemed to speak with extra caution today. Did he really need to thank her for staying at the estate to work?","He was acting a bit too humble.","Just as Song Jinzhao was about to lower her head and continue reading, the study door was pushed open from the outside again.","\"Sister, I saw Lanxi here just now. What did he say to you?\"","After closing the door, Song Shixue walked over, pulled out the chair opposite Song Jinzhao, and sat down.","Song Jinzhao placed a bookmark between the pages of her book, crossed her arms over her chest, and looked at her.","\"He didn't say much. The weather is getting cold, and warm greenhouses need to be built in the flower fields. It will be very busy, so Lanxi will stay at the estate for a while. Why are you suddenly asking about this?\"","Song Shixue rested her hands on the table.","\"When he came back from outside this afternoon, he was holding a bamboo hat, saying he brought it specifically because he was worried it might rain.\"","\"But there was still some sun this morning, and the sky only started to turn cloudy at noon. He went out in the morning; how could he have been worried about rain back then?\"","\"The most important thing is that he was completely out of sorts when he returned. I called out to him normally, but he was so startled that he dropped what was in his hands.\"","\"I asked him what was wrong, and when he lied to brush me off, his face was full of guilt. It's obvious he's hiding something from me.\"","Recalling Lanxi's cautious attitude just now, Song Jinzhao grew suspicious.","\"What do you think it is?\"","Song Shixue shook her head and explained, \"I came to you precisely because I don't know. His attitude was very strange today, as if he was afraid of something. I just feel like it's nothing good.\"","Recalling his blinded eye, broken arm and leg bones, and the injuries all over his body when they bought him.","Could it be that he ran into the people who tried to kill him back then? He already knew martial arts now, yet he still felt the need to hide at the estate. How powerful must the other party be?","Lanxi's unusually pale blue pupils appeared in Song Jinzhao's mind. A flash of inspiration hit her, and she suddenly remembered that the diplomatic mission from the Shuobei Kingdom was entering the capital today. Could there be a connection between the two?","If the person who wanted to kill him was in the diplomatic mission, and Lanxi happened to see them on the street, that would explain why he was terrified out of his wits.","Because of the other party's status, he wouldn't even dare to fight back, rushing to hide at the estate so they wouldn't find him. It all made perfect sense.","If that was really the case, who exactly was Lanxi?","\"Sister?\" Seeing Song Jinzhao lost in thought, Song Shixue waved a hand in front of her eyes.","With her line of sight blocked, Song Jinzhao looked up at Song Shixue, temporarily suppressing the speculations in her mind.","\"Everyone has secrets. Maybe he didn't go to the shop today and slacked off to play outside instead.\"","If Lanxi really had a grudge against someone in the Shuobei diplomatic mission, he definitely should go hide at this critical juncture.","\"Impossible. He has always been very diligent. He wouldn't lie to me about slacking off,\" Song Shixue said with absolute certainty.","Song Jinzhao replied, \"Then go ask him yourself.\"","Speaking of which, she had only bought him in passing back then because he was cheap, literate, and both Shixue and Anhao were captivated by his pale blue eyes.","Over the past few years, he had indeed been capable and obedient, but wasn't Shixue paying a bit too much attention to him?","By the time Song Shixue came out of the study and went to find Lanxi to ask him, she was informed by the servants that he had already packed his things and left for the estate.","The doubts in Song Shixue's heart grew even stronger.","\"In such a rush! It's almost dark and he still had to leave. Is he going to work there at night?\"","The servant shook his head in bewilderment. \"This lowly one doesn't know, but Manager Lanxi has always been diligent.\"","The sky had darkened. Bright lanterns were hung inside the Huitong Guesthouse, the candlelight stretching all the way from the entrance to the banquet hall.","Xiao Rongyan stepped out of his sedan chair at the entrance. He wore a purple robe with a curved collar and wide sleeves embroidered with cloud and dragon motifs, and a far-roaming crown on his head. An exquisite jade pendant with dragon patterns hung from his belt, swaying slightly as he walked and reflecting a gentle, lustrous glow.","Kang Zhibo followed behind him with two officials from the Ministry of Rites. Their mission today was to entertain everyone well, with the exception of Gong Linjue.","Entering the banquet hall, Cao Mo, who had sent people to urge the guests three times already, looked at Prince Ying in a panic.","Seeing that the hall was empty and no one was at the tables yet, Xiao Rongyan frowned in displeasure.","\"Have the people from the diplomatic mission not arrived yet?\"","Cao Mo lowered his head and wiped the sweat from his forehead with his sleeve.","\"This humble official has already sent people to invite them three times. The people from the mission said that Prince Wei is taking a nap and hasn't woken up yet, so they will arrive a bit late.\"","Xiao Rongyan glanced at the pitch-black sky and said with a dissatisfied expression, \"It's already this hour and he still hasn't woken up? A short nap takes four hours?\"","Worried that Xiao Rongyan would lose his temper, Kang Zhibo quickly shot a meaningful glance at Cao Mo.","\"Go invite them one more time, and say that His Highness Prince Ying has arrived.\"","Wiping his sweat, Cao Mo bowed repeatedly and nodded. \"This humble official will go right away.\"","\"Am I late?\"","Gong Linjue walked over with his deputy envoy and two guards.","His gentle voice was completely different from how he sounded during the day, and he even wore a warm smile, leaving Kang Zhibo utterly baffled.","How could this man change faces so quickly?","Xiao Rongyan was initially startled by Gong Linjue's height; it felt as if his hair crown was about to scrape the top of the corridor.","Since he referred to himself as a prince, he had to be Prince Wei, Gong Linjue.","Since Prince Wei has traveled thousands of miles to celebrate our Emperor's birthday, with such sincerity, how could we ever say you have arrived late?","After everyone took their seats, the dishes were served.","The hostel attendants carried trays, walking up to the tables one by one and kneeling down.","Exquisite dishes were placed on the tables; both the color combinations and the aromas were incredibly enticing.","Orangutan lips and roasted deer tongue—every dish featured expensive ingredients that showcased the nation's wealth and power.","The Huairou Eight Treasure Duck and the Dragon and Phoenix Auspiciousness dish carried political undertones of good fortune and conciliation.","Sitting opposite each other, Xiao Rongyan and Gong Linjue's gazes met in midair; their calm smiles both concealed wariness and probing.","After the attendants withdrew, Xiao Rongyan raised his wine cup in a gesture to Gong Linjue.","Prince Wei, you have endured a long and arduous journey. On my royal father's orders, I am hosting this welcoming banquet for the delegation. I have prepared this modest feast and ask for your forgiveness for the humble setting. I shall toast you first.","Gong Linjue raised his cup and responded with a smile, I have long heard that His Highness Prince Ying possesses a majestic bearing and is the most like the Emperor of Dongzhao among all the princes. Seeing you today, you truly live up to your reputation.","These words left Xiao Rongyan elated.","Prince Wei overpraises me. This wine is the Spring Scenery of Dongting, unique to the Jiangnan region of our Dongzhao. Please, give it a taste.","Gong Linjue drank the wine. This wine is crisp and sweet; it truly resembles the rainy season of your esteemed country's Jiangnan.","Xiao Rongyan's hand paused slightly as he set down his cup, and he asked instinctively, Has Prince Wei been to Jiangnan?","The hypocritical smile in Gong Linjue's eyes suddenly froze, but in the next second, it became gentle again, as if nothing had happened.","I have read about the pavilions and terraces of Jiangnan in books. Not only is the scenery pleasant, but even the rainy season is picturesque and holds a unique charm. I imagine it is just like this Spring Scenery of Dongting.","Saying this, he raised his cup and offered a toast in return to Xiao Rongyan."]},{"number":318,"title":"Chapter 318: A Night Banquet at the Hall of Gathering","paragraphs":["Watching the two men chatting merrily, Kang Zhibo shot a meaningful glance at Cao Mo.","The sound of string and bamboo instruments began to play. Dancers wearing lotus fairy skirts slowly emerged from behind the screens, their light steps accentuating their graceful, swaying figures.","However, Gong Linjue's gaze only lingered on the dancers for a brief moment before he resumed his polite conversation with Xiao Rongyan.","As they talked, the two drank more and more.","After a whole pot of wine was emptied, the attendant in charge of pouring wine for Gong Linjue and Xiao Rongyan noticed the empty pot and hurriedly signaled the others to bring up another.","On the other side, the deputy envoy was also drinking with Kang Zhibo and the others. Accompanied by the sounds of music and dancing, it made one involuntarily become intoxicated by the atmosphere.","Seeing a hint of drunkenness tinge Xiao Rongyan's brows and his eyes lose their initial clarity, the gentle expression on Gong Linjue's face gradually faded.","I have heard that the southwestern region of the Dongzhao Kingdom has been restless lately. With the approaching birthday banquet, your Emperor even sent the Prince of Qi out of the capital to quell the rebellion. I wonder how the situation is now, and if he will be able to make it back in time for the birthday?","Hearing the words southwest and Prince of Qi, Xiao Rongyan's distracted mind instantly snapped halfway back to attention.","It is nothing major. Just two hereditary noble families fighting over some trivial matters. Halfway through the fight, they wanted a way out to save face, but having no other choice, they appealed to the imperial court. My royal brother just went there to mediate. It is just that the southwest is a bit far. With the round trip, he probably will not make it back in time for my imperial father's birthday banquet.","Gong Linjue raised his wine cup and gestured towards Xiao Rongyan.","I see. These are indeed trivial matters. In my Shuobei Kingdom, several nomadic tribes also frequently clash over cattle and sheep. With my temper, I just take my men over and beat them up, and they quickly settle down.","Speaking of which, when I entered the city, I ran into the Duke of Qing. With his abilities, dealing with a few local nobles would be a breeze.","Xiao Rongyan took a small sip. It is just like two children in the family fighting; a few words of mediation are enough. There is no need to involve the Duke of Qing.","Gong Linjue lowered his head and swept his gaze over the dishes on the table, casually picking up a piece of fish with his chopsticks and putting it in his mouth.","He said in a seemingly careless tone, I have heard that your noble country discovered a type of crop called potatoes that yields a thousand catties per mu. It can be eaten as a vegetable dish or as a staple food. Why is it not at today's banquet?","Cough, cough, cough! Kang Zhibo, who was sitting lower down, choked on his wine and coughed repeatedly.","He spoke sharply to the attendant waiting nearby, Hurry and pour me some tea. Drinking too much wine has burned my throat.","Xiao Rongyan, holding his wine cup, felt a sudden jolt of clarity in his mind. He touched his flushed, warm cheeks and finally realized that Gong Linjue had been continuously toasting him in an attempt to get him drunk.","Xiao Rongyan picked up his teacup and took a sip, using the bitterness to wash away the taste of wine in his mouth.","Saying it yields a thousand catties per mu is actually an exaggeration. The quantity of potatoes presented by County Princess Linghui was not much to begin with. The imperial court is still cultivating them, and even the palace has not gotten to eat them yet, so how could they appear at this banquet?","To be honest with you, Prince Wei, I only tasted it once a few years ago. Although the yield is a bit higher than rice, the taste is far inferior. It tastes like sand, and if kept for too long, it becomes toxic. It cannot be stored for long periods.","Gong Linjue's narrow eyes swept over Kang Zhibo, who was sitting opposite him and frantically drinking tea, finding the man to be an extreme eyesore.","After that, every time Gong Linjue toasted Xiao Rongyan, he would only pretend to take a tiny sip.","It had to be said that the people of the Shuobei Kingdom had an excellent tolerance for alcohol. After downing two pots of wine, Gong Linjue's expression remained unchanged, as if he were just drinking water.","Stepping out of the banquet hall, the cold wind blowing against his face completely sobered Xiao Rongyan up.","He whispered an order to Kang Zhibo, Tell the servants in the Huitong Guesthouse to be sharp. I want to know every word and action of the diplomatic mission, especially Gong Linjue's.","Kang Zhibo nodded solemnly. Glancing at the subordinates trailing behind him, who were so drunk they could not even stand steady, he felt a wave of frustration at their incompetence.","I understand. Please rest assured, Your Highness.","Upon returning to his room, Gong Linjue's face turned completely cold, the disguised gentleness in his eyes vanishing without a trace.","The imperial estates of the Court of National Agricultural must be near the capital. Send men out to find them.","The deputy envoy said hesitantly, Your Highness, when the Dongzhao Kingdom sells potato seeds to the commoners next spring, we will be able to get them easily. Why go through the trouble of searching everywhere now?","We are currently in the capital. If we are discovered, it will be dangerous.","Gong Linjue replied, The popularization of a new crop often takes several years. The Dongzhao Kingdom is already two years ahead of us. The sooner we get it, the sooner we can narrow the gap. If they do not sell the potatoes to the commoners next year, we will not be left helpless.","As for the danger you mentioned, even if we are discovered, they would not dare do anything to me. Given the current national strength of the Dongzhao Kingdom, they would not dare start a war.","The deputy envoy thought about it and agreed. Only when something was in their own hands was it absolutely secure. If they waited, what if something went wrong?","Rest assured, Your Highness. I will see to it immediately.","In the imperial palace, Xiao Chengjing was already preparing for bed.","Just at that moment, a eunuch came in from outside to report.","Your Majesty, Prince Ying is outside requesting an audience. He says he has an urgent matter to discuss with Your Majesty.","Eunuch Zhao paused his hands, which had been unfastening the Emperor's collar buttons.","What is he doing here at this hour?","Remembering that Xiao Rongyan was hosting a banquet for the Shuobei Kingdom's diplomatic mission at the Huitong Guesthouse tonight, Xiao Chengjing reached out and re-fastened the unbuttoned collar.","Let him in.","As soon as he entered the room, Xiao Chengjing smelled alcohol and immediately scolded, How could you drink so much wine while hosting foreign envoys?","Xiao Rongyan wrinkled his nose. He had let the wind blow on him all the way here; was the smell of alcohol still that strong?","Imperial Father, it was not that I wanted to drink. Gong Linjue harbored ill intentions and tried to get me drunk to fish for information. Fortunately, I was clever enough to avoid falling into his trap.","Xiao Chengjing sat down on the soft couch in the outer room.","What information was he trying to fish for?","Xiao Rongyan answered animatedly, gesturing with his hands and feet, He asked me about the unrest in the southwest, and also questioned why there were no potatoes at the banquet. His covetous intentions are glaringly obvious.","Xiao Chengjing's expression remained calm, as if he had expected this all along.","And how did you answer him?","Xiao Rongyan repeated what he had told Gong Linjue.","I believe he absolutely will not give up easily. He will definitely send men to search all over the capital. We must take precautions early, especially regarding the imperial estates.","Xiao Chengjing said, I anticipated this day would come. Before the diplomatic mission even entered the capital, I had already arranged for men to patrol around the imperial estates day and night. The granaries are also heavily guarded; no one can get in.","Xiao Rongyan looked at Xiao Chengjing with eyes full of admiration.","Imperial Father truly has great foresight. I am in awe.","After the morning court session the next day, the Emperor held his first meeting with the Shuobei Kingdom's diplomatic mission in the Hall of Preserving Harmony.","I am highly pleased that your Emperor sent Prince Wei personally to congratulate me on my birthday.","Trekking over mountains and wading through rivers must have been exhausting. There is still half a month until my birthday. During this time, I will have Prince Ying accompany your mission to tour the capital and experience the local customs and practices of my Dongzhao Kingdom.","Gong Linjue cupped his hands in a salute to Xiao Chengjing, but his spine did not bend in the slightest.","It is my honor to be accompanied by a prince. Thank you, Your Majesty, Emperor of Dongzhao.","At the same time, the events that transpired at the Huitong Guesthouse the previous night began to spread among the high-ranking officials in the court.","For a time, everyone secretly began to worry that their precious treasures would be stolen by the people of Shuobei.","After all, the commoners of their own Dongzhao Kingdom had not even gotten to eat them yet!"]},{"number":319,"title":"Chapter 319: Utilizing Potatoes to Construct a Defensive Tuntian System","paragraphs":["After the Emperor finished meeting with the diplomatic mission from the Shuobei Kingdom, an impatient Dongfang Shaoting and the others immediately requested an audience with His Majesty.","\"My beloved subjects, there is no need to worry. I have already strengthened the defenses around the imperial estates and granaries, strictly forbidding anyone from entering or leaving. Even if Gong Linjue knows where the potatoes are kept, they won't be able to take them.\"","Gu Qishan, his face full of solemnity, said, \"To reply to Your Majesty, according to the imperial court's original measures, the common people would be able to plant potatoes by next spring. No matter how strictly the court guards them, it cannot guard against everyone in the world. In this humble subject's view, such a high-yielding divine crop should be firmly controlled in the hands of the court, and there is no need to let the common people plant it.\"","The Minister of Revenue looked at Gu Qishan with an astonished expression. \"If we don't let the common people plant them, we still have to let them eat them. The result will be the same.\"","Gu Qishan: \"We can process them into potato starch for sale. Not only will this ensure that the seeds are not obtained by others, but it will also increase the court's revenue.\"","Dongfang Shaoting stepped forward and said, \"The Prime Minister's method is too fanciful. The court does not have that much land, nor that many people, and cannot plant that many potatoes.\"","Fei Yanzhang: \"Today, the common people all over the world know that the court possesses a divine crop that yields a thousand catties per mu, and they are all waiting for the court's seeds. If we do not allow them to plant it, the people's hearts will become unstable, inevitably breeding resentment among the populace, which could even shake the foundation of the state. This is truly the worst possible plan.\"","The Imperial Study descended into a chaotic argument, and the Emperor felt as if his ears were going to explode from the noise.","But after all was said and done, not a single practical and feasible solution was devised.","That evening, Song Qiming returned home and told Song Jinzhao about the matter.","\"Today, Lord Fei and the others argued in the Imperial Study for the entire day, but they couldn't come up with any useful ideas.\"","\"In the end, someone even suggested trading potatoes with the Shuobei Kingdom for warhorses, and at the time, the Emperor actually hesitated for a moment.\"","Song Jinzhao shook her head and said, \"It is impossible to achieve a long-term, comprehensive blockade on food crops. As long as it is planted on a large scale, it will definitely be obtained by people from other countries. It's nothing more than a matter of time, unless we burn it all and no one plants it.\"","\"The comprehensive popularization of a crop takes a very long time. What the court should do now is to quickly seize the advantage.\"","\"The Court of Agricultural Affairs has already been planting potatoes for two years and possesses a very stable potato seed production base. But now, the land of the imperial estates can no longer accommodate that many potatoes, and there is not enough manpower. Thus, we must acquire more land and labor.\"","\"The court's original plan was to sell potatoes to the common people at the beginning of next spring, letting them plant them to solve their food and clothing problems. But in reality, the potato seeds the Court of Agricultural Affairs can sell can only cover the capital; there won't be enough to reach other places.\"","\"The treasury of the Dongzhao Kingdom is empty, and we face internal strife and external threats. If a war breaks out, we would even have to scrape together rations. The very first thing that should be solved is the problem of the army having no food to eat, lest the country perish before the common people can even prosper.\"","Song Qiming stared intently at Song Jinzhao, his lips slightly parted. \"What does Ah Jie mean?\"","Song Jinzhao walked over to the wall and used her finger to draw a few circles on the map.","\"First, let the armies at the border passes and strategic strongholds establish military agricultural colonies to plant them, achieving self-sufficiency in army rations and alleviating logistical pressure. This guarantees that when others attack, the army will have food to eat, and it won't require long-term transportation.\"","\"Once the seeds are sufficiently abundant, they can then be distributed or sold through local government offices. At the same time, the court can issue laws prohibiting the mutual trade of potatoes with the Shuobei Kingdom, and set up checkpoints to search those heading to the Shuobei Kingdom.\"","\"Although it's impossible to completely prevent it, it can delay the speed of the potato's popularization in the Shuobei Kingdom. By the time they achieve universal popularization, the population and national strength of the Dongzhao Kingdom will have already seen great improvements. When we dispatch troops to conquer them then, our chances of winning will be very high.\"","Song Qiming stood up and walked over to the map.","\"But the border passes and strategic strongholds are all very close to the Shuobei Kingdom. If we plant potatoes there, wouldn't it be very easy for them to be snatched away?\"","Song Jinzhao: \"Planting at the borders cannot be simple planting; rather, we must construct a defensive military agricultural colony system that integrates military, agriculture, and engineering.\"","\"First, concentrate the planting within the army's defensive perimeter instead of spreading it out. If conditions permit, planting can even be done inside the city walls. If the army of the Shuobei Kingdom wants to snatch the potatoes, they must dispatch troops to fight, which will exact a heavy price. Before plundering, they will have to weigh whether it is worth it.\"","\"Second, potatoes are buried underground and are difficult to dig up in large quantities in a short amount of time. While they are digging, we can turn around and attack them.\"","\"Third, the soldiers will not tolerate foreign enemies snatching away the potatoes they worked so hard to plant, so their fighting will to defend their fields will become stronger.\"","\"Previously, the food for the border armies had to be transported from other places, and after a war, more than half of the men had to return. But with fields and the ability to be self-sufficient, they can station at the borders long-term, forming a permanent, stable stronghold capable of long-term garrisoning.\"","\"By that time, a defensive military agricultural colony system integrating military, agriculture, and engineering will be complete. We can also rely on these strongholds to slowly expand our territory outward; it won't be easy even if the enemy wants to attack.\"","Song Qiming remained silent in front of the map for a long time.","After figuring it out, he turned to look at Song Jinzhao, his expression shocked as he said, \"Ah Jie, how did you think of all this?\"","\"I could rack my brains and still never think of these things.\"","Song Jinzhao walked over to the table and poured herself some tea to drink. \"Read more books and you'll be able to think of it.\"","\"Read more military strategy books in the future; just knowing literary classics is not enough.\"","\"It's getting late and I need to sleep. You can write these contents into a memorial and submit it to the court for them to handle.\"","Song Qiming nodded vigorously. He stayed up all night to write the memorial, even revising it twice.","Having not slept all night, he went to Ye Liangyu's house before dawn and blocked him there.","After reading the contents of the memorial, Ye Liangyu looked at Song Qiming in a daze. \"Are all these thought up by County Princess Linghui?\"","Song Qiming nodded vigorously, the admiration for Song Jinzhao in his eyes still undiminished after an entire night.","\"Yes, Ah Jie said it's impossible to completely blockade food crops from being obtained by others. The only superior strategy is to utilize the head start to seize the advantage.\"","Ye Liangyu lowered his head and read the contents of the memorial from beginning to end once more.","\"I knew County Princess Linghui was smart, but I didn't expect her to also possess the talent to govern the world.\"","\"Skilled in both pen and sword. If she could enter the court as an official, her achievements would surely surpass yours and mine; even being enfeoffed as a marquis and appointed as prime minister wouldn't be impossible.\"","\"When you go to the Hanlin Academy, give this memorial to Lord Fei. He will take you to see the Emperor.\"","It was exactly as Ye Liangyu had anticipated.","After the morning court assembly ended, Song Qiming handed the memorial to Fei Yanzhang. After reading it, he didn't say anything and directly took Song Qiming to the Imperial Study.","After being brought into the Imperial Study, Fei Yanzhang bowed and offered the memorial with both hands.","\"Your Majesty, this is the memorial that Compiler Song just showed to this subject. This subject was greatly shocked and benefited immensely from it. I beseech Your Majesty to take a look.\"","Xiao Chengjing glanced at Song Qiming standing next to Fei Yanzhang, then signaled Eunuch Zhao to bring the memorial to him.","Fifteen minutes later, Xiao Chengjing put down the memorial with slightly trembling fingers and looked up at Song Qiming.","\"Compiler Song, did you write this memorial?\"","Song Qiming raised his head, looked into the Emperor's eyes, and said, \"To reply to Your Majesty, the memorial was written by this subject, but the contents within were spoken by my Ah Jie.\"","Like a sudden clap of thunder, Xiao Chengjing's voice spiked as he blurted out in sheer disbelief, \"County Princess Linghui?\"","Song Qiming's eyes burned with fervor as he nodded emphatically and spoke with solemn earnestness.","\"Last night, while I was racking my brain in my study at home, trying to figure out how to keep the potatoes out of the hands of the Shuobei Kingdom, Ah Jie brought in some ginseng soup. She saw what I had written on the paper and told me that once potatoes became widely cultivated, it would be impossible to keep them contained. That is how the words in this memorial came to be.\"","Xiao Chengjing slammed his hand onto the table, stood up, and let out a hearty laugh.","\"She is truly worthy of the title County Princess Linghui that I personally bestowed upon her! Such insight and strategic thinking are remarkably brilliant. This is exactly what it means for a woman to be no less capable than any man.\"","Song Qiming bowed with cupped hands. \"Thank you for your high praise, Your Majesty. Relieving the court's urgent crisis is precisely what Ah Jie wished to do.\"","Xiao Chengjing sat back down, sighing with deep gratification. \"If all the people in the world possessed County Princess Linghui's loyalty, patriotism, and devotion to the state, I would finally be able to rest easy.\""]},{"number":320,"title":"Chapter 320: Struck by Lightning","paragraphs":["Prince Ying's Manor.","\"What! Gong Linjue expects this prince to accompany him for a stroll through the streets?\" Xiao Rongyan frowned in disbelief.","\"Imperial Father was merely exchanging pleasantries, yet he actually took it seriously!\"","A servant hesitated before asking in a low voice, \"Then, will you still go?\"","Xiao Rongyan took a deep breath, gritted his teeth, and said fiercely, \"I will. Since he is a guest, this prince will entertain him.\"","By the time he arrived at the Huitong Guesthouse, Gong Linjue was already in the front hall, drinking tea as he waited.","Seeing Xiao Rongyan walk in, he stood up and said with a smile, \"After resting for two days, this prince has recovered his spirits. Today, I wish to purchase some specialty items of the Dongzhao Kingdom in the capital to take back with me. I will have to trouble Your Highness to give me a proper introduction.\"","Are you blind or mute? Can't you look and ask around yourself?","Xiao Rongyan nodded with a fake smile. \"The markets of our Dongzhao Kingdom are bustling and filled with a dazzling array of goods. I suppose Prince Wei will have quite a lot to explore.\"","A glint of coldness flashed in Gong Linjue's eyes.","If it weren't for you sending people to tail this prince, I wouldn't have resorted to such a poor plan. The people of Dongzhao Kingdom are truly an eyesore.","They had already discovered the location of the imperial estate. This time, when they headed out of the city to scout the area, they could not afford to be followed.","As they walked to the door and prepared to board the carriage, Gong Linjue turned back to look at the soldiers standing under the eaves and said:","\"Have them all follow along, lest there be no one to carry the things we buy.\"","The soldiers standing guard under the eaves were stunned.","They were not servants of the Shuobei Kingdom. How could they be ordered around by the other party time and time again?","For a moment, all the imperial guards disguised as ordinary soldiers shifted their gazes toward Xiao Rongyan.","Here, Prince Ying held the most noble status, so they had to listen to him.","Seeing that they did not obey his orders, Gong Linjue looked at Xiao Rongyan meaningfully.","\"The servants sent by your esteemed Emperor to serve this prince are not obedient in the slightest. Such servants would have died eight hundred times over in our Shuobei Kingdom.\"","Xiao Rongyan's face stiffened, too lazy to argue with this domineering foreign prince.","\"Imperial Father governs the world with benevolence and filial piety. He does not casually call for beatings and killings. Naturally, we are not like the Shuobei Kingdom, which advocates violence.\"","Saying that, he turned his head and deliberately raised his voice toward the soldiers, his tone rising and falling in an utterly strange manner.","\"The delegation has come from afar, so you must serve them well. Especially regarding the safety of Prince Wei, you must protect him without leaving his side. Everyone, follow along.\"","The soldiers cupped their hands and responded in unison, \"We will strictly follow the orders of His Highness Prince Ying.\"","After speaking, they raised their heads and cast a glance at Gong Linjue.","We listen to the orders of our own prince, not yours.","Just as everyone stepped away, the deputy envoy, dressed in the attire of a servant, quietly slipped out through the back door.","Inside the County Princess's Manor, Song Jinzhao had just sent off the eunuch who delivered the rewards.","Looking at the silks, satins, hairpins, and jewelry in the servants' hands, she waved her hand and instructed, \"Register everything and place them into the storehouse.\"","It was always these same things every time. The Emperor was becoming increasingly stingy.","\"Sister, I will head to the estate now.\" Song Shixue walked up to Song Jinzhao carrying a medicine box.","Song Jinzhao said, \"Come back early. Take the carriage; it might rain in the afternoon.\"","Song Shixue nodded obediently and voiced her agreement.","In the small woods outside the imperial estate, the delegation's deputy envoy, who had climbed up a tree, gazed ahead with a solemn expression.","He hadn't expected the Dongzhao Kingdom to be on guard so early. Not only had they built wooden platforms around the imperial estate to keep a constant watch, but there were also numerous soldiers patrolling the grounds. The only way to get in and steal the potatoes would be to fight their way through.","Dark clouds loomed overhead, and the sky gradually darkened.","Even though it wasn't even noon yet, it looked as though evening had already fallen.","A sudden, earth-shattering clap of thunder roared in the sky not far away, sending a terrified shiver down the deputy envoy's spine.","This thunder was far too loud. It was about to rain, and he needed to head back quickly.","He looked down below him, grabbed onto the branches, and slowly climbed down.","Seeing that the height was about right, he pushed off with his legs and jumped.","A blinding white light suddenly flashed around him. The piercing flash struck right on the deputy envoy's head, immediately followed by the roar of thunder.","The man who fell to the ground had his hair standing straight up, with faint sparks of fire flickering at the ends.","His body felt as if it had taken a heavy punch, and his limbs twitched, trembling continuously.","\"Second Miss, it looks like someone got struck by lightning!\"","The maid driving the carriage looked in horror at the man who was slowly approaching her step by step.","\"Ah?\"","Song Shixue curiously lifted the carriage curtain, only to see a monster whose hair was half standing on end and half burnt to a crisp, with a face as black as coal.","\"Old sir, are you alright?\" As a physician, Song Shixue subconsciously asked out of concern.","The deputy envoy reached up, wiped a hand across his face, and looked at her with dull, wooden eyes.","\"I'm not old. I'm only forty.\"","Looking at the man whose facial features were now slightly visible, Song Shixue reined in her expression, a flicker of vigilance passing through her eyes.","He was someone from the Shuobei Kingdom delegation. The day they entered the city, he had been following right behind that prince.","Why would he appear here all alone?","And to be struck by lightning, no less.","Changing her tone, Song Shixue feigned a relaxed manner and said, \"It seems you're fine. Heye, let's go. It's about to rain.\"","The maid nodded, grabbed the reins, and continued driving.","Seeing them leave, the deputy envoy continued his slow, sluggish walk toward the city gates, his lightning-struck brain feeling somewhat dazed.","The sky slowly began to drizzle. Just as Song Shixue arrived at the estate, the rain started pouring heavily, as if the heavens were dumping out bathwater.","Lan Xi walked over, bowed, and said, \"The roads are difficult to travel in the rain. Second Miss should wait for the rain to lighten up before heading to the Qu family's place.\"","Song Shixue untied her rain-dampened cloak and handed it to Hehua.","She then turned to ask Lan Xi, \"Has the estate been very busy lately?\"","Lan Xi nodded. \"We need to set up greenhouses for the flower fields. It determines whether the perfume shop can maintain a continuous supply later on, so it has been a bit busy. Does Second Miss have any tasks to assign to this lowly one?\"","He was calling himself a lowly one again.","Song Shixue replied, \"No, I was just asking casually.\"","He looked perfectly fine. Even if something had been bothering him, it seemed to have passed.","Chen Fu, the manager of the Daohua Estate, came in carrying hot tea.","\"This is the newly made rose tea from this year. Please have a taste, Second Miss.\"","Song Shixue picked up the teacup and took a sip. The faint floral fragrance was refreshing and uplifting, and the added honey made the sweetness just right.","\"It's delicious. Pack some up for me to take back so my sister can try it. Perhaps we could sell it in our tea shops.\"","\"Yes.\" Chen Fu nodded and quickly hurried out to prepare it.","Remembering the envoy who had been struck by lightning, Song Shixue turned to Lan Xi and said, \"Tell the people on the estate not to run around outside on rainy days. It's easy to get struck by lightning.\"","\"Especially tell them not to stand under large trees to seek shelter from the rain, nor to hold sharp objects above their heads. Sister mentioned before that doing so makes it even easier to get struck.\"","Hearing this, Lan Xi looked up and down at Song Shixue with a nervous expression.","\"Why bring this up so suddenly? Was Second Miss struck by lightning?\"","Song Shixue set down her teacup and spread her arms. \"Do I look like I've been struck by lightning?\"","Lan Xi closed his mouth. Indeed, she did not.","\"On the way to the estate, Hehua and I saw a man who had been struck by lightning. He was even a member of the Shuobei Kingdom delegation.\"","\"His hair was blown out and half burnt off, and his face was as black as if it had been smeared with pot ash. He looked quite badly injured.\"","As if an alarm had been triggered, Lan Xi instantly raised his head, the skin all over his body pulling taut.","\"Someone from the Shuobei Kingdom delegation?\"","Song Shixue nodded and said, \"Yes, and it seems he holds a rather significant official position.\""]},{"number":321,"title":"Chapter 321: Still Hiding It, Seeking Medical Treatment for Qu Ya's Son","paragraphs":["\"Was there only one person?\"","\"Where did you run into him?\"","\"How old is he? Is he exceptionally tall?\"","Lanxi's face was pale, and the questions tumbled out of his mouth one after another.","His trembling hands and anxious expression all revealed that something was unusual, but he couldn't care less at this moment.","He desperately wanted an answer.","Had he been discovered?","Had Gong Linjue already found his way here?","If his identity was exposed and it implicated the Song family, what would he do?","Should he flee or fight to the death? They shouldn't have seen him that day.","Seeing his flustered state, Song Shixue was absolutely certain that Lanxi was hiding something.","His face had changed at the mention of the Shuobei diplomatic mission. Could it be related to them?","\"There was only one person;\"","\"I ran into him not long after leaving the city, about three or four miles out;\"","\"He said he was in his forties, not very tall, about the same as Fushun.\"","\"When entering the city, he was following behind the Prince of Shuobei.\"","Lanxi's tense nerves relaxed slightly, but his mind was a mess as he lowered his head in thought.","It wasn't Gong Linjue, but that deputy envoy?","Why would he appear alone outside the city? Was it for him or for something else?","\"Lanxi, are you hiding something from me?\" Song Shixue asked calmly.","Lanxi looked blankly at Song Shixue, his hands hanging by his sides as if drained of all strength and rendered numb.","He forced a stiff twitch of his lips.","\"No, how could this servant dare hide anything from the Second Miss? I was just a little surprised to hear that someone was struck by lightning.\"","Stared at by Song Shixue's calm eyes, Lanxi guiltily averted his gaze to the door after saying this.","\"The rain seems to have let up a bit. The Qu family's child is still waiting. How about the Second Miss heads over now?\"","Song Shixue lowered her eyelids in disappointment, stood up, and said, \"In that case, let's go now.\"","The pattering light rain was blown about wildly by the wind.","The maid walked on the right, holding most of the umbrella over Song Shixue's head.","On the left, Lanxi held an umbrella at an angle to prevent the rain from blowing onto Song Shixue.","The Qu family's house was built of bamboo and thatch. Because of leaks, two wooden buckets were placed on the floor to catch the water.","Seeing Song Shixue enter, the woman watching over the child by the bed hurried over to greet her.","\"For the Second Miss to make this trip in such heavy rain, this common woman is shedding tears of gratitude.\"","Lanxi looked around the room and saw no one else besides the child on the bed.","\"Where is your husband?\"","Woman: \"It's a bit cold with the rain, and we haven't bought charcoal for the house this year, so he went to borrow some.\"","Song Shixue walked to the bed.","The boy lying on the bed looked about eleven or twelve years old. His pale lips were dry and peeling, and his eyes were closed as if he was asleep.","Song Shixue reached out and felt his forehead, cheeks, and neck a few times.","He was so cold he was breaking out in a cold sweat; even his neck was chilly.","She took a tongue depressor out of her open medical box, then pinched the boy's chin to pry his mouth open a crack and inserted the tongue depressor, pressing down firmly.","Seeing this, the woman hurriedly said, \"Half a month ago he started coughing and said his throat hurt. He was spitting phlegm all the time, and speaking felt like being cut with a knife. A few days later, he started running a fever.\"","\"Manager Chen found a doctor to come take a look. He took the medicine and the fever went down, but his throat still hurt. Later on, he didn't even dare to speak.\"","Song Shixue nodded and removed the tongue depressor.","\"His throat is severely inflamed and is already bleeding. We need to prescribe medicine to stop the cough immediately.\"","\"Cough, cough, cough.\" The boy suddenly opened his eyes and began to cough violently.","Liquid surged in his throat. He tried to lean over the edge of the bed to throw up, but he didn't make it in time.","Song Shixue stood up to dodge, but she was a step too late.","Vomit containing yellow phlegm and white rice sprayed onto her cloak, and a sour smell spread through the room.","Qu Ya came through the door and saw his son had thrown up all over Song Shixue. He hurriedly put down the charcoal and walked over quickly.","\"My son is gravely ill and has soiled the Second Miss's clothes. Please forgive us, Second Miss. We can pay whatever silver is needed for compensation.\"","The woman looked with difficulty at the cloak on Song Shixue, which obviously did not come cheap.","How much silver would it cost to pay for it?","Song Shixue untied her cloak and handed it to her maid. \"It's fine. It just needs a wash when we get back. No need to compensate.\"","She walked over to a table with a crippled leg, which was propped up with a stone underneath.","She had known before coming that the patient had caught a chill, so she had brought a complete set of medicinal herbs.","After dividing and wrapping the herbs, she first handed Qu Ya three paper packets.","\"This is the medicine for the first three days. Take one dose daily, divided into morning, noon, and night. It must be taken after meals. Pay attention to a bland diet with less oil and salt so as not to irritate the throat.\"","After Song Shixue finished speaking, she handed the other four packets to Qu Ya.","\"Three days later, when the cough stops, the yellow phlegm turns white, and the throat pain is greatly relieved, he can then take this prescription. This is a four-day supply. Once he finishes it all, he should be just about cured.\"","\"If he hasn't recovered, have Manager Lan send someone to let me know.\"","Clutching the medicine packets, Qu Ya bowed to Song Shixue in thanks. \"Thank you so much, Second Miss. How much silver is the consultation fee plus the herbs in total?\"","Song Shixue closed her medical box. \"You are people employed by my Song family. My elder sister said that the medical expenses for internal staff and their families are all reduced by thirty percent. Calculating it, the total comes to four hundred and sixty-three copper coins.\"","With the Song family's current status, Song Shixue didn't need to go out and treat people to make money, but she needed practical experience to improve her medical skills and expertise. Therefore, as long as someone came to her, she generally wouldn't refuse if she had the time.","Qu Ya looked at his wife, who was rubbing the boy's back with her hand. Seeing this, she hurriedly took out the silver and handed it to Song Shixue's maid.","Fortunately, working on the estate nowadays provided wages, otherwise over four hundred copper coins might not have been so easy for them to scrape together.","After leaving the Qu family and returning to the estate, Chen Fu had already prepared the rose tea.","Song Shixue glanced at Lanxi and instructed Hehua, \"Take the floral tea, we are returning to the manor.\"","Lanxi looked up at her with an astonished expression.","\"Lunch is almost ready. Won't the Second Miss eat before leaving?\"","Seeing him acting as if nothing had happened, anger surged in Song Shixue's heart.","\"No need, I'll go back to eat.\"","Seeing Song Shixue walking out, Hehua hurriedly picked up the floral tea and followed.","Watching the carriage gradually move away, Lanxi stood there for a long time with a dim expression.","After returning to the manor, Song Shixue immediately ran into Song Jinzhao's courtyard calling for her elder sister.","Song Anhao's personal guard, Yao Ying, worried that she would wake up her master, hurriedly lowered her voice and said, \"The County Princess is at the martial arts training ground.\"","Song Shixue quickly turned and headed for the martial arts training ground; Hehua, holding the umbrella, almost couldn't keep up.","Light rain drifted in the air, the moisture turning into a misty drizzle, and visibility was somewhat low.","Inside the martial arts training ground, Song Jinzhao was holding an enhanced crossbow, standing under the eaves and shooting arrows at the target in the courtyard.","Qingshuang, standing to the side, was quickly throwing copper coins into the air, and the sound of the arrowheads scraping against the copper coins rang out incessantly.","The bullseye was completely filled with short arrows piercing through copper coins, even more densely packed than the quills on a hedgehog."]},{"number":322,"title":"Chapter 322: Confirm that the person Lanxi is afraid of is Gong Linjue","paragraphs":["\"Sister, when I went to the manor for a medical consultation today, I ran into the envoys from the Shuobei Kingdom on the road.\"","\"I told Lanxi about it, and his reaction was strange. It was as if he knew those envoys.\"","Song Jinzhao put down the crossbow and turned to walk into the room.","\"Today, Prince Ying took Gong Linjue shopping all over the city. Which envoy did you meet?\"","If the master was staying in the city, why would a subordinate run out of the city?","Song Shixue sat down and said, \"It was the man who followed behind Prince Wei that day. He is a head shorter than him and looks to be in his forties.\"","Song Jinzhao recalled the scene of them entering the city that day. \"It should be the deputy envoy of the diplomatic mission. Was he alone, or were there several people?\"","Song Shixue: \"He was alone, and he was struck by lightning.\"","Song Jinzhao raised her eyebrows in surprise. \"Is he still alive?\"","Song Shixue nodded. \"Alive, but his hair was completely scorched.\"","Thinking of the Shuobei Kingdom's covetousness toward potatoes a few days ago, Song Jinzhao pondered for a long while before asking, \"Where did you meet him? Was it near the imperial manor?\"","Song Shixue: \"It was only three or four miles away from the capital at the time, not yet at the imperial manor. I just don't know how long he had been walking.\"","Song Jinzhao absentmindedly tasted the hot tea in her hands. After thinking for a moment, she looked up and instructed Qingshuang, \"Go to the Zhenguo Duke's estate and inform the Duke of Qing that the deputy envoy left the city alone today.\"","\"This servant will go immediately.\" Qingshuang placed the box containing the short arrows and crossbow on the shelf, turned, and walked out of the room.","Song Shixue continued, \"Sister, when I mentioned the Shuobei diplomatic mission, Lanxi pressed me on whether the person was exceptionally tall. I suspect the person he was thinking of is Gong Linjue, and he is very afraid of him.\"","Song Jinzhao looked up at Hehua. \"Go out and close the door. There is no need to leave anyone outside.\"","\"Yes.\" Without another word, Hehua went out, closed the door, and even took away the two servants responsible for cleaning.","After making sure there was no one around, Song Jinzhao spoke, \"Do you still remember the injuries on Lanxi's body when we first met him?\"","Song Shixue answered softly, \"I remember. He was severely injured at the time, blind in one eye, covered in knife wounds, and had been beaten several times by beggars.\"","Song Jinzhao: \"The color of Lanxi's pupils is either a genetic mutation like a snowball, or the blood of a foreigner flows in his body. I suspect he escaped from the Shuobei Kingdom, and the person who wants to kill him is probably Gong Linjue.\"","Originally, Song Jinzhao's object of suspicion was someone in the diplomatic mission. Since Lanxi cared so much about whether the person was tall or not, the possibility of it being Gong Linjue became very high.","Song Shixue recalled Lanxi's reaction from a few days ago and his reaction today.","\"So that's why he was so nervous and afraid. But why would a prince of the Shuobei Kingdom want to hunt him down?\"","\"When we bought Lanxi, he was only fourteen. Who could he have offended?\"","Song Jinzhao: \"That is something we have to ask Lanxi himself.\"","Song Shixue bit her lip tightly, thinking of the two times he had hidden things from her. \"If he refuses to tell me, it must be something major.\"","Seeing her worry, Song Jinzhao formed a guess in her heart.","\"Before the diplomatic mission leaves the capital, let Lanxi stay at the manor and not come back, lest he be discovered. I will ask him after they leave.\"","Song Shixue nodded, her face showing concern.","If the person who wanted to kill him really was Gong Linjue, then he definitely could not be discovered and had to stay hidden.","After shopping in the city all day, no one returned to the Huitong Guesthouse empty-handed.","Xiao Rongyan, who had been walking all day, had sore and aching feet. After dropping Gong Linjue off at the guesthouse, he immediately climbed into his carriage to return to his estate.","When he got home and took off his shoes, sure enough, several blisters had formed on his feet.","Inside the Huitong Guesthouse, the mission's guards stood outside the room. Inside, Gong Linjue leaned against the couch, while the hat-wearing deputy envoy stood before him.","\"There are heavy guards stationed near the imperial manor, making it impossible to approach. It seems the Emperor of Dongzhao had taken precautions early on.\"","Gong Linjue's gaze was dark as he said, \"Since the Court of Agricultural Affairs manages the potatoes, we will start with them.\"","\"Men die for wealth just as birds die for food. Find a way to make contact, use silver to bribe someone, and bring some potatoes out.\"","The deputy envoy nodded. \"This subordinate understands.\"","Gong Linjue looked at his curled, short hair on the side. \"What happened to your hair?\"","The deputy envoy smiled bitterly and took off his hat. \"This subordinate was struck by lightning outside the city today. Fortunately, it didn't take my life, but this hair is practically unpresentable now.\"","Gong Linjue looked at the top of his head, which looked worse than if a dog had chewed on it.","\"Since it's this ugly, just shave it all off. Say it was accidentally burned by a candle. Don't let anyone know you went to the imperial manor.\"","The deputy envoy touched his coarse hair with a pained expression.","\"This subordinate understands. I will shave it in a moment.\"","After Qingshuang left the Zhenguo Duke's estate, Chu Liuyun immediately went to Commander Fan's house.","\"Today, Gong Linjue used a trick to transfer all the Imperial Guards away from the Huitong Guesthouse. The deputy envoy took the opportunity to leave the city and go to the imperial manor, presumably for the potatoes. We need to dispatch more personnel outside the guesthouse. It's best not to do it openly this time. Arrange for people to disguise themselves as street vendors and guard the surrounding areas. Don't let them be noticed.\"","Fan Guanshan was startled at first, then confused.","\"If the Imperial Guards didn't notice, how did the Duke know?\"","Chu Liuyun replied, \"Someone saw a man struck by lightning outside the city. They were curious, took a few extra glances, and recognized him.\"","\"Ah! The deputy envoy was struck by lightning!\"","Chu Liuyun nodded. \"I heard he is fine, but his hair is a bit of a mess.\"","The next morning, several unfamiliar faces appeared at the stalls and shops around the Huitong Guesthouse. Their eyes constantly monitored the opposite side, not even sparing the walls.","On the twenty-fifth day of the tenth month in the twenty-eighth year of Yongyuan, the Emperor of the Dongzhao Kingdom celebrated his fifty-second birthday.","The birthday banquet in the Baohe Hall was basically the same as in previous years. The difference was that Prince Ying now sat in the seat originally meant for Prince Qi, and Gong Linjue took Prince Ying's seat, with the deputy envoy sitting just below him.","As the bells and drums sounded, the birthday banquet officially began.","After presenting gifts and taking their seats, palace maids and eunuchs flowed in like water, carrying trays to serve the dishes.","Sitting in his seat, Gong Linjue looked toward Chu Liuyun. Today, he was going to make the Dongzhao Kingdom lose face.","\"Your Highness,\" the deputy envoy stretched his head over and called out softly.","Gong Linjue turned his head to look at him.","The deputy envoy leaned close to his ear and whispered, \"Sitting below the Empress is Dongzhao's Eldest Princess, Xiao Yongjia. She just looked at Chu Liuyun several times, her face flushed with spring affection. It looks a bit unusual.\"","Gong Linjue looked up and happened to see the two of them making eye contact.","One was full of tender affection, and the other responded gently. It seemed they were a couple.","\"No rush. Let me test Chu Liuyun's skills first.\"","The deputy envoy nodded. Their main purpose in coming to Dongzhao to celebrate the birthday this time was to observe the strength of Dongzhao's military generals.","Chu Liuyun, who was able to withstand the Second Prince back then, was their key observation target.","Song Jinzhao, who was separated from Princess Yongjia by two tables, had been secretly observing the situation of the other people in the Baohe Hall the entire time.","Gong Linjue and the others' focus on Chu Liuyun was seen clearly by her.","On the first day they arrived, they said they wanted to spar. It had been over ten days with no movement. Could it be that he wanted to compete with Chu Liuyun at the birthday banquet?!"]},{"number":323,"title":"Chapter 323: Combat Entertainment","paragraphs":["After the dishes were served, the Emperor, sitting high on the dragon throne, raised his wine cup and spoke loudly to the crowd: \"Since I received the Mandate of Heaven and ascended the throne twenty-eight years ago, the world has been at peace, and the people have lived and worked in contentment. All of this relies on the blessings and protection of our ancestors. I offer this first cup of wine to the ancestors of our Dongzhao State.\"","As the first cup of wine was poured onto the fleece-covered floor, Eunuch Zhao raised a tray holding the second cup of wine.","Xiao Chengjing placed his empty cup on the tray and picked up the second cup, facing the civil and military officials seated below.","\"This second cup of wine, I offer to all of you, my beloved subjects. You are the pillars of the Dongzhao State's court. Without you, I could not support this empire alone. I hope you will all share this cup with me.\"","In an instant, the civil and military officials raised their wine cups, stood up, and bowed to the Emperor.","\"We dare not claim such merit. Thank you for your profound grace, Your Majesty!\"","After everyone drank the wine and took their seats, Xiao Chengjing raised the third cup of wine toward Gong Linjue.","\"Peace between our two nations is truly the fortune of all people. The Prince of Wei has traveled a long way to celebrate my birthday. I offer this third cup of wine to you, and to the Emperor of your esteemed nation in Yandu. May the friendship between our two countries remain as cordial as it is today.\"","Gong Linjue stood up with his wine cup and cupped his hands toward Xiao Chengjing in a salute. \"On behalf of the monarch of my country, I thank Your Majesty for your kindness.\"","Friendship was impossible. It was the survival of the fittest, natural selection.","Only the strong deserved the best things, and the weak were meant to be devoured.","Amidst the clinking of cups and the sound of string and bamboo instruments, the palace dancers slowly entered the hall.","A massive temporary circular stage had been set up in the center of the Hall of Preserving Harmony. The crowd enjoyed the music and dance performances while drinking.","After a few songs, Gong Linjue slowly stood up and faced the Emperor seated on the dragon throne.","\"Your Majesty, Emperor of the Dongzhao State, the string and bamboo music and dances are mostly the same. Watching too much of them becomes dull. On my first day in the capital, I made an agreement with the Duke of Qing of your esteemed nation to have a martial arts spar. Why not hold this competition right here at the birthday banquet, as a way to add to your entertainment?\"","The Hall of Preserving Harmony fell into absolute silence. Everyone seemed to have been struck dumb as they all looked at Gong Linjue.","To have a martial arts competition at the Emperor's birthday banquet—if the Duke of Qing won, it would be fine, but if he lost, it would not only be a slap to the Emperor's face but also cause the imperial court to lose all its dignity.","However, if they refused, they would be accused of fearing battle. If word spread, the common people would think the military generals of the Dongzhao State were as cowardly as mice, not even daring to accept a challenge.","Xiao Chengjing, who was sitting on the dragon throne drinking, already had several cracks in his composure.","Why did it have to be at the birthday banquet, with all the civil and military officials present? Should he agree to it or not?","Seeing that Xiao Chengjing did not speak immediately, Gong Linjue directed his aim at Chu Liuyun, who was sitting opposite him.","\"Duke of Qing, regarding our chance encounter on Vermilion Bird Street, does the Duke's promise still hold?\"","Chu Liuyun remained expressionless.","\"A promise is worth a thousand pieces of gold, so naturally it holds. However, fighting at a birthday banquet is somewhat too violent. It would be better to reschedule for another day.\"","Gong Linjue: \"It is precisely because it is at a birthday banquet that it is interesting. A competition between our two nations is meant to add to the fun. Could it be that the Duke is afraid?\"","Saying this, he looked toward the Emperor. \"Or is it that not a single military general in your esteemed nation's court can fight, and you are afraid of losing?\"","As soon as these words came out, the military generals sitting below collectively exploded.","Who said they couldn't fight?","They had to teach this arrogant Prince a lesson.","The Principal Fourth Rank General of Loyal Martial Arts, Shan Congwu, immediately stood out and said, \"I have heard that the Prince of Wei is the number one expert of the Shuobei State. I would also like to spar with you.\"","The Principal Fifth Rank General of Roving Cavalry, Fang Leitian, closely followed.","\"I would also like to compete with the Prince of Wei. Please enlighten me, Your Highness.\"","Seeing the military generals of the court stepping forward one by one to demand a match, Song Jinzhao, who had been kneeling for a long time, simply sat cross-legged on her soft cushion.","A simple taunt had achieved its goal. This competition had to be fought now.","Xiao Rongyan looked at the indignant military generals below, and the anger in his chest inevitably began to rise.","He took a breath and slowly said to Gong Linjue, \"Several of my beloved subjects wish to compete with you. What does the Prince of Wei think?\"","Let these people test Gong Linjue's true strength first, to see if he was really as formidable as the rumors said.","Even if they were no match for him, Chu Liuyun would at least be prepared.","Gong Linjue did not take these people seriously at all. What were fourth or fifth-rank officials to him?","\"Since it is to entertain His Majesty, the Emperor of your esteemed nation, I would be disrespectful to decline.\"","The massive circular stage was cleared to become an arena, and dozens of weapons were carried into the hall one by one by the Imperial Guards.","The General of Roving Cavalry, Fang Leitian, chose a pair of iron hammers weighing forty catties, while Gong Linjue casually picked up a longsword and stepped onto the stage.","As the two stood on the arena at the same time, Fang Leitian was a full head shorter than his opponent.","Fortunately, he was on the heavier side, so it looked like he still had the strength for a fight.","Song Jinzhao was watching with rapt attention when Princess Yongjia, who was sitting above, quietly got up and walked over from behind a pillar.","Hearing the movement, Song Jinzhao turned her head and found that the other party was coming straight for her. A trace of confusion could not help but arise in her heart.","What did she want?","Their eyes met, and Princess Yongjia smiled and nodded at Song Jinzhao.","She walked to Song Jinzhao's side and was just about to sit down, only to find that the other party was sitting cross-legged against the rules, leaving no room at all.","\"County Princess Linghui knows quite a bit about martial arts. Could you explain it to me?\"","Song Jinzhao helplessly got up and moved aside a bit to make some room. \"What does the Princess want to know?\"","Princess Yongjia: \"I want to know if the General of Roving Cavalry can win.\"","If all the military generals lost, Gong Linjue would have to fight her Brother Liuyun, and she was a little worried.","\"Hah!\" A low roar came from the stage.","Turning to look, they saw Fang Leitian, wielding the dual hammers, charging toward Gong Linjue. His ferocious face looked as if he was using every ounce of his strength.","The muscles in his arms bulged. There were no fancy tricks, just pure brute force, swinging with the full power of a landslide or a tsunami.","Gong Linjue's sword remained in its sheath as he dodged to the side, his speed so fast it left afterimages.","Song Jinzhao pursed her lips and shook her head.","\"When one's strength is not great enough, a heavy weapon will slow down their speed. Gong Linjue is no ordinary military general. Fang Leitian is not his match.\"","Princess Yongjia's shoulders slumped in disappointment, and she continued to watch with some uncertainty in her heart.","With a forceful strike of the sword hilt against Fang Leitian's wrist, the twenty-catty iron hammer slipped from his grasp and fell to the ground, smashing a pit into the circular stage.","Immediately after, Gong Linjue spun around and kicked Fang Leitian off the stage.","The hall erupted in an uproar.","How much time had passed? Fang Leitian was defeated in less than twenty moves!","Was Gong Linjue too powerful, or was Fang Leitian too weak?","The civil officials were full of doubt, while the military generals wore solemn expressions, each of them standing in strict formation, ready to take the stage at any moment.","The General of Loyal Martial Arts, Shan Congwu, gripped a long saber and leaped onto the stage, cupping his hands toward Gong Linjue. \"Please enlighten me, Your Highness.\"","Half a cup of tea's time later, a longsword, only half-drawn from its sheath, rested against Shan Congwu's neck.","Song Jinzhao's right hand, resting on her leg, was tightly grasped by Princess Yongjia. The fingernails dyed with balsam flowers dug deeply into her hand.","Feeling the pain, Song Jinzhao exerted a little force to pull her hand out.","There were several crescent moon marks on the back of her hand; any deeper and it would have bled.","\"Princess, you don't need to worry too much. A birthday banquet martial arts competition will not endanger anyone's life. Even if these people cannot defeat Gong Linjue, the Duke of Qing will not be in any mortal danger when he goes up.\""]},{"number":324,"title":"Chapter 324: Five Consecutive Losses, Want to Abandon Chu Liuyun","paragraphs":["Princess Yongjia bit her lip so hard that her rouge was almost smudged.","\"Today is Imperial Father's birthday banquet. If no one in the court can defeat Gong Linjue, Imperial Father will inevitably be furious and blame others, and the imperial court will suffer a massive loss of prestige.\"","Song Jinzhao cast a surprised glance at Princess Yongjia; she certainly knew her father well.","Seeing the defeats of Fang Leitian and Shan Congwu, many military officials began to feel intimidated and shrank back.","Three more men went up after that. Although they managed to exchange more moves than the first two, the result was exactly the same.","In the end, they were all carried off, either limping or clutching their chests.","The Emperor's complexion grew increasingly ugly, to the point where he had almost scraped the gold powder off his dragon throne.","If this continued, every military official in the court would be defeated by Gong Linjue alone.","Sitting in his seat, Chu Liuyun stared at Gong Linjue with a dark and heavy expression.","In terms of individual martial skill alone, this man was even stronger than He Mingnan.","\"Is there anyone else who wishes to spar with this prince?\" Gong Linjue's wicked and charming gaze swept over everyone present.","The smile tugging at the corners of his lips seemed to mock the military officials of the Dongzhao Kingdom as a bunch of weak-kneed, useless trash.","The crowd dared to be angry but dared not speak. No matter how much fire burned in their hearts, they could only suppress it.","Seeing no one answer, Gong Linjue raised his sword and pointed it at Chu Liuyun. \"Duke of Qing, it is your turn.\"","Princess Yongjia gasped, her gaze falling straight onto Chu Liuyun, her eyes full of worry.","\"County Princess Linghui, do you think the Duke of Qing can win?\"","Seeing Gong Linjue sweep away five men in a row, Xiao Yongjia was extremely panicked, worried that Chu Liuyun would not be able to defeat him.","Song Jinzhao shook her head, her brows furrowing slightly.","\"The five men just now failed to push Gong Linjue to his limits. I don't know exactly how high his martial arts are, so I cannot judge.\"","Chu Liuyun also chose a longsword, as it was what he was most skilled at.","The two sides stood facing each other. The civil and military officials, including the members of the imperial family, all held their breath, their hearts in their throats.","If the Duke of Qing lost as well, the Dongzhao Kingdom would lose all its face.","Swords were drawn. The two longswords reflected a piercing light under the glow of the candles.","A sharp sound of slicing through the air broke the tranquility within the Hall of Preserving Harmony.","The figures of the two men on the stage approached each other swiftly like swimming dragons. As their sword blades clashed, the ear-piercing sound of vibrating metal reached everyone's ears.","Many people covered their ears in discomfort, feeling as if their eardrums had suddenly been pierced by chopsticks.","Clang! Clang! Clang!","Short, crisp striking sounds rang out frequently, and the exploding sparks frightened people into covering their eyes.","It could be seen that both men on the stage were masters of the sword, neither losing the upper hand in their exchanges.","Seeing this scene, Xiao Chengjing, who was sitting on the dragon throne, truly breathed a sigh of relief.","It seemed that Chu Liuyun still had the strength to put up a fight against Gong Linjue.","He did not ask for a win; as long as they could draw, he would be satisfied.","A cup of tea's time passed, and the two had exchanged no less than a hundred moves, yet a victor had not been decided.","Both sides' attacks could always be neutralized by the other, making it difficult for either to secure a victory.","When she saw Gong Linjue temporarily avoid Chu Liuyun's vital points for the second time, choosing instead to strike where the opponent could block, Song Jinzhao's hands resting on her lap began to gradually clench.","Was it a coincidence, or was he going easy?","Something was not right.","Not only did Song Jinzhao notice something wrong, but Fan Guanshan, standing beside Xiao Chengjing, also sensed the anomaly.","He leaned in and whispered into the Emperor's ear, \"Gong Linjue is not using his full strength. I am afraid the Duke of Qing is no match for him.\"","A dark glint flashed in Xiao Chengjing's eyes. He raised his gaze to meet Fan Guanshan's, and his heart could not help but start drumming.","On the arena, Chu Liuyun grew increasingly anxious in his heart every time he was about to succeed, only for his opponent to dodge just in time.","Breathing slightly heavily, the movements of his hands began to speed up.","Withstanding a blow, Gong Linjue flew over Chu Liuyun's head and landed behind him.","Seeing that Chu Liuyun's turning speed was no longer as fast as before, a faint, almost imperceptible smile appeared on Gong Linjue's face.","It seemed his martial arts were only slightly stronger than He Mingnan's, far from being his match.","Having tested him for so long, it was time to let this proud son of heaven know his power. He would gladly take the face of the Dongzhao Kingdom.","Upon seeing that smile on Gong Linjue's face, realization dawned on Song Jinzhao.","He was not going easy; he was luring Chu Liuyun.","Worried that his opponent was hiding his true strength, he deliberately fought back and forth, giving Chu Liuyun the illusion that they were evenly matched.","Step by step, he lured him in until all of his true strength was revealed.","A fierce sword glare flashed in front of Chu Liuyun. He quickly raised his sword to block it, the shock numbing his palms.","A cold sneer appeared on the corner of Gong Linjue's mouth as he raised his foot and kicked Chu Liuyun's trembling calf.","Bang! His knee slammed heavily against the stage, emitting a loud thud.","Realizing that the two hundred or so moves just now were Gong Linjue toying with him, Chu Liuyun's bulging eyes filled with the anger of humiliation.","He gripped the sword hilt forcefully with both hands, his blade grinding against his opponent's. An ear-piercing metallic screech rang out, sounding like a knife being sharpened on a stone.","\"You overestimate yourself,\" Gong Linjue spat out coldly, his dark gaze falling on the wrist with which Chu Liuyun held his sword.","His tall figure appeared before Chu Liuyun like a phantom. His sword struck out like a rainbow, cold light flashing.","Fan Guanshan, standing beside the Emperor, widened his eyes in horror, a roar tearing from his throat.","As the word \"Careful\" blurted out, he was already rushing down the steps.","At the same time, Song Jinzhao quickly reached out and flicked a cup full of hot tea from the table, sending it flying.","The white porcelain cup turned into a streak of light, crashing directly into the blade of Gong Linjue's sword just as it was about to slash Chu Liuyun's wrist.","Accompanied by a crack, the sword blade deflected half a foot to the side, striking nothing but air.","The exploding porcelain shards and tea splashed onto Chu Liuyun and Gong Linjue, simultaneously leaving several bloody scratches on both their cheeks.","Rushing over to save him, Fan Guanshan swiftly pulled Chu Liuyun's arm and shielded him behind his back.","He said to Gong Linjue with a vigilant face, \"Prince Wei, since this is for entertainment, why resort to lethal moves? The Duke of Qing concedes.\"","This man was unpredictable and audacious.","As an envoy, he actually dared to try and cripple Chu Liuyun at the Emperor's birthday banquet. In the future, he would definitely become a major threat.","Half the people in the hall had already stood up. If that cup had not blocked it just now, Gong Linjue's sword would have likely severed the Duke of Qing's wrist.","Gong Linjue lowered his eyes to look at the sword in his hand. The blade vibrated violently, unable to stop for a long time.","One could only imagine how immense the force of that strike had been.","\"Commander Fan is mistaken. Since it is a martial arts spar for entertainment, how could this prince deal a lethal blow? I naturally know when to stop and would not have harmed the Duke of Qing.\"","He turned sideways and looked in the direction from which the teacup was shot, his gaze falling straight onto Song Jinzhao.","\"On the contrary, it was County Princess Linghui who smashed a cup over and cut this prince's face. Shouldn't your esteemed country give this prince an explanation?\"","Fan Guanshan narrowed his eyes in displeasure. \"Do you think we are blind? Just now, if we had been a step later, the Duke of Qing's hand would have been crippled.\"","Gong Linjue chuckled lightly, completely disregarding Fan Guanshan.","He looked around and mocked, \"Just because you cannot stop does not mean this prince cannot stop. If you couldn't see that, it only proves that you are too weak.\""]},{"number":325,"title":"Chapter 325: The Gamble, Come and Fight","paragraphs":["Everyone in the Hall of Preserving Harmony felt as though a basin of cold water had been poured over them. Their bodies were freezing, yet a fire burned in their hearts—a frustration they could only suppress, unable to vent.","Fan Guanshan was so furious his teeth itched, wanting nothing more than to jump into the fray himself.","Sitting on her soft cushion, Song Jinzhao rested one hand on the table and slowly stood up.","This man was incredibly arrogant and conceited; if an explanation wasn't given, the blame would eventually fall on her own head.","\"I, the County Princess, consider my martial skills to be no inferior to Prince Wei's. It was precisely because I saw what was happening that I intervened, so no explanation is needed.\"","\"On the contrary, Your Highness, your sword was aimed directly at the hands of the Duke of Qing. Was it because you lacked the ability to control your own blade, or was it intentional? You are the one who should give the Duke of Qing and the Emperor an explanation.\"","The words Fan Guanshan was about to say choked in his throat.","The civil and military officials all turned to look at Song Jinzhao, too shocked to speak.","Even the Duke of Qing had been defeated, yet she was claiming she was no worse than Gong Linjue.","They knew Song Jinzhao knew martial arts, but they hadn't expected her to boast so brazenly on such an occasion.","Gong Linjue sneered, \"Even Chu Liuyun couldn't defeat me. Is County Princess Linghui perhaps more skilled than him?\"","Song Jinzhao's expression remained unchanged. \"Whether I am skilled or not, Your Highness will know once you try. I'm just afraid you don't dare.\"","At this moment, the person put on the spot had shifted from the military generals of the Dongzhao Kingdom to Gong Linjue. If he didn't accept, it meant he was afraid.","Sitting on the dragon throne, Xiao Chengjing swallowed hard in astonishment.","Were these words a woman could even say?","Gong Linjue tightened his grip on his longsword; the numbness from earlier hadn't completely faded.","This Song Jinzhao might actually have some skill, but how could he possibly lose to a woman?","\"Why wouldn't I dare? But what if the County Princess loses?\"","Song Jinzhao curled her lips into a smile. \"I will be at your disposal. But what if Your Highness loses?\"","Gong Linjue replied, \"If I lose, I will apologize to the Duke of Qing on the spot and admit that the final strike just now was a slip of the hand.\"","Song Jinzhao shook her head and smiled, \"This wager is unfair. If Your Highness truly slipped, then my intervention just now was an act of assistance. Not only can Your Highness not blame me, but you should also give me a gift of gratitude.\"","Gong Linjue's face grew cold. \"What do you want?\"","Song Jinzhao raised her chin. \"The Akhal-Teke horse Your Highness rode when you first arrived in the capital is quite nice. I like it very much. If you lose, give it to me.\"","The great hall was dead silent as everyone watched the back-and-forth between Gong Linjue and Song Jinzhao.","A martial arts duel wasn't enough; they even had to place wagers.","County Princess Linghui's courage was as big as the sky. With a single phrase 'at your disposal,' wasn't she afraid that if she lost, Gong Linjue would hack her into pieces?","Was it confidence or sheer stupidity?","Gong Linjue pressed his lips into a thin line; in his heart, he had already sentenced Song Jinzhao to death.","\"I accept.\"","After saying this, he turned to face the Emperor, who sat high upon the dais.","\"Your Majesty, Emperor of Dongzhao, you have heard the words of your noble country's County Princess. If she loses, she is at my disposal. When the time comes, whether I choose to kill her or slice her to pieces, I hope Your Majesty will not interfere.\"","Xiao Chengjing could barely swallow his saliva anymore.","He looked at Song Jinzhao with a hint of nervousness. \"County Princess Linghui, have you thought this through?\"","Song Jinzhao replied decisively, \"To reply to Your Majesty, I intervened because I was confident I saw correctly. Since Prince Wei boasts of his high martial arts skills and claims accidents are impossible, I simply must fight him until he is utterly convinced.\"","Xiao Chengjing took a deep breath and straightened his posture. \"Since that is the case, let the duel begin. I haven't watched to my heart's content yet either.\"","Things had reached a point of no return. At worst, after Song Jinzhao died, he would just compensate the Song family a bit more.","Sitting in his seat, Xiao Rongyan clenched his fists tightly, afraid he might burst out laughing on the spot.","He had never seen anyone rush so eagerly to their death. It would be best if Gong Linjue killed Song Jinzhao; that would truly vent his anger.","Song Jinzhao selected a long spear from the weapon rack.","After stepping onto the stage, she said, \"Your Highness expended some stamina just now. Do you want to rest a bit, lest you claim after losing that my victory was dishonorable?\"","The sword in Gong Linjue's hand gleamed in the light. \"They were all incompetents; how much stamina could they possibly drain from me? The County Princess shouldn't intentionally stall for time.\"","Song Jinzhao raised her eyebrows slightly, pointing her spear directly at Gong Linjue's eyes.","\"In that case, let us fight.\"","A cold wind howled past the hall outside, sending a chill into the room and lifting the long hair draped over Song Jinzhao's shoulders.","Sitting on his cushion, Chu Liuyun was so tense he hardly dared to breathe. If it weren't for saving him, Song Jinzhao wouldn't have gotten into this trouble.","It was he who had underestimated the enemy.","Tapping the ground with her toes, Song Jinzhao gripped the spear and lunged straight at Gong Linjue's face. The heavy spear, weighing over a dozen pounds, was like a bamboo pole in her hands, wielded effortlessly.","Sword and spear clashed. A loud clang echoed like a thunderbolt striking inside the room, startling the surrounding officials so much that they trembled.","Gong Linjue's long, elegant eyebrows furrowed deeply. His legs sank half a foot down, and the webbing between the thumb and forefinger of his right hand instantly split open.","This force was millions of times heavier than the cup flicked at him earlier. How could she have such monstrous strength?","Without giving Gong Linjue a moment to react, Song Jinzhao increased the force in her hands, raising her right leg to strike directly at his lower body.","Gong Linjue quickly bent over to dodge, using the momentum to twirl his longsword against Song Jinzhao's spear.","Her slender wrists rotated with incredible agility, the spearhead blurring into a swift silver shadow.","Before Gong Linjue could even steady himself, the second spear strike chopped down toward his head.","So fast!","Gong Linjue's heart skipped a beat, and he decisively threw himself to the ground to avoid it.","Crack.","As the spearhead and shaft smashed into the ground, the wooden floorboards of the circular stage instantly exploded, sending wood splinters of all sizes flying in every direction.","Song Jinzhao's seat faced the side of the stage. A dumbfounded Princess Yongjia had turned into a statue; it was only because a palace maid timely shielded her with a hand that the wood splinters didn't hit her face.","\"Princess, it's a bit dangerous here. Let's return to your seat.\"","Xiao Yongjia shook her head woodenly, her gaze locked unblinkingly on Song Jinzhao fighting on the stage.","\"No, I can see more clearly from here.\"","Why did it feel like Song Jinzhao had the upper hand!","As the wooden boards of the stage were flipped up one by one by Song Jinzhao, leaving him nowhere to hide, Gong Linjue had no choice but to gather his breath and leap through the air.","However, Song Jinzhao's reaction speed was even faster.","With a slight flick of her wrist, the spear tip swung vertically upward, snagging Gong Linjue's collar before slicing straight forward.","\"Ah!\" All the female guests present hurriedly covered their eyes with their hands, but the image in their minds simply wouldn't fade.","A stark strip of bare white skin, a dark mass of black—they saw everything.","Gong Linjue had barely stabilized his footing, unable to even care about his exposed body, as Song Jinzhao's next spear thrust charged right at him.","The clashing of metal rang out like a fierce storm. The sharp wind whipped up by the spearhead stung his cheeks, feeling as though thousands of needles were piercing his skin.","Song Jinzhao was incredibly strong and astonishingly fast. Every move and stance left Gong Linjue powerless to fight back, forcing him to dodge continuously.","Suddenly, Song Jinzhao gripped the spear with both hands and, using all her strength, brought it crashing down.","With nowhere to evade, Gong Linjue had no choice but to swing his sword with both hands and brace for the impact."]},{"number":326,"title":"Chapter 326: You Lose, Ferghana Horse","paragraphs":["The moment the two clashed, the sword broke in half with a sharp clang.","The momentum of the spear remained undiminished. The spearhead fell right past the top of Gong Linjue's head, cleaving his golden hair crown in two.","The spearhead smashed heavily onto the ground. Without the slightest pause, Song Jinzhao quickly turned her wrist.","As she spun around, the sharp spearhead was already resting against his neck.","Beads of blood slowly dripped from the spearhead to the ground; advancing even a fraction more would sever Gong Linjue's neck and carotid artery.","\"You've lost,\" Song Jinzhao coldly spat out the words, the battle intent radiating from her body yet to dissipate.","Her face held no joy or smugness of victory, only a chillingly extreme calmness, as if winning was merely an inevitable result for her.","Inside the Hall of Preserving Harmony, there was absolute silence. Everyone was frozen in place.","Gong Linjue, who had easily defeated six military officials in a row, was actually beaten by a woman, the Linghui County Princess!","On the shattered circular platform, Gong Linjue's hair was disheveled and his clothes were in tatters. His front was entirely exposed, and his torn white underpants had been reduced to a thin piece of fabric barely covering his waist.","The scratch on his face had turned into over a dozen, all cut by flying wood splinters.","Gong Linjue's eyes were bloodshot. Disregarding his humiliation, the only thought in his mind right now was to tear Song Jinzhao into pieces.","Ever since he helped the Third Prince ascend the throne, no one had ever subjected him to such a deep humiliation.","Song Jinzhao was the first, and she must be the last.","Seeing him remain silent and just glaring at her with a face full of hatred, Song Jinzhao pushed the spear in her hand forward just a tiny bit more.","\"Does the Prince of Wei refuse to admit defeat and wish to continue fighting? I have plenty of time and can keep you company.\"","The deputy envoy sitting below nearly fainted.","How could His Highness lose! And to a woman, no less.","With this single battle, everything they had done earlier was in vain.","The sharp pain at his neck stimulated Gong Linjue's nerves, and he gritted his teeth as he squeezed out the words.","\"I admit defeat.\"","Continuing to fight would only make him look more pathetic and lose more face.","Song Jinzhao withdrew her spear, her expression calm as she stepped aside and gestured. \"Don't forget our wager. After you, Your Highness?\"","Seeing him concede, the deputy envoy hurriedly took off his own official robe, ran up to the stage, and draped it over Gong Linjue's shoulders.","The loose outer robe fell short on Gong Linjue; as he walked, his lower half felt empty and drafty.","He stepped down from the platform and stopped in front of Chu Liuyun, speaking with a dark expression: \"I accidentally slipped earlier and almost injured the Duke of Qing. Please forgive me, Duke of Qing.\"","Chu Liuyun clenched his fists. \"It's fine.\"","It was a fact that Gong Linjue lost to Song Jinzhao, but it was also a fact that he himself was no match for Gong Linjue.","He had no complaints about being inferior in skill; he only hated that he wasn't strong enough.","Gong Linjue cast a fleeting glance at Chu Liuyun, completely disregarding him.","He turned to face Xiao Chengjing.","\"Your Majesty the Emperor of Dongzhao, I am improperly dressed and need to change. I shall take my leave from the birthday banquet for today.\"","The stage had been turned into a pile of ruins, and fearing that Gong Linjue might cause more trouble, Xiao Chengjing immediately agreed.","He said cheerfully, \"Today's martial arts sparring for entertainment was truly interesting and an eye-opener for Us.\"","\"Someone, bring out the treasured sword from Our private vault and bestow it upon the Prince of Wei, as compensation for the pain of his broken sword.\"","Gong Linjue's face darkened, wishing he could flick his sleeves and leave immediately.","The dog emperor was humiliating him, reminding him of his pathetic loss to Song Jinzhao just now, where even his sword was broken.","\"Qingshuang, go with the Prince of Wei to the Huitong Guesthouse to fetch the horse. I want to see it when I get back.\"","\"Clatter.\" Someone's cup fell to the ground.","With one foot over the threshold, Gong Linjue's figure paused. He turned to look at Song Jinzhao.","\"I am a man of my word and will never break a promise. It's just a horse; it's not worth my concern.\"","Song Jinzhao curled her lips into a smile. \"It seems the Ferghana horse is nothing but a common item in Your Highness's eyes. It is I who haven't seen enough of the world.\"","The military officials sitting in the hall all kept their thoughts hidden.","A Ferghana horse was one in ten thousand and incredibly precious. Right now, Gong Linjue must be dying of regret inside.","After the Shuobei diplomatic mission left, Xiao Chengjing soon dismissed the banquet.","By the time Song Jinzhao returned to her estate with two chests of rewards, Qingshuang had already brought the horse back.","\"Princess, this horse has a fierce temper and won't let anyone ride it. Fortunately, the guards at the Huitong Guesthouse helped, otherwise I wouldn't have been able to lead it back.\"","Qingshuang held out her hands, revealing two bloody marks on her palms, caused by the reins digging into her skin while she was pulling the horse.","Song Jinzhao walked around to the horse's rear and leaned down to take a look; sure enough, it was a stallion.","\"Lock it in the stable and let Xuetuan scare it for a night. It'll behave tomorrow.\"","Although Xuetuan was a bit slow-witted and had a rather soft temperament, it was still a tiger.","As the king of the forest, its mere presence was enough to overwhelm other animals, and even a Ferghana horse would be afraid.","Hearing the news, Song Qiming and Song Shixue walked over from the backyard. Seeing an extra horse in the front hall and two large chests on the ground, they were full of doubts.","Their older sister had been invited to the Emperor's birthday banquet, so what was going on now?","Since Qingshuang couldn't pull it alone, she called over several guards to help pull together.","Song Shixue looked closely, taking the lantern from Hehua's hand to shine it carefully.","\"Sister, this horse doesn't seem to belong to our family.\"","So tall and muscular, their family didn't have a horse like this.","Song Jinzhao nodded. \"This is Gong Linjue's horse, but he has already lost it to me.\"","The siblings were stunned. How could the horse of the Prince of Wei from Shuobei be lost to their sister?","Song Qiming felt a sense of foreboding and asked uncertainly, \"Sister, did something happen at the birthday banquet today?\"","Having been tense all night, Song Jinzhao was also a bit tired.","She turned and led her younger siblings towards the backyard, explaining as they walked.","\"At the banquet, Gong Linjue proposed to spar with the Duke of Qing to entertain the Emperor. The military officials of the court lost five matches in a row. Finally, when the Duke of Qing fought him, Gong Linjue maliciously almost crippled his hand.\"","\"I intervened and scratched Gong Linjue. He clung to that tiny, almost healed wound, forcefully demanding an explanation from the Emperor, and arrogantly claimed that the court's military officials were too weak and all useless. So I made a wager with him and fought him. That Ferghana horse is what I won back, and the things in the chests are rewards from the Emperor.\"","Song Qiming's toe caught on a stone slab, and he almost lost his balance.","\"Sparring at the birthday banquet and trying to cripple the Duke of Qing, this Prince of Wei is too bold.\"","Song Jinzhao yawned as she walked.","\"He is bold because he has the strength to back it up, and Dongzhao has always avoided war and advocated for peace, which has only fueled Shuobei's arrogance.\"","\"The border won't remain peaceful; there will definitely be another war in a few years.\"","Song Qiming sighed. \"Since the founding of Dongzhao, there's a war with Shuobei every ten years at the shortest, or every few decades at the longest. Every time, it drains the people and resources, causing countless casualties.\"","\"If one day we can fight back and completely wipe them out, there won't be any more wars.\"","Song Qiming smiled and shook his head. \"The current Emperor definitely won't be able to fulfill this wish of yours.\"","Xiao Chengjing was a typical conservative. Unless he was a hundred percent sure of winning, he would never initiate a war.","Compared to unifying the world, he was more afraid of losing his grip on the dragon throne beneath him."]},{"number":327,"title":"Chapter 327: Everything has its conqueror: using a tiger to tame a horse","paragraphs":["Inside the Huitong Guesthouse, the deputy envoy stood in the room with his head bowed, not daring to make a sound.","On the soft couch in the outer room, Gong Linjue had just finished bathing and changed into fresh clothes. His uneven hair was tied up high with a slightly narrow white jade crown, and his entire being exuded a forbidding aura that warned strangers to stay away.","\"Has the horse been taken away?\" Gong Linjue's gaze was cold and gloomy, his voice deep.","The deputy envoy nodded tremblingly. \"Song Jinzhao's maid couldn't lead it away; it was the soldiers outside who helped.\"","\"Please do not be angry, Your Highness. It is just a horse. We can find another one when we return.\"","Gong Linjue's eyes turned sinister as he looked at the deputy envoy.","\"If a blood-sweating steed were that easy to find, I wouldn't be this heartbroken.\"","\"I didn't expect this Song Jinzhao to be so formidable. No wonder the spies in Xining City were all defeated by her.\"","The deputy envoy voiced his comfort, \"No matter how formidable she is, she is still a woman. She cannot lead troops into battle, so Your Highness need not take it to heart.\"","The broken strands of hair falling over his forehead grew more annoying the more he looked at them. Gong Linjue decisively reached out and pushed them back to the top of his head.","\"If pushed to a desperate situation, it wouldn't be surprising for the Dongzhao Kingdom to send a woman to the battlefield.\"","The deputy envoy replied, \"No matter how formidable Song Jinzhao is, she doesn't understand military tactics. If she really goes to the battlefield, with a thousand men attacking her alone, are we afraid she can't be killed?\"","Gong Linjue closed his eyes and took a deep breath.","\"Have the people from the Court of Agricultural Review been bribed?\"","The deputy envoy lowered his head with a troubled expression.","\"For some unknown reason, the Dongzhao court has added many more soldiers to patrol outside the Huitong Guesthouse day and night. As soon as our people go out, they are followed, making it impossible to contact the officials from the Court of Agricultural Review.\"","Gong Linjue's brows furrowed tightly. Everything was going wrong, which only fueled the fire in his heart.","\"Their guard is so high. It seems we can only make our move after we leave the capital.\"","The deputy envoy looked up. \"For now, I'm afraid this is the only way. However, it won't delay our schedule. After we get the potatoes and return, it will be just in time for spring planting. That will be the perfect time to plant them.\"","The image of being defeated by Song Jinzhao reappeared in his mind. Gong Linjue closed his eyes and waved his hand to dismiss the man.","The deputy envoy turned and went out, closing the door behind him.","A cold wind blew through the corridor, making the scalp exposed outside his hat feel chilly.","He had thought they could celebrate their success tonight. Who knew a Song Jinzhao would pop up and beat the Prince until he wet himself in terror? This was a massive loss.","The morning sun slowly shone on the roof of the stables.","The blood-sweating steed, having not slept all night, pressed tightly against the corner of the wall, looking much more haggard.","On the straw mat outside the fence, Xuetuan opened its tiger eyes.","As soon as it stood up, all the horses in the stable began to neigh frantically, louder than the crowing of roosters, almost tearing the roof off.","The servant responsible for feeding the fodder hurried out of the room, pulling up his belt.","Seeing that Xuetuan was awake, he didn't dare to go inside and could only stop outside to watch.","Even though this beast was as obedient as a cat in front of its master, it was still extremely fierce to everyone else.","If anyone was given any respect, it was only the few managers who had a bit of standing.","Hearing the commotion, Qingshuang walked over from the inner courtyard.","Xuetuan looked up at her, then climbed up from the haystack, walked with a cat-like gait to the fence, and tilted its head to signal her to open the gate.","Qingshuang stretched her neck and glanced at the blood-sweating steed in the stable.","With haggard eyes and half-drooping eyelids, it looked nothing like the extraordinarily majestic and arrogant creature from yesterday.","\"Everything has its vanquisher. The County Princess truly has her ways.\"","Saying that, she let Xuetuan out and patted its head.","\"Good job. I'll reward you with twenty catties of the freshly slaughtered sheep from the estate this morning.\"","Xuetuan proudly turned its head away, as if to say twenty catties wasn't enough; it wanted to eat the whole sheep.","Seeing Xuetuan being led away and disappearing from sight, the blood-sweating steed cowering in the corner immediately collapsed to the ground.","After trembling in fear all night, it was already exhausted beyond measure. It closed its eyes and fell into a deep sleep.","After breakfast, just as Song Jinzhao walked to the stable door, the blood-sweating steed, which had been sleeping soundly, suddenly opened its eyes and scrambled up from the ground, looking as alert as if facing a formidable enemy.","Song Jinzhao gently curled her lips and instructed Qingshuang, \"Take some people to the horse market and pick out a hundred of the best mares. Send them to the farm on the estate to be raised. They need to be suitable for breeding, ideally between five and twelve years old.\"","Such an excellent bloodline had to be widely propagated. If they couldn't find female blood-sweating steeds, they would find the best of other breeds.","When the breeding season arrived, they would mate, and a year later, the foals would be born.","Fushun ran over from the front hall to report, \"County Princess, the Duke of Qing and Commander Fan are here.\"","Song Jinzhao frowned slightly.","What were they doing here?","Walking into the front hall, she found Chu Liuyun and Fan Guanshan strolling around the room with their hands behind their backs.","Seeing Song Jinzhao enter, Chu Liuyun hastily cupped his hands and said, \"Thank you, County Princess, for coming to my rescue at the birthday banquet yesterday. My mother knew I was coming today and prepared some thank-you gifts for you. Please accept them.\"","Last night, after Chu Liuyun returned home, the Duchess of Zhenguo noticed the injuries on his face and asked about them.","Only then did she learn that her son's hands had almost been crippled by Gong Linjue. In a fit of rage, she cursed Gong Linjue to the thin air for a full half-hour before the Duke of Zhenguo managed to calm her down.","Knowing this morning that Chu Liuyun was coming to express his gratitude, she hurriedly prepared several chests of gifts for him to bring along.","The combined value of the three chests was already comparable to the two chests of items rewarded by the Emperor yesterday.","\"Since they are gifts of gratitude, I shall accept them.\" Song Jinzhao raised her hand, gesturing for the servants to carry the chests away.","\"Why did Commander Fan come with the Duke of Qing? Does the Emperor have any orders?\"","As a close minister to the Emperor, although she had interacted with Fan Guanshan during the previous assassination incident, they were merely acquaintances who nodded to each other since then, and he had never visited the County Princess's manor.","Fan Guanshan stood with his toes pointing outward, shaking his head while his eyes sparkled.","\"The Emperor didn't send me. Has Gong Linjue's blood-sweating steed been brought to the County Princess's manor?\"","Song Jinzhao paused slightly. \"Yes, it has been brought back.\"","Fan Guanshan said with an excited expression, \"I've never ridden a blood-sweating steed before. Could the County Princess take me to see it?\"","Song Jinzhao gave a knowing smile and said calmly, \"Of course, but you can only look at it. It hasn't slept all night and can't be ridden right now.\"","\"Huh? Did the County Princess train it all night?\" Fan Guanshan asked curiously.","Worried that Song Jinzhao had used forceful methods and was too eager for success, Chu Liuyun couldn't help but offer some advice.","\"A good horse is hard to tame, especially a blood-sweating steed.\"","\"If you want to completely tame it, you have to spend time rebuilding affection and mutual understanding with it. You can't rush it.\"","Song Jinzhao pointed to her own eyes and said, \"Do I look like I stayed up all night?\"","\"A good horse is indeed hard to tame, but even the fiercest horse is afraid of a tiger. I had Xuetuan guard the stable all night. It didn't dare to sleep and has pretty much yielded.\"","Chu Liuyun and Fan Guanshan froze at the same time. Using a tiger to wear down a horse—how could anyone come up with such a method?","Seeing Song Jinzhao walking out, Chu Liuyun and Fan Guanshan hurriedly followed."]},{"number":328,"title":"Chapter 328: Absolutely Not for Sale, the King of Qi's Eyes Were Gouged Out","paragraphs":["Hearing the noise, the Ferghana horse lying in the corner suddenly opened its eyes. Seeing that it was a human and not a tiger, it closed its eyes again.","Chu Liuyun clicked his tongue in amazement. \"To make a horse lie on the ground to sleep, it must have been terrified all night.\"","Horses usually sleep standing up. They only sleep lying down when they are so exhausted that they can't even stand steadily.","Fan Guanshan sighed with regret. \"It seems impossible to take it for a ride today.\"","After speaking, he looked at Song Jinzhao. \"Can the County Princess sell this horse to me? I am willing to offer one thousand taels of silver.\"","Chu Liuyun held up two fingers and said decisively, \"I offer two thousand taels.\"","Song Jinzhao crossed her arms over her chest, having long anticipated their reactions.","\"Gold is easy to get, but a precious horse is hard to find. I won't sell it for any amount of silver.\"","Fan Guanshan eagerly tried to persuade her.","\"An ordinary high-grade horse is enough for regular transportation. Using a Ferghana horse is too much of a waste. County Princess, please just sell it to me.\"","Song Jinzhao shook her head. \"I'm not selling. I also want to ride the best.\"","\"If Commander Fan wants one, you can go pick a fight with Gong Linjue. Maybe they still have some on hand.\"","Fan Guanshan instantly fell silent. If he had absolute certainty of winning, he wouldn't have hesitated yesterday.","Standing nearby, Chu Liuyun guiltily averted his gaze. He had just lost yesterday.","\"Roar!\" Smelling the scent of a stranger, Xuetuan bared its fangs and brandished its claws, charging toward Fan Guanshan.","Fan Guanshan turned pale with fright and stumbled backward in panic.","Chu Liuyun dodged and leaped up onto a tree trunk.","\"Xuetuan!\"","Song Shixue chased after it and grabbed its collar, then gently patted its head with her hand.","\"These are guests, don't scare them.\"","Half-crouching on the ground, Xuetuan turned its head to look at Song Shixue with an innocent expression.","Didn't you tell me to act fierce toward them?","Song Shixue suppressed the secret delight in her heart and feigned an apologetic tone as she apologized to Chu Liuyun and Fan Guanshan.","\"Xuetuan gets especially vigilant when it smells strangers. Please forgive us for frightening you two lords.\"","The things her older sister won back absolutely could not be taken away by others.","A Ferghana horse is so precious, priceless even with a market for it. The family doesn't lack silver now, so it won't be sold for any amount.","Meeting Song Shixue's credit-seeking gaze, Song Jinzhao couldn't help but curl her lips into a smile.","The retreating Fan Guanshan fearfully patted his chest to catch his breath.","Didn't everyone say that the tiger raised by County Princess Linghui was incredibly docile? Why did it look so fierce?","Chu Liuyun jumped down from the tree trunk, his gaze circling between Song Jinzhao and Song Shixue.","It seemed that buying the Ferghana horse was definitely out of the question.","\"County Princess, this Ferghana horse is a stallion. When spring comes next year, it can be used for breeding, and the foals born will also be of relatively excellent quality.\"","Song Jinzhao: \"I have already sent people to the horse market to pick out the best mares to buy. When the foals are born, I can sell one to you.\"","Hearing this, Fan Guanshan hastily pleaded, \"Can I buy one too?\"","Song Jinzhao nodded in agreement.","\"As long as the price is right, of course. However, I will only sell two, so don't tell anyone else.\"","\"No problem,\" the two agreed in unison.","With only two for sale, they didn't want anyone else competing with them anyway.","Just as the three were talking, Fu Shun ran over in a hurried panic.","With a terrified look on his face, he said, \"County Princess, an edict has come from the palace ordering you to quickly go to the Prince Qi's manor to treat Prince Qi.\"","Song Jinzhao frowned in confusion. \"Prince Qi has returned from the southwest?\"","Chu Liuyun and Fan Guanshan were equally bewildered. Had Prince Qi returned?","Fu Shun was panting heavily, his back drenched in sweat.","\"This servant is not sure either, but the eunuch who came to call said that Prince Qi had one of his eyes gouged out, and asked you to head over immediately.\"","Song Jinzhao blinked, a bit slow to process the information.","Had an eye gouged out? Xiao Rongche?","Chu Liuyun and Fan Guanshan exchanged a glance, immediately sensing that things were bad.","Prince Qi went to the southwest to negotiate peace. If he had an eye gouged out, wouldn't the situation in the southwest be terrible?","When the three rushed to Prince Qi's manor, many soldiers were standing in the courtyard.","The General of Assured Might, Wen Yong, rushed up as soon as he saw Song Jinzhao.","\"County Princess, you absolutely must save His Highness Prince Qi.\"","His eye sockets were deeply sunken, the whites of his eyes were full of bloodshot veins, his beard was messy, his lips were cracked and bleeding, and he smelled of sour sweat.","How many days had it been since he bathed, changed clothes, or slept?","Song Jinzhao shook off his hand. \"I need to take a look first.\"","Being injured in the southwest, even if they traveled day and night without rest, at least ten days must have passed.","She didn't know the exact condition of the gouged-out eye.","\"County Princess,\" Gu Jupu walked from the inner room to the door, his voice hoarse, as if he had exhausted all his strength.","Song Jinzhao steadily stepped over the threshold.","As soon as she walked into the inner chamber, she saw Xiao Rongche, whose right eye was injured, raise a white jade pillow and smash it heavily onto the imperial physician's head.","\"Trash, you're all trash! If you can't save my eye, you can all go die.\"","In his heart-wrenching voice, aside from anger, there was mostly despair.","Imperial Physician Xu, who instinctively dodged, was still struck on the forehead. The moment the pillow hit the ground, warm blood flowed from the wound.","Gu Jupu, standing next to Song Jinzhao, tightened his hands. That was a pillow made of white jade; hitting someone on the head with it could kill them.","Through his blurred vision, he saw two figures walking over, and only when they got closer did he realize that one of them was Song Jinzhao.","Xiao Rongche scrambled off the bed in a wretched state and grabbed her sleeve.","\"You can cure my eye, right? I order you to treat me immediately, treat me immediately—\"","Song Jinzhao stared at his deeply sunken, scar-covered eye socket.","There was localized necrosis and atrophy. Being able to keep his life was already considered lucky.","Looking up to meet Gu Jupu's complex gaze, both of them knew clearly in their hearts that this eye could not be cured.","Song Jinzhao pulled her hand away from Xiao Rongche's grasp, her voice steady and clear.","\"Your Highness's eye is completely necrotic. This subject is powerless to help.\"","The other imperial physicians kneeling in the inner chamber felt tense upon hearing this, but at the same time, they breathed a sigh of relief in their hearts.","This time it wasn't because their medical skills were lacking. Since even County Princess Linghui couldn't cure it, it was perfectly normal that they couldn't either.","Unwilling to accept this, Xiao Rongche forcefully swung his arm at Song Jinzhao.","\"Aren't you a divine doctor? Why can't you cure my eye?! Are you deliberately refusing to treat me?\"","He roared furiously, \"Song Jinzhao, I'm telling you, if my eye isn't cured, I want all of you to be buried with me!\"","Song Jinzhao took a step back to avoid his striking hand.","\"I am a doctor, not an immortal. With an arrowhead piercing your eyeball, your eye was ruined. Being alive is already a stroke of immense luck.\"","Xiao Rongche shook his head frantically. \"Impossible, you're lying! You hate me, so you won't treat me.\"","Song Jinzhao watched him go mad expressionlessly. \"Then tell me, why do I hate you?\"","Xiao Rongche opened his mouth, but the words caught in his throat.","Everyone tacitly acknowledging it in private was one thing, but admitting it himself was another.","He couldn't speak of the time he sent assassins to murder Song Jinzhao.","\"I don't care, you must cure me.\"","Song Jinzhao furrowed her brows and turned to walk outside.","Gu Jupu hurriedly followed. \"County Princess, the Emperor is still waiting in the palace for our report.\"","Song Jinzhao didn't stop walking. \"Then we enter the palace. Either way, it can't be avoided.\""]},{"number":329,"title":"Chapter 329: The Other Eye Will Also Go Blind","paragraphs":["Inside the Funing Palace, Prince Qi's biological mother, Concubine Jin, had nearly fainted from crying in the Emperor's arms.","Hearing the eunuch report that Song Jinzhao and Gu Jupu were requesting an audience outside, she hurriedly lifted her head and looked toward the door.","Seeing the two enter, she couldn't wait to ask, \"How is it? Can the First Prince's eye be cured?\"","Song Jinzhao glanced at her, then met Xiao Chengjing's eyes and knelt.","\"To reply to Your Majesty, His Highness Prince Qi's right eye is completely necrotic. This subject is powerless to save it.\"","Xiao Chengjing's heart sank to the bottom. If even Song Jinzhao said there was no way, it was definitely beyond saving.","Song Jinzhao continued, \"Not only that, but the dead eyeball will also affect the other eye.\"","\"Right now, his vision is merely blurry, but I fear he will go completely blind in another month or two.\"","\"Furthermore, the eye is connected to the cranial and facial nerves. His Highness Prince Qi will be continuously tormented by illness from now on; chronic headaches and facial pain are unavoidable.\"","These words were like a bolt from the blue.","No matter how dissatisfied he had been before, this was still his own son.","Finding it hard to accept, Xiao Chengjing stood up. \"Is there really no way to save the other eye?\"","Song Jinzhao replied, \"It is practically impossible. Even with daily medicinal treatment, it will only delay the blindness, probably by just a few months.\"","Concubine Jin slumped to the ground, her body utterly limp.","Dazed, she shook her head and muttered to herself, \"This is impossible. How could my son become blind? He cannot become blind.\"","A blind man could not become the Emperor; a blind man was a useless cripple.","Xiao Chengjing fell back into his chair, beginning to regret why he had sent Xiao Rongche to the southwest.","If he hadn't gone, this accident wouldn't have happened.","\"Who shot the arrow at Prince Qi? Where is Wen Yong? What was he doing?\"","Xiao Chengjing picked up the vase at hand and smashed it heavily onto the ground.","Even though the floor was covered with a carpet, the vase still shattered all over the floor.","Song Jinzhao lowered her eyes to look at the back of her hand, which had been scratched by a broken porcelain shard, and furrowed her brows.","Throwing things at the slightest provocation—who did he learn such a bad habit from?","Knowing that he was being summoned by the Emperor, Wen Yong's legs gave out on the spot.","With Prince Qi's eye incurable and the Emperor furious, he would be the first to suffer the consequences.","His mind in chaos, Wen Yong immediately pulled over a man wearing a mask.","\"General Huo, the Emperor has just summoned me. You will come with me.\"","Huo Chong waved his hand in refusal, looking troubled.","\"The Emperor did not summon me, so I won't go. General Wen should go by himself.\"","How could Wen Yong agree to that? With one more person facing the Emperor, the anger he had to bear might be lessened.","Moreover, Huo Chong belonged to the Mu clan, making it incredibly fitting to bring him along.","\"General Huo, do not forget your purpose in coming to the capital.\"","\"Right now is when the Emperor's anger is at its peak. You only need to say a few words, and the Emperor will deploy troops to help you annihilate the Yang clan!\"","Huo Chong furrowed his brows in suspicion. \"Really?\"","Wen Yong patted his chest in guarantee, though he felt guilty on the inside.","\"Of course it's true. They blinded His Highness Prince Qi's eye; how could the Emperor not deploy troops?\"","Seeing him still hesitating, Wen Yong simply dragged and coaxed the man into the carriage.","After leaving the Funing Palace, Song Jinzhao and Gu Jupu went to the Prince Qi Manor.","On the way, Song Jinzhao leisurely said to Gu Jupu, \"After examining Prince Qi's eye, regarding what medicine to use and how to apply the acupuncture needles, I must ask Court Envoy Gu to send someone to learn it properly, or you can come personally.\"","Gu Jupu widened his eyes in astonishment. \"The County Princess will not treat Prince Qi personally?\"","Song Jinzhao raised her eyes to stare at him, her gaze dark and profound as she said, \"Do you think I am willing to treat him?\"","Going blind was nothing; it would be better if he died.","Gu Jupu's expression froze, and he silently lowered his head, speaking no more.","If he were County Princess Linghui, he wouldn't be willing to treat him either; it would be best if he died to relieve the hatred.","After bringing Huo Chong to the palace gates, Wen Yong said, \"General Huo, wait here for a moment. Once I report to the Emperor, His Majesty will surely summon you into the palace immediately.\"","As he spoke, he gave his attendants a look, signaling them to guard Huo Chong and not let him run away.","By the time Wen Yong entered the palace, Xiao Chengjing was already sitting in the Imperial Study. Also present were Chu Liuyun, Fan Guanshan, Dongfang Shaoting, and others.","They had all heard that Prince Qi had returned to the capital injured and hurried into the palace out of concern for the situation in the southwest.","Before Wen Yong even had time to kneel, an inkstone was smashed right in front of him.","\"My beloved Minister Wen, I ordered you to lead troops to protect Prince Qi. How exactly did you protect him?\"","Wen Yong knelt and kowtowed in a panic, feeling a bitterness in his heart that he couldn't express.","You told me to lead troops to awe the southwest, but you didn't say I had to follow your son around without leaving his side for a single step.","I wasn't even present when he was injured.","\"Your Majesty, this humble subject is truly wronged.\"","\"At that time, this humble subject was leading troops to guard the city, while His Highness Prince Qi ventured deep into the enemy camp to persuade the Yang clan to call a truce. Who knew that the two sides would fall out during the peace talks? An arrow shot by the Yang clan accidentally injured His Highness Prince Qi. Since this humble subject was not present, there was truly no way to stop it.\"","Xiao Chengjing slammed his hand on the desk forcefully, spittle flying.","\"What about the guards? Are they all dead?\"","Wen Yong's eyes darted around in panic.","\"The situation was chaotic at the time, and this humble subject is unclear on the specific details. However, this humble subject brought back a general of the Mu clan who was present at the scene to the capital. This person is currently waiting outside the palace for Your Majesty's summons.\"","Xiao Chengjing's brows relaxed slightly as he confirmed with him in surprise, \"You brought someone from the Mu clan to the capital?\"","It was well known that the foreign tribes in the southwest had a very weak sense of belonging to the imperial court, and unless forced, they generally would not come to the capital on their own initiative.","Sensing a slight softening in the Emperor's attitude, Wen Yong hurriedly explained.","\"This person is named Huo Chong. He is the right-hand man of Mu Ji'an, the Pacification Commissioner of Ningzhou. He came to the capital this time specifically to thank Your Majesty.\"","Seeing that the two of them were taking too long to get to the point, Dongfang Shaoting couldn't help but interject and ask, \"What happened after the peace talks broke down?\"","\"Since you and Prince Qi have already returned to the capital and even brought Huo Chong back, what is the current situation in the southwest?\"","Wen Yong lifted his head. \"Prince Qi's eye was injured. Knowing that they had caused a massive disaster, the Yang clan has already called a truce.\"","\"This humble subject thought that there were imperial physicians in the palace and that County Princess Linghui was also in the capital, so I brought His Highness back first. The ten thousand-strong army is still waiting in the isolated city for Your Majesty's explicit decree.\"","Dongfang Shaoting and the others breathed a sigh of relief upon hearing this. In contrast, Gu Qishan, who was standing to the side, still had just as poor of an expression.","If Prince Qi's eye hadn't been injured, achieving such a great merit would have surely allowed his status to advance even further.","But now he was going to become blind. No matter how great his merits were, he could not become the Emperor. It was all useless.","Waiting at the palace gates, Huo Chong looked up at the impossibly high palace walls. His gaze was distant and calm, as if he were looking through them at something else. His face, hidden beneath the mask, exuded a chilling aura.","About to meet the enemy who had murdered his entire family, Huo Chong's heart was surging with emotion.","But in order to avoid exposing himself, he had to forcefully suppress this excitement and try his best to appear very calm.","Not long after, a young eunuch hurried over to lead the way.","\"Which of you is General Huo Chong?\"","Huo Chong stepped forward and replied, \"I am.\"","The young eunuch's gaze lingered for a moment on the mask he wore on his face, then extended a hand and said, \"The Emperor has summoned you. General Huo, please follow this servant to the Imperial Study.\"","The Imperial Guards responsible for standing watch at the palace gates made way. Huo Chong took a deep breath and stepped inside."]},{"number":330,"title":"Chapter 330: Huo Chong Appears Before the Emperor","paragraphs":["In the imperial study, seeing someone walk in wearing a mask, Xiao Chengjing's brows instantly furrowed.","\"Who is so bold as to dare wear a mask in Our presence?\"","Huo Chong paused for a moment before continuing forward, stopping beside Wen Yong to kneel and pay his respects.","\"Your humble subject, Huo Chong, greets Your Majesty. Long live the Emperor.\"","\"My face has been disfigured. Fearing I might offend the imperial presence, I did not remove my mask. I beg Your Majesty's forgiveness.\"","Xiao Chengjing was still displeased.","In his view, no matter the reason, seeking an audience while wearing a mask was a sign of blatant disrespect toward him as the Emperor.","\"We are the true Son of Heaven; how could We be frightened by you? Take off the mask.\"","Huo Chong reached up and removed the mask.","Everyone standing in the imperial study instantly held their breath.","\"Ugh!\" Gu Qishan turned his back, feeling a bit nauseous.","The area around Huo Chong's eyes was covered in dense, snake-like patterns. It looked both terrifying and repulsive, like a monster.","Xiao Chengjing subconsciously averted his gaze, but that hideous face lingered in his mind.","He took short, shallow breaths, feeling slightly sick himself after hearing Gu Qishan gag.","\"Put the mask back on.\" Had he known this face was so disgusting, he would never have looked.","Long accustomed to such reactions, Huo Chong calmly put his mask back on.","My face is like this all because of you.","You find it disgusting now, but sooner or later, I will make you pay for all of it.","Xiao Chengjing caught his breath, trying his best not to think about the face he had just seen.","Suppressing his disgust, he questioned Huo Chong.","\"What happened during the peace talks? Who shot Prince Qi in the eye?\"","Huo Chong replied, \"Under the mediation of His Highness Prince Qi, the two clans had originally agreed to a truce.\"","\"Unexpectedly, the Yang clan of Panzhou suddenly demanded that we pay them two hundred thousand taels of silver as compensation for the war. Commissioner Mu refused, and the two sides began to argue, eventually drawing their weapons.\"","\"A guard belonging to Envoy Yang picked up a bow and arrow to shoot my lord. However, his aim was poor, and His Highness Prince Qi happened to lose his footing and stumbled right into the path of the arrow, which struck his right eye.\"","Xiao Chengjing's breathing grew heavy, his eyes widening like copper bells.","\"Where is that guard?\"","Huo Chong lowered his head. \"He was killed on the spot by Envoy Yang. They knew they had caused a disaster and were in a rush to treat His Highness Prince Qi, so they dropped the demand for the silver.\"","Dongfang Shaoting and Chu Liuyun exchanged a glance.","In this way, Prince Qi's injury had ironically stabilized the situation in the southwest completely.","Xiao Chengjing frowned and demanded, \"Having blinded Prince Qi's eye, why hasn't the Yang clan sent someone to beg for forgiveness?\"","Huo Chong replied, \"Your subject is unclear about their affairs. Presumably, they are too terrified to come.\"","After answering Xiao Chengjing's questions, Huo Chong continued, \"To reply to Your Majesty, my visit to the capital this time is partly to express our deep gratitude for Your Majesty's grace in sending troops to our aid.\"","\"On the other hand, it is also our hope that the imperial court can help us reclaim our lost cities. Especially regarding the salt fields discovered in Binzhou, the Yang clan should at least give us half.\"","Everyone in the room merely cast a fleeting glance at Huo Chong, completely disregarding his words.","Xiao Chengjing spoke impatiently, \"We will discuss this matter later. You may withdraw for now.\"","He had no desire to deploy troops to the southwest at the moment. Moreover, the diplomatic mission from the Shuobei Kingdom was still in the capital, so the more peaceful the southwest was, the better.","As for the salt fields, it would be better to keep them for himself rather than give them to the Mu clan. This matter still needed to be fought for.","After Huo Chong was led out of the imperial study, Xiao Chengjing instructed Wen Yong.","\"The Yang clan of Panzhou has committed such a grave mistake that they must pay the price. Return to the southwest immediately and tell Gu Zhongxun to negotiate with the Yang clan. The imperial court wants half of the salt fields in Binzhou.\"","Wen Yong looked up uncertainly and asked, \"If the Mu clan asks, what should your subject say?\"","Xiao Chengjing replied, \"After this battle, the Mu clan's strength has been greatly diminished, and they are no longer a match for the Yang clan.\"","\"From now on, they can only rely on the imperial court. Even if they find out, they won't dare to do anything about it. Just go and do as I say.\"","Looking slightly hesitant, Wen Yong kowtowed and left.","Gu Qishan stole a glance at Xiao Chengjing's expression, took a deep breath, and lowered his head, remaining silent.","If he had known things would turn out like this, he never would have suggested sending a prince to the southwest in the first place.","He had failed to sabotage Prince Ying, and now Prince Qi was ruined instead.","In the Huitong diplomatic residence, the deputy envoy, who had just returned from the teahouse, hurried urgently toward the courtyard where Gong Linjue was staying.","Arriving at the door, he spoke in an excited and jubilant tone, \"Your Highness, this subordinate has an important matter to report.\"","\"Come in.\" Gong Linjue set down the broken sword in his hand.","The deputy envoy stepped over the threshold and turned to close the door behind him.","He cautiously walked up to Gong Linjue and spoke in a low voice.","\"Your Highness, the First Prince of the Dongzhao Kingdom, Xiao Rongche, has just returned to the capital. He is blind in one eye.\"","The sharp blade of the sword sliced a small cut on the pad of Gong Linjue's finger.","\"Has the Dongzhao imperial court gone to war with the foreign tribes in the southwest?\"","The deputy envoy shook his head. \"That remains unclear, but the general who led the troops to the southwest has already returned alongside Xiao Rongche.\"","Gong Linjue used the cloth meant for wiping his sword to wipe the blood from his finger.","\"Send a few more people out to wander around, especially to the brothels and teahouses. News travels fastest in such places.\"","The deputy envoy replied, \"Rest assured, Your Highness. I have already made the arrangements.\"","A guard who returned in the middle of the night from drinking at a brothel stood in the room and reported, \"The Dongzhao imperial court and the southwestern tribes did not fight. Furthermore, the Yang and Mu clans have called a truce. They rushed back so urgently to find Song Jinzhao to treat Xiao Rongche's eye.\"","\"But it seems it cannot be cured. Your subordinate also learned from the brothel women that both princes of the Dongzhao Kingdom had previously sent assassins after Song Jinzhao. There is bad blood between them. Even if she could cure him, Song Jinzhao definitely wouldn't do it.\"","The corners of Gong Linjue's lips curled upward in an almost imperceptible arc.","\"It seems this prince must go and meet this First Prince.\"","Song Jinzhao stayed at the Prince Qi's estate until the afternoon before returning. For half of that time, Xiao Rongche was screaming for people to be beaten and killed.","It wasn't until Song Jinzhao told him that if he didn't cooperate with the treatment, his left eye would soon go blind as well, and his life would be in danger, that he finally quieted down.","Song Qiming, who had finished his shift at the Hanlin Academy early, hovered around Song Jinzhao and asked, \"Sister, what exactly is the situation with Prince Qi's eye injury? Yukun said he will go blind in both eyes, and he said you were the one who said it.\"","Song Jinzhao placed her hands into a wooden basin filled with hot water and washed them clean.","She nodded and said, \"In at most three months, Prince Qi will become completely blind. Moreover, his eyes will repeatedly become inflamed and ooze pus. Coupled with chronic headaches and facial pain caused by nerve damage, his future days will be extremely excruciating. It can be said that he will live in agony every single day.\"","While Song Qiming was surprised, a trace of joy flashed in the depths of his eyes.","Before they even had to make a move, Prince Qi had brought about his own destruction. Could this be considered karma?","If only Prince Ying would end up like this too.","Upon learning that Song Jinzhao had washed her hands of treating Prince Qi and passed the task entirely to Gu Jupu, Xiao Chengjing did not say a single word.","Firstly, it was because of the assassination incident last year.","Secondly, it was because Song Jinzhao had just performed a great merit at the birthday banquet. With the Shuobei Kingdom's diplomatic mission still in the capital, he could not show any dissatisfaction toward Song Jinzhao, lest it boost Gong Linjue's arrogance."]},{"number":331,"title":"Chapter 331: The Palace Enters the Qi Prince's Mansion on the Final Night","paragraphs":["A few days later, at the beginning of the month, Song Jinzhao left the manor to inspect her shops. When she walked into the Hotpot Palace, she happened to see Gong Linjue eating hotpot by the window on the second floor.","Their eyes met, and Gong Linjue spoke with a faint, enigmatic smile.","\"I heard that this hotpot restaurant was opened by the Princess of Linghui. The cooking method is quite similar to the copper pot boiled mutton of our Shuobei State. It is a pity that I cannot order beef here.\"","Song Jinzhao's lips curled up, but the smile did not reach her eyes.","\"The Dongzhao State prohibits the slaughter of draft cattle. Eating beef depends on luck. Your Highness can buy some hotpot base to take back and boil. I am sure Shuobei State does not lack beef to eat.\"","Gong Linjue cast a cold glance at Song Jinzhao, then put down his chopsticks and left.","Song Jinzhao walked to the window and looked down, only to see them enter the weapon shop across the street.","It had been several days since the Emperor's birthday banquet. Why hadn't the Shuobei delegation left yet?","At the dinner table that evening, Song Jinzhao asked Song Qiming, \"When is the Shuobei delegation leaving the capital?\"","Song Shixue, who was picking up food, paused her chopsticks to wait for Song Qiming's answer.","Lan Xi was still hiding at the estate, not daring to return. She also wanted to know when the delegation would leave.","Song Qiming replied, \"They say that the roads are hard to travel now that winter has arrived and it is snowing. They want to wait until the weather gets a bit warmer before leaving.\"","\"Doesn't that mean they will wait until February or March of next year?\" Song Shixue exclaimed in astonishment.","It was only November, the beginning of winter, and the first snow had not even fallen yet. For it to be warmer than it was now, they would have to wait until at least February of next year.","Song Qiming nodded.","\"Lord Fei said that there are pros and cons to Gong Linjue staying in the capital. The advantage is that we do not have to worry about Shuobei starting a war. The disadvantage is that we have to constantly guard against him. The Imperial Guards stationed outside the city will probably have to spend the New Year at the royal estate.\"","Song Jinzhao frowned slightly, feeling a bit worried.","\"Over a long period of time, it is inevitable that some people will let their guard down. Gong Linjue will not just sit around doing nothing while in the capital. We must be strictly on guard.\"","Song Qiming said, \"Lord Fei said the same thing. I have this lingering feeling that they are planning to secretly pull some underhanded tricks.\"","After learning that Xiao Rongche's eye could not be cured and that his other eye would also go blind, the gates of the Prince Qi Manor became thoroughly deserted.","Every day, only imperial physicians came to treat him. Originally, the Emperor sent people to check on him every few days, but unfortunately, after half a month, he stopped paying much attention.","The massive fall from grace and the resentment of being abandoned made Xiao Rongche's temperament increasingly volatile.","He would smash things at the drop of a hat, beating and cursing the servants.","His emotional instability caused the healing of his eye to be highly pessimistic.","The pain in his head and face intensified. He spent his days in a daze, looking like a vengeful ghost crawling out of a gutter.","It was past midnight, the time when people were the sleepiest.","Dressed in black nightclothes, Gong Linjue climbed up the rockery inside the Huitong Guesthouse, then used a willow tree near the wall to vault over the high courtyard wall.","A dry leaf fell onto a guard's face, making him jolt awake.","Realizing it was just a leaf, he hugged his sword and went back to dozing, muttering a complaint to himself, \"So sleepy, why isn't it dawn yet?\"","Gong Linjue stealthily made his way to the back door of the Prince Qi Manor and jumped in from the lowest point of the wall.","Ever since Prince Qi was crippled, the manor's guards had become much slacker. He easily found the room where Xiao Rongche was sleeping.","Two guards were dozing at the door. Looking around, there were no other shadows. Even the lanterns were scarce, making the area look very dim.","After waiting for a moment and confirming that the surrounding defenses were lax, Gong Linjue jumped down from the eaves. His footsteps were so light that the two guards did not notice a thing.","With a few quick steps, he closed in and delivered two backhanded chops.","The guards opened their eyes but fainted before they could even make out his figure.","Pushing open the door, Xiao Rongche, who had been throwing tantrums all day, was sleeping soundly. Approaching him, one could even hear his snoring.","It was not until he felt a stinging pain on his neck that he jolted awake, as if he had suddenly fallen into an abyss.","Gong Linjue's dark red pupils were like a blade stabbing straight into Xiao Rongche's heart.","He was just about to scream when the dagger pressed against his neck moved a fraction closer, scaring him so much that the words died in his throat.","Trembling, Xiao Rongche asked in a hoarse voice, \"Who are you? Who sent you to kill me?\"","He had already been reduced to this state, yet someone still wanted to kill him.","Was it Prince Ying, or someone else?","A cold sneer curled the corners of Gong Linjue's mouth.","\"His Highness Prince Qi has stayed in the manor ever since returning to the capital. Unable to meet you, I had no choice but to come at night. Please forgive me, Your Highness.\"","He asked for forgiveness, but his eyes were full of mockery. He did not take the other party seriously at all.","The pupil of Xiao Rongche's throbbing left eye contracted. He stared fixedly at the person in front of him, his tone filled with disbelief.","\"You are Gong Linjue, the Prince of Wei from the Shuobei State?\"","The only person who would refer to himself as a prince, whom he did not recognize, could only be the Prince of Wei from Shuobei, who had come to celebrate the Emperor's birthday.","But why would a dignified prince sneak into his manor in the middle of the night?","They did not even have a grudge against each other.","Gong Linjue withdrew the dagger and straightened his upper body.","\"I came here today to discuss a deal with Your Highness. I wonder if you are interested?\"","Xiao Rongche sat up in bed, looking at Gong Linjue coldly.","\"As a prince of an enemy nation, what deal do you want to discuss with me?\"","Gong Linjue scoffed. \"An enemy prince, indeed. Your Highness speaks quite bluntly.\"","A cold, self-deprecating smile appeared on Xiao Rongche's face.","\"I am already blind. I have no mood to beat around the bush with you. If you have something to say, say it directly.\"","Gong Linjue pulled over a chair and sat down. \"I have a way to save Your Highness's other eye.\"","Hearing these words, Xiao Rongche, whose heart had been as dead as ashes, was instantly energized.","As if grabbing a lifeline, he eagerly asked, \"Is what you say true?\"","Gong Linjue gave a slight nod.","\"Of course it is true. I have seen someone exactly like Your Highness. However, his left eye was injured. Ten years have passed, and his right eye remains clear and bright, completely unaffected.\"","After pondering for a moment, Xiao Rongche frowned.","\"But Song Jinzhao said my eye cannot be cured. Does Shuobei State actually have a doctor with more superb medical skills than hers?\"","Gong Linjue raised his long eyebrows.","\"As far as I know, Your Highness once sent assassins to kill Song Jinzhao. If it were you, would you save someone who once tried to kill you?\"","Xiao Rongche could not help but clench his fists.","Of course not.","\"But the imperial physicians also said it cannot be cured.\"","Gong Linjue's tone dripped with sarcasm. \"If their medical skills cannot even compare to a woman's, how superb could they possibly be?\"","\"If Your Highness does not believe me, the moment I return to Shuobei, I will have that person come see you immediately. I can also bring along the doctor who treated him.\"","After a long silence, Xiao Rongche raised his head, staring at Gong Linjue with burning eyes.","\"What do you want me to do for you?\"","Gong Linjue replied, \"I want a cartload of potatoes. This should not be difficult for Your Highness.\"","Xiao Rongche took a deep breath. After thinking for a moment, he nodded in agreement.","\"I can give you a cartload of potatoes, but you must cure my eye first.\"","Gong Linjue leaned back in his chair. \"Your Highness is a prince of an enemy nation, and that doctor is an imperial physician from my Shuobei State's Imperial Hospital. Without the Emperor's permission, it is impossible for him to travel thousands of miles to the capital to treat Your Highness's eye. If the Emperor does not see your sincerity, he will not agree.\""]},{"number":332,"title":"Chapter 332: Drawing a Grand Vision for Xiao Rongche, the Diplomatic Mission Leaves the Capital","paragraphs":["The dim candlelight from the bedside stand flickered across Xiao Rongche's gloomy face. After pondering for a long time, he ultimately had no choice but to nod.","Song Jinzhao and the Imperial Hospital had already pronounced a death sentence on his eye. Other than trusting Gong Linjue, he had no other options left.","It was nothing more than a cart of potatoes. Handing it over would have no impact on him; it just meant letting the Shuobei State get it a little earlier.","\"You must leave the capital as soon as possible. Only when you are gone will the Court of Agricultural Affairs relax its guard. Set a location, and I will have someone deliver a cart of potatoes there.\"","Gong Linjue stood up and clasped his hands behind his back. \"Since Your Highness is so sincere, I will also say a word here on behalf of the Shuobei State.\"","\"If Your Highness encounters difficulties in the fight for the throne in the future, as long as the deal is beneficial to both sides, our Shuobei State is willing to lend a helping hand.\"","A bitter smile touched the corners of Xiao Rongche's lips.","\"Even if I manage to keep my left eye, my imperial father and the civil and military officials will never let a prince blind in his right eye become the emperor. Seizing the throne is already impossible for me.\"","However, since they were thinking about the future, the matter of curing his eye should be true.","Gong Linjue's tone carried a subtle, persuasive edge.","\"As long as all the other princes are dead, even if Your Highness cannot see with your right eye, you can still become the emperor.\"","\"If anyone disagrees, just kill them. As for how the history books will be written, once Your Highness ascends the throne, you can dictate whatever you want.\"","\"At the very least, Your Highness could let your son be the emperor, and you could be the Supreme Emperor. Wouldn't that be even more satisfying?\"","The coldness and bloodthirstiness revealed in Gong Linjue's eyes startled Xiao Rongche, as if he had actually done such things before.","The next morning, just as Song Jinzhao was about to go out, snow began to fall from the sky.","Snowflakes like cotton wadding fell in sheets. By the afternoon, the snow accumulated on the ground was already as deep as a fingernail.","Song Qiming returned from outside, wearing a thick cloak.","\"Sister, the Shuobei diplomatic mission is leaving the capital.\"","Song Jinzhao frowned in confusion. \"Didn't they say they were staying until after the New Year? Why are they leaving so suddenly?\"","Song Qiming shook his head. \"I'm not sure about that either. I only heard Lord Fei say that Gong Linjue bid farewell to the Emperor this morning. It seems the Emperor of Shuobei ordered them to return.\"","After pondering for a moment, Song Jinzhao asked, \"Has the mission met with anyone these past few days?\"","Song Qiming thought for a moment and replied, \"Probably not. The Huitong Guesthouse is surrounded by soldiers inside and out, and no one dares to make contact with them.\"","\"We'll have to ask Commander Fan for the specific details; he would know best.\"","It was still snowing when the mission left the capital.","After the carriage drove out of the city gates, Gong Linjue lifted the curtain and looked up at the towering characters for 'Capital City'.","Sooner or later, he would lead an army to invade the capital and plant the flag of the Shuobei State upon these walls.","Gong Linjue left in such a hurry that everyone in the court, including the Emperor, harbored suspicions. They worried whether the Shuobei Emperor's urgent recall meant they were planning something major.","In the Imperial Study, Xiao Chengjing instructed the Minister of War, Wu Jianzheng, \"Notify Qin Guo to carefully investigate the movements at the Shuobei border, reorganize the military, and strictly strengthen our defenses.\"","Wu Jianzheng cupped his hands in acknowledgment. \"I obey Your Majesty's decree.\"","Once it was confirmed that the entire mission had left the capital, the Imperial Guards stationed inside and outside the Huitong Guesthouse were the first to be withdrawn.","Three days later, the guards stationed at the imperial estate were also reduced by nearly seventy percent.","The steward of the Prince of Qi's manor quietly pushed open the door to Xiao Rongche's bedchamber.","\"Your Highness, Lord Li says you can rest assured. He will deliver the potatoes to the manor in three days.\"","Xiao Rongche clenched his fists, his throat trembling as he exhaled.","\"At a time like this, only my uncle is still willing to help me.\"","The steward comforted him, \"Don't lose heart, Your Highness. The days ahead are long; we can take our time to plan.\"","Darkness fell especially early in winter. By the time Qu Ya returned home from the farm, he could barely see the road.","Fortunately, there was snow all around. Even though there was no moon in the sky, the snow reflected a faint black-and-white glow.","Guan Nianshan asked as they walked, his voice laced with concern.","\"Has your boy recovered from his illness? I haven't seen him come out these past few days.\"","The snow on the ground froze his feet, but Qu Ya's heart felt warm.","\"He's already better after taking the medicine prescribed by the Second Miss of the Song family. It's just been so cold lately, and his mother is worried, so she wants the child to rest for a couple more days.\"","Guan Nianshan breathed a sigh of relief. \"As long as he's recovered, that's what matters. The weather will only get colder now that winter is here. We can't let him catch a chill again.\"","Qu Ya blew hot air into his dry, red, and frozen hands.","\"A few days ago, I asked Steward Chen to buy a new quilt, and we've hoarded more charcoal this year. We won't freeze this winter.\"","Guan Nianshan nodded in cheerful agreement. \"My wife also bought a lot of charcoal. Every household has made some silver this year, so we can finally have a good New Year.\"","The large tree by the ditch not far away looked incredibly lonely against the backdrop of the dark night. Its towering canopy and branches seemed to pierce right into the sky.","A gust of cold wind blew past, sending the snow on the leaves cascading down. The sudden icy touch on his bare neck made Huo Chong quickly brush it away with his hand.","Just as Qu Ya and Guan Nianshan walked beneath the big tree, a bird's nest dropped right in front of them with a smack.","\"Ah!\" Unable to pull back his foot in time, Guan Nianshan stepped on it. The twigs slipped, and he instantly fell backward.","Qu Ya immediately reached out to grab his arm, planting his feet firmly on the ground to support him.","After steadying himself, Guan Nianshan patted his chest in relief. \"Thank goodness I didn't fall. I only have this one set of padded clothes. If it got dirty, I'd have nothing to wear tomorrow.\"","Qu Ya didn't respond; he raised his head and looked up into the tree.","The branches and leaves were clustered together, forming nothing but a dark mass. Yet, he felt that something was not quite right in the darkest spot in the center.","There was not a single gap, making it look as if a person was standing there.","\"Wait for me a moment.\"","Qu Ya picked up a frozen, hard clod of dirt from the ground and threw it at the dark silhouette in the tree.","The dirt clod hit clothing. Huo Chong gripped the tree trunk tightly and looked down. He was discovered so quickly!","Spotting something resembling a head moving, Qu Ya and Guan Nianshan instantly became alert.","\"Who's there?\" the two demanded sternly. \"If you don't come down right now, I'll stone you to death.\"","\"Don't throw anything. Uncle Qu, Uncle Guan, it's me.\"","The sealed memories in their minds were unlocked by this familiar address.","Qu Ya and Guan Nianshan suddenly froze in place, looking as if they had lost their souls. It was as if time had stopped at this very moment.","Huo Chong pushed off with his legs and jumped down from the tree. He walked up to the two men and said softly, \"It's been over twenty years. I wonder if Uncle Qu and Uncle Guan still remember me?\"","The dark night made it impossible to see his face clearly, but the two could tell that Huo Chong was wearing a mask.","Qu Ya's hand, hanging by his side, trembled uncontrollably. His throat felt as if it were blocked by something, and his mouth opened and closed, unable to form words.","Instead, Guan Nianshan was calmer than him.","He asked uncertainly, \"Young Master?\"","Huo Chong's eyes reddened slightly. \"I remember that later on, Uncle Guan always called me Xiaofeng.\"","This time, not only were Huo Chong's eyes red, but Qu Ya and Guan Nianshan's eyes also grew red.","The two men immediately grabbed Huo Chong's arms, one on the left and one on the right, dragging him forward until they entered the most secluded and deserted thatched cottage before letting go."]},{"number":333,"title":"Chapter 333: Reunion After More Than Twenty Years, the Son of My Former Master","paragraphs":["Qu Ya reached into the dark under the straw pile and pulled out a candle and a fire starter.","The moment the candlelight flickered on, his and Guan Nianshan's eyes were entirely focused on Huo Chong's face.","Seeing the mask, the two exchanged a glance, hesitating for a moment.","Seeing this, Huo Chong smiled calmly and took off his mask.","\"During the exile, we encountered a landslide. I was crushed under the rocks for four days. By the time I was rescued, my face had already been ruined.\"","Qu Ya and Guan Nianshan stared blankly at the disfigured upper half of his face. The bitterness in their hearts felt even worse than when their own fingers were severed or their eyes blinded.","This was the Marquis's most precious youngest son. They had even held him a couple of times right after he was born.","Qu Ya choked up, shaking his head with a low voice, \"It doesn't matter if your face is ruined, as long as you're alive.\"","Guan Nianshan pulled over a straw mat for Huo Chong to sit on.","\"Not having seen the young master return for over twenty years, Qu Ya and I thought you were dead.\"","Huo Chong put the mask back on and sat on the straw mat with a bitter smile.","\"All these years, I have been serving as a general under the Ningzhou Pacification Commissioner, Mu Ji'an. If I hadn't taken the opportunity to enter the capital while escorting the Prince of Qi, I wouldn't know when I'd ever get to see you two uncles.\"","Staring at the lower half of Huo Chong's face exposed outside the mask, looking closely, there was still some resemblance to the old Marquis.","Qu Ya wiped the tears from the corners of his eyes with his hand.","\"You were only eight when the Chen family was exiled. Word came back that you all encountered a landslide and no one survived. At that time, Old Guan and I deeply regretted letting you go to the Chen family. Keeping you by our side would have been better than letting you lose your life.\"","Guan Nianshan asked, \"How did the young master end up serving under the foreign tribes in the southwest? What exactly happened on the road to exile back then?\"","The memories buried deep in his mind were dug up. Huo Chong's pupils dilated slightly as his thoughts drifted back to the past.","\"After entering the southwestern territory back then, it rained heavily for several days straight. While we were resting at night, the earth shook and the mountains trembled. Rocks smashed onto my head, and by the time I woke up, several days had passed. It was Third Uncle Chen who saved me.\"","\"He was left with a crippled leg, and my face was disfigured. Later, we lived incognito in the mountains outside a small city in Ningzhou.\"","\"Third Uncle Chen was afraid I would forget the past, so he talked to me about my father and the Chen family every day, and even drew portraits of you all so I would remember.\"","\"Five years later, Third Uncle Chen died of illness. When I went down the mountain to exchange for grain in the village, I was surrounded by bandits and nearly lost my life. It was Commissioner Mu who saved me. Seeing that I knew some martial arts, he brought me into the military camp, and I have been working under him ever since.\"","\"The southwest is thousands of miles away from the capital, and I couldn't leave Ningzhou. Plus, having not made a name for myself, I didn't have the face to come back and see you. Before I knew it, so many years had passed.\"","Qu Ya frowned and asked anxiously, \"The Yang clan of Panzhou and the Mu clan of Ningzhou have had many conflicts over the years. Back then, Zeng Qing took the Yuecheng Army to seek refuge in Panzhou. Have you ever been in contact with him?\"","Huo Chong shook his head and said with a heavy expression, \"In my third year in the military camp, the Mu clan and the Yang clan had a conflict in the Zhang River region. I saw General Zeng from a distance once, but I never saw him again after that.\"","\"Although Panzhou took in the Yuecheng Army, they were ultimately not their own people. The Yang clan ordered Zeng Qing to lead the Yuecheng Army to help clear out the minority tribes near Panzhou. After years of fighting campaigns north and south, more than half of them were killed or wounded.\"","\"I heard that Zeng Qing is now retiring in Panzhou, and the remaining Yuecheng Army has been handed over to his son, though they have almost completely merged with the Panzhou Army.\"","Qu Ya and Guan Nianshan exchanged a glance.","Time flew by. During the more than twenty years they had hidden in the manor, many things had changed.","Recalling the hatred and grievances of the past, they still held resentment in their hearts, but it seemed they could no longer do anything about it.","The token hidden against his chest was still hard, but just as cold.","After a moment of silence, Qu Ya pulled open his collar and forcefully tore the inner pocket of his undergarment. The pure gold token reflected a red glow under the candlelight.","Qu Ya's intact left hand stroked the token a couple of times. Then, taking a deep breath, he handed the token to Huo Chong.","\"This is the commander's token of the Wu Family Army. Seeing it is like seeing the Marquis. I have kept it for all these years waiting for your return. Now, returning it to its rightful owner, I hope it can still be of use.\"","Taking the token, Huo Chong felt it was as heavy as a thousand pounds.","His father's face in his memory had blurred to the point of being unrecognizable, yet this token was something he had always carried with him.","Seeing the token handed over by Qu Ya, half the heavy burden in Guan Nianshan's heart was also lifted.","\"Those who once served in the Wu Family Army in the past will more or less remember the old Marquis's past kindness when they see this token. Especially the Yuecheng Army. Since Zeng Qing is still alive, if the young master wishes to do anything, he will definitely help you.\"","Huo Chong solemnly tucked the token into his robes.","\"I only hope that one day I can personally lead troops to attack the capital, chop off Xiao Chengjing's dog head, and avenge the Wu and Chen families as well as the fallen soldiers of the Wu Family Army. Then my life will be complete.\"","Qu Ya lowered his head.","Attacking the capital, killing the emperor.","It was easy to say, but how could it be easy to do.","Although they never left the manor, they had more or less heard about the affairs of the outside world.","The Mu clan, unable to defeat the Yang clan, sought help from the imperial court. If the young master were in the Panzhou Army, there might still be hope, but since he was in the Ningzhou Army, uniting the foreign tribes of the southwest would be highly difficult.","After putting away the token, Huo Chong looked up at Qu Ya and Guan Nianshan.","He spoke earnestly, \"Returning this time, I also want to take Uncle Qu and Uncle Guan to the southwest. Once you get there, you won't have to keep hiding anymore, and you will never have to worry about your lives again.\"","Qu Ya and Guan Nianshan both paused at the same time.","At first, when Chancellor Chen arranged for them to stay at the manor, they had thought about leaving, but at that time they had nowhere to run.","Now, both of them had long since married and had children. Suddenly hearing that Huo Chong wanted to take them away, they momentarily didn't know what to do.","After some careful consideration, their eyes met, and they already had an answer in their hearts.","Qu Ya spread out his right hand, missing three fingers. \"Young master, my right hand can't hold a sword. If I go to the southwest, I would only be a burden.\"","Guan Nianshan echoed, \"Now we have wives and children at home. Even if we could bring them all along, there are still over two hundred people in the manor. Most of them have physical disabilities far more severe than Qu Ya's and mine. They also have families. We can't abandon them and leave on our own, so we won't be going to the southwest.\"","Huo Chong frowned in a dilemma.","\"If you stay in the capital, you will have to hide for the rest of your lives. If you go to the southwest, you will be free.\"","Qu Ya said in a calm tone, \"The oldest among us is sixty-one, and the youngest is forty-nine. We have already hidden for twenty-five years. Hiding for another twenty or thirty years, our lives will probably be at their end anyway. Besides, even if we could go out, the others wouldn't be willing to.\"","Huo Chong recalled the man crawling on the ground when he was peeking around the farmstead during the day, and for a moment his chest felt tight.","To think that back in the day, these men had also wielded weapons and galloped across the battlefield, yet now they could only drag their crippled bodies and live with heavy burdens.","He thought of the horrified and disgusted expressions of outsiders when he took off his mask.","If the same deformities were on him, he probably wouldn't want to go out and see people either.","That humiliating feeling of having one's dignity trampled upon truly made life worse than death."]},{"number":334,"title":"Chapter 334: Being Found","paragraphs":["\"Who's in there?\"","Seeing a light shining from the unoccupied thatched cottage, Lan Xi, who had come out for a walk to relieve his boredom, called out loudly.","The pupils of the three people who were talking shrank, and the hairs all over their bodies stood on end.","As the footsteps grew closer, Qu Ya reached out to signal Huo Chong not to move.","\"I'll go out and deal with it. Old Guan, hurry up and hide the young master.\"","Guan Nianshan stood up and looked around the bare thatched cottage.","In such a small place, where could they hide someone!","His eyes happened to fall on a pile of straw in the corner, and he immediately walked over and picked up the straw.","\"Young Master, lie down quickly. I'll cover you with the straw.\"","Through the bamboo door, Huo Chong saw Qu Ya and Lan Xi interacting. Gripping his sword tightly, he lay down in the pile of straw.","After walking up and finding it was Qu Ya, Lan Xi raised his eyebrows in confusion.","\"What are you doing here? Why didn't you go home after work?\"","This thatched cottage was not in the same direction as the Qu family's home.","Qu Ya smiled and lied to explain, \"The weather is getting colder. Guan Nianshan and I came here to get some straw to put on our beds so it'll be warmer sleeping at night.\"","Listening intently, Guan Nianshan hid Huo Chong well, then picked up a bundle of straw stalks himself and walked out.","He took the initiative, speaking as if making casual conversation.","\"Steward Lan, why are you here at this hour? Have you eaten? How about coming to my house for a bite?\"","Lan Xi waved his hand. \"I just finished eating and came out for a walk to digest. If you're done, why didn't you put out the candle? It's full of straw stalks inside, be careful of starting a fire.\"","Saying that, he was about to enter the house.","Qu Ya decisively reached out to stop him.","\"There's no need for Steward Lan to bother with such a small matter. I'll go put it out. It just so happens I haven't brought my straw stalks out yet.\"","Hearing the feigned flattery in the other party's tone, and as the candle was brought out, the slightly stiff smile on Guan Nianshan's face also caught Lan Xi's attention.","Something was wrong with these two people. They didn't usually have this attitude towards him.","\"It's dark and hard to see the road. Steward Lan, we'll walk you back.\"","The sky had completely darkened. If it weren't for the white light reflected from the snow, it would truly be pitch black.","Lan Xi put his hands behind his back, his feet planted firmly on the spot.","\"No need. I still want to walk around outside. You guys go back first.\"","Qu Ya and Guan Nianshan felt a little panicked.","If Steward Lan didn't leave, how could Huo Chong come out?","Guan Nianshan spoke with feigned concern, \"It's cold at night, and it might snow later. Steward Lan, you should go back early to avoid catching a chill.\"","Lan Xi replied, \"I'm wearing a lot, so I'm not afraid of the cold. On the contrary, you two are dressed very thinly. The weather will be even colder tomorrow, so remember to put on more clothes.\"","It would be strange to keep talking, so Guan Nianshan smiled and said, \"Then Qu Ya and I will leave first. Steward Lan, you should also head back early.\"","Lan Xi nodded and watched the two leave, the corner of his eye constantly paying attention to the bamboo fence door of the thatched cottage.","Qu Ya and Guan Nianshan walked side by side, looking back every few steps.","Seeing that Lan Xi was taking his time to leave, the two were extremely anxious, terrified that Lan Xi would discover Huo Chong's presence.","After walking far away, Qu Ya blew out the candle and pulled Guan Nianshan to hide behind a tree.","\"Don't move, let's keep watching.\"","Once their shadows disappeared from sight, Lan Xi took out a fire stick from his pocket and walked toward the thatched cottage.","Hiding in the pile of straw, Huo Chong gripped his sword even tighter upon hearing someone approaching.","Seeing a gleam of light enter the thatched cottage, the hearts of Qu Ya and Guan Nianshan, who were hiding behind the large tree, almost stopped from fright.","\"Oh no, the young master is going to be discovered.\" Guan Nianshan was about to rush over immediately.","Qu Ya quickly stopped him. \"Don't move. The light from the fire stick is too dim, he might not notice.\"","Walking into the thatched cottage, there was nothing but the pile of straw in the corner.","Lan Xi hunched over and took a couple of steps inside the room.","He blew on the fire stick to make the light brighter and noticed a dark piece of fabric sticking out of the straw.","The surroundings were so quiet that he could only hear his own breathing.","\"I've already found you. Come out.\"","The voice reached Huo Chong's ears, and the vigilance accumulated in his eyes instantly turned into murderous intent.","He suddenly drew his sword and attacked Lan Xi.","The sound of the longsword being unsheathed was particularly distinct in the dark night. Lan Xi quickly threw the fire stick in his hand at the opponent, then swiftly drew the dagger tucked in his waist to block.","Sparks fell on the pile of straw, and it quickly caught fire.","The sound of clashing weapons coupled with the growing firelight made Qu Ya and Guan Nianshan immediately realize that Huo Chong had been discovered and was already fighting with Lan Xi.","\"Let's go, quick.\"","The two threw the straw stalks in their hands onto the ground and rushed toward the thatched cottage at top speed.","The rising flames illuminated the surroundings brighter and brighter. Seeing that the opponent was wearing a mask, Lan Xi's doubts deepened.","What was the relationship between this man and Qu Ya and Guan Nianshan?","\"Who are you, and what are you doing here?\"","Set against the mask, the murderous intent in Huo Chong's eyes grew even stronger.","\"It's useless for a dead man to know this. Just consider yourself unlucky today.\"","His identity could not be exposed, and the identity of the Wu Army on the estate absolutely could not be revealed. This person had to die.","The force in the opponent's hands noticeably increased. Lan Xi gripped his dagger with both hands and struggled to parry forward.","Huo Chong bent his legs and swiftly leaned back to avoid it.","The blade scraped across the mask, and the two swapped positions before clashing together once again.","Just at this moment, Qu Ya and Guan Nianshan pushed open the bamboo door and rushed in.","Seeing the flames rising from the straw pile growing larger, Guan Nianshan quickly rushed over and pulled the unburnt straw stalks to the side.","This was to prevent the fire from getting too big, burning down the house, and attracting others.","Meanwhile, Qu Ya rushed between the two, using a bamboo stick to disrupt their attacking rhythm.","\"Stop fighting, it's all a misunderstanding. We are all on the same side.\"","Hearing him say this, Huo Chong took a step back and asked, \"Uncle Qu, you say he's on our side?\"","So young, could he be the son of someone in the Wu Army?","Lan Xi, whose arm had been slashed by the sword, sternly questioned, \"Qu Ya, what do you mean? Who exactly is he?\"","This man was at least twenty-five years old, and his martial arts and footwork didn't resemble those of the Qingshuang Cult. He was definitely not among the guards trained by the Princess.","Qu Ya shielded Huo Chong behind him and whispered a sentence to him.","\"This person cannot be touched. I'll explain it to you later.\"","After saying that, he turned to Lan Xi and said, \"Steward Lan, he is a distant relative of mine and Old Guan. He's just staying here for the night and will leave tomorrow. He means no harm.\"","Lan Xi's brows locked tightly. \"Do you take me for a fool? Would a distant relative need to hide, and then try to kill someone when discovered? Who exactly is he?\"","This person was so dangerous, and Qu Ya and Guan Nianshan were very close to him. There was definitely a problem.","The expression on Qu Ya's face became very serious.","\"Steward Lan, when the Princess first took over Daohua Estate and Shiquan Estate, she had a private talk with the two stewards, and she certainly didn't tell you the contents of that conversation.\"","\"Feel free to tell the Princess what happened today. If she asks, Old Guan and I can explain.\"","Recalling the suspicions Song Jinzhao had towards the tenant farmers when she first took over the estate, which ultimately resulted in nothing, Lan Xi's heart began to waver.","Judging from their brief exchange just now, this person's martial arts skills were very high, and it was highly likely he couldn't beat him.","Now with Qu Ya and Guan Nianshan helping him, continuing to fight would only put himself at a disadvantage. He might even lose his life.","The most pressing matter right now is to uncover this person's identity. Whether the Young Miss knows or not, she must be informed immediately."]},{"number":335,"title":"Chapter 335: Can't Kill Him, Song Jinzhao Knows Our Identities","paragraphs":["After a moment of stalemate, Lan Xi spoke solemnly, \"I will definitely confirm today's matter with the County Princess. What is his name?\"","Unable to reveal Huo Chong's true identity, Qu Ya casually made one up.","\"His surname is Gou. He is the son of a deceased old friend of Old Guan and me. Just tell the County Princess and she will understand.\"","Song Jinzhao knew their identities. Mentioning a deceased old friend would most likely make her think that Huo Chong was the son of some soldier from the Wu family army, and this matter could be glossed over.","Lan Xi tightly gripped his dagger and backed out of the thatched cottage.","After he had gone far, a bewildered Huo Chong immediately asked the two, \"What do you mean 'one of our own'? It didn't sound like it just now.\"","Guan Nianshan's eyebrows knitted together like a tangled mess of hemp that couldn't be untied.","\"Manager Lan is County Princess Linghui's man. He cannot die on the estate, nor can he even go missing.\"","\"Why?\" Huo Chong's face was full of confusion.","Guan Nianshan answered in a deep voice, \"Because once someone has an accident on the estate, the County Princess will be the first to suspect us, and it will implicate everyone else on the estate.\"","Qu Ya explained, \"Back when the Emperor bestowed the Daohua Estate and Shiquan Estate to County Princess Linghui, she had already discovered our identities.\"","\"Perhaps out of pity, she didn't inform the imperial court, nor did she drive us away. Later, she opened a farm and planted flower fields, even hiring us to work for her. Everyone's lives are much better now than before, so no matter what, Manager Lan cannot be killed.\"","Hearing that Qu Ya and Guan Nianshan had already been exposed, Huo Chong's eyes widened larger than a bull's.","Seeing him stay silent, Guan Nianshan took over and continued, \"Since the County Princess chose to hide it, even if Manager Lan tells her about this matter tomorrow, she will pretend not to know. But once a murder occurs, things will blow up.\"","\"The County Princess would also suspect your identity. After all, killing someone over something that was tacitly accepted long ago just doesn't make sense no matter how you think about it.\"","Qu Ya lowered his head and cupped his hands. \"A while ago, when my son was sick, it was Manager Lan who begged Second Miss Song to come and treat him so he could recover. In terms of both reason and emotion, I couldn't just watch him die. Please forgive me, Young Master.\"","Huo Chong quickly shook his head and reached out to help him up.","\"I didn't know about these things, which is why I acted so rashly. According to what you said, if I had really killed him, I would have caused a massive disaster.\"","After entering the capital, he had heard of this County Princess Linghui.","Someone who could overshadow all the military generals of the Dongzhao Kingdom at a birthday banquet and defeat Gong Linjue was definitely not someone to be trifled with.","It would have been one thing if she didn't know Qu Ya and the others' identities, but since she knew, they couldn't afford a conflict.","He could leave, but the over two hundred households on the estate could not. Once exposed, everyone would die.","\"I've only been in the capital for a few days and haven't met this County Princess yet. What kind of person is she?\"","Knowing oneself and one's enemy ensures victory in a hundred battles. He had to be prepared in case they crossed paths.","Qu Ya pondered for a moment before speaking, \"To rise from a commoner to a County Princess in just five short years, she is a very extraordinary woman.\"","Guan Nianshan counted on his fingers, \"Song Jinzhao has exquisite medical skills, superb martial arts, and she also knows how to do business.\"","\"She is very smart and quite bold. However, she doesn't come to the estate often, so we aren't entirely clear about her temperament.\"","Seeing the two full of praise for Song Jinzhao, Huo Chong's heart was filled with a lot of curiosity in addition to his worry.","He would have to take a peek at her another day. At the very least, he needed to know what this incredibly capable woman they spoke of looked like.","It was getting late and the city gates were closed. Lan Xi stayed awake all night and rode away from the estate early the next morning.","Staring at his gradually receding figure, Qu Ya said to Huo Chong, \"If the Young Master has no other business, it would be best to return to the Southwest early.\"","Guan Nianshan added, \"The County Princess might call the two managers in for questioning. Qu Ya and I need to go and brief them.\"","Huo Chong nodded. \"I will leave once I'm sure you guys are alright.\"","With his face wrapped, Lan Xi hurried back to the County Princess's mansion.","As soon as he entered, he asked a maid, \"Is the County Princess awake?\"","The maid holding a copper basin stopped in her tracks and nodded at Lan Xi. \"She just got up and is preparing to have breakfast.\"","Lan Xi turned sideways and quickly walked towards the main courtyard.","Hearing a series of rapid footsteps approaching, Song Jinzhao looked up towards the door.","Seeing Lan Xi walking over with the wind in his steps, she slowly put down the porcelain bowl of milk in her hands.","\"Lan Xi? When did you get back?\" Song Shixue looked at the door in surprise, still holding half an unchewed wonton in her mouth.","He hadn't been here yesterday.","Lan Xi stepped over the threshold and bowed to the three masters sitting on stools eating breakfast.","\"This servant just returned. I have an urgent matter to report to the County Princess.\"","Song Jinzhao took the handkerchief handed by a maid and wiped her mouth. \"To the study.\"","Lan Xi kept his back bent and immediately followed.","Seeing Song Shixue constantly looking at the door instead of eating, Song Anhao, who was holding half a tea egg, urged, \"Second Sister, hurry up and eat. You promised to take me to the academy today.\"","Snapping out of her thoughts, Song Shixue hurriedly replied, \"There are only a few left. I'll be done eating right away.\"","She picked up her spoon and quickly ate the remaining three wontons in her bowl.","\"Finished eating. I'll take you.\"","Not expecting her to be so fast, Song Anhao climbed down from the chair while stuffing the remaining bit of egg white into his mouth.","\"Yao Ying, quickly go to the kitchen and grab the tea eggs. Remember to pour a little bit of the broth over them.\"","Song Shixue, who was tying her cloak, asked in confusion, \"Why are you bringing tea eggs? If you're not full, just eat a few more bites. We have plenty of time anyway.\"","Song Anhao shook his head and explained, \"I'm full. The tea eggs are for Dongfang You. He said our family's tea eggs are delicious and insisted I bring some for him.\"","Dongfang You was the youngest grandson of the Dongfang family's second branch, and also Song Anhao's best friend at the academy.","Song Shixue blinked. \"Then remember to wrap the lunchbox holding the eggs with a cotton cloth, so they don't get cold and taste bad later.\"","Song Anhao put on a velvet hat that completely covered his cheeks and ears, and said in a milky voice, \"There's a charcoal basin in the academy. If they get cold, I can heat them up on it.\"","Inside the study, Lan Xi stood before the desk and carefully recounted everything that had happened last night to Song Jinzhao.","\"That man possessed extraordinary skills. This lowly one was no match for him.\"","\"He looked to be around thirty years old. He wore a mask over the upper half of his face, and since it was night, I couldn't really see his appearance clearly.\"","Tapping her fingertips on the desk, Song Jinzhao thoughtfully lowered her eyes.","Could there still be surviving members of the Wu family army who were not on the estate?","If it was a descendant, why would he go to the estate to look for people?","\"What was Qu Ya and Guan Nianshan's attitude toward him?\"","Lan Xi tilted his head up at a forty-five-degree angle, recalling Qu Ya and Guan Nianshan's reactions from the previous night.","After a long while, he said hesitantly, \"They were very protective of that man, and their attitude carried a trace of respect. They shouldn't be relatives or friends.\"","Seeing Song Jinzhao deep in thought and silent, Lan Xi couldn't suppress his curiosity. After struggling with himself for a long time, he finally asked.","\"County Princess, what exactly is going on with those tenant farmers on the estate? Who are they?\"","Song Jinzhao looked up at Lan Xi, her gaze fixed unblinkingly on him.","\"The diplomatic mission from the Shuobei Kingdom has already left. Who exactly are you?\""]},{"number":336,"title":"Chapter 336: Lanxi's identity is the Fourth Prince of Shuobei Kingdom","paragraphs":["Lanxi opened his mouth in astonishment, the color slowly draining from his face.","Song Jinzhao's sudden question had caught him off guard and terrified him.","\"My Lady, what are you talking about? This servant doesn't quite understand.\" Terrified of being exposed, his tongue trembled slightly as he spoke.","Unlike facing Song Shixue, lying to Song Jinzhao made Lanxi feel far more afraid.","During these few seconds of standoff, his heart was about to leap out of his throat.","Song Jinzhao stood up and stared at him.","\"Ever since the diplomatic mission from the Shuobei Kingdom entered the capital, you started giving yourself away.\"","\"Normally, you'd rather stay in the manor every day and never leave. Asking you to work at the estate was like asking for your life. Yet this time, not only did you volunteer, but you also stayed away for more than half a month.\"","Lanxi's eyes darted around as he stammered an explanation.","\"That is because the estate was busy. This servant wanted to perform well to earn a bit more reward money for the New Year.\"","Song Jinzhao curled her lips into a playful chuckle.","\"Could it be busier than before the perfume shop opened? Back then, you didn't even have enough time to sleep, yet you still managed to come back every few days.\"","\"The moment you heard the word 'mission,' you reacted like a startled hedgehog. Shixue saw right through it at a glance.\"","\"Now that they have left, and considering you are a member of my County Princess Manor, you must let me know what is going on, lest I fail to protect you when things come to light later.\"","Hearing this, Lanxi shuddered violently. He had not expected Song Jinzhao to say such a thing.","When she first bought him from the human trafficker, she was clearly reluctant.","If the Second Miss and the Young Master hadn't liked his blue eyes, she definitely wouldn't have bought him.","Seeing that he had not completely dropped his guard, Song Jinzhao shifted the topic to Qu Ya and the others.","\"Those physically disabled men at the estate were soldiers of the Wu Family Army over twenty years ago. Marquis Wuying was defeated and branded with the crime of treason, perhaps also dragged down by the struggle for the throne.\"","\"The current Emperor decreed that they all be executed. Chen Yan, the former Prime Minister of the Dongzhao Kingdom, was a close friend of Marquis Wuying. Unable to bear it, he saved them all and hid them at the estate.\"","\"The man you met yesterday should also be connected to the Wu Family Army.\"","Lanxi's thoughts began to be led along.","He couldn't help but think to himself: If the County Princess is willing to protect people the Emperor of Dongzhao wants to kill, then would it be fine for him too?","Song Jinzhao changed her tone and brought the topic back to Lanxi.","\"Once the seed of doubt is planted, I cannot fully trust and rely on you.\"","\"As long as you are not at fault, have committed no evil, and can guarantee that the Song family will not be implicated, I will naturally protect you.\"","\"Or, just like facing those innocent tenant farmers at the estate, I will choose to turn a blind eye.\"","Lanxi's hands, hanging by his waist, nervously clenched into fists and rubbed together.","Without trust and reliance, wouldn't he eventually have to leave the Song family after a while?","Just as she was about to lead Song Anhao out of the courtyard, Song Shixue turned back and ran to the study door.","Seeing this, Qingshuang first knocked on the door, then pushed it open.","Song Shixue stepped over the threshold with both feet and stopped, her gaze sweeping past Lanxi's face to land on Song Jinzhao.","\"Sister, I'm going to take Anhao to the Dongfang family for school. I'll be back soon.\"","A faint smile hung on Song Jinzhao's lips, and she nodded gently.","\"Go ahead. It's cold outside, so come back early.\"","Song Shixue nodded slightly, turned, and walked out of the study without looking at Lanxi again.","Noticing Song Shixue's somewhat cold profile as she left, Lanxi's heart sank to the bottom of a cliff.","He recalled the scene when Song Shixue went to the estate to treat Qu Ya's son and later left without a word.","She must have known he was lying back then and gotten angry, and she was still angry now.","The study door was once again closed from the outside by Qingshuang.","The room was deathly quiet. Outside the window, an icicle hanging from the eaves suddenly snapped and smashed onto the ground. The sharp crack seemed to strike right at the tip of Lanxi's heart.","He squeezed his eyes shut, took a deep breath, and when he opened them again, his eyes were filled with resolve.","\"Actually, my original name is He Mingjue.\"","The gentle expression on Song Jinzhao's face instantly vanished. He was the royal surname of the Shuobei Kingdom.","\"What is your relationship with the current Emperor of Shuobei, He Mingyuan?\"","Lanxi's heart pounded nervously. \"He is my third brother. I am the Fourth Prince of the Shuobei Kingdom.\"","Song Jinzhao blinked. This matter was much bigger than she had imagined. \"Go on.\"","\"Why did you appear in Anyang Prefecture?\"","\"Were the injuries on your body caused by Gong Linjue's men? Why?\"","Lanxi gritted his teeth, a touch of sorrow appearing on his face.","\"My mother was from the Dongzhao Kingdom. Not long after she gave birth to me, she contracted an illness and died.\"","\"No one in the palace liked me. Even my imperial father looked at my eyes with utter disgust. He threw me into the most remote palace in the imperial grounds, right next to the cold palace. Every year, I could count the number of times I saw him on one hand. They called me a prince, but in truth, even the eunuchs could bully me.\"","\"I thought my days would just pass by in a blur like that. Who knew that the year the Shuobei Kingdom and Dongzhao Kingdom went to war, He Mingyuan conspired with Gong Linjue to poison our imperial father, and even forged an edict of succession.\"","\"When He Mingnan returned for the funeral, he was also murdered by Gong Linjue. I happened to witness them committing the murder, so I secretly told He Mingnan's mother. As a result, she was killed before she could even send the news out.\"","\"I was so terrified that I secretly hid in a wooden bucket meant for night soil and escaped the palace. They sent people to chase me all the way, forcing me to a cliff. With no other choice, I jumped. Fortunately, I survived the disaster by falling into a river, which saved my life.\"","\"After that, I traveled through the mountains toward the Dongzhao Kingdom. Worried about being discovered, I figured the further away from the border, the better. Eventually, I arrived in Anyang Prefecture, and then I met you, My Lady.\"","Killing his father and murdering his brother—this Third Prince was certainly exceedingly bold.","Willing to bear the title of a good-for-nothing and hide for over twenty years, such a person must have incredibly deep cunning, strong capabilities, and massive ambition. He was exactly cut from the same cloth as Gong Linjue.","Song Jinzhao stared at Lanxi and asked, \"From a prince to a servant, are you resigned to this?\"","Lanxi looked at Song Jinzhao with a serious expression. \"When I was a prince in the past, I never felt my life was better than it is now.\"","\"Compared to the past, I am much more willing to be a servant in the Song Manor. At least I am treated like a human being, I have things to do, and no one calls me a bastard because of my mother's background. I like the present much more than the past.\"","Song Jinzhao remained silent for a long time before speaking. \"In that case, forget the past completely. In the Song Manor, there is no He Mingjue, only Lanxi.\"","His tense muscles completely relaxed at this moment, and Lanxi stared blankly at Song Jinzhao.","He hadn't expected the matter to pass so easily.","The identity that made him tremble with fear and kept him awake night after night was so easily accepted by Song Jinzhao.","It was as if it were just an ordinary, trivial matter, not worth taking to heart at all.","Song Jinzhao said, \"When Shixue comes back, I will tell her about your identity. This matter will remain strictly between the three of us. No one else needs to know.\"","Lanxi widened his eyes, feeling uncertain. \"What about the Eldest Young Master?\"","Song Jinzhao leaned back.","\"The fewer people who know about this, the better. The Shuobei diplomatic mission has already left, so Qiming doesn't need to know.\"","\"Go back to the estate now and bring Chen Fu and Li Hou to me. I still have some questions about what happened yesterday.\"","Lanxi gave a soft nod and drifted toward the door, her mind completely elsewhere. She couldn't shake the feeling that she was walking through a dream."]},{"number":337,"title":"Chapter 337: Song Shixue's Worry","paragraphs":["After dropping her youngest brother off at the Dongfang Manor, Song Shixue hurriedly urged the driver to turn the carriage around and head back.","The moment the carriage stopped, she jumped down and dashed inside.","Reaching the study, she saw that Lan Xi had already left. She walked over to a chair, sat down, and asked, Sister, what did Lan Xi report?","Song Jinzhao finished writing the last character and set down her brush. A small incident occurred at the estate yesterday, but it has been resolved now.","I also managed to ask about Lan Xi's past. Do you want to know?","Song Shixue nodded vigorously, bobbing her head like a chick pecking at grain.","Seeing this, Song Jinzhao let out a faint, barely perceptible sigh.","Fifteen was simply too young. She couldn't even see what was so great about Lan Xi, yet her sister's heart was already fluttering with first love.","Should she pretend not to know, or step in to stop it? She needed to think this over carefully.","After Song Jinzhao explained the entire sequence of events, Song Shixue sat there, pondering for quite a while.","If the Emperor of Shuobei finds out Lan Xi is still alive, wouldn't he be in terrible danger?","Song Jinzhao gave a slight nod.","Murdering his father and brother, forging an imperial decree to usurp the throne—if word gets out, He Mingyuan's hold on the crown will be in jeopardy. Until they find Lan Xi's corpse, they can never be completely at ease. The people of Shuobei might still be searching for him. I'll have someone look into it.","Song Shixue bit her lip, her heart weighed down with worry.","Sister, let's not have Lan Xi go out to work anymore. Let him stay at the estate or within the manor, away from outsiders.","His light blue eyes were certainly beautiful, but they also easily drew attention and left a lasting impression.","It would be far too dangerous if he were unlucky enough to be recognized.","Seeing what Song Shixue was thinking, Song Jinzhao spoke up to comfort her. Lan Xi was never favored in Shuobei. Let alone commoners, even among the officials, very few know him. So as long as he doesn't go to Yandu, he generally won't be recognized.","Song Shixue furrowed her delicate brows. I know, but it still feels like a hidden danger. I just can't stop worrying.","Sister, do you have any way to change a person's appearance, or perhaps change the color of Lan Xi's eyes?","Song Jinzhao was rendered speechless.","In modern times, one could change their eye color with colored contacts, but there were no such things in ancient times, nor could she make them.","Lan Xi's light blue eyes are natural; they cannot be changed.","As for his appearance, we could make a human-skin mask, but everyone in the manor already knows him. Suddenly changing his face would be even stranger.","Song Shixue slumped dejectedly over the table, muttering, If only the Emperor of Shuobei would just drop dead.","Song Jinzhao: ...","By the time Lan Xi rode out of the city, his mood had completely brightened.","Having finally revealed the secret that had weighed on him for so long, even the dark clouds in the sky looked more beautiful than before.","He rode his horse toward the estate, unable to stop smiling as he thought about what had just happened.","Unfortunately, his extreme joy turned to sorrow. Distracted while riding, his horse lost its footing, sending both man and beast tumbling into the nearby snowbank.","Fortunately, the thick snow cushioned the fall, but the impact still jolted him, leaving his head buzzing.","Lan Xi groaned as he scrambled up from the ground. The horse that had fallen into the snow also managed to stand back up.","He circled the horse, feeling completely relieved only when he saw it was unhurt.","Sorry, brother. It was my fault for not paying attention and making you fall. I won't get distracted again.","Its nose tickled by his touch, the fine steed snorted and sneezed, spraying saliva right onto Lan Xi's face, instantly shutting him up.","Disgusted, Lan Xi scooped up a handful of snow and rubbed his face into it. By the time he lifted his head, his face was numb from the freezing cold.","If you don't accept my apology, fine, but why spit on me? I'm docking one of your meals when we get back.","The horse stared at Lan Xi with a gentle expression, its deep, large eyes making him feel a bit guilty.","He grabbed the reins and said, Alright, I won't dock your meal. I'll give you extra food when we get back.","Just as Lan Xi looked down to step into the stirrup, a pale yellow, round object caught his attention.","He reached out and picked it up, surprise flickering in his eyes.","What the horse had stepped on just now was a potato. But why would there be a potato on the road?","Lan Xi let go of the reins and walked further down the road, discovering two more potatoes about the size of eggs, both frozen solid into blocks of ice."]},{"number":338,"title":"Chapter 338: Discovering the Potatoes Were Stolen","paragraphs":["Looking at the two lines of wheel tracks in the snow, Lan Xi pondered for a moment before mounting his horse and riding forward at a slow pace.","One after another, he picked up over a dozen unusually small potatoes. Some were almost completely covered by the white snow, impossible to spot without looking closely.","The wheel tracks disappeared at the intersection, along with horseshoe prints, all turning in from the small path on the left.","Lan Xi gazed into the distant woods; past there lay the imperial estate.","To drop so many along the road meant the carts were fully loaded. Transporting potatoes right after the diplomatic mission had left...","Weren't they supposed to be kept for seeds? Why transport so many at a time like this?","A group of people emerged from behind the woods, seemingly all wearing armor.","Wanting to dispel the doubts in his mind, Lan Xi dismounted and waited by the side of the road, intending to ask them a few questions.","As they drew closer, he could see there were about twenty people.","Two were on horseback while the rest walked. Their armor was exquisitely crafted, unlike that of ordinary soldiers.","From a distance, Chang Shiming noticed a man leading a horse at the intersection, and suspicion inevitably arose in his heart.","He seemed to be looking in their direction. Could it be that the Shuobei State diplomatic mission had left someone behind?","Chang Shiming clamped his legs tightly around his horse's belly, speeding up to reach Lan Xi.","He was just about to ask a question when he noticed the potatoes in Lan Xi's hands. His expression instantly changed.","\"Officers—\" Lan Xi had barely spoken when he saw the leading general draw his sword and swing it at him.","His face paled drastically. He grabbed the longsword hanging from his saddle and began to defend himself.","\"What are you doing? Attacking me for no reason!\"","Blades clashed. Chang Shiming's face was ashen, his dark eyes glaring like Guan Gong.","\"Who gave you the nerve to steal potatoes from the imperial estate? Men, take him down!\"","At his command, the other nineteen soldiers drew their swords in unison, pointing them at Lan Xi and surrounding him.","Hearing the man's words, Lan Xi's mind went blank.","He shouted in disbelief, \"You're making baseless accusations! When did I ever steal potatoes?\"","Chang Shiming lifted his chin, gesturing toward the potatoes that had fallen to the ground when Lan Xi drew his sword.","\"Do you take me for a blind man? If these aren't potatoes, what are they?\"","\"To sneak into the imperial estate to steal, you've got a lot of nerve. Who sent you?\"","Lan Xi glanced down at the potatoes on the ground, then looked back up.","He raised his voice, \"I am a steward from the manor of County Princess Linghui. I picked these potatoes up on the road.\"","Chang Shiming froze. \"A servant from the manor of County Princess Linghui? What are you doing out here in the heavy snow?\"","Lan Xi pointed to the main road on the right. \"I was on my way to our estate and just happened to pass by.\"","\"If I had stolen these potatoes, why would I stand here waiting to be caught when I saw you coming?\"","Seeing no trace of guilt on Lan Xi's face, Chang Shiming gradually calmed down.","The man had a point. If he really had stolen the potatoes, he would have fled the moment he got his hands on them. He wouldn't be standing here waiting to die.","But why would there be potatoes on the road?","Thinking of this, Chang Shiming sheathed his sword. \"Where did you pick them up? Take me there.\"","Seeing this, the others also lowered their weapons.","Lan Xi pointed to the road on the left. \"Just down this road, for about three miles. I followed the wheel tracks all the way here.\"","As he spoke, he untied the cloth bag hanging from his saddle and opened it for the other man to see.","\"I picked all these up. They're frozen solid like blocks of ice.\"","Chang Shiming looked down at his feet. Sure enough, there were two lines of wheel tracks on the ground.","He nervously waved his hand and ordered loudly, \"Search the area! See if there are any more on the ground.\"","Watching these men frantically bending over to search for potatoes in the snow, the doubts in Lan Xi's mind suddenly vanished.","So, the potatoes from the imperial estate had been stolen; they weren't being transported by the Court of the Imperial Stud.","Chang Shiming and his men found many more potatoes along the road—a significant amount.","For a moment, all the imperial guards felt as though the sky had fallen.","The Emperor had ordered them to guard the imperial estate, yet someone had stolen the potatoes right from under their noses. How were they going to explain this?","\"You, take nine men and return to the imperial estate immediately. The remaining nine will follow me along the wheel tracks to find the potatoes.\"","Now that things had come to this, they had to recover the stolen potatoes.","Watching their swift and decisive departure, Lan Xi stood there for a moment in thought. Then, he turned, mounted his horse, and prepared to head back to the city to inform Song Jinzhao first.","Inside the County Princess's manor, Song Jinzhao was sitting on the heated brick bed, discussing medicine with Song Shixue.","Seeing Lan Xi return, one felt surprised while the other felt delighted.","It hadn't been long at all. How had he returned so quickly?","Noticing the snow on his clothes, Song Shixue instinctively looked toward the door. \"It's snowing?\"","Lan Xi nodded. \"It just started when this humble servant entered the city.\"","With that, he cupped his hands toward Song Jinzhao. \"County Princess, the potatoes from the imperial estate have been stolen.\"","Song Jinzhao placed the medical book in her hands onto the table, frowning as she stared at Lan Xi.","\"When? How much was stolen?\"","Lan Xi answered with absolute certainty, \"Just today. At least a cartload.\"","He slowly recounted the entire process of discovering the stolen potatoes, then shared his own thoughts.","\"Although these potatoes were frozen solid, they weren't covered by snow. It started snowing last night but stopped before dawn, so they must have been dropped today. Moreover, the wheel tracks were fresh.\"","Song Jinzhao asked, \"Did you see any wheel tracks when you left the capital this morning?\"","Lan Xi furrowed his brows in frustration. \"This humble servant was in too much of a hurry at the time, and the sky was still a bit dark. I didn't pay attention to whether there were wheel tracks on the ground.\"","At this very moment, about a mile away from the city walls, Chang Shiming stood with his hands on his hips.","He stamped his feet in frustration as he looked at the crisscrossing wheel tracks on the ground.","\"Heading north goes into the city, while heading east or west leads to neighboring cities. We haven't found any potatoes on the ground for a while now. Which road did they take?!\"","The snow was falling heavier now. Everyone's faces were flushed from the freezing cold, and their jaws trembled as they spoke.","\"My Lord, how about we split into three groups? They were driving carts; if they entered the city, the city guards would definitely remember them.\"","Chang Shiming rubbed his freezing face with his hands.","\"Then we'll split into groups of three. The remaining person must return to the palace immediately to report the matter to Commander Fan. This is of grave importance; the Emperor must be informed at once.\"","The nine men replied in unison, \"Yes, sir.\"","Snowflakes drifted into their mouths. Everyone's hearts, along with their backs, were freezing cold.","If they couldn't recover the potatoes, they would be doomed.","Upon learning that the potatoes had been stolen, Fan Guanshan rushed straight to the imperial study to inform the Emperor.","Hearing the news, Xiao Chengjing slammed his wolf-hair writing brush heavily onto the desk, sending ink splattering halfway across the imperial study.","\"Send people to search immediately! You must recover the stolen potatoes.\"","\"The Shuobei State diplomatic mission left only a few days ago, and their people are still within the borders of the Dongzhao Kingdom. This matter is definitely tied to them.\"","\"Summon Wu Jianzheng for an audience at once!\""]},{"number":339,"title":"Chapter 339: The Emperor's Fury, Silencing the Witnesses","paragraphs":["When the imperial eunuch hurried to the Ministry of War with quick, short steps, Wu Jianzheng and other ministry officials were gathered together discussing the court's procurement of warhorses for the coming year.","\"Lord Wu, please stop your discussion. His Majesty urgently summons you to the Imperial Study.\"","Wu Jianzheng immediately stood up from his chair, walked over to the eunuch, and asked in a low voice, \"Eunuch, for what matter has His Majesty summoned me?\"","Seeing the Ministry of War officials behind Wu Jianzheng all stand up and look their way, the imperial eunuch silently led him to the door.","\"The potatoes in the imperial estate were stolen. His Majesty is furious, so you had best be careful, My Lord.\"","Wu Jianzheng's eyes widened in shock. \"Hasn't the diplomatic mission from the Kingdom of Shuobei already left? Who else would steal the potatoes?\"","The imperial eunuch shook his head. \"That, this servant does not know.\"","When Wu Jianzheng and the imperial eunuch walked out of the Ministry of War, they happened to see Fan Guanshan leading the Imperial Guards hurrying past not far away.","Inside the Imperial Study, a palace maid was carefully kneeling on the floor, cleaning up the mess.","Seeing Wu Jianzheng enter, everyone silently retreated to the sides of the pillars, terrified that the Emperor would lose his temper again and bring disaster upon their heads.","\"This humble official greets His Majesty.\"","As soon as Wu Jianzheng knelt down, Xiao Chengjing's questioning voice rang out.","\"Have the people I ordered you to send to track the Shuobei mission sent any letters back?\"","Wu Jianzheng's heart skipped half a beat, and his forehead began to sweat with tension.","\"Replying to His Majesty, there is no news as of yet.\"","Smack! Xiao Chengjing slammed a memorial hard onto the desk. \"They have already been gone for five or six days. Why is there absolutely no news?\"","\"I had barely withdrawn the majority of the Imperial Guards stationed at the imperial estate when someone went and stole from it. This was premeditated. Did the people you sent out not notice anything at all? They must have been discovered by Gong Linjue long ago.\"","Separated by a journey of five or six days, it took time to send messages back. Without having received any news, Wu Jianzheng was completely unable to answer the Emperor's question.","\"The people this humble official sent to track the mission are extremely skilled at hiding and trailing. They shouldn't have been discovered so easily. Perhaps they were delayed because of the snowy weather and slippery roads. There might be news in a few days.\"","Having thrown away the memorial, Xiao Chengjing slapped his palm against the desk, making loud smacking sounds.","\"No matter how skilled they are, can they subdue Gong Linjue? Out of all the civil and military officials, not a single one can, not even comparing to a woman! When war breaks out in the future, who will lead the troops?\"","Kneeling on the ground, Wu Jianzheng kept his head bowed, unable to refute a single word.","The truth was, if it weren't for County Princess Linghui, not only would the Emperor have lost face this time, but the entire Dongzhao Kingdom would have been thoroughly disgraced.","It might have even affected the current situation between the two countries.","If war broke out in the future, the great army would feel fear in their hearts just hearing the three words 'Gong Linjue', and their will to fight would be greatly diminished.","After a moment of heavy silence in the Imperial Study, Xiao Chengjing's anger also slowly subsided.","\"Send people immediately to catch up with the Shuobei mission. This time, remember not to expose your whereabouts. Once the potatoes are found, immediately join forces with the local officials and soldiers to intercept them. The mission can leave, but under no circumstances can they take the potatoes with them.\"","Wu Jianzheng heavily knocked his forehead against the ground. \"This humble official obeys the decree.\"","Inside Prince Qi's Manor, the steward, who had just seen off the imperial physician, heard a subordinate's report and turned to walk towards Xiao Rongche's sleeping quarters.","\"Your Highness, Lord Li sent someone with a message. The matter regarding the potatoes has been discovered, so there is no way to deliver them to the manor.\"","\"However, he asks you to rest assured. All loose ends have been cleaned up, and the potatoes have already been transported to a safe place. You only need to stay in the manor and pretend you know nothing.\"","Xiao Rongche's heart, which had just jumped to his throat, settled halfway down again. \"Are you certain this won't be traced back to me? Not even uncle can be implicated.\"","The steward nodded expressionlessly and made a slicing motion across his neck with his right hand.","\"Everything has been cleaned up.\"","Xiao Rongche took a deep breath, thought for a moment, and then reached out to motion for the steward to come closer.","\"We cannot delay. Go to the Li Manor personally and tell uncle the location for the rendezvous with Gong Linjue, and have him send someone to deliver it.\"","The steward nodded. \"This servant understands. This servant will go do it immediately.\"","If one wanted to know the whereabouts of the stolen potatoes, the best method was to find the people who stole them.","Although seventy percent of the Imperial Guards in the imperial estate had been transferred away, the twenty men led by Chang Shiming were still on the estate before the theft. To steal a cartload of potatoes without anyone noticing, there must have been someone inside the imperial estate working with the thieves from the inside.","Therefore, after leading his troops out of the city, Fan Guanshan rushed to the imperial estate outside the city at the very first opportunity.","As soon as he entered the gates, he smelled a strong stench of blood.","Looking at the two corpses lying on the ground, the faces of the Imperial Guards who followed him in all changed.","\"What happened?\" Fan Guanshan sharply questioned his subordinate.","The general who had split up with Chang Shiming lowered his head, his face full of self-blame.","\"When this subordinate brought people back, I only shouted once before they all drew their swords and slit their own throats. We didn't even have time to ask a single word.\"","Fan Guanshan clenched his fists, his face ashen and his eyes full of anger.","\"Where is everyone else from the Court of Agricultural Affairs? It wasn't just one or two, it was an entire cart of potatoes. Did no one notice?\"","The man lowered his head even further, not daring to look up at all.","\"We truly didn't notice any problems with these two men before. During today's withdrawal, everyone was in the front courtyard. The granary was handed over to the people from the Court of Agricultural Affairs to guard last night. After so many days of peace, no one thought something like this would happen.\"","Dong Yuanbin, who arrived a step late after hearing the news, saw the two corpses laid out on the ground and was immediately so frightened that his legs went weak.","\"What is going on here? Commander Fan, even if they are guilty, you cannot use lynching!\"","Fan Guanshan rolled his eyes at him speechlessly.","\"Lord Dong, with which eye did you see this commander abusing private punishment? These two men committed suicide out of fear of punishment.\"","\"Instead, it is you, Lord Dong, who had such a blunder occur under your command. You had better think carefully about how to explain this to His Majesty.\"","Dong Yuanbin's face turned deathly pale. \"Commander Fan, the Imperial Guards haven't completely withdrawn today. If there is guilt, it does not solely belong to my Court of Agricultural Affairs.\"","\"In my opinion, the best plan is to quickly find the stolen potatoes. Otherwise, when the Emperor's wrath falls, neither you nor I will be able to bear it.\"","Too lazy to waste words with the other party, Fan Guanshan directly issued orders.","\"You, immediately take inventory of the storehouse to see how many potatoes were lost. The rest of you, immediately interrogate everyone staying in the imperial estate. Additionally, dispatch thirty men to go and support Chang Shiming.\""]},{"number":340,"title":"Chapter 340: Find My Car in the Neighboring City","paragraphs":["The snow fell heavier and heavier, gradually covering all the tracks on the official roads and small paths.","Upon arriving at the neighboring city, Chang Shiming asked the yamen runners standing at the city gate, \"How many vehicles have entered today? Count every type of vehicle.\"","Seeing them wearing the exclusive armor and uniforms of the Royal Guards, the yamen runners couldn't help but feel nervous.","What had happened? Why would the Royal Guards come here?","The four of them checked the situation with each other, then sent one person to answer.","\"One horse-drawn carriage, two ox-carts, one donkey-cart, and four hand-pulled flatbed carts.\"","Chang Shiming pressed on, \"What was loaded on the carts?\"","The runner replied, \"The two ox-carts were loaded with charcoal, the donkey-cart had vegetables, and the four flatbed carts were carrying firewood.\"","Chang Shiming frowned. \"Are you sure? Could anything be hidden on them?\"","The four looked at each other and shook their heads in unison.","\"Probably not. They make a trip every few days; they are all familiar faces.\"","Chang Shiming asked, \"What about the horse-drawn carriage? Did you lift the curtain to look inside?\"","The runner shook his head. \"No, we didn't. That was the carriage belonging to Scholar Guo's family in the city. Their old madame just returned from paying respects to their ancestors in their hometown.\"","Chang Shiming's face darkened. \"Where is the Guo family? Take me there immediately.\"","Old Madame Guo, who had just finished a grueling four-month journey and was about to lie down for sleep after a meal, was suddenly informed that the Royal Guards had come to search their carriage.","Scholar Guo, looking bewildered, grabbed his outer robe and rushed to the front hall. \"My lord, what crime has my Guo family committed? You must have a reason for coming to search our premises.\"","Chang Shiming raised a hand to stop him. \"Which carriage did your old madame ride in when she entered the city today? Take me to see it.\"","Scholar Guo's gaze lingered on Chang Shiming for a long time. The Royal Guards were no ordinary soldiers; it was better to endure this.","\"It is in the backyard. I will take you lords there.\"","When they reached the backyard, the snow on the largest carriage had not yet melted.","Scholar Guo gestured with his hand. \"This is the carriage. Please, feel free to inspect it, my lords.\"","Chang Shiming looked at the yamen runner who had followed them.","The man nodded. \"This is the carriage that entered the city halfway through the hour of Chen.\"","Lifting the curtain and stepping into the cabin, he found it very clean, with a faint scent of sandalwood.","There were only a few footprints on the carpet; it didn't look like it had been loaded with potatoes.","Seeing Chang Shiming lift the carpet to inspect underneath, Scholar Guo's doubts grew.","What on earth was going on?","\"Yunlong.\" Old Madame Guo, who had gotten out of bed, was helped down the steps by an older maid.","Scholar Guo hurriedly went over to support her.","\"Mother, why are you up? I can handle things out here. It's cold, go back inside and continue sleeping.\"","Old Madame Guo slowly shook her head. \"The officials have come to our home; how could I possibly sleep? What is going on?\"","After confirming this wasn't the vehicle, Chang Shiming jumped down from the carriage, walked up to Old Madame Guo, and asked politely, \"Old Madame, on your way back to the capital this morning, did you see any carts fully loaded with goods, especially ones that looked sneaky or suspicious?\"","Old Madame Guo replied, \"My lord, I was sitting inside the carriage and couldn't see outside.\"","After speaking, she turned her head and instructed the older maid standing next to her, \"Go and call the driver and all the servants who returned today, so the official can question them properly.\"","Before long, the backyard was filled with people, about twenty of them at a glance.","After some questioning, everyone shook their heads. \"We didn't see any carts, only a few pedestrians.\"","At the back of the crowd, a guard carrying a sword, who had just come out of the latrine, narrowed his eyes.","Just as Chang Shiming and the others were giving up and preparing to leave, the guard raised his hand and spoke up hesitantly in a low voice.","\"My lord, I think I saw something.\"","Instantly, everyone's eyes focused on the guard.","The guard instinctively raised his hand and pointed to the right. \"At the third intersection before entering the city, there is a river nearby. At the time, I think I saw someone driving a carriage along the small path by the river, but I don't know if they are the people you are looking for, my lord.\"","Chang Shiming recalled which intersection the guard was talking about, and after figuring it out, he frowned in confusion.","At that intersection, only the road leading to the city gate had wheel tracks; they had checked the other two paths, and there were no tracks.","There weren't even any footprints or hoofprints.","\"Are you sure you saw it?\"","The guard nodded. \"It had a carriage roof, and there were two people following behind it. I shouldn't be mistaken.\"","Half an hour later, the three men brought the guard to the intersection he had mentioned.","The guard pointed to the most conspicuous towering willow tree on the left. \"Right there. I was riding in front at the time, glanced over, and didn't pay much attention.\"","Chang Shiming and the others crouched down again to observe the small path leading in that direction. They had looked when they passed by earlier, and there were no traces.","Now, with another layer of snow, it was even harder to see anything.","\"Let's go and take a look.\"","Upon arriving at the location the guard pointed out, there were still faint traces of trampling in the snow.","\"My lord, some bushes have been crushed here!\" a Royal Guard shouted at Chang Shiming, holding up a broken branch.","Everyone ran over together. Looking at the obviously crushed bushes, their expressions turned extremely grim.","The people who stole the potatoes hadn't taken the road; they had trampled over the bushes and gone down the steep slope.","\"Commandant Chang, have you found the tracks of the thieves?\" Seeing people by the river, ten Royal Guards who had rushed over to provide backup stopped on the official road and shouted.","Seeing that backup had arrived, Chang Shiming's eyes instantly lit up.","\"Come here, they escaped from this way.\"","After coming down, everyone hurried forward along the small path by the river.","The temperature by the river was even colder than elsewhere. Coupled with the relentless wind and snow, everyone's exposed skin felt as if it were being sliced by knives, painful and freezing, and soon lost all sensation."]},{"number":341,"title":"Chapter 341: Five Dismembered Corpses","paragraphs":["The tracks on the ground were gradually covered completely by the heavy snow. At a glance, the surroundings were a vast expanse of white; there was nothing but the frozen riverbank and an endless forest.","Having not seen a trace of the thieves for a long time, coupled with being cold and hungry, some began to anxiously consider retreating.","\"My Lord, did we go the wrong way?\"","The man's nose was red from the freezing cold.","\"We wasted a lot of time entering the city. They must still be ahead. Keep chasing.\"","Chang Shiming insisted, so the others had no choice but to struggle forward, lifting their feet that were completely soaked by the melting snow.","An unknown amount of time passed before a carriage appeared in the distance before everyone's eyes.","Strangely, the carriage wasn't moving; it was parked in place, completely still.","Even so, everyone couldn't help but shout when they saw it.","The imperial guard walking at the very front pointed at the carriage and yelled, \"There's a carriage ahead!\"","Chang Shiming spurred his horse and rushed over quickly, only to find that there was no one around the carriage.","Lifting the carriage curtain, he saw a lot of dirt debris inside the cabin.","He also found a small potato left behind in the corner of the cabin.","\"My Lord, there are people here!\" A subordinate searching the perimeter pointed at a giant pit ahead and shouted.","Everyone gathered around the giant pit and looked down, only to see five people lying face down at the bottom, motionless, with bloodstains on their clothes.","\"Bring a rope,\" Chang Shiming ordered his subordinates to find tools, while he propped his hands on the ground and jumped down himself.","Turning over the corpse lying on the very top, a bloody, mangled face was revealed to the crowd.","The imperial guards standing by the pit were so frightened they turned and ran, and even Chang Shiming subconsciously recoiled.","After calming down, Chang Shiming successively turned over the other four corpses.","It was exactly the same; the skin on all of their faces had been completely peeled off.","Their throats had been slit, killing them in a single strike. There were no signs of struggle on their bodies, meaning the killer must have been someone they knew.","After hoisting the five corpses up from the bottom of the pit, the crowd looked at Chang Shiming at a loss.","\"My Lord, what do we do now?\"","Chang Shiming looked around. By the desolate winter riverbank, not even a bird could be seen.","\"Deploy more men. Even if we have to turn over every inch of land for dozens of miles around, we must find them.\"","In the freezing weather, the Hanlin Academy finished work early.","The carriage stopped at the entrance of the County Princess's estate. Song Qiming, wearing a cloak, emerged from the cabin.","He walked quickly and anxiously toward the backyard. Hearing laughter coming from inside the room, he unfastened his cloak as he walked and handed it to a servant.","\"Sister.\" His voice arrived before he did.","Song Anhao, who was sitting on the heated kang doing her homework, immediately looked up and called out to her brother.","Song Qiming patted her head and walked into the inner room. \"Sister, the potatoes at the imperial estate were stolen, did you know?\"","Song Shixue, who was grinding medicine, suddenly raised her hand, her eyes shining.","\"I know, Lanxi found out.\"","Song Qiming widened his eyes in astonishment. \"What!\"","Song Jinzhao lifted the teapot resting on the iron grate, poured a cup of steaming milk tea, and handed it to Song Qiming.","\"Lanxi found the dropped potatoes on the way back to the estate. It just so happened that the guards patrolling the imperial estate passed by, so she told them.\"","Song Qiming took the teacup with both hands, warming them while blowing on the tea.","\"I heard a whole cart of potatoes was stolen?\"","Song Jinzhao nodded slightly. \"At least a cart, and it was packed very full, otherwise they wouldn't have dropped so many on the ground.\"","Song Qiming took a sip of the milk tea and frowned from the heat.","\"The Shuobei envoy delegation has been gone from the capital for so many days. Who else would risk targeting the potatoes? They are too bold.\"","Song Jinzhao said calmly, \"Carrying one or two on your person is one thing, but a whole cart is very difficult. The thieves must have an inside connection at the imperial estate.\"","His fingertips burned, Song Qiming looked up at Song Jinzhao, his eyes full of shock.","\"Sister, do you mean someone committed treason?\"","Song Jinzhao analyzed, \"Originally, the Shuobei envoy delegation was supposed to leave next spring, but they suddenly changed their minds and left in a hurry.\"","\"Given Gong Linjue's personality, he wouldn't easily give up on something he wants. Before leaving the capital, he definitely found an ally to do this for him.\"","\"The delegation's departure would make the imperial court relax its guard. Once the security at the imperial estate decreased, their opportunity to steal arrived.\"","Song Qiming stood up and paced back and forth in the room, his mind in a mess.","\"As far as I know, during the time Gong Linjue was in the capital, the imperial estate was completely sealed off—no one could enter or leave. How did Gong Linjue collude with them?\"","\"Furthermore, there were over a hundred imperial guards stationed day and night outside the Huitong guesthouse. Wherever the delegation went, they were followed. How did they make contact?\"","Countless thoughts raced through Song Qiming's mind, and many guesses were dismissed as soon as they surfaced.","After pondering for a moment, Song Jinzhao said, \"With Gong Linjue's martial arts skills, avoiding the imperial guards outside the Huitong guesthouse would be easy. Especially at night, sneaking out wouldn't be difficult.\"","Song Shixue raised her hand and interjected, \"Before, when I bumped into that vice envoy outside the city, he was near the imperial estate. He definitely went to scout it.\"","Song Qiming pinched his chin in thought. \"I remember the vice envoy was struck by lightning before the Emperor's birthday banquet.\"","Song Shixue nodded. \"That was still several days away from the banquet.\"","Song Qiming's eyes lit up in sudden realization.","\"So during that time they were exceptionally well-behaved because they knew there were guards and they couldn't sneak in.\"","Song Jinzhao said with certainty, \"Not only that, but after the banquet, they delayed their departure until after spring, which shows they hadn't figured out a way yet. Later, when they had a plan, they found an excuse to leave. In the few days in between, Gong Linjue definitely met with someone.\""]},{"number":342,"title":"Chapter 342: House Raid, Confession","paragraphs":["The bodies were carried to the Ministry of Justice. After the coroner's autopsy, the findings were exactly the same as Chang Shiming's assessment.","Their carotid arteries had been severed. In addition to their facial skin being peeled off, one of the men had also had his nose sliced off.","The coroner reported, \"These five men are all around thirty years old. Judging by the thick calluses on their hands, they were all martial artists.\"","With that, he walked over to the corpse on the far right, pointed at its left hand, and continued, \"What is worth noting is that his calluses are all on his left hand. He was left-handed.\"","Fan Guanshan inspected each body. The killer had struck decisively, leaving almost no evidence behind.","\"Besides this, are there any other clues on the bodies that could help us identify them?\"","The coroner shook his head. \"Aside from a few moles, there are no special markings. The blade used to pierce their eyes was also very ordinary, the kind you could buy at any blacksmith shop.\"","Fan Guanshan took a deep breath.","This meant that trying to identify these men starting from their corpses would be extremely difficult.","After pondering for a moment, Fan Guanshan rode his horse back to the palace to report the situation to the Emperor.","Xiao Chengjing's face suddenly darkened as he slammed his hand on the table and stood up.","\"Colluding with the enemy and betraying the country is an unforgivable crime!\"","\"Throw the entire Sang and Gou families into the imperial prison. Torture them severely. If they don't reveal the mastermind behind this, execute them all.\"","Fan Guanshan knelt on one knee. \"I obey Your Majesty's command.\"","Half an hour later, Fan Guanshan led his men to raid the Sang and Gou estates. Even the maids and servants were locked up in the imperial prison, totaling forty-two people.","When Dong Yuanbin heard the news, his knees went weak, and he nearly fainted.","The two officials who had committed suicide out of fear of punishment were both from the Court of the National Granaries.","If the true mastermind couldn't be found, as their superior, he would definitely be implicated. Would his entire family be executed as well?","The candles in the Ministry of Justice's imperial prison burned from day to night. After a full day and night of severe torture, the straw on the ground was soaked with blood.","The father of one of the officials had been beaten until he was covered in blood and on the verge of death.","Squinting his eyes, he said weakly, \"My lord, my eldest son hasn't been home for a month since he went to the imperial estate. We truly know nothing about the stolen potatoes.\"","Hearing this, the Sang family members locked in the adjacent cell repeatedly cried out about their innocence.","\"My lord, we are wronged! We truly are innocent.\"","Sui Zhuangling, the Minister of Justice, frowned as he stared at them.","They had interrogated them for two days without getting a single piece of useful information. Had Sang Yu really not revealed anything to his family?","After a day's delay, when Chen Fu and Li Hou were brought to the county princess's manor the next day, they were no longer as anxious as they had been the day before.","Song Jinzhao slowly sipped her tea and asked, \"Who was the person that fought with Lanxi the night before last?\"","Thinking of all the help Song Jinzhao had given the tenant farmers on the estate over the past year, as well as their previous concealment, Chen Fu and Li Hou had already made up their minds before coming.","Huo Chong was still in the capital. Rather than running into him later, it would be better to just come clean now.","Otherwise, once she discovered they were lying, Song Jinzhao would only be even more displeased.","Li Hou knelt down and said, \"To answer the county princess, this man's name is Huo Chong. His father used to be in the Wu family army, in the same military camp as Qu Ya and the others.\"","\"Chen Fu and I only found out yesterday that aside from the people on the estate, the Wu family army still had other old subordinates.\"","\"His father died over ten years ago. Now, Huo Chong works under Mu Ji'an, the Pacification Commissioner of Ningzhou. He only entered the capital to escort the Prince of Qi. He will leave in a few days and won't cause any trouble.\"","Song Jinzhao's right hand paused slightly as she set down her teacup.","To be able to escort the Prince of Qi into the capital, this Huo Chong must hold a fairly high official position under Mu Ji'an.","Chen Fu and Li Hou stared at Song Jinzhao with honest and straightforward expressions.","In reality, Qu Ya and Guan Nianshan hadn't told them Huo Chong's true identity, so both of them thought Huo Chong was just the son of an ordinary soldier."]},{"number":343,"title":"Chapter 343: Huo Chong's Guarantee","paragraphs":["After dismissing the two of them, Song Jinzhao went to the study.","She stood before the wall where the map hung, pausing for a long time, and finally picked up a charcoal pencil to draw a circle around the words Ningzhou.","The identities of the five corpses could not be discovered.","From the forty-two people of the Sang and Gou families, the Ministry of Justice had failed to interrogate a single useful piece of information.","The Imperial Guards who were dispatched fanned out to search the area where the bodies were discovered, but after two days and two nights, not a single suspicious figure was seen.","A cartload of potatoes seemed to have grown wings and flown away on its own.","In a fit of rage, Xiao Chengjing immediately issued an edict to have all forty-two members of the Sang and Gou families taken to the Meridian Gate and beheaded as a public warning.","Dozens of prisoner cages were carried by horse-drawn carts through Vermilion Bird Street. On the second floor of the hot pot restaurant, Song Jinzhao thoughtfully played with a potato the size of half an egg in her hand.","If those two officials from the Court of Agricultural Affairs knew that their entire families would be beheaded as a public spectacle after their deaths, she wondered if they would regret it.","A piercing flash of golden light crossed Song Jinzhao's eyes.","Looking up, she saw a masked man on the third floor opposite her, watching her.","Their eyes met, and a dark gleam flashed through the pupils hidden beneath the black and gold mask.","Song Jinzhao stared at him with burning eyes.","Wearing a mask, could he be the one who fought with Lanxi?","Huo Chong nodded to Song Jinzhao in greeting, then turned and left his spot.","A moment later, footsteps sounded as the waiter led Huo Chong upstairs.","After taking a seat, the waiter placed the menu on the table.","Catching a glimpse of Song Jinzhao standing by the window from the corner of his eye, Huo Chong looked at the menu while asking the waiter.","What are your restaurant's signature dishes?","The waiter pointed to the thumbs-up signs on the menu and said, These are all our signature items.","If you can handle a spicy broth, you can order the nine-grid pot; if not, you can get the half-and-half twin pot.","Huo Chong returned the menu to the waiter. I will have the half-and-half pot, and bring one portion of every signature boiling dish on the menu.","After the waiter nodded and left, Huo Chong stood up and walked toward Song Jinzhao.","He cupped his hands in a salute and said, I, Huo Chong, pay my respects to County Princess Linghui.","Song Jinzhao turned sideways and looked him up and down.","She had guessed right; he was indeed Huo Chong.","General Huo comes from the southwest, how is it that you recognize me?","Huo Chong straightened his back, a faint smile playing on his lips.","Who in the capital does not know the County Princess's great name? Your portraits are sold at street stalls for five copper coins each.","The tail end of the prisoner carts disappeared around the corner. Song Jinzhao turned and went back to sit at the table.","She leisurely picked up her chopsticks and asked, When is General Huo returning to the southwest?","Without asking for permission, Huo Chong pulled out the long bench opposite Song Jinzhao and sat down. I will leave tomorrow after I submit my departure documents to the Ministry of War.","He looked around.","It was not mealtime yet, and only three surrounding tables were occupied.","Even so, Huo Chong lowered his voice.","A few days ago, I visited old friends on behalf of my father and intruded upon the County Princess's territory. Please forgive me.","Song Jinzhao remained silent.","Seeing this, Huo Chong continued, Qu Ya and Guan Nianshan are my father's old friends, and I consider them my uncles. The County Princess was kind enough not only to conceal their identities but also to hire them for work. I will never forget this kindness.","If there is anywhere I, Huo Chong, can be of help in the future, the County Princess need only ask, and I will not hesitate even if it means my death.","Song Jinzhao picked up her water cup to wash away some of the spicy taste in her mouth.","The Mu clan of Ningzhou is steadily losing ground under the attacks of the Yang clan of Panzhou, and the imperial court will not step in to help you reclaim your lost cities. What does the Mu clan plan to do next? Will you eke out a miserable existence, or will you fight back to retake the cities?","Huo Chong's expression paused slightly; he had not expected Song Jinzhao to react this way.","He had imagined she might ask who his biological father was, or angrily warn him not to come to the capital to cause her trouble again.","The only thing he had not anticipated was that Song Jinzhao would steer the conversation toward the conflict between the Mu and Yang clans in the southwest.","This was a matter for court officials and the Emperor to ponder. Hearing it asked from a woman's mouth was truly quite surprising.","The County Princess also cares about the situation in the southwest?","Song Jinzhao replied, When a great building collapses, no eggs remain unbroken. The situation in the southwest affects the entire Dongzhao Kingdom. As a County Princess, how could I not care?","The gentle expression on Huo Chong's face gradually faded.","Panzhou is growing stronger day by day, and Ningzhou is no longer their match. With the imperial court watching from the sidelines, how can we even talk about fighting back?","I am afraid it will not be many years before the entire southwest is swallowed up by the Yang clan. When they march their troops north, the imperial court will surely be in grave danger.","Thinking of what Ye Liangyu had said, Song Jinzhao locked her eyes on Huo Chong's face, refusing to miss a single subtle expression.","Since General Huo's father is a former subordinate of the Wu Family Army, he must surely know Zeng Qing, the commander of the Yuecheng Army. They sought refuge with the Yang clan of Panzhou back then; has General Huo really had no contact with them?","Huo Chong's eyes widened and his pupils contracted.","He looked at Song Jinzhao in disbelief. In his panic, his right hand accidentally knocked against the teapot on the table.","The lid fell off, and the sweet, cloying sour plum juice poured out, soaking Huo Chong's clothes.","He stood up in a flurry, shaking his clothes with his hands, while cold sweat broke out on his back.","He had only just obtained the token; how could Song Jinzhao have already thought of the Yuecheng Army and Zeng Qing?","Was it a coincidence, or...","Huo Chong's heart pounded relentlessly, and his mind was in absolute chaos!"]},{"number":344,"title":"Chapter 344: The King's Calculation, Huo Chong Leaves the Capital","paragraphs":["Seeing the teapot knocked over, the waiter serving on the second floor quickly grabbed two dry rags and rushed over.","He handed a clean rag to Huo Chong. Please wipe it quickly, sir. It is cold when your clothes get wet in winter.","Without any hesitation or disgust, Huo Chong wrapped the rag around his clothes to wring out the water, his mind racing frantically for an answer to Song Jinzhao's question.","After bowing and nodding to Song Jinzhao, the waiter swiftly picked up the dishes and began wiping the table.","The waiter carrying the hot pot broth upstairs saw Huo Chong standing by Song Jinzhao's table, a flash of confusion in his eyes.","Did he know the County Princess? Were they going to share a table?","He stopped in the aisle next to Huo Chong and asked in a low voice, Sir, should I still serve this broth?","The appearance of the waiter carrying the pot was like a timely rain for Huo Chong, and he nodded hastily.","Serve it, serve it! I am starving, please bring the food quickly.","After saying that, he smiled and said to Song Jinzhao, County Princess, I will go back to my seat first. Whenever you visit the Southwest, I will definitely host you well.","After returning to his table, Huo Chong did not even look across; he moved the long bench and sat with his back facing Song Jinzhao.","Seeing guilt written all over him, Song Jinzhao knew she had guessed right.","One was a former subordinate of the Wu family army, and the other was the son of a soldier from the Wu family army. With this connection, it was easy for them to join forces.","Judging by Huo Chong's reaction, they must have already made contact.","Zeng Qing worked for the Yang Clan, and Huo Chong worked for the Mu Clan, but it was unknown which of them was the one whose heart belonged elsewhere.","Sitting on the stool, Huo Chong felt like he had thorns in his back. No matter how delicious the hot pot was, he had no appetite.","He hastily dumped all the dishes into the clear broth pot, inhaled the tasteless food like a tornado, paid the bill, and left.","Looking down at Huo Chong's retreating figure as he ran off, Song Jinzhao curled her lips in amusement.","According to the original plan, we can send our people to the Southwest and Shuobei.","Qingshuang bowed and nodded slightly. Yes, this servant understands.","Meanwhile, in the Prince Ying's Manor, Xiao Rongyan held a small slip of paper in his hand and threw his head back, laughing heartily.","The person who stole the potatoes from the imperial estate is actually Xiao Rongche! He even plans to give the potatoes to the Shuobei Kingdom. If Imperial Father and the court officials find out, his merits in the Southwest will be completely ruined.","His subordinate gloated, Your Highness, before the potatoes are delivered to Gong Linjue, do you want to go and tell the Emperor right now?","Xiao Rongyan pondered for a moment, then raised his hand and shook his head.","Inappropriate. Xiao Rongche made a deal with Gong Linjue to cure his eyes. If Imperial Father finds out now, he might feel sorry for him and cover the matter up. It is best to wait until the potatoes fall into Gong Linjue's hands before exposing it. By then, even if Imperial Father wants to protect him, the court officials will not agree.","The subordinate was a bit worried. But what if the imperial physician sent by the Shuobei Kingdom really cures Prince Qi's eyes?","A cold smile appeared on Xiao Rongyan's lips, and he lightly drew his hand across his neck.","Once the person arrives at Prince Qi's Manor, we will have our people kill him. Xiao Rongche's eyes must never recover.","The subordinate's eyes lit up, and he nodded vigorously. This subordinate understands. I will go and send the message immediately.","After the Sang and Gou families were all beheaded, the Emperor did not let Fan Guanshan continue tracking the whereabouts of the potatoes. Instead, he ordered the local government offices to strictly inspect passing vehicles.","Especially at the borders, the imperial decree had already been sent to the Jinglei Army.","The people sent by the Ministry of War to track the diplomatic mission sent back news. After reading the letter, Wu Jianzheng went to the Imperial Study with a bitter expression.","He knelt down and said, Reporting to Your Majesty, the spies sent to track the Shuobei Kingdom's diplomatic mission sent a letter saying they found no trace of the potatoes. Gong Linjue and his group have been rushing all the way, and they will reach the border in twenty days.","Xiao Chengjing felt a fire pressing on his chest and his head throbbed.","Is there any news from the Southwest?","Wu Jianzheng shook his head. We have not yet received any memorials from the General of Xuanwei or the Provincial Administration Commissioner of the Southwest.","Xiao Chengjing closed his eyes and took a deep breath, feeling that nothing was going smoothly.","You may step down. Keep following them until the Shuobei Kingdom's diplomatic mission leaves the Dongzhao Kingdom.","Wu Jianzheng continued, Your Majesty, seeing that the imperial court is reluctant to dispatch troops, Huo Chong submitted a document to the Ministry of War yesterday requesting to leave the capital. Should we let him go?","Xiao Chengjing frowned in annoyance. Pacify him with a few words and tell him to scram. He just opens his mouth and expects me to send troops without offering anything in return. Not even a ghost would make such a losing deal.","Tell him to go back and inform Mu Ji'an to stop dreaming about the Binzhou salt fields. The remaining half belongs to the imperial court.","Wu Jianzheng kowtowed and took his leave. This humble subject obeys the decree.","After leaving the palace, Wu Jianzheng sent someone to relay the Emperor's words to Huo Chong.","Upon hearing this, Huo Chong pretended to be disappointed and lowered his head, then returned to his room and closed the door.","Just when Wu Jianzheng thought he would come to beg and struggle a bit more for the Mu Clan, Huo Chong took his people and left early the next morning.","He ran even faster than Gong Linjue, as if someone were chasing him to kill him."]},{"number":345,"title":"Chapter 345: Handing Over Potatoes, the Emperor of Shuobei Kingdom Wants to Kill Song Jinzhao","paragraphs":["Only after the diplomatic mission entered the territory of the Shuobei Kingdom did the spies sent by the Ministry of War finally turn back and return home.","The Thunder Army stationed at the border maintained strict defenses, but even after the New Year passed, they found no trace of the stolen potatoes.","Gong Linjue waited in Ironclad City on the border of the Shuobei Kingdom for a month and a half before the people delivering the potatoes finally began to arrive in a slow, staggered trickle.","Hidden in the secret compartments of chests, mixed into sacks of grain... it took five merchant caravans to scrape together a single cartload of potatoes.","Gong Linjue picked up an egg-sized potato and examined it closely. This is the divine crop that can yield a thousand catties per acre?","A guard from the Li Residence, who had blended in with the caravan, took a piece of paper from his chest and handed it to Gong Linjue.","The method for planting the potatoes is written on here. We ask that Your Highness send an imperial physician to the Prince Qi Residence as soon as you return to Yandu.","After reading the planting instructions on the paper, Gong Linjue asked doubtfully, These potatoes are so small, how are we supposed to cut them into pieces? One isn't even enough for a single bite.","The guard replied, We brought small ones to make them easier to hide. Once they are grown, they won't be this small.","Gong Linjue folded the paper and tucked it into his robes. Once I return to Yandu, I will have the imperial physician set out immediately. He should arrive by the third or fourth month, at the start of spring.","Having received this guarantee, the guard's tense nerves finally relaxed. He turned and led the others back to report their success.","A month later, in Yandu, the capital of the Shuobei Kingdom.","Upon entering the city, Gong Linjue headed straight for the imperial palace to present the potatoes to the Emperor of Shuobei, He Mingyuan.","The young emperor, only twenty-three years old, wore an eerily bright red everyday dragon robe. Even the dragon's scales and eyes were crafted from red agate stones.","I didn't expect you to have such a harvest from your diplomatic mission this time. A yield of a thousand catties per acre—it truly is a monumental treasure.","His narrow eyes tilting up slightly, Gong Linjue said, This thing is not only high-yielding but also drought-resistant. It can be planted on the grasslands and in the mountains. If we use it to replace rice, it won't be long before our Shuobei Kingdom will no longer lack food.","He Mingyuan nodded and tossed the potato into a bamboo basket. It's just that there are a bit too few seeds. It will probably take some time if we want every household to plant them.","Gong Linjue deliberately lowered his voice. Dongzhao is only two years ahead of us. When they distribute them to their commoners to plant, this subject will take people to buy some more and bring them back.","He Mingyuan returned to his dragon throne and crossed his legs. His eyes were bottomless, surging with a dark, blood-red gleam.","I heard that at the Dongzhao Emperor's birthday banquet, you lost to a woman, and it was Dongzhao's County Princess Linghui?","During the time Gong Linjue stayed in Ironclad City and his return journey, rumors of the martial arts tournament at the birthday banquet had already reached Yandu. He Mingyuan had known about it for half a month.","Gong Linjue looked at the ground guiltily, and in the next second, he bent his knees and knelt down.","After consecutively defeating five of Dongzhao's generals, this subject faced Chu Liuyun. I had originally intended to cripple his hand, but Song Jinzhao ran out to stop me.","This woman possesses boundless strength and is extremely skilled in close-quarters combat. This subject also underestimated the enemy, which is why I lost to her.","He Mingyuan's tone was low and slow, yet it brought about a strong sense of suffocation.","So, the other military generals of Dongzhao are nothing to fear, and only this Song Jinzhao is someone you cannot defeat?","Gong Linjue gritted his teeth, recalling the scene of his duel with Song Jinzhao. Finally, he helplessly nodded and admitted, Although I underestimated her, this subject is indeed no match for her.","He Mingyuan smiled, but the smile didn't reach his eyes. I know how highly skilled your martial arts are. To be defeated at the hands of a woman, it seems she is truly formidable.","Being repeatedly reminded of his loss to Song Jinzhao, Gong Linjue's hands resting at his sides involuntarily clenched into fists.","Your Majesty need not take this matter too much to heart. No matter how formidable Song Jinzhao is, she is just a woman who doesn't know how to lead troops in battle. In the future, when we attack Dongzhao, it will definitely still be Chu Liuyun leading their army.","He Mingyuan spoke slowly and methodically, Just because she won't now doesn't mean she won't in the future.","Gong Linjue said, There is no precedent in the history books of a woman leading troops in battle. If they really let Song Jinzhao command the three armies, Dongzhao's military generals would be reduced to the laughingstock of the world. They will definitely oppose it.","He Mingyuan replied, The winner becomes king, and the loser is vilified; the strong are revered. When a true crisis arrives, even a ten-year-old child can be sent to the battlefield. What does a woman matter?","Gong Linjue furrowed his brows and blinked. Your Majesty means?","He Mingyuan said expressionlessly, Any threat must be eliminated. Song Jinzhao is in the capital and difficult to kill, so let us make her come to Yandu.","I hear she is not yet married, and my imperial harem happens to be lacking concubines. A marriage alliance to solidify diplomatic relations between our two countries is perfectly logical and reasonable.","... Gong Linjue's pupils shrank. After thinking it through, he felt that this method was extremely good.","As long as Song Jinzhao came to Yandu, her life and death would be in their hands.","There were tens of thousands of imperial guards in the palace. Song Jinzhao would be isolated and without help; killing her would be as easy as lifting a finger.","Given the Dongzhao Emperor's temperament, even if Song Jinzhao died, they wouldn't dare to start a war.","When the time came, they could just invent a random cause of death to gloss over the matter. This idea was simply brilliant."]},{"number":346,"title":"Chapter 346: Spreading News: The King of Qi Is the Mastermind Behind the Scenes","paragraphs":["With a single imperial decree from He Mingyuan, Minister of Rites Wang Nie set off from Yandu three days later, carrying betrothal gifts as he headed to the Dongzhao Kingdom to propose marriage.","Song Jinzhao, who was currently in the capital, knew nothing of this. The profits handed in by her various shops before the new year had been extremely generous.","During the New Year festivities, she had made another fortune. With spring fast approaching, the number of her shops needed to be doubled.","This was not just for the sake of making money, but more importantly, to establish a sprawling network of intelligence strongholds.","Fushun walked into the study and respectfully offered a wedding invitation to Song Jinzhao with both hands. \"County Princess, this is an invitation sent by the Duke of Zhenguo's estate. They are inviting you to attend the wedding banquet in ten days.\"","After a series of complex procedures, Chu Liuyun was finally going to marry Princess Yongjia.","The wedding date was set for the nineteenth day of the second lunar month, an auspicious day for marriage.","Song Jinzhao looked at the names on the invitation and chuckled softly. \"They are quite a match. Tell the servants of the Duke's estate that I will definitely arrive on time.\"","Although Xiao Yongjia was no longer the only princess of the Dongzhao Kingdom, the other seven were still nursing infants, so this wedding would absolutely be exceedingly grand.","Once Chu Liuyun became the Prince Consort, his status within the royal court would rise significantly.","Compared to the jubilant atmosphere permeating the capital and the imperial palace, the mood in the Prince of Qi's estate was so oppressive that everyone was in a state of extreme paranoia, jumping at every shadow.","Despite Gu Jupu, the Director of the Imperial Academy of Medicine, trying his utmost to treat Xiao Rongche's eyes, without removing the right eye, the vision in his left eye had begun to deteriorate. He was already experiencing double vision and blurriness when looking at things beyond five feet.","Terrified of going completely blind, he constantly wrote letters to Gong Linjue, urging him to send an imperial physician over as soon as possible.","However, the distance between the two countries was vast. Every letter sent out was like a stone dropped into the ocean, yielding absolutely no reply.","Under the dual torment of physical and mental anguish, Xiao Rongche began to suffer from severe insomnia.","He stayed awake night after night, and even his hair started falling out in handfuls.","Inside the Prince of Ying's estate, Xiao Rongyan held three letters in his hand and burst into loud laughter.","\"With both witnesses and material evidence in our hands, Xiao Rongche is completely finished this time.\"","\"Immediately send someone to spread the news in the capital that the Shuobei Kingdom has already obtained the potatoes. Also, deliver these three letters to Ye Liangyu.\"","The man smiled and nodded in agreement, \"This subordinate will do it right away.\"","In just one day, rumors began to spread throughout the capital that it was the First Prince, Xiao Rongche, who had stolen the potatoes and given them to the Shuobei Kingdom.","For a time, the common people were engaged in spirited discussions. When the news reached the palace, the Emperor, who was dining with Princess Yongjia, instantly had his face darken in anger.","He slammed his chopsticks forcefully onto the table and sharply reprimanded, \"Have Fan Guanshan investigate this immediately! Who exactly is spreading these baseless rumors?\"","The person who stole the potatoes for the Shuobei Kingdom could be anyone, but it absolutely could not be his own son.","Such a massive scandal would bring immense shame to the royal family.","Eunuch Zhao carefully bowed and withdrew.","Sitting opposite him, Princess Yongjia looked at the soup spilled on the table, too nervous to even breathe.","It had been nearly three months since the potatoes were stolen from the imperial estate. The Ministry of Justice had failed to find anything and had already given up on the case.","This was a major crime tantamount to treason. How could it be her eldest imperial brother who stole them?","What could possibly be his motive?","Harboring pent-up anger, Xiao Chengjing had completely lost his appetite.","He reached out his hand, and the young eunuch serving by the table immediately handed him a wet towel.","Xiao Chengjing said in a deep voice to Princess Yongjia, \"Your Imperial Father still has memorials to review. I will take my leave first.\"","Princess Yongjia hurriedly stood up to see him off. \"Court affairs are busy, but Imperial Father must also remember to rest.\"","Only after Xiao Chengjing left did Princess Yongjia pick up her chopsticks to continue eating.","Ever since the imperial decree for her marriage was issued, there hadn't been a moment when she wasn't happy.","At the thought of marrying Chu Liuyun so soon, her heart bloomed with joy, wishing time would pass just a little faster.","That evening, just as Ye Liangyu, who had recently returned from the Censorate, stepped out of his sedan chair, a little beggar in tattered clothes rushed over from a nearby corner."]},{"number":347,"title":"Chapter 347: Kill to Silence, Arrest in the Ruined Temple","paragraphs":["The sedan bearers noticed this and immediately spread their arms to block the person.","\"What are you doing! How dare a beggar like you cause a scene in front of the Ye Manor? Go beg somewhere else.\"","The dirt-streaked little beggar held the envelopes high and shouted at Ye Liangyu, \"My Lord, someone asked me to give these to you. They said it involves a monstrous injustice!\"","\"Please, My Lord, seek justice for the people!\"","Ye Liangyu, who already had one foot on the steps, turned around.","He narrowed his eyes, looking the little beggar up and down, before his gaze finally landed on the three letters held high in the boy's hands.","\"Go fetch the letters.\"","Hearing this, an attendant immediately ran over, took the letters, and handed them to Ye Liangyu.","Standing at the doorway braving the cold wind, Ye Liangyu tore open the seal and pulled out a white sheet of paper covered in writing.","Just as Ye Liangyu was reading the letter, the little beggar turned and quickly ran away.","By the time the sedan bearer who had blocked him gave chase, the boy had already darted into a narrow alley.","When the bearer reached the entrance of the alley, the boy had vanished without a trace.","\"My Lord, he ran too fast. I couldn't catch him,\" the sedan bearer reported back to Ye Liangyu, his face full of guilt for his failure.","After waiting a long time without hearing a reprimand, the bearer couldn't help but look up, only to find Ye Liangyu looking grim, his hands trembling.","He looked so furiously enraged that it seemed he would tear the letter to shreds in the next second.","After finishing the first letter, Ye Liangyu held the paper between his trembling fingers and proceeded to open the second letter.","Ten thousand thoughts of killing Xiao Rongche flashed through his mind, his internal organs trembling with every breath.","Seeing that no one was chasing him, the little beggar tightly clutched his silver and excitedly ran to a bun stall on the street, shouting, \"Boss, I want one meat bun and one steamed bun!\"","Seeing that the customer was a beggar, the vendor waved his hand impatiently to shoo him away.","\"Go beg at the tavern. I run a small business here; you have to pay for the food.\"","\"I have money.\" The little beggar stood on his tiptoes and held his silver high, grinning widely to show his teeth.","Seeing that he actually had money, the vendor swiftly moved the steamer aside, picked up a steamed bun and a meat bun, and wrapped them in a hemp leaf.","\"The steamed bun is one copper coin, the meat bun is three. That makes four copper coins in total.\"","The little beggar handed the silver to the vendor, who gave him a smaller piece of silver and a handful of copper coins as change.","After safely tucking the change into an inner pocket of his clothes, he held the leaf-wrapped buns tightly against his chest to protect them, running excitedly toward the city gates.","Wait for me, little sister. You'll have a meat bun to eat very soon.","Running out of the city, just as he was about to reach the ruined temple, a masked man stepped out from behind a large tree.","A sharp sword pierced the little beggar through the back.","The blade went straight through his frail body and protruded from his upper abdomen. When it was pulled out, it left a gaping hole that spurted blood.","The snow-white buns fell from the hemp leaf, rolling onto the ground and turning a dirty, ashen black.","The little beggar stared blankly in the direction of the ruined temple. He opened his mouth slightly as tears completely soaked his eyes.","Finally, the man dragged him by the ankles and tossed his body into a mass grave.","His once bright and lively young eyes were now devoid of life, radiating a heavy aura of death under the faint sunlight.","The cold wind blew across the mass grave, making his exposed skin feel even colder than the copper coins hidden in his chest pocket.","No sooner had the man left than Ye Liangyu arrived, leading the constables of the Jingzhao Prefecture in a mad dash toward the ruined temple.","\"Found him!\" Inside a mud house near the ruined temple, a constable looked at a gagged and tightly bound man, turning his head to shout excitedly at the people behind him.","Initially, seeing the constables rush in, a sliver of hope had survived in the bound man's eyes.","But when he saw Ye Liangyu walk in wearing his official uniform, the hope in his eyes dissipated instantly, replaced by despair and fear.","At that moment, he felt as though his entire world had gone dark."]},{"number":348,"title":"Chapter 348: Both Human and Material Evidence Are Present, Petitioning the Heavenly Court","paragraphs":["Sitting on the threshold of the ruined temple, a seven-year-old girl with little braids tied with hemp rope watched with eyes full of curiosity as the guards took the man away.","Behind her, a fifteen-year-old boy who had just woken up from a nap walked out holding a chipped earthen bowl.","Seeing the little girl sitting upright on the threshold, her eyes staring intently straight ahead, he casually cracked a joke.","\"Stop waiting. You are sick and your medicine costs money. Your brother has definitely abandoned you.\"","The little girl felt wronged.","She stubbornly raised her head and retorted, \"My brother would never do that! He said once he earned some silver today, he would take me to see a doctor and buy me meat buns to eat.\"","The boy let out a mocking sneer, \"Meat buns? You sure have a wild imagination. I would say dog shit is more like it.\"","The little girl turned her head and ignored him. Her thin, frail little face was taut, and her gaze remained fixed on the dirt road next to the rocks not far away.","It was the only path leading to the ruined temple; she would be able to see anyone who passed by.","But this time, the little girl waited from noon until dark, yet her brother never returned.","Ye Liangyu took the man to the Jingzhao Prefecture and interrogated him for a full two hours. Then, holding the signed confession, he gathered everyone from the Censorate and knelt on the steps outside the Imperial Study.","Fei Yanzhang, who had received a message from Ye Liangyu in advance, brought Dongfang Shaoting and many other officials over, waiting for the matter to blow up so the Emperor would have no way to protect the culprit.","When the others saw Ye Liangyu leading all the censors to kneel on the steps, they were extremely curious.","Could it be about the recent rumors in the capital?","But without any evidence, why had the entire Censorate mobilized?","Were they trying to crush Prince Qi using public opinion?","The Emperor never expected that just by sleeping in for a little less than an hour today, the outside world would be turned upside down.","By the time he rushed over from his bedchamber, almost all the officials of the third rank and above had already gathered outside the Imperial Study.","His gaze swept over Ye Liangyu, who was taking the lead kneeling at the very front, and Xiao Chengjing frowned with a headache.","Just as he was about to open his mouth to reprimand them, Fan Guanshan walked over briskly from a distance.","Noticing so many officials kneeling at the entrance of the Imperial Study, his footsteps paused for a moment, and then he looked toward the Emperor and lowered his head.","Seeing Fan Guanshan like this, Xiao Chengjing's heart gave a heavy thud and instantly sank to the bottom of a cliff.","Could the rumors spreading in the capital be true? Was the mastermind behind the scenes really Rong Che?","After walking into the Imperial Study, Xiao Chengjing first had someone call Fan Guanshan inside.","His face was dark, and his brows were filled with a chilling air.","\"How is the matter I asked you to investigate?\"","Fan Guanshan cupped his hands and reported, \"Your subject found out that the rumors all originated from the beggar's temple outside the city. However, I was a step too late. By the time I arrived, the little beggar who spread the rumors had already been killed, and none of the others had seen the person who paid the money.\"","Blood rushed to his head, and Xiao Chengjing clutched his chest, struggling to catch his breath.","Fan Guanshan continued, \"When your subject arrived at the ruined temple, the nearby beggars said that an hour ago, guards had arrested someone in the surrounding mud houses.\"","\"Your subject then rushed to the Jingzhao Prefecture to inquire. The Governor of the Jingzhao Prefecture said that he and Lord Ye had caught a witness to Prince Qi's treason. Presumably, the people from the Censorate kneeling outside the hall right now are here for this very matter.\"","It was as if a bolt of lightning had struck Xiao Chengjing right on the top of his head; saying he was struck by five thunderbolts would not be an exaggeration.","He stumbled and collapsed onto the dragon throne, shaking his head in disbelief, looking just like a withered old tree battered by fierce winds.","Having waited for a summons that never came, Ye Liangyu raised the confession and letters in his hand and shouted loudly, \"For his own selfish desires, Prince Qi instructed Count Zhongqin, Li Mingge, to steal potatoes from the imperial estate to trade with the Shuobei State. Your subject possesses the correspondence between Prince Qi and Prince Wei of Shuobei State, Gong Linjue, as well as the confession of the messenger from the Li residence. I implore Your Majesty to investigate this case thoroughly and mete out severe punishment to answer to the millions of people in the Dongzhao Kingdom!\"","Wave after wave of his shouting hammered against Xiao Chengjing's eardrums, shaking him so much that he could barely sit straight."]},{"number":349,"title":"Chapter 349: Many Seek an Audience but Are Blocked at the Door","paragraphs":["All the air in the imperial study seemed to have been drained away at this moment, the oppressive atmosphere causing everyone to break out in a heavy sweat.","A candle within its lantern cover crackled and popped, the sudden noise startling a palace maid so much that she shrank her shoulders and dared not breathe.","Outside, the voices of the imperial censors continued endlessly. It was unknown how much time had passed before Xiao Chengjing finally straightened his posture.","His words were spat out one by one, sounding as if he wanted to crush someone's bones with his teeth.","\"Let Ye Liangyu enter.\"","By now, the ministers who had figured out the whole story were also engaged in heated discussions.","They had initially thought it was just a rumor, but unexpectedly, both witnesses and material evidence were present, and even Earl Zhongqin had a hand in it.","The imperial court had expended so much manpower searching for so long, yet the potatoes had already been delivered into the hands of the Shuobei Kingdom.","\"As an imperial prince, one should put the world before oneself. For Prince Qi, as a prince, to hand over the potatoes to the Shuobei Kingdom—how is this any different from treason?\"","\"This is rearing a tiger to cause future trouble! Once the Shuobei Kingdom's rations are abundant in the future, they will definitely raise an army to attack us. Prince Qi is so foolish!\"","Gu Qishan, who had arrived a step late, listened to the ministers' crusade against Xiao Rongche, his heart panicking so much it felt as if it would leap out of his chest.","Such a massive matter, why didn't His Highness discuss it with him first!","Eunuch Zhao walked out with an apprehensive expression and said to Ye Liangyu, who was kneeling in the middle, \"Lord Ye, the Emperor summons you inside.\"","Seeing this, the other censors all looked toward Ye Liangyu.","To summon only the Palace Deputy, what does the Emperor mean by this?","Before the people from the Censorate could speak, Dongfang Shaoting stepped out from the side.","\"I also wish to seek an audience with the Emperor. I trouble the eunuch to announce me.\"","Fei Yanzhang closely followed, \"I also wish to seek an audience with the Emperor. I trouble the eunuch to announce me.\"","...","Eunuch Zhao looked at the crowd with a troubled face, nervously swallowing his saliva.","\"The Emperor only summoned Lord Ye. This servant will go and announce you all again.\"","After bringing Ye Liangyu into the imperial study, Eunuch Zhao lowered his voice, \"Reporting to Your Majesty, Secretariat Director Lord Dongfang, Chancellor Lord Gu, Hanlin Academy Grand Secretary Lord Fei, Minister of War Lord Zhong... are outside seeking an audience with Your Majesty.\"","Zhao Yande named thirteen people in one breath. With every name spoken, Xiao Chengjing's face darkened by another fraction.","The look he directed at Ye Liangyu grew increasingly displeased.","In the past, when Prince Qi and Prince Ying had formidable power in the court, it was a good thing for the Censorate to continuously impeach them.","But now, neither of them posed a threat anymore. Especially Prince Qi, who, having been blinded in one eye, was destined to have no hope for the throne. When it was time to let them off the hook, they should be let off.","Such a major incident concerned Prince Qi's life and death, as well as the dignity of the imperial family; Ye Liangyu should have informed him privately.","Now, bringing the Censorate to submit a joint memorial had caused a great shock throughout the court and the public, stirring up endless discussions.","Could it be that they wanted him to personally issue an edict to execute his own son?","Feeling the oppressive aura from above, Ye Liangyu, kneeling on the ground, could not help but clench his fists and hold his breath.","\"Have all the official duties of the court been handled? I have no time to see them today.\"","With a trembling heart, Eunuch Zhao bypassed Ye Liangyu and walked outside.","Dongfang Shaoting and the others immediately took a step forward.","Eunuch Zhao hurriedly used the horsetail whisk in his hand to stop them.","He smiled tactfully and said, \"My Lords, the Emperor asks you to return and handle your official duties. He will not be seeing anyone today.\"","Everyone held in their anger.","What official duty could be more important than a prince committing treason?","If the Emperor could see Ye Liangyu, why wouldn't he see them?","He definitely wanted to protect Prince Qi.","Seeing that they were not leaving, Eunuch Zhao had no choice but to continue persuading them, \"The Emperor is currently furious. It would be best for you Lords to come back another day.\"","Fei Yanzhang walked around Dongfang Shaoting to ask Zhao Yande, \"Eunuch Zhao, do you know what the Emperor's attitude is regarding Prince Qi trading potatoes with the Shuobei Kingdom?\"","Eunuch Zhao pulled a bitter face, crying grievance for himself.","\"Lord Fei, how could a mere servant like me possibly guess the Emperor's thoughts? You all should hurry back, lest you get implicated when the Emperor loses his temper.\"","After saying that, he turned and walked back into the imperial study, having the doors closed behind him."]},{"number":350,"title":"Chapter 350: Forthright Admonition, Thirty Lashes of the Rod","paragraphs":["Staring at the closed doors, Dongfang Shaoting and the others were still unwilling to leave. They stood firmly outside the imperial study, continuing to wait.","No matter what, there had to be an answer today.","Ye Liangyu knelt on the cold bluestone bricks, his kneecaps already aching slightly. The emperor had not told him to rise, so he could only continue kneeling.","Xiao Chengjing's mouth pressed into a deep frown, his voice as sharp as an ice pick.","He ordered Zhao Yande, Bring the items up.","Zhao Yande walked over to Ye Liangyu with quick strides, taking the letter and confession Ye Liangyu was holding up and handing them to the emperor.","Xiao Chengjing first read the confession from beginning to end, then opened the letter with trembling hands.","After reading everything, he remained silent for a long time before looking up. Where is the messenger currently locked up?","Ye Liangyu looked directly into the emperor's eyes and answered, In the prison of the Jingzhao Prefecture.","Xiao Chengjing stacked the letter and confession together and placed them by his hand.","I feel that although the handwriting on these three letters somewhat resembles that of Prince Qi, they were not written by Prince Qi himself. It seems someone is trying to frame him. You do not need to concern yourself with this matter anymore; I will send someone to investigate.","Ye Liangyu's eyes widened in astonishment. The handwriting on the letters was clearly identical to Prince Qi's, and the messenger had also stated that it was written by Prince Qi's own hand. Was the emperor trying to shield Prince Qi?","He bowed low and kowtowed, his forehead striking heavily against the hard bluestone bricks, and said with a resounding tone, Your Majesty, according to the culprit's confession, Prince Qi instructed Earl Zhongqin to steal the potatoes and hand them over to the Northern Shu Kingdom. The purpose was to save his left eye.","The motive, witnesses, and material evidence are all conclusive. Coupled with everything that has happened before, you absolutely must not tolerate this time.","Xiao Chengjing stared fixedly at Ye Liangyu with displeasure.","The culprit you speak of is a servant of Earl Zhongqin's estate, and the letters could also have been forged by Earl Zhongqin. In my view, this entire affair was orchestrated solely by Earl Zhongqin from start to finish. After the incident was exposed, he wanted to save his own life, so he framed Prince Qi. Rong Che's right eye is already blind, and he has been recuperating in his estate all along. He simply had no opportunity to do such a thing.","His nails dug into his palms, veins bulging on the backs of his tightly clenched fists. Ye Liangyu's voice trembled as he persisted unwillingly, That is precisely why Prince Qi ordered Earl Zhongqin to do this. The letters were written by Prince Qi himself, and the steward of Prince Qi's estate personally handed the letters to the messenger. If Your Majesty does not believe it, you can have the Ministry of Justice or the Supreme Court arrest the man immediately.","Bang! Xiao Chengjing slammed his palm onto the imperial desk. The eunuchs and palace maids in the room immediately fell to their knees, not daring to look up.","I said Earl Zhongqin is the mastermind, so he is the mastermind. Prince Qi's right eye is already blind, and his left eye is on the verge of losing its sight. Even if this matter is truly related to him, his merits offset his faults, and he is innocent.","Ye Liangyu clenched his jaw tightly. At the thought of everything that had happened before, his eyes began to turn red.","The emperor had already spared Prince Qi many times.","He held his head high and his chest out, throwing caution to the wind as he said, A prince who breaks the law is as guilty as a commoner. It is true that Prince Qi has merits in pacifying the southwest, but how can the crime of treason be so easily forgiven? If Your Majesty shields Prince Qi, will it not make a mockery of us before the people of the world once word gets out?","The distance was close, and the walls of the imperial study were not soundproof.","The sound of the table being slammed and Ye Liangyu's sonorous, forceful admonitions reached the ears of Dongfang Shaoting and the others loud and clear.","Everyone had already guessed seventy or eighty percent of what was happening inside.","The emperor wanted to protect Prince Qi, turning a major issue into a minor one, and a minor one into nothing.","Ye Liangyu disagreed, which was why he said things like a prince breaking the law is as guilty as a commoner.","Insolent! I am the sovereign and you are the subject. It seems I have been too lenient with you, giving you the audacity to speak such words that offend the imperial dignity.","Ye Liangyu did not retreat a single step. He kowtowed once more, his forehead bruising purple.","Advising the sovereign on his faults above and correcting the officials on their transgressions below is inherently my duty as an imperial censor. I do this for Your Majesty, and for the eternal legacy of the Dongzhao Kingdom. I beg Your Majesty to see clearly.","Xiao Chengjing's face was as dark as deep water. Even Zhao Yande, who was kneeling beside a pillar, began to tremble.","Plucking hairs from a tiger's head—how was this any different from courting death?","Utter nonsense.","Guards, drag Ye Liangyu out and give him thirty strokes of the cane. Without my decree, he is not to attend court for the time being. Let him reflect thoroughly at home.","Ye Liangyu gritted his teeth so hard he almost shattered his molars.","When he straightened his upper body, the look he directed at Xiao Chengjing was filled with heartache and despair, as if his faith had collapsed and his entire worldview had been shattered.","Even as the guards dragged him out, he did not utter a single word begging for mercy."]},{"number":351,"title":"Chapter 351: Unreconciled Fei Yanzhang","paragraphs":["Seeing Ye Liangyu being pressed down by two guards and passing in front of them, the officials of the Censorate showed indignation on their faces.","For such a grave crime, the Emperor not only chose to shield the culprit but also ordered a caning for a loyal and outspoken censor. This was truly not the action of a wise ruler.","Lying face down on the long bench, Ye Liangyu's mind echoed with the Emperor's various tolerances and protections towards Prince Qi and Prince Ying. His heart was extremely complicated.","The eunuch specifically in charge of the execution dragged over a court cane that was two fingers wide and one finger thick. The bulging muscle lines on his thick wrists showed at a glance that he frequently beat people.","\"Lord Ye, pardon the offense.\"","As the light words fell, the surrounding atmosphere instantly quieted down.","The heavy wooden board first struck the clothes, and upon contacting the flesh, it let out a muffled, solid thud.","Ye Liangyu clenched his jaw and buried his head into his chest.","He gripped the two sharp corners of the bench tightly with both hands, his body trembling incessantly as the wooden board fell.","Standing in the front row, Fei Yanzhang saw his good friend being beaten, his chest heaving violently.","He lifted the hem of his official robe and knelt down, then shouted towards the Imperial Study: \"The planting of potatoes concerns the food and clothing of thousands of commoners in the Dongzhao Kingdom. The case of Prince Qi instructing Earl Zhongqin to steal potatoes must be strictly investigated. To manifest the royal majesty, I beseech Your Majesty to issue an edict for a joint trial by the Three Judicial Offices.\"","The other officials stared at Fei Yanzhang as if looking at a madman.","Ye Liangyu was already being beaten; rushing forward at this time was simply courting death.","Seeing Fei Yanzhang kneel, the other censors looked at each other in dismay, then one by one followed suit, shouting in unison: \"We beg Your Majesty to strictly investigate this case and order a joint trial by the Three Judicial Offices.\"","After a dozen strikes, Ye Liangyu was already on the verge of passing out.","However, upon hearing the shouts of Fei Yanzhang and the others from the Censorate, he still struggled to raise his head.","Beads of sweat slid from his forehead into his eyes, bringing a stinging pain accompanied by a strong burning sensation.","He subconsciously closed his eyes and opened them again.","\"Don't shout. Stop,\" he endured the pain, his back molars nearly crushed from gritting them.","But his voice was too small, and the others' voices were too loud, completely drowning him out. Fei Yanzhang and the rest did not hear him at all.","Fan Guanshan, standing to the side, had already furrowed his brow into three deep creases.","Potatoes concerned the lifeblood of the nation.","With both witnesses and material evidence complete, the Emperor still chose to blatantly shield the culprit.","If the ruler is unjust, the court will be unstable; if the people are unsettled, the world will struggle to find peace.","The military generals in the court were no match for Prince Wei of the Shuobei Kingdom. If the nation did not grow stronger, they could not possibly let County Princess Linghui, a mere woman, go to the battlefield when the time came.","Prince Qi had truly caused a massive disaster this time.","Inside the silent Imperial Study, Eunuch Zhao, who was standing by the desk holding his breath, heard the clamor outside and was so frightened that he dropped the inkstick in his hand.","He cautiously raised his eyes to peek.","Xiao Chengjing stared gloomily at the desk without moving an inch. His right hand holding the brush trembled violently, and ink dripped from the tip onto the memorial, blurring into a dark blob.","Eunuch Zhao pursed his lips, his heart involuntarily beginning to palpitate violently.","Ye Liangyu was already taking a beating; why couldn't these officials just give it a rest?","If this continued, not a single one of them would escape punishment.","Seeing the Emperor remain completely silent, Eunuch Zhao quietly lightened his footsteps and withdrew from the Imperial Study.","The moment the doors closed, he hurried over to Fei Yanzhang, the fly whisk in his hand flying along with his brisk pace.","\"Lord Fei, how could you join in this nonsense?\"","\"Prince Qi is a prince after all, and he is on the verge of going blind. The Emperor is already heartbroken over this, so how could he bear to punish him heavily? Even if you kneel here for seven days and seven nights, it won't help. You should all leave quickly. If you keep shouting like this, it's highly likely that every single one of you will be punished.\""]},{"number":352,"title":"Chapter 352: When the Son of Heaven is enraged, it either draws blood or brings death.","paragraphs":["Fei Yanzhang turned his head away, looking toward the empty doors of the Imperial Study.","The heavy thuds of the bastinado continued to echo in his ears. He turned back to look at his good friend lying prone on the long bench.","Their eyes met. Ye Liangyu was shaking his head, while Fei Yanzhang clenched his jaw, his eyes full of defiance.","As he pondered, the defiance vanished, melting into a resolute pool that surged up within him.","He shouted loudly toward the room, Prince Qi is the Emperor's son, but the people of Dongzhao are the Emperor's subjects! Prince Qi used potatoes, which concern the very survival and prosperity of our people and the state, to make a deal with Shuobei. This is tantamount to disregarding the lives of countless citizens and the fate of Dongzhao itself. I implore Your Majesty to weigh which is more important and make a swift decision!","It was like a sudden clap of thunder that left everyone paralyzed with shock.","Dongfang Shaoting instinctively covered Fei Yanzhang's mouth, trying to stop him from saying anything more suicidal.","It was a threat, a naked threat.","Fei Yanzhang's words were effectively forcing the Emperor to choose between Prince Qi and the people of the world.","To shield the former would mean the Emperor cared nothing for the countless subjects of Dongzhao, that the people of the world could not compare to his own son.","Would he still be fit to be the Emperor then?","But if he chose not to protect him, according to imperial law, the crime Prince Qi committed was punishable by death.","Once the common people learned the truth, even if he were spared execution, he would have to be severely punished. At the very least, he would be stripped of his royal status and reduced to a commoner to preserve the imperial dignity.","No matter how he chose, it boded ill for the Emperor.","Bang!","A massive crash suddenly erupted from within the Imperial Study, causing the very ground to tremble.","Eunuch Zhao returned to the Imperial Study in a panic, only to find that the imperial desk, which had previously sat before Xiao Chengjing, was now toppled glaringly at the bottom of the steps. Memorials and documents were scattered all over the floor.","Looking up, he saw a face flushed red with absolute, hair-raising fury.","He had never seen the Emperor so angry. Even years ago, when Prince Qi and Prince Ying had stirred up factional struggles in the court and threatened the imperial power, he had never been like this.","Grand Secretary of the Hanlin Academy, Fei Yanzhang, has offended the imperial majesty. Punish him with fifty strokes of the cane!","Xiao Chengjing gritted his teeth, driven utterly mad with rage.","He was the Emperor, the Son of Heaven. Anyone who dared to oppose him had to die.","With weak legs, Zhao Yande stumbled out of the Imperial Study to announce the decree.","Hearing the sentence of fifty strokes, everyone was stunned.","It was well known that both Ye Liangyu and Fei Yanzhang were civil officials. While thirty strokes might leave a man with his life, fifty strokes would undoubtedly kill him.","How was this any different from outright executing Fei Yanzhang?","As the thirtieth stroke fell, Ye Liangyu, who was barely clinging to his last breath, heard that Fei Yanzhang had been sentenced to fifty strokes. He spat out a mouthful of blood and instantly fainted.","Teacher! Song Qiming's eyes nearly split open in anguish as he rushed over and fell to his knees.","Seeing that Ye Liangyu had lost consciousness, he hurriedly pulled a medicine bottle from his robes, opened it, and stuffed a black life-saving pill into Ye Liangyu's mouth.","Seeing the lower half of his teacher's body covered in blood, Song Qiming was on the verge of tears.","He had rushed to the palace the moment he heard the news, but he was still a step too late.","How could the Emperor be so cruel? Wasn't his teacher the one he valued most?","The guilty went unpunished, while those who offered loyal counsel were beaten.","A tyrant. He was simply a tyrant.","Just as Song Qiming hoisted Ye Liangyu onto his back, Fei Yanzhang was pressed down onto the long bench.","When Song Qiming realized what was happening, he froze completely.","Wasn't beating his teacher enough? Now he was going to beat Lord Fei too? Was Xiao Chengjing planning to kill them all?","With two third-rank officials severely punished in succession, the others no longer dared to make a sound.","How many strokes? a wavering voice drifted from Song Qiming's lips.","Fan Guanshan pressed his chapped lips into a thin line. Fifty strokes. Twenty more than Ye Liangyu.","Song Qiming turned his neck stiffly, his pupils trembling uncontrollably.","The beating began. As the wooden plank slammed down onto Fei Yanzhang's body again and again, he seemed to see the making of another Ye Liangyu."]},{"number":353,"title":"Chapter 353: Disappointment","paragraphs":["Watching the thick wooden boards strike Fei Yanzhang's body again and again, the civil officials standing nearby, reluctant to leave, all clenched their fists.","Dongfang Shaoting's gaze darted back and forth between the Imperial Study, the eunuchs carrying out the punishment, Fei Yanzhang, and the surrounding officials. Especially when he met the smug smile on Gu Qishan's face, the suppression in his heart accumulated to its peak, as if it would erupt in the next second.","The purple official uniform was gradually dyed a dark brown with blood. By the time the fortieth blow landed, Fei Yanzhang had already passed out.","After fifty blows, Song Qiming handed Ye Liangyu over to the hurrying Dongfang Yukun, stepped forward, and stuffed a handful of life-saving pills straight into Fei Yanzhang's mouth.","Seeing that Song Qiming could not carry two people by himself, Cui Zhengyang crouched down without hesitation.","\"Yukun is young, I will carry Lord Cui.\"","Song Qiming and Cui Zhengyang each carried one on their backs, with Dongfang Yukun guarding them from behind.","He turned his head to look at his biological father standing on the steps above, his heart filled with mixed emotions that could no longer be described in words.","When Prince Qi and Prince Ying were throwing their weight around in the court, the Emperor highly valued Ye Liangyu and Fei Yanzhang. Now that the threat was gone, he was burning bridges and showing no mercy at all.","How cold-blooded.","As an emperor, it was fine to have the final say, but one still had to distinguish right from wrong.","Minor matters would be one thing, but Prince Qi had committed a grave mistake this time.","To give no punishment at all and even cover the matter up was simply going too far.","If the monarch bent the law for personal gain and lacked the virtue for his position, who could the people of the Dongzhao Kingdom rely on?","Seeing Dongfang Yukun's taut jaw and intense gaze, how could Dongfang Shaoting, as his father, not see what his own son was thinking?","He turned around, his gaze falling upon the floor tiles of the Imperial Study.","Two people, eighty blows.","Would such things happen again in the future?","Who would be next?","Song Qiming did not send the two unconscious men to the Ye or Fei manors; instead, he took them directly back to the County Princess's Estate.","Inside Song Jinzhao and Song Shixue's apothecary, buckets of hot water were carried in by the servants.","Looking at the bloody and mangled flesh at the base of their thighs, Song Jinzhao's brows never relaxed from beginning to end.","Ye Liangyu had no family, so Song Qiming stood by his side, keeping watch the whole time.","Upon receiving the news, Madam Fei rushed over with her son.","Seeing her husband lying unconscious on the bed, his lower body looking like a puddle of mangled mud, Madam Fei burst into tears on the spot.","She covered her mouth and cried out, \"How could he be beaten like this? What should we do?\"","Qingshuang stopped Madam Fei, preventing her from getting too close.","Young Master Fei, who was blocked by Lanxi, saw that Madam Fei was crying so hard she was about to faint, and hurriedly reached out to grasp her shoulders.","\"Mother, Father is not dead and can still be saved. Please say no more; if word gets out, our entire family could be executed.\"","Madam Fei covered her mouth and buried her head in Young Master Fei's embrace, weeping bitterly.","Song Jinzhao, who was cleaning Fei Yanzhang's wounds, furrowed her brows in irritation.","She spoke in a cold voice, \"Qiming, take them out and close the door.\"","It wasn't just the flesh that was smashed, but the bones as well.","If not handled properly, it would result in lower body paralysis, which was very difficult to treat.","Hearing the seriousness and dissatisfaction in Song Jinzhao's voice, Song Qiming quickly spread his arms, gesturing with his eyes for Young Master Fei and his mother to leave.","\"My eldest sister and the others are treating my teacher and Lord Fei. They need a quiet environment, so it is best if we wait outside.\"","Young Master Fei reached out and grabbed Song Qiming's wrist, his eyes full of worry and pleading.","\"Lord Song, my father will definitely be alright, won't he?\"","Song Qiming turned his hand to grasp the young man's hand, pushing both him and Madam Fei in his arms out of the apothecary.","\"Rest assured, my sister will definitely do her best.\"","After the door was closed, the apothecary instantly quieted down.","Aside from the sound of breathing, only the unconscious, pained groans of Ye Liangyu and Fei Yanzhang could be heard."]},{"number":354,"title":"Chapter 354: Coccyx Fracture, Femoral Crack","paragraphs":["After Song Shixue bandaged Ye Liangyu's wound, she looked up. Sister, I have finished treating things on my end.","After Song Jinzhao cut away the last piece of mangled, ruined flesh, a fractured thigh bone was faintly visible beneath the skin and muscle.","A fractured tailbone and a cracked leg bone. Bring me the wooden splints.","Song Shixue nodded, taking the pre-cut wooden boards from the medical chest.","After realigning and securing the tailbone and thigh bone, Song Jinzhao picked up a needle and thread to stitch the wound closed.","By the time the final step was completed, a full two hours had passed since Song Qiming first brought the injured men back.","When the room door opened, Madame Fei, who had been waiting for a long time, immediately tried to rush inside. Princess, how is my husband?","Song Jinzhao reached out to stop her. Please do not agitate yourself. Lord Fei's injuries have been fully treated. He was given an anesthetic and has not yet woken up. He can only be moved tomorrow.","However, his tailbone is fractured and his leg bone is broken. He must rest in bed from now on, otherwise he is very likely to suffer from lasting complications.","Madame Fei grasped Song Jinzhao's right hand with both of hers, shaking it incessantly while her eyes kept darting inside the room.","Thank you, Princess, thank you so much.","At this moment, her entire mind was on the unconscious Fei Yanzhang. She muttered her thanks, but her soul had already flown to her husband's side.","On the other hand, Young Master Fei stared intently at Song Jinzhao and asked, Princess, what kind of lasting complications? Is it serious?","Song Jinzhao spoke slowly. Inability to squat, inability to stand for long periods, and an inability to engage in strenuous physical activity. He would experience pain when using the chamber pot, and he might walk with a limp. These are the most common ones.","Young Master Fei's eyes widened. Not doing strenuous activities was fine.","But a limp and pain when using the chamber pot were absolutely unacceptable.","He asked urgently, Princess, how should he convalesce to ensure there are no lasting complications? What do we need to pay attention to?","Song Jinzhao turned her head to look at Song Shixue. Write down the precautions and hand them to Young Master Fei.","Song Shixue nodded and walked straight to the next room to begin writing, while Heye stood beside her to grind the ink.","Song Qiming walked up to Song Jinzhao with a crestfallen face, the worry in his eyes so thick it practically spilled over.","Sister, how is my teacher?","Song Jinzhao replied, Lord Ye's injuries are lighter than Fei Yanzhang's. His bones are fine, but the muscles on the back of his thighs are severely damaged. Shixue has already cut away the necrotic tissue. It will take a month or two for the flesh to grow back properly, and he cannot leave his bed during this time.","Song Qiming let out a trembling breath.","As long as his life is saved, that is all that matters. With the Emperor so furious and handing down such a heavy punishment, I do not even want my teacher to return to the royal court.","If he were to be punished like this again, Song Qiming was genuinely worried and a little afraid.","Song Jinzhao lowered her gaze and blinked. Before he is fully healed, let Lord Ye stay in our manor so it is easier to change his dressings.","Song Qiming nodded; he had been harboring the exact same thought.","He had not expected his sister to bring it up before he even mentioned it.","His teacher had no family. Now that he was injured to this extent, staying at the Princess's manor to recuperate was undoubtedly the best choice, especially since the best physicians in the world were right here.","Prince Ying's Manor.","Xiao Rongyan paced back and forth in the front hall, exasperated and furious.","I never expected Imperial Father to protect Eldest Brother to this extent. He never did this in the past.","In previous years, Ye Liangyu had reported even more severe crimes, yet the Emperor had never issued such heavy punishments, at most offering a few words of reprimand.","This time, however, he directly ordered thirty heavy strokes of the cane, and even had Fei Yanzhang beaten with fifty strokes. It was truly beyond all expectations.","A subordinate stood to the side, bowing slightly as he spoke. It must be because the Prince of Qi has gone blind. The Emperor feels pity for him, and thus defends him so fiercely.","Xiao Rongyan tilted his head back, his brows furrowed tightly together.","He said with deep resentment, With Imperial Father protecting him, my efforts have all been in vain.","The subordinate wore a fawning smile on his face.","It was not entirely in vain. At the very least, the Prince of Qi's reputation has been further ruined.","Xiao Rongyan glanced down at him. What does one Prince of Qi matter? The most important targets are the six princes in the palace.","He withdrew his gaze and looked meaningfully at the distant sky. We will take our time and not rush. I have plenty of time and patience."]},{"number":355,"title":"Chapter 355: The case was closed in one afternoon.","paragraphs":["Inside the Imperial Study, Xiao Chengjing quietly gazed at Prince Qi kneeling on the floor, his voice as calm as a placid lake.","\"Do you know your wrongs?\"","Xiao Rongche slowly raised his head, the black cloth binding his right eye looking exceptionally conspicuous.","Stripped of his luxurious and expensive royal attire, he looked just like a bandit or a pirate who had taken to the woods.","With a bit of a beard and a darker face, he could have grabbed a knife and gone robbing.","\"Your son knows his wrongs, but your son had no other choice.\"","He rested one hand on his chest, tears falling like rain, looking as if he could faint at any moment.","\"Even from this close, your son can already barely see Imperial Father's face clearly.\"","\"Gong Linjue told your son that the imperial physicians of Shuobei could save my left eye. I just do not want to become a blind man, I do not want to lose my sight completely.\"","Speaking of his pain, Xiao Rongche's heart twitched; neither his tears nor his expression were fake.","On the throne, Xiao Chengjing looked at his bitterly weeping eldest son, unable to help but think of his high-spirited appearance from before.","A trace of doubt appeared between his brows. \"Even Song Jinzhao said there was no way. Can the imperial physicians of Shuobei really save your left eye?\"","Hearing this, Xiao Rongche nodded frantically as if grasping at a lifesaver.","\"Gong Linjue said there was someone in Shuobei exactly like your son. He went blind in his left eye, but his right eye was saved.\"","Xiao Chengjing furrowed his brows tightly and sighed.","\"You could not even do this cleanly, letting others find out.\"","\"Since there is a reason behind this incident, Imperial Father will help you cover it up this time. If there is a next time, even I will not be able to protect you.\"","Xiao Rongche's eyes filled with hope as he kowtowed in gratitude. \"Thank you, Imperial Father. Your son promises there will not be a next time. If it were not for my eyes, I would not have wanted to do this either.\"","Xiao Chengjing waved his hand, irritated and not wanting to look anymore.","\"You may withdraw. When the imperial physician of Shuobei arrives, if he really can save your left eye, there is no need to send the person back.\"","A flash of surprise crossed Xiao Rongche's blurry eyes. After a moment of thought, he nodded in agreement.","\"Your son understands. When the time comes, the person will be sent into the palace.\"","After Xiao Rongche left the Imperial Study, the Emperor frowned and instructed Zhao Yande. \"Summon the Minister of Justice, Sui Zhuangling, for an audience.\"","\"Yes.\" Eunuch Zhao answered in a low voice and immediately walked out of the Imperial Study.","In less than half an hour, Sui Zhuangling hurried over with an uneasy heart.","He had just entered the room and knelt down when Xiao Chengjing spoke straightforwardly. \"Beloved Subject Sui, I am putting you in charge of the stolen potato case.\"","He threw three letters and a confession on the table. \"This is the physical evidence forged by Earl Zhongqin, and the confession of the person who delivered the letters. They are all Earl Zhongqin's people.\"","\"The person is currently locked in the prison of the Jingzhao Prefecture. After you take custody of the prisoner, interrogate him again and close this case as soon as possible. The imperial court needs a result.\"","Holding the letters and confession handed over by Eunuch Zhao, Sui Zhuangling already had the answer in his heart.","The Emperor's every sentence revolved around Earl Zhongqin, indicating that all the charges could only be borne by Earl Zhongqin.","The Li family could have their home raided and their clan exterminated, but Prince Qi had to be cleanly extracted from this.","He kowtowed solemnly and replied. \"This humble official obeys the decree.\"","After leaving the Imperial Study, Sui Zhuangling immediately went to the Jingzhao Prefecture and transferred the prisoner to the Ministry of Justice's prison.","Two hours later, he walked out of the dungeon holding a brand new confession.","That very night, Earl Zhongqin's estate was raided.","Fifty-six people were thrown into prison. The memorial was submitted overnight, and Xiao Chengjing approved it overnight.","They were to be beheaded and displayed to the public; not a single one was to be spared.","Ye Liangyu and Fei Yanzhang woke up early the next morning.","At this moment, the sky was not yet fully bright, and with the rain outside, it was dark and gloomy.","The moment they opened their eyes, the two of them felt a sharp pain. The bones in their entire lower bodies ached and trembled.","The maid guarding the pharmacy saw that the two had woken up, and one of them hurriedly ran out to call for people.","\"Eldest Young Master, the two lords are awake.\"","Song Qiming, who was having breakfast, put down his spoon and ran towards the pharmacy.","By the time he arrived, Young Master Fei, who had stayed overnight at the County Princess's estate, was already standing beside Fei Yanzhang's sickbed.","\"Father, how do you feel? Does it hurt badly?\"","Just as Fei Yanzhang was about to speak, a spasm of pain shot through his lower body. He bared his teeth in agony, and the words that reached his throat could only be swallowed back down.","He shook his head without speaking. After resting for a good while, he answered softly in a hoarse voice. \"It hurts a little when I don't move, but it hurts terribly when I do.\"","Young Master Fei bent down and gently supported Fei Yanzhang's arm. \"The County Princess said you injured your bones and cannot move. You must rest well, otherwise it will leave lasting effects.\""]},{"number":356,"title":"Chapter 356: Awakening, Utterly Disappointed","paragraphs":["Song Qiming crouched by Ye Liangyu's bed and whispered softly, Teacher, do not move just yet. Ah Jie will be here right away.","The scenes of the execution replayed in his mind. After a moment of silence, Ye Liangyu turned his head to look at Fei Yanzhang, who was lying on the next bed.","Brother Fei, I have dragged you down with me this time.","Fei Yanzhang squeezed his eyes shut and then opened them again.","Do not speak of dragging me down. I could not stomach this matter any more than you could.","What disappoints me even more is His Majesty. He has become deaf to counsel, covering up his faults and acting with absolute tyranny. If this continues, the country will no longer be a country, and the ruler no longer a ruler.","Father! Young Master Fei cried out in terror.","He looked nervously at the maidservants standing in the room, terrified that they might leak these words.","This was the crime of great disrespect; if anyone found out, they would be beheaded.","Suddenly recalling something, Ye Liangyu urgently asked Song Qiming, What happened with the case? Was it left unresolved, or...?","Song Qiming let out a soft sigh. His Majesty ordered the Minister of Justice, Sui Zhuangling, to investigate thoroughly. The case was closed last night. All the charges were pinned on Earl Zhongqin. The entire Li household is to be executed, and the sentence will be carried out at noon today.","Ye Liangyu's eyelashes trembled, and he pressed on unwillingly, Did Prince Qi receive no punishment at all?","Song Qiming's face darkened as he shook his head. None. Not a bit.","His hopes dashed, a wave of coldness surged through his entire body. Ye Liangyu felt as if he were lying in an ice cellar.","A rebellious thought popped into his mind uncontrollably.","Does a monarch who bends the law for personal gain still deserve to be emperor?","Not long after, Song Jinzhao and Song Shixue, dressed in short martial arts attire, walked over from the training room. The two skillfully put on their gloves, preparing for the examination.","Seeing that Song Jinzhao was about to lift the blanket to look at his buttocks, Fei Yanzhang hastily spoke up to stop her.","As he twisted his waist, a sharp pain shot through his tailbone, and his brows instantly furrowed into a tight knot.","County Princess, it would be better to find a male doctor to take a look.","Standard medical observations and questions were one thing, but now she was going to look at his backside. Given the strict boundaries between men and women, he was truly quite embarrassed.","Expressionless, Song Jinzhao grabbed a corner of the blanket and pulled it back.","In the eyes of a healer, there are no men or women. Whatever should or should not be seen, I already saw it all yesterday. Lord Fei, there is no need to be shy.","A chill struck his skin. Seeing his backside exposed before everyone, Fei Yanzhang buried his head in his arms, feeling completely mortified.","Young Master Fei stood nearby and said, County Princess, my father just said his wounds hurt a lot.","After finishing the examination, Song Jinzhao covered him back up with the blanket, took off her gloves, and tossed them into a basin.","With a fractured bone and so much flesh cut away, how could it not hurt? Using too much anesthetic is bad for wound recovery; he will just have to endure it.","Young Master Fei asked, Then can I take my father back to our manor now?","Song Jinzhao nodded. Change the dressing once a day. I will have someone pack the medicine for you to take back. If you do not have a doctor at the manor, Shixue can visit your home.","Fei Yanzhang looked at Song Shixue, who was four years younger than Song Jinzhao, and shook his head faster than a rattle-drum.","No need, no need. We have a doctor at the manor who can help me apply the medicine.","She could tell he was lying, but Song Jinzhao did not expose him.","Applying medicine was something any ordinary doctor could handle. If he was not willing, she would not force it.","I will visit your home in three days for a follow-up. For the time being, keep to a bland diet and strictly avoid stimulating foods.","The father and son nodded simultaneously.","Seeing that it was almost time to report for duty, Song Qiming called out to Ye Liangyu, Teacher, I will head to the Hanlin Academy first. We can discuss other matters when I return.","Ye Liangyu nodded, his voice somewhat heavy. With your teacher being punished, it is inevitable that others will direct their mockery and sarcasm at you. Be careful and cautious during this time.","Song Qiming nodded. Rest assured, Teacher. I will stay inside the Hanlin Academy and not go out. Even if others gossip, they will not be able to say it to my face."]},{"number":357,"title":"Chapter 357: Ye Liangyu and Fei Yanzhang's official positions have been temporarily replaced.","paragraphs":["A long while after he left, Fei Yanzhang suddenly spoke up.","\"Brother Ye, the princes in the palace are still young, and considering the Emperor's current attitude, it would be best if Qiming does not remain in the capital.\"","In front of the medicine cabinet, Song Jinzhao's fingers paused slightly as he reached for the ointment, a dark glint flashing through his eyes.","Ye Liangyu did not respond to Fei Yanzhang immediately. Instead, after pondering for a long time, he silently lowered his head.","After the rain stopped, Young Master Fei summoned two burly men to carry the stretcher out, one in front and one in back. He even specifically found the largest carriage available to ensure the entire stretcher could fit inside.","The moment Song Qiming stepped into the Hanlin Academy, everyone's gaze landed on him.","Confusion, worry, helplessness, and curiosity.","Various emotions collided together; the room felt like a giant dyeing vat, the path ahead completely shrouded in dense fog, making it impossible to see what lay before them.","Dongfang Yukun and Cui Zhengyang emerged from the mist, both of their faces etched with tension and concern.","\"Are Censor Ye and Lord Fei awake?\"","Dongfang Yukun and Cui Zhengyang had visited the County Princess's estate the night before; at that time, Ye Liangyu and Fei Yanzhang had not yet woken up.","Song Qiming swept his gaze over the others before withdrawing it.","\"They are awake. Now they just need to recover from their injuries.\"","The two let out a breath, their hanging hearts finally settling down.","Cui Zhengyang lowered his head and whispered softly into Song Qiming's ear.","\"The Emperor just issued a decree appointing Lord Cai as the acting Chancellor of the Hanlin Academy. The Censorate also received a decree, making Censor Bai the acting Palace Deputy Censor.\"","Song Qiming's voice was as quiet as a mosquito. He spoke with barely a breath, \"I knew before I came. Lord Fei told me.\"","His pupils dilating, Cui Zhengyang covered his mouth in surprise. \"Lord Fei already knew?\"","Song Qiming gave the two of them a nod.","The newly appointed acting Chancellor of the Hanlin Academy, Cai Pei, walked out from the inner hall. \"Compiler Song, come in with me.\"","Dongfang Yukun and Cui Zhengyang were no longer as tense as before. Hearing Cai Pei call Song Qiming inside, they were mostly just curious about what the matter could be.","Enduring everyone's stares, Song Qiming walked expressionlessly into the inner hall and closed the door behind him.","Sitting face-to-face in chairs, Cai Pei let out a heavy sigh and asked, \"When will Lord Fei's injuries heal?\"","Song Qiming pressed his chapped lips into a straight line, biting his lip twice with his front teeth before answering, \"He is injured too severely. He won't recover for at least two months, and he won't even be able to get out of bed in the short term.\"","He stared quietly at Cai Pei, wanting to see how he would react to these words.","Although Fei Yanzhang trusted Cai Pei greatly, Song Qiming dared not lower his guard.","In power struggles, if you relaxed your vigilance even slightly, you wouldn't even know how you died.","His teacher and Lord Fei had simply trusted the Emperor too much; their expectations were too high, which was why they had fallen so miserably.","Cai Pei sighed again. With a face full of exhaustion, he closed his eyes and only opened them after a long time.","\"Did Lord Fei leave any instructions?\"","Song Qiming shook his head. \"He only said that the Emperor would likely have you temporarily act as Chancellor of the Hanlin Academy. He told you not to visit him for the time being and to wait until the storm blows over.\"","Cai Pei sighed for the third time, his brows furrowed tightly, the emotions in his eyes like a tangled mess.","\"I understand.\" After speaking, he raised his head to look at Song Qiming. \"Is Lord Fei still at the County Princess's estate?\"","Song Qiming blinked. \"He should have returned to the Fei Manor by now.\"","Cai Pei nodded in silence.","The inner room fell into complete silence, and Song Qiming didn't know whether he should leave or stay.","After waiting for a good while, the other man seemed to finally snap out of his daze and waved his hand at Song Qiming. \"Go out first, and do not tell Dongfang Yukun and Cui Zhengyang what I discussed with you.\"","Song Qiming gave a slight nod, opened the door, and casually returned to his seat to handle his official duties as if nothing had happened."]},{"number":358,"title":"Chapter 358: Execution Ground","paragraphs":["At a quarter to noon, the road leading to the execution ground was crowded with onlookers.","The moment the guards escorted the prison carts into view, an overwhelming barrage of rotten cabbage leaves and foul-smelling eggs flew toward them.","As the eggs smashed, a sour, putrid stench permeated the air. The people inside the prison carts did not even dare to lift their heads.","\"You treacherous dogs, you deserve to rot in hell!\"","\"Traitors deserve to die! Even death by a thousand cuts wouldn't be enough!\"","\"...\"","The furious curses nearly drowned out the members of the Li household; the spit alone could have filled a bathing barrel.","Earl Zhongqin was locked in the first cart. With the weeping of his wife and children lingering in his ears from behind, he did not utter a single word in his own defense.","It wasn't until they arrived at the execution ground and he was forced to kneel on the ground that Earl Zhongqin raised his head, searching the crowd for the figure of Prince Qi.","Before long, the supervising official looked up at the sun hanging directly overhead. Judging that the time had come, he picked up the execution token and tossed it to the ground.","\"Execute them!\"","The wails of his family echoed in his ears, and the last glimmer of light in his eyes gradually faded.","As his neck was placed on the chopping block, Earl Zhongqin closed his eyes in deep remorse, his entire body trembling as he awaited the arrival of death.","If he had known they would be discovered, he never should have helped in the first place.","Prince Qi remained completely unscathed while he took the fall for everything, dragging his entire family down to be executed. He was filled with endless regret.","The executioner picked up a jar of liquor, took a massive gulp, and sprayed it over the butcher's blade. The liquid dripped onto Earl Zhongqin's face, blurring the line between the wine and his tears.","The blade swung down, and a bloody head rolled onto the ground.","Inside the imperial palace, Concubine Jin, who was standing at the entrance of the Palace of Eternal Longevity, suddenly felt a sharp palpitation in her chest.","She gazed in the direction outside the palace, her face already streaming with tears.","\"Brother, I'm sorry. I have failed you.\"","Not long after, a figure sprinted back to Prince Qi's manor.","He knelt before the couch and reported in a low voice, \"Your Highness, all fifty-six members of the Li household have been beheaded.\"","Xiao Rongche, sitting upright on the bed, did not shed a single tear. Clenching his fists tightly, he asked, \"Did Uncle say anything at the very end?\"","The guard buried his head against the floor, his body trembling.","\"Earl Zhongqin did not say a word. He only cast a glance into the crowd right before the execution.\"","An entire family wiped out—how sorrowful and tragic. Those severed heads with wide-open eyes seemed to appear right before his very eyes.","Xiao Rongche closed his eyes and let out a long breath, forcing himself to calm down.","\"Imperial Father has already promised not to pursue this matter. Where are the imperial physicians from the Shuobei Kingdom? Write a letter to urge them immediately. This time, no one will dare to interfere.\"","The guard dared not look up and replied in a muffled voice, \"Yes, your subordinate will do it at once.\"","The fresh blood on the ground at the execution grounds was washed away with well water.","Not far away, Song Shixue watched the dispersing crowd with a complex expression. The anger on everyone's faces had already vanished.","\"Sister, is this really where it ends? The true culprit is clearly still at large.\"","Song Jinzhao's eyes gleamed with murderous intent, as if she had already locked onto her target.","\"Being at large is nothing. What's truly sickening is that the grain taxes the commoners pay every year are used to feed Xiao Rongche. Silks, satins, and exotic delicacies... he deserves to rot in hell.\"","Song Shixue frowned in distress.","\"With the Emperor around, Prince Qi will never be beheaded no matter what crimes he commits. The ones who suffer will only be others. Lord Ye and Lord Fei are living examples of this.\"","A cold, curved smile crept onto Song Jinzhao's lips.","\"Water can carry a boat, but it can also capsize it. When Xiao Chengjing is no longer the Emperor, Prince Qi will naturally have no one to protect him.\"","Song Shixue turned her head to look at Song Jinzhao, unable to stop herself from pondering the meaning behind those words.","The Emperor is no longer the Emperor... unless someone usurps the throne and kills him."]},{"number":359,"title":"Chapter 359: Finding Scolding at a Wedding Banquet","paragraphs":["This storm came to an abrupt halt after Earl Zhongqin was beheaded in public, and following closely behind was the wedding day of Princess Yongjia and the Duke of Qing.","A grand dowry stretching for ten miles entered the Zhenguo Duke's estate, and just the copper coins scattered along the wedding procession route amounted to thousands of taels of silver.","Aside from the Emperor and Empress, who did not attend, all the high-ranking officials and imperial relatives in the capital were present.","Including the military generals, the hundred tables were barely enough to seat everyone.","After the wedding ceremony concluded, the four Song siblings were arranged at two different tables.","Song Qiming took Song Anhao to sit at the men's banquet, while Song Jinzhao and Song Shixue sat at the women's banquet.","A piercing gaze fell upon Song Jinzhao through the gauze curtain. Noticing someone watching from the opposite side, Song Shixue whispered, \"Sister, Prince Ying is looking this way.\"","Song Jinzhao calmly picked up her wine cup, seemingly completely unbothered by the other party's hostility.","\"I know. He is just a stray dog, ignore him.\"","Xiao Chengjing was unfit to be emperor, and Xiao Rongyan, this prince, was even less worthy of her attention. Since some things had already begun, they would not stop.","Not long after, Madam Zhenguo came over with a wine cup to toast the female guests.","\"Today is my son's grand wedding day. Please eat and drink well, everyone. If there is any lack of hospitality, feel free to ask the maids.\"","Madam Zhenguo, her face glowing with joy, drank the clear wine in her cup, and the crowd stood up one after another to return the toast.","\"The Duke of Qing and Princess Yongjia are a perfect match of talent and beauty, a match made in heaven. Surely, it won't be long before the Duke's estate welcomes a new addition to the family.\"","The older women brought up children right away, as if Princess Yongjia could get pregnant this very day.","However, these words touched Madam Zhenguo's heart. She grinned and exchanged pleasantries, \"I certainly hope so. Chu Yun, like his father, married late. If they can have a child early, I will finally be able to enjoy playing with my grandchild.\"","Song Jinzhao sat in her chair listening, smiling but saying nothing.","Unexpectedly, after Madam Zhenguo left, the gauze curtain separating the men's and women's banquets was suddenly pulled open from the opposite side.","Prince Ying walked toward Song Jinzhao with a wine cup and malicious intent.","Song Qiming, sitting in the middle of the men's banquet, had just put down his wine cup. Seeing this, he immediately picked up Song Anhao and hurried over.","\"County Princess Linghui is in a good mood today. It's a pity that my eldest brother is completely blind and couldn't come today.\"","\"Come to think of it, it's quite strange. The County Princess has superb medical skills and could even bring the Zhenguo Duke back from the brink of death. Prince Qi merely injured his eyes, yet the County Princess claimed she couldn't save him. Those who don't know better might think you hold a grudge and are deliberately refusing to save him.\"","The banquet, previously filled with smiling pleasantries, instantly fell dead silent. Everyone panicked, and no one dared to speak.","What did His Highness Prince Ying mean by this?","Was he insinuating that County Princess Linghui deliberately refused to treat Prince Qi?","Song Jinzhao smiled faintly, stood up, and said to Xiao Rongyan, \"His Highness Prince Qi's left eye is not blind yet, but His Highness Prince Ying claims he is completely blind. Do you sit around your manor all day hoping your own brother goes blind?\"","\"...\" The women at the table widened their eyes in terror, staring at Song Jinzhao's face in disbelief.","Was that something she could say? County Princess Linghui was far too bold!","Before Xiao Rongyan could retort, the curve of Song Jinzhao's lips widened.","\"Merely injured his eyes? Your Highness speaks far too lightly. I wonder how Prince Qi would feel if he heard this.\"","With a change of expression, Song Jinzhao feigned ignorance and asked in confusion, \"Furthermore, why would this County Princess hold a grudge and refuse to save him? Did Prince Qi do something to wrong me? How come I don't know about it? Your Highness looks like you know something; could you tell me?\"","At the same table, seven or eight pairs of eyes darted around wildly, exchanging significant glances with whoever they made eye contact with.","Truly worthy of being the woman who surpassed the Duke of Qing and defeated Prince Wei of the Northern Shuo Kingdom. County Princess Linghui was incredibly tough and refused to swallow even the slightest grievance."]},{"number":360,"title":"Chapter 360: The King of Qi, Enraged, Drives Away the Popular Figure","paragraphs":["Song Qiming immediately stopped in his tracks, silently put Song Anhao down, took his hand, and walked behind Song Jinzhao to back her up.","With fierce eyes and a highly raised chin, there was not a trace of fear on his face.","Xiao Rongyan was so furious he almost snapped his teeth.","Taking a deep breath, he forced the stifling frustration in his chest down into his stomach to endure it.","\"How would I know about the grudge between you and Prince Qi? I was merely curious as to why the County Princess couldn't cure him. It seems your reputation as a divine doctor is nothing but a sham.\"","Song Jinzhao retorted in a calm tone, \"I have never claimed to be a divine doctor. It is merely an empty title given by the common people who think too highly of me. Only a god can cure any disease, and how could a mere mortal like me dare to compare myself to the divine? Your Highness would do well to listen less to such baseless rumors.\"","Looking around and seeing everyone staring at him as if watching a play, the intense sense of humiliation made Xiao Rongyan clench his fists so hard they nearly shattered.","To be openly contradicted in public by a lowly born County Princess of a different surname meant she completely disregarded him as a prince.","\"Your Highness Prince Ying, this is the women's banquet area. You have come the wrong way.\"","Duke Zhenguo walked over with a smile, lifting the curtain and gesturing for Xiao Rongyan to return to the men's seating area.","This single sentence made the gazes of all the female guests present turn meaningful once again.","He hadn't taken the wrong way at all; he had clearly barged in on purpose to cause trouble for County Princess Linghui.","Today was the wedding banquet of Princess Yongjia and the Duke of Qing.","As an older brother causing a scene at his own sister's wedding, His Highness Prince Ying truly had no sense of propriety.","Xiao Rongyan sharply flicked his sleeves and left the Duke Zhenguo's estate with a dark face, not looking back once.","Seeing this, the crowd began to whisper among themselves.","\"I didn't expect the conflict between County Princess Linghui and His Highness Prince Ying to be so deep. There will definitely be more drama to watch in the future.\"","A woman at the next table discreetly signaled toward Song Jinzhao's back with her eyes. \"When County Princess Linghui was assassinated back then, everyone knew in their hearts who the real mastermind was. The grudge was forged long ago.\"","\"Do you think County Princess Linghui really refused to treat Prince Qi's eye on purpose?\"","Another woman curled her lips and said disdainfully, \"Who knows? But if it were me, I wouldn't want to treat him either.\"","Why would you save someone who wanted to kill you? You'd only wish for them to die faster.","The crowd fell silent, a hundred different thoughts racing through their minds.","This just proved that doctors were the last people you should provoke, especially highly skilled ones, lest you fall gravely ill one day and have no choice but to wait for death.","They wondered if the imperial physicians from the Shuobei Kingdom could save Prince Qi's left eye.","If he truly became blind, he would be a ruined prince. Not to mention losing any chance at the throne, what difference was there between being unable to see and being dead?","After the wedding banquet ended, the conversation between Song Jinzhao and Prince Ying quickly spread.","Eventually, not only did Xiao Chengjing in the imperial palace learn of it, but even Xiao Rongche, who was staying in his own princely estate, heard the news.","He flipped the table over with a single slap, his body trembling uncontrollably.","\"I think he's just gloating! How dare he use my eye as a topic of gossip! Xiao Rongyan, you've really done it now!\"","His towering rage terrified everyone in the Prince Qi's estate so much that they didn't dare to move. They felt a chill around their necks, as if their heads would roll in the very next second.","Seeing that no one spoke up, Xiao Rongche roared loudly, \"Why hasn't the imperial physician that Gong Linjue promised arrived yet?\"","\"Has the letter been delivered? If they still don't come, send someone to the Shuobei Kingdom to hurry them up!\"","Everyone fell to their knees in unison, not even daring to breathe loudly.","A trusted aide who had rushed over to calm him dropped to his knees with a thud. Ignoring the pain, he crawled over to Xiao Rongche.","\"Your Highness, the letter has already been sent urgently by courier. Perhaps the imperial physician from the Shuobei Kingdom is already on the way. Please wait just a little longer.\"","Xiao Rongche stomped his foot forcefully to vent his frustration.","He roared in anger, his eyes filled with sorrow and despair.","\"Wait, wait, wait! Gong Linjue has been gone for almost half a year! Why hasn't the imperial physician arrived yet? Why hasn't he come?!\""]},{"number":361,"title":"Chapter 361: The Emperor of Shuobei Kingdom is not even worthy of holding his elder sister's shoes.","paragraphs":["Three days later, an armored soldier rode his horse into the capital, kicking up a cloud of dust that made people sneeze.","The city guards covered their mouths and noses, their eyes watering profusely.","\"What is going on? It looks like the Jinglei Army.\"","Another guard said, \"The envoy delegation from the Shuobei Kingdom left only half a year ago. Why is someone from the border here again? Has a war broken out?\"","They exchanged glances, the anxiety in their hearts difficult to dispel for the moment.","Half an hour later, the Minister of War, Wu Jianzheng, with a bitter expression and holding a bamboo tube, arrived at the door of the imperial study to seek an audience with the Emperor.","Xiao Chengjing remained silent for a long time after reading the report.","Asking to marry Song Jinzhao as an imperial concubine, the Shuobei Kingdom really had a good scheme going.","\"Beloved Subject Wu, what do you think of this matter?\"","Wu Jianzheng said without hesitation, \"To reply to Your Majesty, He Mingyuan's intentions are glaringly obvious. The Linghui Princess of the County absolutely cannot go for a marriage alliance.\"","Xiao Chengjing tapped his fingers repeatedly on the table. \"I certainly know what the Emperor of the Shuobei Kingdom is thinking, but how should we refuse?\"","\"A marriage alliance between two countries is outwardly to stabilize diplomatic relations. If we refuse, it will inevitably leave them with something to use against us, and it won't sound good when word gets out.\"","Wu Jianzheng furrowed his brows and pondered left and right. After a long while, he spoke tentatively.","\"Marriage alliances between two countries usually involve a princess or a daughter of the imperial clan. Although Song Jinzhao is a Princess of the County, she is not of the imperial family. As long as she disagrees, and Your Majesty puts on an attitude of not wanting to force her, refusing the marriage alliance will be perfectly logical.\"","Xiao Chengjing stroked his chin and considered it for a long time, unable to make a decision in his heart for the moment.","\"You may step down first. Do not tell anyone else about this matter for now.\"","Wu Jianzheng first nodded, then asked again, \"Not even telling the Linghui Princess of the County?\"","Xiao Chengjing nodded. \"No need to tell her. I have my own plans for this matter. Everything can wait until the Shuobei Kingdom's marriage proposal delegation arrives in the capital.\"","At the entrance of the desolate Ye Manor, the messenger soldier, who had just gone back to change his clothes, knocked on the main door of the Ye Manor.","\"Is Lord Ye in the manor? My general has something for me to tell Lord Ye.\"","The gatekeeper asked in confusion, \"May I ask which general it is?\"","The soldier replied, \"General Qin Guo, the Commander of the Jinglei Army.\"","Hearing this, the gatekeeper hurriedly opened the door to let the person into the manor.","\"My lord is not in the manor. Please wait a moment, sir. I will go call Steward Yunhe.\"","Half a cup of tea's time later, Yunhe walked briskly into the front hall.","\"Sir, I wonder what General Qin Guo is looking for my lord for?\"","The soldier did not answer Yunhe's question, but continued to inquire about Ye Liangyu's whereabouts.","\"Is Lord Ye still on duty at the Censorate? When will he be back?\"","Yunhe looked him up and down and, seeing his serious face as if he had an important matter, finally explained, \"My lord is staying at the Princess of the County's manor during this time. If the matter is very important, I will take you there now.\"","Without a second thought, the soldier said straightforwardly, \"The Young General specifically instructed that the letter must be delivered into Lord Ye's hands personally. Please take me there, Steward.\"","Yunhe nodded. Without going through the front door, he led the person out the back door and arrived at the Princess of the County's manor.","Half an hour later, Ye Liangyu, who was lying on the sickbed, gradually darkened in complexion after opening the letter.","By the time he finished reading it, his eyes had turned completely dark, as thick as ink.","Seeing this, Song Shixue, who was pounding medicine, asked curiously.","\"Lord Ye, has something happened?\"","Ye Liangyu put the letter down absentmindedly. \"The Emperor of the Shuobei Kingdom wants your elder sister to be his imperial concubine.\"","With a clang, the iron pestle for pounding medicine smashed into the stone jar, and Song Shixue stood frozen in place.","After blinking and snapping out of it, she quickly ran out from behind the cabinet, moving so fast that her figure became a blur.","After picking up the letter by Ye Liangyu's hand and reading it quickly, Song Shixue was so angry that her chest felt tight.","She opened her mouth and cursed loudly, \"A toad wanting to eat swan meat!\"","\"What kind of thing does that Emperor of the Shuobei Kingdom think he is, daring to covet my sister! He is not even worthy of carrying my sister's shoes.\"","In a fit of anger, with a ripping sound, the letter in Song Shixue's hands was torn into two halves."]},{"number":362,"title":"Chapter 362: I want Qi Ming to be the Southwest Provincial Governor.","paragraphs":["Ye Liangyu hurriedly caught the letter that Song Shixue had thrown away. \"Keep your voice down. No one else knows about this yet.\"","Song Shixue clenched her jaw, her heart filled with repulsion and disgust at the thought of a marriage alliance.","\"I am going to tell my sister. She absolutely cannot be sent off for a marriage alliance.\"","In Song Shixue's eyes, no one in the world was worthy of Song Jinzhao, let alone marrying into the Shuobei Kingdom to be a concubine.","If she really married over there, the moment the two countries went to war, her sister would be the first to die.","Watching Song Shixue run out, Ye Liangyu read the letter from beginning to end once more.","\"You all head back first. Do not spread a word of this before the imperial court makes an official announcement.\"","The soldier cupped his hands and took his leave. \"Rest assured, My Lord. General Qin specifically instructed us on this before we even left the border.\"","Ye Liangyu looked toward Yunhe. \"Take him back, and make sure no one sees you.\"","Yunhe gave a slight nod. \"This humble servant understands. We came in through the back door when we arrived.\"","Ye Liangyu nodded in satisfaction.","Song Shixue ran all the way to the study. Pushing open the door, she found Qingshuang and Lanxi both inside.","Seeing her burst in so suddenly, Song Jinzhao asked in confusion, \"What is wrong?\"","Song Shixue took a deep breath and slowed her steps, her heart heavy.","She walked toward Song Jinzhao with a worried expression.","\"Sister, Lord Ye just received a letter sent by General Qin from the border. The Emperor of Shuobei wants to ask for your hand in marriage to make you his imperial consort. The marriage envoy is already on the way.\"","Lanxi's pupils shrank, and she cried out in shock as if struck by lightning.","\"He Mingyuan wants to marry the County Princess? How is that possible! Even if it is a marriage alliance, it should be a royal princess.\"","Song Shixue nodded vigorously. \"That is exactly what the letter says. The memorial has already been delivered to the Ministry of War, so the Emperor definitely knows by now. What if he makes my sister go for the marriage alliance?\"","The eyes of all three instantly focused on Song Jinzhao, only to see her staring silently at the tabletop.","A moment later, Song Jinzhao stood up and walked out.","Upon arriving at the apothecary room, Ye Liangyu silently handed her the letter.","\"County Princess, your martial arts are formidable and your medical skills are exquisite. Neither the Emperor nor the civil and military officials would want to send you to the Shuobei Kingdom. This matter is highly unlikely to succeed, so you need not worry too much.\"","With a talent like Song Jinzhao, even though she was a woman, the Emperor would never be willing to give her to an enemy nation and freely hand them such an advantage.","After reading the letter, Song Jinzhao held it over a candle and burned it to ashes.","\"I am not worried. I just feel that having someone holding me by the throat is a very unpleasant feeling.\"","\"Qiming has been in the Hanlin Academy for two years now. Does My Lord have any way to have him transferred to a provincial post?\"","Ye Liangyu looked at Song Jinzhao with an astonished expression.","Was she trying to avoid the conflicts of the capital?","\"Where does the County Princess want him to go?\"","Song Jinzhao turned her head, a sharp glint flashing in her eyes.","\"The Southwest.\"","Ye Liangyu gasped, his mind buzzing.","\"County Princess, the Southwest is not a good place. The Yang clan of Panzhou, the Mu clan of Ningzhou, and the various foreign tribes—none of them are to be trifled with.\"","\"If you truly wish to avoid the court's conflicts, he could go to Jiangnan for a few years. The Southwest is far too dangerous.\"","Song Jinzhao replied, \"Wealth and honor are sought amidst danger. How can you catch tiger cubs without entering the tiger's den? Qiming is currently a sixth-rank compiler in the Hanlin Academy. Without a few exceptionally great merits, rapid promotion in a short time is absolutely impossible.\"","\"I heard that the Administration Commissioner of the Southwest, Gu Zhongxun, will retire in four years. I want Qiming to fight for that position.\"","The Southwest was far from the capital and had the foreign tribes to act as a shield.","As long as one could control the military and political affairs of a region, certain things would become much easier to accomplish.","Ye Liangyu swallowed hard in shock.","Having Qiming become the Administration Commissioner of the Southwest in four years—was that not a bit too fast?"]},{"number":363,"title":"Chapter 363: I Am Willing to Go to the Southwest","paragraphs":["In the evening, Song Qiming returned from the Hanlin Academy.","Before he could even sit down, Song Shixue pulled him aside and quietly told him about the political marriage.","\"What! They want A-jie to go for a political marriage?\" Song Qiming sprang up like a frog, his eyes wide with shock.","Song Shixue nodded vigorously with a heavy expression. \"The marriage proposal delegation is already on its way.\"","Song Qiming opened and closed his mouth repeatedly. He shook his head, then sprinted toward the apothecary without looking back, as if his pants were on fire.","A-jie could not be married off. Absolutely not.","With a loud bang, Song Qiming forcefully pushed the door open, startling Ye Liangyu, who was lying on his stomach on the sickbed reading a book.","He jerked violently and nearly fell off the bed.","\"Panicking like this, where is the composure I taught you?\"","Song Qiming's eyes burned with anxiety, his gaze as intense as a raging fire.","\"Teacher, is what Shixue just said true or false? The Shuobei Kingdom wants A-jie for a political marriage. Can it be stopped?\"","Looking at the anxious Song Qiming, Ye Liangyu couldn't help but recall what Song Jinzhao had said that afternoon.","Sixteen years old, and only twenty in four years. The Provincial Administration Commissioner of the Southwest—isn't he too young? Gender aside, it would make more sense for Song Jinzhao to take the position.","\"Look at you, all in a panic. Your sister is much more composed than you; she didn't even furrow her brow.\"","Ignoring the scolding, Song Qiming began to analyze the situation.","\"Teacher, A-jie's martial arts are highly formidable. Gong Lin is absolutely no match for her. The Emperor of Shuobei must have found out and wants to marry her for that reason. She might even be killed the moment she arrives in Shuobei. This marriage absolutely cannot happen.\"","Ye Liangyu rolled his eyes at Song Qiming. \"Of course I know what the Shuobei Kingdom is plotting. Not only do I know, but the Emperor knows as well. Rest assured, this marriage will never go through.\"","Song Qiming furrowed his brows. After calming down, he sat on a stool and thought for a long time without speaking.","Seeing him like this, Ye Liangyu thought of what Fei Yanzhang had said and what Song Jinzhao had said, and gradually came to a decision.","\"Your sister wants you to leave the Hanlin Academy and go to the Southwest to serve as an official. What do you think?\"","Hearing Ye Liangyu's words clearly, Song Qiming suddenly raised his head, his eyes filled with surprise.","\"A-jie wants me to go to the Southwest?\"","Ye Liangyu gave a slight nod. \"The Emperor's mind is hard to fathom, and the political situation in the court changes too quickly. If you want to avoid conflict, leaving the capital for a while is a good idea.\"","\"The Southwest is vast and impoverished, with foreign tribes governing themselves. It can be said that danger lurks everywhere. But alongside danger comes great opportunity. The foreign tribes in the Southwest have always been a major threat to the imperial court. If you can solve this problem, it will be an unparalleled achievement.\"","\"The County Princess has high expectations for you. She wants you to take over the position of Provincial Administration Commissioner of the Southwest in four years.\"","Song Qiming was stunned for a moment, but he didn't have to think long before saying, \"Since it is A-jie's wish, I am willing to go to the Southwest.\"","With his decision made, Song Qiming began to ponder.","\"Many officials are unwilling to go to the Southwest, so there should still be vacant positions. I will go ask around tomorrow and see what posts are available.\"","Seeing Song Qiming agree so readily, Ye Liangyu opened his mouth, somewhat at a loss for words.","\"This concerns your future political career. Don't you need to think about it some more?\"","Song Qiming shook his head. \"Since it's A-jie's intention, she definitely has her reasons.\"","\"To be honest, Teacher, I've been thinking these past few days. A-jie has offended Prince Qi and Prince Ying, and now the Emperor's attitude has changed as well. If they ever make a move against A-jie again, the outcome might not be like before. So, I think leaving the capital now is a good thing.\"","Their eyes met, and Ye Liangyu noticed that when Song Qiming spoke of the Emperor, his eyes no longer held the passion and reverence they once did.","They had been replaced by suspicion and wariness.","Thinking about how the Emperor had ordered him and Fei Yanzhang to be caned to protect Prince Qi, nearly costing them their lives, Ye Liangyu's finally eased mood became depressed again, and he looked somewhat dispirited.","\"Since both you and the County Princess have this idea, then go do it.\"","\"According to convention, you were supposed to stay in the Hanlin Academy for a full three years before being transferred or retained. Now it has only been two years, and the time for the imperial court's selection of officials has already passed this year. Even if there are vacancies in the Southwest, you can't just be transferred on a whim. This matter still requires careful planning.\"","\"More importantly, the marriage proposal delegation is already on its way to the capital. Whether the Emperor wants to agree or not, as long as this matter is not resolved, he will not let your sister leave the capital.\"","Song Qiming knitted his brows tightly, his mind in turmoil.","Troubles came one after another. After coming to the capital, things were not as relaxed and happy as when they were in Anyang Prefecture.","His official rank was still too low; he couldn't help with anything."]},{"number":364,"title":"Chapter 364: Dongfang Yukun Secretly Brings News","paragraphs":["\"Eldest Young Master, the meal has been set in the front hall. The County Princess asks you to go over,\" a maid ran over and reported.","At the same time, the servants from the kitchen happened to bring over the food.","Ye Liangyu could not get up; these past few days, he had been taking his meals alone in the apothecary.","Song Qiming took a deep breath, trying to dispel the stifling feeling in his chest, but the heavy feeling returned right after he exhaled.","Unable to shake off his gloom, Song Qiming bid farewell to Ye Liangyu in a depressed mood, \"Teacher, I will go eat first. I'll come find you later.\"","Arriving at the front hall, Song Anhao, who had been waiting for a long time, raised his chin and complained, \"Brother, what took you so long? The chicken claws are freezing cold.\"","Song Qiming was in a bad mood. After a brief, perfunctory reply of \"I had something to discuss with my teacher,\" he cast his gaze upon Song Jinzhao.","Seeing her calm expression, just like usual, Song Qiming's heart grew even heavier.","The meal was eaten without any taste. Just as they put down their chopsticks, Song Jinzhao stood up and said, \"Come with me to the study.\"","Song Anhao, who was still gnawing on a chicken claw, looked at Song Jinzhao and Song Qiming in confusion.","How did they finish eating so quickly? He had just started, only taking two or three bites from his bowl of rice.","\"Second Sister, what's wrong with Big Brother and the others? They seem to be in a bad mood.\"","Song Shixue's throat felt tight.","She blinked, picked up her chopsticks, and placed some food in Song Anhao's bowl. \"They have matters to discuss. Second Sister will eat with you.\"","\"Bang, bang, bang.\"","Someone knocked on the manor's gate. The gatekeeper opened it just a crack. \"Who is it?\"","The sky was almost dark; who would come visiting at this hour?","Dongfang Yukun was wearing a cloak. Seeing the door open, he pulled down the veil covering his face.","\"It's me. I'm looking for your Eldest Young Master.\"","The gatekeeper raised his eyebrows in surprise. \"Young Master Dongfang, why are you dressed like this?\"","Dongfang Yukun turned sideways and squeezed in through the gap in the door.","\"The wind outside is strong and a bit cold, so I wore a little extra. Where is Qiming? I have business with him.\"","The gatekeeper closed the door and slid the latch into place.","\"The Eldest Young Master is in the front hall having dinner with the County Princess. I will take you there.\"","Dongfang Yukun nodded as he walked inside, his steps so fast he was almost running.","The gatekeeper quickened his pace to lead the way, a trace of doubt in his heart.","What was going on? Walking so fast, as if fleeing for his life.","As they neared the front hall, a sharp-eyed maid immediately went in to report.","\"Second Miss, Young Master Dongfang is here.\"","Song Shixue put down her chopsticks and stood up to look outside.","The orange candlelight shone on his face; his entire being radiated the word anxious.","Seeing an outsider arrive, Song Anhao also put down his chopsticks.","He jumped down from his chair to greet him, \"Brother Dongfang.\"","Not seeing Song Qiming and Song Jinzhao, Dongfang Yukun immediately asked Song Shixue, \"Second Miss Song, where are the County Princess and Qiming? I have an urgent matter for them.\"","Song Shixue replied, \"They just finished eating and went to the study. Sit down and wait for a moment, I will have someone call them right away.\"","Dongfang Yukun nodded.","He did not sit, but kept pacing back and forth at the door.","The two who had not yet reached the study were called back by Heye.","Seeing them arrive, Dongfang Yukun rushed up at lightning speed and pulled Song Qiming to the side of a pillar.","He covered his mouth with his hand and whispered, \"My father just told me that the Emperor of Shuobei wants to marry the County Princess and make her his concubine. The marriage proposal delegation is already on its way. The Emperor hasn't made a decision yet and said he will wait to discuss it when the delegation arrives. There is still more than a month left. You must quickly have the County Princess find a good husband and marry him, so she can avoid being sent to Shuobei for a political marriage.\"","\"Do this secretly. The faster, the better. You must make it a done deal.\""]},{"number":365,"title":"Chapter 365: Not Planning to Get Married for Now","paragraphs":["The fierce wind howled past, its wailing echoing through the courtyard.","While the others could not hear what Dongfang Yukun was saying, Song Jinzhao, with her keen hearing, heard every word clearly.","The Ministry of War had received the news at the hour of Wei, and the Dongfang family found out in just an afternoon. Even with Xiao Chengjing's gag order in place, they must have someone planted in the palace.","Hearing Dongfang Yukun say this, Song Qiming's first reaction was one of deep gratitude.","For the other party to willingly and secretly pass on a message about something the Emperor had forbidden to be spoken of was already taking a great risk.","\"Getting married right now definitely won't work. No matter who we find, the news will spread, unless it's someone with no parents who doesn't need to host a wedding banquet.\"","Dongfang Yukun scratched his head in frustration.","The idea of marriage was something he had thought up on the spur of the moment on his way here; he truly hadn't considered it too deeply.","\"That's true. As long as a wedding is being prepared, the news will get out, unless we discuss it with the other party, close the doors to bow to heaven and earth, and then go straight to the bridal chamber.\"","The more Dongfang Yukun thought about it, the better the idea seemed.","He let go of the arm he had wrapped around Song Qiming's shoulder and, ignoring the others, began pacing in circles. He ran through every unmarried young man he knew in his head, and finally grabbed Song Qiming's arm, his eyes shining.","\"What about Cui Zhengyang? His age is suitable, his looks are passable, and he can barely be considered a match for the County Princess.\"","Song Qiming's mouth twitched, somewhat at a loss for how to answer.","Song Jinzhao walked over, her face full of helplessness.","\"You two are playing matchmaker here, but have you asked the person involved?\"","Dongfang Yukun, looking slightly awkward, put his hands behind his back. \"County Princess, you heard all of that?\"","Song Jinzhao nodded solemnly. \"Don't even think about Cui Zhengyang.\"","\"If he marries me at a time like this, he can forget about his official career for the rest of his life. After so many years, the Cui family has finally managed to send an heir into the court; let's not ruin the man.\"","She still had many things to do, and getting married was not within her current considerations.","Dongfang Yukun pursed his lips. \"If Cui Zhengyang won't do, then we'll find someone else. The Shuobei Kingdom is not a good place. If the Emperor decrees that you must go for a political marriage, I'm afraid you will never return in this lifetime.\"","Anyone with a discerning eye knew that the two countries would eventually go to war again. Marrying over there meant, at best, losing your husband and becoming a widow, and at worst, dying without a trace.","As Song Qiming's best friend, Dongfang Yukun truly did not want Song Jinzhao to be sent off for a political marriage.","Song Jinzhao smiled faintly. \"Things haven't reached that point yet. Let's wait and see.\"","Dongfang Yukun looked at Song Qiming.","Song Qiming shrugged, an expression on his face that said since his older sister disagreed, they had no choice but to drop it.","Dongfang Yukun understood and sighed helplessly. \"Alright. At worst, when the time comes, I'll have my father lead the civil and military officials to oppose it together. They still have some prestige in the court.\"","Song Jinzhao smiled gently, shaking her head, the emotion in her eyes akin to looking at a younger generation.","Dongfang Yukun left not long after.","In the study, Song Jinzhao looked at the map on the wall.","Routes, cities, and local factions all seemed to begin reconstructing before her eyes.","Song Qiming said with some remorse, \"If I had known the Emperor would turn out like this, it would have been better if he never had a child in the first place. That way, Teacher and Lord Fei wouldn't have been beaten.\"","Song Jinzhao reached out and brushed her hand over the southwest section of the map. \"The father and his two sons are cut from the same cloth. The result would be roughly the same, only the targets of their attacks would be different.\"","Song Qiming sighed helplessly. \"Going to the southwest to stay for a few years is fine too. It would be best to wait until the other princes grow up before coming back; maybe things will be better then.\"","Song Jinzhao turned around and looked at Song Qiming, her face completely serious as she said, \"Rather than relying on others, it is better to rely on oneself. I proposed going to the southwest not to stall for time, but because I have other plans.\""]},{"number":366,"title":"Chapter 366: Frightened Song Qiming, the Difficulty of Rebellion Is Great","paragraphs":["Outside, it began to rain. The raindrops pattered against the window, sounding like the frantic, unsettling beat of a death drum.","What other plans could there be besides avoiding the conflict? Song Qiming looked at Song Jinzhao with a puzzled expression.","\"Sister, what do you mean by relying on ourselves?\"","The Emperor held the power of life and death over everyone; whoever he wanted dead would die. There was simply no way to resist.","Song Jinzhao stared intently at Song Qiming, her calm eyes hiding a surging, violent storm.","\"If the ruler is merciless and unworthy of his position, then we change the emperor.\"","\"How about dragging Xiao Chengjing off the dragon throne and taking the seat ourselves?\"","Seeing the highly aggressive smile on Song Jinzhao's lips, a chill ran down Song Qiming's spine.","He subconsciously glanced at the window to make sure there was no draft before looking back.","Flustered, Song Qiming lowered his head, blinking rapidly. His mind was a mess.","His sister was too bold. How could she even think of rebellion?","Although this revelation came far too suddenly and he was completely unprepared, Song Qiming subconsciously began to weigh the feasibility of Song Jinzhao's idea.","Song Jinzhao watched him in silence, giving Song Qiming plenty of time to calm down and think.","An unknown amount of time passed, and the sound of the rain outside began to fade.","Song Qiming furrowed his brows tightly.","He looked up with difficulty, his eyes filled with an unprecedented seriousness and earnestness.","\"Even if I become the Provincial Governor of the Southwest, I will only have twenty thousand troops under my command. The imperial court has six hundred thousand troops on paper, and in reality, they have at least four hundred and fifty thousand. Twenty thousand against four hundred and fifty thousand—isn't that like striking a stone with an egg?\"","Calling it suicide wouldn't be an exaggeration; they could easily be crushed to death.","Song Jinzhao reached out and drew a large circle north of the Southwest. \"What if we add the troops of all the foreign tribes in the Southwest?\"","Song Qiming clenched his jaw, hesitating for a long time before he couldn't help but speak.","\"Sister, you want to ally with the southwestern tribes to raise an army together?\"","Song Jinzhao's tone revealed a chilling dominance.","\"Not ally. Annex.\"","Song Qiming blinked in horror. He covered his forehead with his hand, spun around twice in place, and then quickly looked up.","\"There are over thirty foreign tribes in the Southwest, large and small. Together, they have about two hundred thousand troops. These men are genuine fighting forces, without any exaggeration.\"","\"Among them, the Yang clan of Panzhou has seventy thousand, and the Mu clan of Ningzhou has fifty thousand. The remaining eighty thousand are scattered among the other tribes—some have seven or eight thousand, while others have only a few hundred. But if we want to gather all of them, the first two alone will be tough nuts to crack.\"","\"Especially when facing the imperial court. At the slightest sign of trouble, these tribes, who usually fight among themselves, will unite against the common enemy. Gathering all of them will be extremely difficult. It wouldn't be an exaggeration to say it's like fighting half of the Dongzhao Kingdom.\"","Song Qiming didn't object; he just felt it was highly unlikely to succeed.","If it were Chu Liuyun or Qin Guo, the chances would be higher. At least they held heavy military power and had the strength to rebel.","Song Jinzhao turned to face the map. \"The Southwest is poor. The Yang and Mu clans have money, but the commoners in their territories do not.\"","\"Across all the southwestern tribes, apart from the soldiers, there are the commoners, and their numbers far exceed two hundred thousand.\"","\"According to imperial regulations, the territories of the southwestern tribes also fall under the jurisdiction of the Provincial Governor of the Southwest. It's just that over the years, Gu Zhongxun hasn't been able to control them at all. The imperial court has never given the people of the Southwest any benefits, so the hearts and minds of the people are controlled by the tribes.\"","\"If we want to overthrow the rule of the southwestern tribes, the first step is to win the hearts of the people over to our side.\""]},{"number":367,"title":"Chapter 367: Unconditional Support Forever: The Marriage Envoy Enters the Capital","paragraphs":["Song Qiming wiped the beads of sweat from his forehead, his expression a mix of conflict and unease.","\"Winning the hearts of the people in the Southwest is no easy task. Are you certain about this, Sister?\"","Song Jinzhao gave a slight nod. \"For the common people, having enough to eat and warm clothes to wear is their primary need. They will submit to whoever can give them a good life. Going to the Southwest is about securing a proper status. Otherwise, even if I accomplish this, the prestige and the support of the people will fall to someone else, and I won't achieve my desired goal.\"","Song Qiming bit his lip so hard that two deep teeth marks appeared.","His early aspirations when he first entered the royal court, the danger of Song Jinzhao's assassination attempt, the Emperor's favoritism toward the two princes, and the cold-blooded ruthlessness of his order to flog Ye Liangyu and Fei Yanzhang—all of it echoed in his mind.","After a moment of thought, Song Qiming looked up at Song Jinzhao with a resolute gaze, his final decision already made.","\"Since you want to do this, Sister, then do it. Whether it's going to the Southwest or launching a rebellion, I will support you. No matter what, the four of us siblings will always be of one heart for the rest of our lives.\"","After saying this, Song Qiming couldn't help but smile, though a hint of bitterness lingered at the corners of his mouth.","\"Whether it is my teacher, Lord Fei, or the Duke of Qing, they have all lamented in front of me that if you were a man, Sister, you would surely achieve unprecedented greatness. But alas, you were born a woman.\"","\"But now, I feel that whether you are a man or a woman might not be so important after all.\" Because even as a woman, no one could defeat her.","Just having the audacity to harbor thoughts of rebellion was enough to prove her immense courage.","Song Jinzhao smiled faintly and turned back to look at the map, her dark eyes filled with absolute determination.","A month and a half later, a marriage delegation from the State of Shuobei entered the capital with thirty full carriages of betrothal gifts.","On both sides of the street, the commoners pointed and murmured at the endless line of carriages.","\"Didn't they just leave during the New Year? Why are people from Shuobei here again?\" a tavern keeper asked, stroking his beard in confusion.","The proprietress standing next to him looked at the carriages covered in red silk and couldn't help but mutter.","\"Why are these carriages all covered in red cloth, and bright red at that? It doesn't block the wind or the rain. Shouldn't they be using oiled paper?\"","The tavern keeper smiled and shook his head.","\"I have no idea. This color makes it look like a wedding. Two months ago, when the Duke of Qing presented betrothal gifts to Her Highness, it was this exact same spectacle.\"","In an instant, all the onlookers in the crowd whipped their heads around to stare at the tavern keeper.","Betrothal gifts? A wedding?","It couldn't be.","What kind of joyous occasion could they possibly have with the State of Shuobei?","Stared at by over a dozen people, the tavern keeper froze at first. When he finally realized what he had said, his eyes widened larger than a cow's.","\"No way, Princess Yongjia just got married, and the remaining seven princesses are still toddlers. Could it be that Shuobei is marrying one of their princesses over to us?\"","The crowd swallowed hard. \"If they are marrying a princess over, does that mean our State of Dongzhao and the State of Shuobei won't go to war anymore?\"","After all, becoming in-laws would definitely improve relations.","Hearing this, the commoners blinked in realization. For a moment, they weren't entirely sure, but having a theory felt like having hope.","They couldn't wait to find out the truth, and so the rumors of a marriage alliance between the two nations began to spread rapidly, faster than a tornado.","Less than half a day after the marriage delegation checked into the Huitong Guesthouse, before Xiao Chengjing even had the chance to receive them, the streets and alleys were already buzzing with talk of a marriage alliance between the two countries."]},{"number":368,"title":"Chapter 368: King Qi's Marriage Proposal Delegation","paragraphs":["Song Jinzhao received the news even faster than the palace did.","\"Does the State of Shuobei have any princesses?\"","Lan Xi nodded. \"There are three. The eldest and second princesses are He Mingnan's full sisters.\"","Song Jinzhao pressed, \"Are they already married?\"","Lan Xi shook his head.","\"The eldest and second princesses are married. When I fled Shuobei, the third princess was still quite young and hadn't wed yet.\"","After a moment of thought, Song Jinzhao said, \"The leader of the marriage proposal delegation this time is Wang Nie, the Minister of Rites of Shuobei. He has probably seen you before. Just in case, you should stay inside the estate for the time being. Do not go out, lest you be recognized.\"","Lan Xi suggested, \"I can go to the country estate. The factory has been working overtime lately, so it is a good time for me to go keep an eye on things.\"","Song Jinzhao thought it over. \"That works. Take the Ferghana horse with you when you go; the next few months are its mating season.\"","Lan Xi's expression froze for a second. He had not expected Song Jinzhao to speak so bluntly.","Mating season.","Even if they were talking about an animal, hearing those words from a woman's mouth was still slightly disconcerting.","The County Princess really was quite different from ordinary women.","After Lan Xi left, Song Jinzhao swiveled her chair, rubbing her fingers together repeatedly.","After a while, she called out toward the door, \"Qingshuang, come in for a moment.\"","Qingshuang, who had been guarding the door, immediately turned and pushed it open.","Song Jinzhao looked at her and ordered, \"The Emperor will receive the marriage proposal delegation very soon. Once the news spreads, arrange for our people to stoke the flames among the commoners. Do it discreetly. Use the people we have planted in the beggars' gang.\"","Qingshuang nodded solemnly. \"This servant understands. I will tell them to be careful.\"","Outside the Huitong Guesthouse, the carriage from the Prince of Qi's estate charged forward rapidly, as if the horses had been spooked.","When it came to a halt, the entire carriage rocked violently, nearly flipping over.","Dust billowed into the air. The guards standing at the entrance instinctively covered their mouths and noses, even squeezing their eyes shut.","\"Your Highness, please slow down.\"","The wooden floorboards of the carriage thumped loudly under Xiao Rongche's heavy footsteps.","Upon seeing who had arrived, a guard looked puzzled and nudged his companion to go inside and fetch someone.","\"Why is His Highness the Prince of Qi here? Shouldn't he be staying at his estate?\"","After all, ever since the Prince of Qi returned to the capital, he had never stepped foot outside his gates unless summoned by the Emperor.","Rumor had it that the Prince of Qi was going blind in his left eye. Why would he come to the Huitong Guesthouse at a time like this?","\"There are steps ahead. Please slow down, Your Highness.\" Supported by two servants, one on each side, Xiao Rongche was practically carried as he rushed inside.","Cao Mo, the director of the Huitong Guesthouse, ran over holding onto his hat. Seeing that the prince had already entered, he hastily dropped to his knees to pay his respects.","\"This humble official, Cao Mo, greets His Highness the Prince of Qi.\"","Xiao Rongche's vision in his left eye was now severely impaired; he could only vaguely make out a dark silhouette appearing before him.","He reached out frantically, grabbing onto a pair of shoulders and gripping them tightly.","\"Where is the marriage proposal delegation from Shuobei? Who is the chief envoy? Take me to him. I need to see him immediately.\"","Cao Mo blinked in a panic, feeling as though his shoulders were about to be crushed by Xiao Rongche's grip.","Gritting his teeth, he answered, \"It is Wang Nie, the Minister of Rites of Shuobei. He is in the rear courtyard. He said he was going to take a nap. This humble official will take Your Highness there right away.\"","The courtyard where Wang Nie was staying was the exact same one Gong Linjue had stayed in during his previous visit.","However, the cotton rose flowers had already withered. It was now the growing season for the foliage, and the branches were covered in newly sprouted shoots, creating a lush, pale green canopy.","The guards stationed at the door saw Cao Mo charging toward them aggressively with eight men in tow, their expressions grim. The guards' hearts instantly leaped into their throats.","What was going on? It felt like they had come with ill intentions."]},{"number":369,"title":"Chapter 369: Xiao Rongche: Bring Me the Imperial Physician","paragraphs":["The four men couldn't help but tighten their grip on their weapons and take a step forward simultaneously.","\"Lord Cao, what are you—\" Before the guard could finish his sentence, he was forcefully shoved aside by Prince Qi.","The other three quickly closed ranks to block Xiao Rongche.","\"What are you trying to do?\" one of the guards cried out in alarm.","The four of them drew their swords and pointed them at Prince Qi, making it clear that they would strike if he took another step forward.","Seeing them draw their swords against Prince Qi, the guards Xiao Rongche had brought with him immediately drew their own blades and aimed them right back.","Seeing that a fight was about to break out, Cao Mo was frightened out of his wits.","He hurriedly reached out to stop them, his face filled with panic.","\"Don't misunderstand, this is His Highness Prince Qi. Is Minister Wang inside? Our prince wishes to see him.\"","The guards furrowed their brows, their gazes sweeping over Xiao Rongche, who was wearing an eye patch.","\"What is going on here?\" a thunderous shout boomed from behind the crowd.","The newcomer was clad in armor and gripped a thick-bladed sword; his imposing and fierce demeanor made it obvious that he was not someone to be trifled with.","When the four guards responsible for watching the door saw Qi Xiong approaching, their eyes instantly filled with the relief of having survived a disaster.","The guard who had just been shoved to the ground by Prince Qi immediately began to complain.","\"Captain, the prince of the Dongzhao Kingdom suddenly charged over looking for Minister Wang and tried to force his way in. When your subordinates tried to stop him, they even wanted to attack us.\"","Qi Xiong looked at Xiao Rongche, his eyes brimming with disdain.","\"I had heard that the Dongzhao Kingdom was a nation of etiquette, but I never expected their manners to be like this. If even a prince acts with such crude, unruly, and rule-breaking behavior, one can only imagine how terrible the customs of the Dongzhao Kingdom must be.\"","Cao Mo was just about to retort when he was interrupted by Xiao Rongche.","He pointed his finger right at Qi Xiong's face, spittle flying onto the captain's face as he shouted.","\"What kind of thing are you, to dare dictate terms in front of this prince? Hurry up and bring the imperial physician out, or I will kill you!\"","Cao Mo's eyes widened as he looked at Xiao Rongche in disbelief.","An imperial physician? An imperial physician from the Shuobei Kingdom?","Qi Xiong's thick eyebrows twisted into a deep frown as he asked, completely bewildered, \"What imperial physician?\"","Xiao Rongche roared in agitation; if it weren't for the people holding him back on either side, he would have lunged right at Qi Xiong.","\"The imperial physician to treat my eyes! Didn't Gong Linjue have you bring him over?\"","Hearing this, Qi Xiong's face was full of confusion.","What did this have to do with Prince Wei?","What imperial physician? How come he didn't know anything about it?","Right at that moment, the door to the room was opened from the inside.","Wang Nie, with a coat draped over his shoulders, first glanced at Xiao Rongche and then signaled Qi Xiong with his eyes.","Qi Xiong's heart stirred, a flash of understanding passing through his eyes.","There must be something going on here that he just wasn't aware of.","He walked over to stand beside Wang Nie, silently handing the matter over for him to handle.","Seeing Wang Nie come out, Cao Mo's hanging heart finally settled.","Panting, he began to introduce them, \"Your Highness, this is Wang Nie, the Minister of Rites of the Shuobei Kingdom, and the chief envoy of this delegation.\"","\"Minister Wang, this is our His Highness Prince Qi.\"","Wang Nie's lips curled up slightly as he asked with a look of feigned ignorance, \"I have long heard that your esteemed country has two very capable princes. Seeing you today, what on earth has happened to His Highness Prince Qi's eye?\"","Hearing him say this, Xiao Rongche completely exploded.","He couldn't see Wang Nie's face clearly, so he could only point at the blurry dark silhouette that had just appeared in his vision and question him loudly.","\"What do you mean by that? Where is the imperial physician Gong Linjue promised me? He agreed to save my left eye!\"","Wang Nie feigned confusion and said, \"If Your Highness's eye is blind, you should seek treatment from the imperial physicians of your own Dongzhao Kingdom. What does this have to do with our Shuobei Kingdom? When did Prince Wei ever promise you an imperial physician? How come this official has never heard of such a thing?\"","\"Furthermore, I've heard that your esteemed country's County Princess Linghui is a divine doctor who can bring the dead back to life. If even she cannot cure it, how could our Shuobei Kingdom possibly have an imperial physician capable of doing so? Your Highness must be joking.\"","The highly pitched, deliberately prolonged drawl at the end of his sentence fell into Xiao Rongche's ears like a knife sharpening against his heart.","Dragging back and forth, relentlessly torturing him."]},{"number":370,"title":"Chapter 370: They're Fighting","paragraphs":["Cao Mo's newly settled heart leaped into his throat once again.","What did that mean? No imperial physician?","Had Prince Qi been deceived?","Xiao Rongche's mind buzzed as if someone were stirring his brain with a stick.","His blind right eye, his blurry left eye, the throbbing pain in his eyeballs and nerves.","Accompanied by Wang Nie's cold sarcasm, the emotions he had suppressed for five months could no longer be contained, finally erupting suddenly like a volcano.","He shook his head in agitation, sending his eyepatch flying. The pale, shriveled eyeball looked exceptionally terrifying.","\"You are spouting nonsense! Gong Linjue promised to send an imperial physician over; that was the only reason I stole the potatoes for him. He cannot go back on his word.\"","\"Tell him to send the imperial physician over immediately, or none of you will leave here.\"","Wang Nie straightened his chest, showing not the slightest trace of fear on his face.","He raised his chin righteously. \"Trading potatoes for an imperial physician? Does Your Highness have any witnesses? We have our own potatoes in the State of Shuobei; there is absolutely no need to make a deal with your State of Dongzhao. You can't just pin this dirty deed on our Prince Wei based solely on your own words. You're dreaming.\"","It was a bolt from the blue, shattering them to pieces.","Cao Mo clenched his fists tightly, staring at Wang Nie in disbelief.","He had never seen such a brazen and shameless person.","To claim stolen goods as their own—as a scholar and the Minister of Rites, how could he be so shameless?","Xiao Rongche panted heavily, his chest heaving violently.","Wang Nie's mouth did not stop, quacking away like a duck.","\"Two warring nations do not execute envoys, not to mention that our State of Shuobei and your State of Dongzhao have long since ceased hostilities. This diplomatic mission is specifically to forge a lasting alliance of marriage.\"","\"Your Highness threatens this official with wild words. Could it be that you wish to start a war?\"","Hearing the mention of starting a war, the others, including Cao Mo, gradually calmed down.","Now was not the time for conflict. Today's matter had to be reported to the Emperor first.","\"A mere Minister of Rites dares to speak to me like this! If there is no imperial physician, then go to hell!\"","Along with his furious roar, Xiao Rongche lunged like a madman at the speaking silhouette in front of him.","He seized Wang Nie's neck in a death grip.","The crowd was horrified. Qi Xiong immediately raised his blade and slashed toward Xiao Rongche.","Seeing this, the guards of Prince Qi's estate quickly drew their swords to intercept him.","The two sides clashed, and the guards of the State of Shuobei also joined the fray.","All the color drained from Cao Mo's face. For a moment, he froze in place, not knowing what to do.","At the entrance of the Huitong Guesthouse, the gatekeeping runners suspiciously pricked up their ears and looked inside. \"I think I heard fighting.\"","His companion, who was sneaking a bite of a steamed bun, looked up. \"You must have heard wrong. How could anyone be fighting in the Huitong Guesthouse in broad daylight?\"","The man frowned, stepping over the threshold and walking two paces inward.","Once he heard it clearly, his expression turned to one of shock.","\"There really is fighting! It's coming from the rear courtyard, it seems to be the courtyard where the Shuobei diplomatic mission is staying.\"","The other men turned their heads. Once they quieted down, the noise grew louder and became very obvious.","The four of them looked at each other, decisively threw away their steamed buns, and charged forward.","They shouted for backup as they ran.","In the courtyard, Wang Nie could not breathe; his face had already turned livid.","Afraid that Xiao Rongche would strangle him to death, Cao Mo hurriedly rushed forward to pry Xiao Rongche's hands away. \"Your Highness, please let go! He is dying!\"","\"Wang Nie is the Minister of Rites of the State of Shuobei, the chief envoy of this marriage-seeking mission! He cannot die in the State of Dongzhao, and he certainly cannot die in the Huitong Guesthouse! Hurry and let go!\"","The more Cao Mo tried to pry his hands apart, the tighter Xiao Rongche squeezed.","\"Die! You all must die! If you cannot cure my eyes, you will all be buried with me!\"","Xiao Rongche repeatedly muttered this phrase, acting as if he had lost his mind, completely blocking out everything around him.","He could not hear Cao Mo's voice, nor the fierce sounds of fighting in the courtyard. He was entirely consumed by his own emotions.","Seeing Wang Nie's eyes beginning to roll back in his head, Cao Mo panicked completely.","He tore his throat open and shouted, \"Somebody! Somebody come quickly!\"","Hearing Cao Mo's cries for help, the runners who were rushing over quickened their pace.","By the time they arrived, blood had already been spilled in the courtyard.","Seven or eight people lay on the ground; a few were still moving, but others looked as though they were dead.","After striking down all the guards of Prince Qi's estate, Qi Xiong glared with his bear-like eyes and charged toward Xiao Rongche."]},{"number":371,"title":"Chapter 371: Xiao Rongche Vomits Blood and Falls Unconscious After Being Beaten","paragraphs":["Seeing this, Cao Mo was so frightened that he scrambled out of the way, practically rolling and crawling.","In the moment he raised his blade, taking Xiao Rongche's identity into consideration, Qi Xiong ultimately held back from dealing a lethal blow.","He switched the blade to his left hand, grabbed Xiao Rongche's collar with his right, and then delivered a solid kick to his back.","Watching Xiao Rongche roll down the steps, the yamen runners who had rushed over gasped in shock.","This was an imperial prince! How dare the people of Shuobei do such a thing!","\"To dare lay a hand on His Highness Prince Qi within our Dongzhao Kingdom, you are far too audacious!\" One of the runners took the lead, drawing his curved blade and pointing it at Qi Xiong, looking as if he would charge forward at any second.","Cao Mo hurriedly scrambled up from the ground, his face covered in snot and tears.","\"Stop, don't attack! This is all a misunderstanding.\"","With a dark expression, Qi Xiong helped Wang Nie up from the ground.","Wang Nie gasped for air. His neck had been choked purple, aching at the slightest touch.","He opened his mouth, every word tearing at his injured throat.","\"I have been here for less than a day and was nearly choked to death, and you tell me this is a misunderstanding?\"","\"If your Emperor does not give me an explanation for what happened today, our Shuobei Kingdom will absolutely not let this go.\"","As they spoke, dozens of yamen runners flooded into the courtyard, packing it so tightly that there was barely room to stand.","What exactly was going on?","Why did it sound like it was His Highness Prince Qi's fault, yet the Shuobei people were the ones drawing blades to kill?","When Xiao Rongche was helped up from the ground, a sharp pain shot through his knee, as if he had injured the bone.","After calming down, he glared darkly at Wang Nie and the others. However, because he couldn't see their faces clearly, he felt both aggrieved and sorrowful.","\"You treacherous liars, you will face the wrath of heaven.\"","As soon as his words fell, Xiao Rongche began to cough.","Along with the violent shuddering of his chest, a mouthful of fresh blood spewed from his throat.","Looking at the blood on the ground, Cao Mo suddenly felt as if the sky had collapsed.","Xiao Rongche closed his eyes and completely lost consciousness.","\"His Highness Prince Qi!\" the runner supporting him cried out in alarm, hastily catching his falling body.","Cao Mo's face turned deathly pale. Panic-stricken, he looked up and shouted to his subordinates, \"Quick, go fetch the imperial physician!\"","The previously overbearing Wang Nie immediately furrowed his brows, shooting a hesitant glance at Qi Xiong.","Did you kick him hard?","Pressing his thick lips into a straight line, Qi Xiong shook his head slightly.","Not that hard, I only used a little bit of strength.","Wang Nie didn't say a word, his gaze carrying a trace of worry as he watched Xiao Rongche being carried away.","\"Send someone to follow them. If he really dies, it will be quite troublesome.\"","Qi Xiong couldn't help but feel a twinge of regret.","If he had known the other party was so weak, he wouldn't have kicked him just now.","In the Imperial Study, Xiao Chengjing had just finished discussing the matter of the political marriage with Dongfang Shaoting and the others.","After all the ministers had left, he instructed Zhao Yande in a deep voice, \"Summon County Princess Linghui to the palace.\"","\"Yes, Your Majesty.\" Just as Zhao Yande was about to step out, a eunuch bumped into him from the right.","His body swayed, and even his hat was knocked off.","Lowering his voice, Zhao Yande glared and scolded, \"Why are you running so fast? If you bump into the Emperor, watch your head!\"","The eunuch's shoulders trembled. With a face full of panic, he said to Zhao Yande, \"Master, something terrible has happened.\"","\"His Highness Prince Qi and the people from the Shuobei Kingdom got into a fight at the Huitong Guesthouse. They say he coughed up blood, and the imperial physicians just rushed over.\"","Zhao Yande's gaze suddenly sharpened, and he pressed coldly, \"Who coughed up blood?\"","The eunuch swallowed hard in fear.","\"It's His Highness Prince Qi. They say it doesn't look good; he has already passed out.\"","No longer caring about summoning Song Jinzhao, Zhao Yande abruptly turned and ran back into the Imperial Study.","\"Your Majesty, news just arrived. The Huitong Guesthouse has called for the imperial physicians. They say His Highness Prince Qi was beaten by the Shuobei diplomatic mission until he coughed up blood, and he is already unconscious.\""]},{"number":372,"title":"Chapter 372: Life-threatening Danger May Loom","paragraphs":["With a clatter, the teacup dropped onto the table.","Ignoring the water-soaked memorials, Xiao Chengjing stood up abruptly, his voice striking toward Zhao Yande like a thunderbolt.","\"How bad are his injuries? Why would Prince Qi go to the Huitong Guesthouse? Shouldn't he be staying in his manor?\"","Zhao Yande looked at his apprentice.","The eunuch who had come to deliver the news hurriedly knelt down and reported, \"They say the conflict started over a royal physician. His Highness Prince Qi tried to strangle Wang Nie, the chief envoy of the marriage delegation, and was subsequently beaten by the guards of Shuobei. It seems someone even died.\"","As if struck by something, Xiao Chengjing quickly calmed down.","Prince Qi must have sought out the marriage delegation to get a royal physician to treat his eyes.","Could it be that the royal physician sent by Shuobei couldn't cure him? Is that why they fought?","Xiao Chengjing clenched his fists and issued orders to Zhao Yande in a rapid-fire tone.","\"Pass on my verbal decree: have all the royal physicians on duty at the Imperial Academy of Medicine today head over there immediately. Both Prince Qi and Wang Nie must remain unharmed.\"","Zhao Yande asked with a nervous expression, \"Your Majesty, should we also summon County Princess Linghui today?\"","Xiao Chengjing's eyes lit up, and he said without hesitation, \"Have County Princess Linghui go as well. Once she has examined them, she is to enter the palace immediately to report back.\"","Cupping his hands holding the fly whisk forward, he replied, \"This servant obeys the decree.\"","Lan Xi had barely ridden out of the manor when the people from the palace arrived.","The little eunuch waited before Song Jinzhao and urged her, his voice trembling with anxiety.","\"County Princess Linghui, something has happened to Prince Qi at the Huitong Guesthouse. His Majesty asks that you hurry over to take a look.\"","Song Jinzhao looked at him with a cold expression, while beside her, Song Shixue was rolling her eyes so hard they almost reached the heavens.","There are so many royal physicians in the palace, yet they have to invite her elder sister every single time. Are they all just useless freeloaders?","Song Jinzhao slowly opened her mouth, her tone calm and devoid of any fluctuation.","\"Have the royal physicians not gone over?\"","The little eunuch's back was covered in sweat, his clothes soaked from running.","\"Director Gu has already hurried over, but His Majesty is not at ease, so he wishes for the County Princess to go and take a look as well. Furthermore, it is not only Prince Qi who is injured; Wang Nie, the envoy sent by Shuobei, is also hurt.\"","Song Jinzhao lifted her eyelids in surprise. \"Prince Qi got into a conflict with the Shuobei delegation?\"","The little eunuch scrunched up his face and stomped his feet in urgency. \"Time is of the essence, County Princess, please don't ask any more questions. Hurry and follow this servant over.\"","Outside the Huitong Guesthouse, Song Jinzhao had just stepped down from the carriage when she saw several yamen runners carrying stretchers walking out from inside.","The stretchers were covered with white cloths, looking like they held dead bodies.","\"Greetings, County Princess.\"","Seeing Song Jinzhao approach, the yamen runners carrying the stretchers quickly stopped, placed the stretchers on the ground, and bowed to her.","Lifting the white cloth, it was indeed a corpse.","The knife wound on the chest was wide and deep, unlike those caused by ordinary swords. It was likely the work of someone from Shuobei.","Not only were there injuries, but someone had also died. It seemed today's incident was no small matter.","Upon entering the rear courtyard, Xiao Rongche had already been carried onto a bed in the side room.","Gu Jupu, his face weathered by time, looked as if he had aged several more years.","\"This kick was too ruthless. Not only did it damage his heart meridian, but the stagnant blood has also blocked his airway, which is why he cannot wake up.\"","\"We must first dissipate the blood stasis, otherwise, his life may be in danger. This official will write a prescription immediately.\"","Cao Mo stood nearby, nodding continuously, his chin bobbing like a chick pecking at rice.","\"My Lord, please write it quickly. This lower official will immediately have someone brew the medicine.\"","Outside the room, a man from Shuobei wearing a hat was eavesdropping.","Hearing that his life might be in danger, the man immediately turned and ran into the main room.","Song Jinzhao, whose right foot had just stepped onto the stairs, saw everything clearly.","\"County Princess Linghui!\" Inside the room, Cao Mo unconsciously cried out in surprise upon seeing her enter, his expression appearing particularly agitated.","Gu Jupu, who was sitting on a stool writing the prescription, snapped his head up.","After clearly seeing who had arrived, he quickly finished writing down an herbal ingredient, then picked up the prescription and walked up to greet Song Jinzhao, briefly recounting Xiao Rongche's condition to her."]},{"number":373,"title":"Chapter 373: Wang and Nie Pretend to Be Ill, Get Vomited Out by the Stench","paragraphs":["Song Jinzhao walked over to the bed and gave his pulse a cursory check. Xiao Rongche's condition was indeed very serious, but she had no intention of getting too involved.","\"The prescription is correct. Just go with this one.\"","Gu Jupu shot Song Jinzhao a slightly surprised glance.","Usually, when seeing a patient, the County Princess would add some details he hadn't noticed. Was she really done just like that today?","It felt a bit too brief.","Cao Mo hurriedly took the prescription. \"Will His Highness wake up after taking the medicine?\"","If something really happened to him here at the Huitong Guest House, even chopping off his head wouldn't be enough to make amends.","Song Jinzhao replied, \"It depends on when the blood clots dissolve.\"","As soon as she finished speaking, a man's shout came from outside.","\"Someone come quickly! My lord has fainted from a terrible headache!\"","Cao Mo clutched his chest, his heart palpitating so hard he could barely catch his breath.","\"He was perfectly fine just a moment ago. How could he have fainted?\"","Meeting his gaze, Song Jinzhao was the first to step outside, with Gu Jupu following closely behind.","At a glance, there were at least ten guards in the room. Qi Xiong stood by the bed, looking grim.","Seeing Song Jinzhao enter, he immediately said, \"Prince Qi nearly snapped Minister Wang's neck just now. The prolonged lack of air might have injured his internal organs.\"","Pausing slightly, Song Jinzhao walked over to the bed expressionlessly and began to examine Wang Nie.","His throat bones were intact, and his airway wasn't blocked. Only the subcutaneous capillaries were injured, which couldn't possibly cause a headache and fainting.","Recalling how the people of Shuobei had been eavesdropping outside the room earlier, Song Jinzhao formed a guess.","Xiao Rongche was severely injured, and they were afraid of taking the blame, so they were faking an illness.","However...","Song Jinzhao placed her fingers on Wang Nie's wrist. It wasn't just a simple feigned illness; his pulse indicated he had taken some sort of drug to alter it.","Qi Xiong accused her indignantly, \"Is Minister Wang gravely injured? Your Dongzhao Prince was far too ruthless. This matter is far from over.\"","Keeping a straight face, Song Jinzhao raised her eyebrows at him.","\"He fell ill from anger. It's not a severe injury. One dose of my medicine and he'll be perfectly fine.\"","Saying this, Song Jinzhao took a small medicine bottle from her medical box, pulled out the stopper, and poured out a black pill.","A foul stench instantly permeated the air, causing Qi Xiong and the others to hold their breath.","\"Ugh!\" Cao Mo, who was a step too slow, felt his stomach churn violently.","Unable to hold it in, he scrambled outside to throw up.","Covering his nose, Qi Xiong asked, \"What is that? It stinks!\"","It smelled even worse than the feces in a latrine.","Pinching the pill, Song Jinzhao smiled. \"A good medicine that will wake your lord up immediately.\"","Seeing that she didn't seem to be joking, and worried that their ruse of taking drugs to fake an illness would be exposed, Qi Xiong immediately reached out to stop her.","But Song Jinzhao simply jabbed him with her elbow, sending him crashing back against the wall, immobilized for a moment.","No wonder she could defeat the Prince of Wei; this County Princess Linghui possessed incredible strength.","Song Jinzhao shoved the pill into Wang Nie's mouth, then used a silver needle to stimulate his philtrum.","The next second, the man who had been lying unconscious on the bed suddenly opened his eyes, leaned over the edge of the bed, and began to vomit.","Yellowish-brown mushy meat, green vegetable scraps, and white rice came pouring out, until he was heaving up nothing but bitter bile and saliva.","Fighting back his own nausea, Qi Xiong glared angrily at Song Jinzhao. \"What exactly did you feed Minister Wang?\"","Song Jinzhao closed her medical box and turned to leave. \"I told you, it's a good medicine to wake him up immediately.\"","After walking out of the room, Gu Jupu asked Song Jinzhao in confusion, \"County Princess, was he really made ill by anger just now?\"","If he had truly fainted from anger, taking medicine and vomiting wouldn't have woken him up so instantly.","He would rather believe the man was woken up by the stench.","Song Jinzhao shook her head. \"No, he only sustained a minor injury to his neck. His pulse was disguised by medicine.\"","As the sun began to set, a young eunuch walked up to Song Jinzhao and said, \"County Princess, the Emperor is still waiting in the palace for your report on His Highness Prince Qi's condition.\"","Song Jinzhao asked, \"Shouldn't I wait until Prince Qi wakes up?\"","The young eunuch replied, \"Since the medicine is already brewing, it will be fine to have Imperial Physician Gu keep watch here. Please hurry into the palace with me, do not make the Emperor wait.\"","Having her leave before the patient had even woken up felt a bit suspicious.","\"Does the Emperor want to ask about Prince Qi's condition, or is he summoning me for another matter?\"","The young eunuch swallowed nervously, glanced around, and whispered to Song Jinzhao, \"Both.\"","Song Jinzhao pressed, \"What is the other matter?\"","The young eunuch took a step back, smiled faintly, and extended his hand in a guiding gesture.","\"That, this servant does not know.\""]},{"number":374,"title":"Chapter 374: Entering the Palace, Xiao Chengjing: Fierce in Appearance but Feeble in Heart","paragraphs":["Inside the carriage bound for the imperial palace, Qingshuang whispered, \"I have looked into the matter. It was Prince Qi who made the first move and grabbed Wang Nie by the throat, and it was Qi Xiong who kicked him down the stairs. The guards from Prince Qi's estate fought with those brought by the diplomatic mission. Three were severely injured and four were killed—those were the four corpses we saw being carried out just now.\"","Through the gap in the curtains, Song Jinzhao quietly glanced out the window.","The eunuch sent by the emperor walked closely beside them, never leaving their side, his profile looking extremely stern.","Earlier, there hadn't been a single imperial physician in the quarters of the Shuobei diplomatic mission.","Song Jinzhao mused, \"So Gong Linjue played a trick to get something for nothing, and completely deceived Xiao Rongche?\"","Qingshuang nodded heavily.","\"Not only that, but they also mocked him and turned the tables, claiming that Shuobei already has potatoes of its own.\"","\"When Prince Qi realized he had been tricked, he insisted that the Shuobei mission find someone to cure his eyes, threatening that he wouldn't let them leave otherwise.\"","\"In response, not only were they unafraid, but they even counter-threatened Prince Qi with war.\"","\"In a fit of rage, Prince Qi lunged forward to strangle their chief envoy. The guards from both sides clashed, and then Prince Qi was kicked by their captain of the guards, Qi Xiong.\"","With the sun already halfway set, Eunuch Zhao had even specially arranged for a palanquin to be waiting just inside the palace gates upon their arrival.","Once Song Jinzhao was seated, she was swiftly carried to the outside of the Qianqing Gate before alighting.","By the time she walked to the entrance of the Imperial Study, Eunuch Zhao had already paced back and forth on the steps hundreds of times.","At the sound of footsteps, he abruptly lifted his head. Upon clearly seeing Song Jinzhao, his eyes lit up brighter than a fire starter.","He hurried down the steps.","\"County Princess Linghui, you are finally here. His Majesty has been waiting for you for three hours.\"","Song Jinzhao did not speak.","Traveling from her estate to the diplomatic hostel, and then from the hostel to the palace, not to mention the time it took for the eunuch to deliver the message to her estate—three hours was actually incredibly fast.","The moment she stepped into the Imperial Study, an oppressive atmosphere washed over her.","Everyone stood perfectly still with their heads bowed, rooted to the spot like wooden stakes.","The instant she entered the inner chamber, Xiao Chengjing's gloomy gaze landed on her.","\"Your subject Song Jinzhao greets Your Majesty.\" Song Jinzhao knelt and bowed without a change in expression. She imagined Xiao Chengjing as a giant winter melon, completely ignoring the anger radiating from him.","Xiao Chengjing held his breath, forcing the surging emotions in his chest back down into his stomach.","He asked in a deep voice, \"What is the condition of Prince Qi and the chief envoy from Shuobei?\"","Song Jinzhao stared at her knees resting on the floor, a fleeting trace of displeasure flashing through her eyes.","She blinked, seamlessly concealing her emotions, so that when she raised her head, her face showed nothing but the utmost respect for her sovereign.","\"To answer Your Majesty, His Highness Prince Qi has suffered damage to his heart meridian. I have already consulted with Director Gu and prescribed a remedy to clear the blood stasis and soothe his nerves. Once he takes it, he should wake up by tomorrow.\"","\"As for the chief envoy from Shuobei, he only sustained minor injuries, though the bruises look rather alarming. However, while I was treating His Highness Prince Qi, Chief Envoy Wang Nie took a drug to feign severe illness. I have already revived him.\"","Xiao Chengjing closed his eyes and took a deep breath. When he opened them again, his mood appeared slightly better than before.","\"It is good that they are fine. Shuobei has stirred up trouble time and time again; one day, I will wipe them out.\"","Song Jinzhao stared blankly at the steps with a calm expression, having already cursed Xiao Chengjing ten thousand times in her head.","Anyone could spout empty threats.","He was incompetent, foolish, selfish, and complacent.","If he actually had to take the initiative to deploy troops, it wouldn't happen even in his next lifetime."]},{"number":375,"title":"Chapter 375: Playing Both Sides, Proposing at the Morning Court","paragraphs":["Only after speaking his big words did Xiao Chengjing remember that Song Jinzhao was still kneeling. He smiled and motioned with his chin.","\"Rise. Give her a seat.\"","Zhao Yande, who had finally managed to catch his breath, hastily brought a chair over for Song Jinzhao himself.","After she sat down, the faint smile on Xiao Chengjing's face was withdrawn, replaced by a very calm demeanor.","\"I summoned you to the palace not only to inquire about the injuries of Prince Qi and Wang Nie, but also to discuss an important matter with you, regarding your lifelong marriage.\"","Finally, they were getting to the main point.","Song Jinzhao feigned confusion and raised her eyebrows. \"What does Your Majesty mean?\"","\"After my parents passed away, I swore before my elders that I would not marry until my younger brother started a family. If Your Majesty wishes to bestow a marriage upon me, it can wait a few more years.\"","These words struck a chord in Xiao Chengjing's heart, and his stern face instantly thawed.","\"It is not that I wish to bestow a marriage, but the Emperor of the Shuobei Kingdom wants to marry you as his imperial consort.\"","\"The dozens of carts of gifts brought by Wang Nie are all betrothal gifts for you. I have not agreed yet, thinking I should ask for your opinion first.\"","Song Jinzhao pretended to be very surprised, then quickly shook her head.","\"My home is in the Dongzhao Kingdom, and the Shuobei Kingdom is so far away. I do not want to marry there.\"","Xiao Chengjing deliberately rubbed his forehead, pretending to be in a difficult position.","\"You are a county princess personally titled by me, and I do not want you to go for a political marriage either. However, this matter concerns the peace between our two nations, placing me in a difficult spot. If I refuse, it will inevitably draw criticism and make the people of the world think I am too biased towards you. Therefore, you must refuse this matter yourself.\"","This was wanting to have his cake and eat it too; he had said all the good and bad things himself.","\"What does Your Majesty mean?\"","Xiao Chengjing straightened his back. \"At tomorrow's morning assembly, I will summon the chief envoy of the diplomatic mission. After the other party explains their intentions, I will immediately summon you.\"","\"Then you will repeat what you just said in front of all the civil and military officials. If the courtiers insist on you going for the marriage alliance and you truly cannot refuse, you can agree to the engagement first, and marry only after Beloved Subject Song starts a family. By dragging it out for four or five years, this matter will just fade away.\"","Song Jinzhao's mouth twitched, somewhat not knowing how to reply.","Is it really that hard to firmly say no?","Being this cowardly, and he still wants to conquer the Shuobei Kingdom?","It would save more lives if you just knelt down and surrendered.","Even with so much dissatisfaction in her heart, Song Jinzhao could only agree for now.","\"Your Majesty is wise. I would never have thought of such a brilliant plan.\"","Xiao Chengjing nodded in satisfaction.","At the morning assembly the next day, Wang Nie deliberately opened his collar wide, completely revealing the purple finger marks.","The civil and military officials lowered their heads one after another, pretending not to see.","They had already heard about the matter yesterday afternoon, but no one dared to speak.","There was now one more piece of evidence that Prince Qi was the mastermind behind stealing the potatoes, and he had even admitted it voluntarily.","But so what? If the Emperor said he wasn't, there was nothing they could do.","Fei Yanzhang and Ye Liangyu still hadn't attended court. After seeing their fates clearly, who would dare to say another word?","Even the Censorate, which always dared to bluntly remonstrate, had now turned mute.","As for helping Wang Nie denounce Prince Qi for trying to strangle him, that was even more impossible.","\"I, the foreign minister Wang Nie, have come on the orders of His Majesty the Emperor of the Shuobei Kingdom to propose marriage to your esteemed country, seeking to marry your esteemed country's County Princess Linghui as an imperial consort, in order to solidify the everlasting diplomatic relations between our two nations.\"","The courtiers who had been lowering their heads playing dead instantly raised their heads, their rhythm never having been so unified.","They weren't marrying a princess over; they wanted to take County Princess Linghui back!","How could this do? If there were no princesses of marriageable age, there were still daughters of the imperial clan. It would never be the turn of a commoner county princess without royal blood to go for a marriage alliance.","It would be one thing if Song Jinzhao were an ordinary woman, but she simply wasn't.","She could not marry into the Shuobei Kingdom, absolutely not.","The courtiers who had not been informed in advance all focused their gazes on Dongfang Shaoting, Gu Qishan, and the others.","At such a critical moment, someone had to take the lead to stand out and object, and it had to be the highest-ranking officials.","But after waiting for a while, they found that whether it was Dongfang Shaoting or Gu Qishan, they were both very calm, as if they had known all along.","Just as they were hesitating in confusion, Xiao Chengjing, sitting on the dragon throne, spoke.","\"County Princess Linghui is not a member of the imperial family. I cannot immediately agree to her lifelong marriage; I must ask for her own opinion.\"","\"Summon County Princess Linghui and Compiler Song to the palace at once. If she agrees, I am naturally willing to play the matchmaker.\""]},{"number":376,"title":"Chapter 376: Song Qiming: My Sister Only Takes a Son-in-Law into Her Family, She Doesn't Marry Out","paragraphs":["The hall was dead silent. With a mocking smile, Wang Nie said to Xiao Chengjing, \"To think that the Emperor of Dongzhao, the esteemed Son of Heaven, cannot even dictate the marriage of a single woman.\"","Just as the courtiers were debating whether to retort, the Minister of Rites, Kang Zhibo, who was standing at the front left, stepped forward.","Looking at Wang Nie, he said, \"Chief Envoy, you are mistaken. Our Dongzhao was founded on propriety, and His Majesty loves his people like his own children. When it comes to a lifelong matter such as marriage, it is only natural to respect the County Princess's own wishes.\"","As soon as his voice faded, Dongfang Shaoting strolled out.","He offered a faint smile, though a hint of coldness lingered in his eyes.","\"Although County Princess Linghui comes from the common folk and lacks royal blood, her talent and character are superior. Furthermore, she has repeatedly rendered meritorious service to the benefit of our Dongzhao people. She is the supreme treasure of our nation, and those in this world worthy of her can be counted on one hand. Now, you ask her to marry far away to Shuobei to become a concubine to your Emperor. Naturally, we must ask the County Princess about such a grievance, lest it chill the hearts of the people and the County Princess herself.\"","Wang Nie's face darkened. \"The status of an Imperial Consort is incredibly noble. How can it be compared to an ordinary concubine?\"","The newly appointed Chancellor of the Hanlin Academy, Cai Qiong, stepped forward and said, \"An Imperial Consort is still a concubine. If your Emperor were to propose to the County Princess with the position of Empress, only then would it be considered sincere.\"","If looks could kill, Cai Qiong would already be dead.","The Empress of a nation could never be a foreign woman. Making Song Jinzhao the Empress—was he crazy, or were they?","Soon, the well-prepared Song Jinzhao and Song Qiming were brought into the palace.","The moment they stepped into the hall, everyone turned to look at Song Jinzhao.","She was dignified, elegant, and perfectly composed in the face of the unexpected.","To remain entirely unfazed in such a situation, perhaps only County Princess Linghui could manage it.","\"Your subject, Song Jinzhao, greets Your Majesty. Long live, long live, long live Your Majesty.\"","\"Your humble official, Song Qiming, greets Your Majesty. Long live, long live, long live Your Majesty.\"","The siblings knelt and bowed simultaneously, one slightly ahead of the other. Neither their voices nor their movements betrayed a trace of nervousness or panic.","\"Rise,\" Xiao Chengjing said, extending a hand with a smile.","\"I summoned you siblings to the palace today because there is an important matter on which I wish to ask your opinion.\"","\"County Princess Linghui, the Emperor of Shuobei intends to ask for your hand in marriage to make you his Imperial Consort. I wonder, are you willing?\"","Wang Nie stared unblinkingly at Song Jinzhao, ready to retort at any moment.","But just as everyone was waiting for Song Jinzhao to speak, Song Qiming, standing beside her, reacted like a dog whose tail had been stepped on. He opened his mouth and began to bark fiercely.","\"How could that work? Grandfather said that my sister is to take a live-in husband, not marry out.\"","Everyone looked at Song Qiming in unison, their eyes filled with astonishment.","A live-in husband? Really? The Song family seemed to have two male heirs already.","Sitting on the dragon throne, Xiao Chengjing paused. Why was this different from what they had agreed upon?","He seized the opportunity to play along and asked, \"Is this true?\"","Song Jinzhao nodded. \"It is indeed true.\"","\"After my parents passed away, I made a vow before my elders that I would not marry until my younger brother started a family of his own.\"","\"When I returned to my hometown last year, my grandfather discussed my marriage. Considering that I am growing older, he relented and agreed that I could marry, but demanded that I take a live-in husband. Otherwise, it would have to wait a few more years. After all, my youngest brother is only five years old and needs someone to take care of him.\"","Xiao Chengjing said, \"So that is how it is. In that case, a marriage alliance is out of the question.\"","Seeing Wang Nie preparing to speak, Song Qiming hurriedly opened his mouth to add more weight to the matter.","His voice boomed from his mouth like thunder, loud enough to shatter a person's eardrums.","\"It's not entirely impossible. As long as the Emperor of Shuobei is willing to marry into our family as a live-in husband, this marriage can proceed.\""]},{"number":377,"title":"Chapter 377: Step by Step, Wang Nie Was Furious to the Point of Fainting","paragraphs":["Someone's ceremonial tablet dropped to the ground, the sudden clatter making those nearby jolt in shock.","The civil and military officials stared at Song Qiming in disbelief.","How did he dare to suggest that the Emperor of Shuobei marry into the bride's family? What was he thinking?","Song Jinzhao's lips curled up slightly; along with her amusement, she couldn't help but feel a trace of gratification.","The fact that he could say such a thing meant his mindset had finally changed.","Xiao Chengjing's mouth hung open in astonishment, his heart beating a little faster.","Was this the top-tier scholar he had personally appointed? He didn't seem like this a few years ago.","The most shocked of all was Wang Nie. His vision went dark, and he nearly lost his footing and collapsed.","Hadn't they said the civil officials of the Dongzhao Kingdom were all timid cowards who feared war like tigers? How could this young official be so audacious?","Pointing an angry finger right at Song Qiming's nose, he began to curse.","\"Insolent! How dare a petty official like you speak so disrespectfully and insult the Emperor of our Shuobei Kingdom? Do you have any regard for our nation at all?\"","\"I have come by imperial decree to propose marriage, not solely to ask for the County Princess's hand, but to secure peace for the people of the world. Not only do you lack sincerity, but you also spout such arrogant nonsense. Are you trying to start a war?\"","Song Qiming covered his mouth, feigning ignorance.","\"I was just stating the facts. If he doesn't want to marry into her family, then forget it.\"","Wang Nie stood with his mouth half-open. A breath caught in his throat, he couldn't swallow it down, nor could he spit it out, making him feel terribly stifled.","Seeing this, the Minister of Rites, Kang Zhibo, stepped forward once again.","\"A marriage alliance between our two nations is indeed beneficial for the people of the world. Our nation has plenty of fine women, and in my opinion, a daughter of the imperial clan would be more suitable to marry your esteemed Emperor. If she could give birth to a prince carrying the royal bloodlines of both nations, that would truly be adding close ties to close ties.\"","Wang Nie's pupils dilated.","What use did they have for a woman of the imperial clan? The one they wanted was Song Jinzhao.","Dongfang Shaoting bowed to Xiao Chengjing with hands clasped.","\"The best candidate for a marriage alliance is a princess, as only she would be worthy of a monarch. Since our Dongzhao Kingdom has no princesses of marriageable age, in this humble subject's opinion, we can simply have Shuobei marry one of their princesses over to us.\"","In the crowd, Chu Liuyun couldn't help but frown.","Thank goodness Princess Yongjia was already married to him. Otherwise, the burden of this marriage alliance might really have fallen on her, which would have been far too dangerous.","Wang Nie was speechless.","Failing to bring back Song Jinzhao and having to give away a princess instead, not even a ghost would agree to such a losing deal.","He had threatened war, so why weren't they afraid?","Logically speaking, shouldn't they have immediately agreed to marry off Song Jinzhao?","Sitting on his high throne, Xiao Chengjing furrowed his brows in confusion.","Although the actions of Kang Zhibo and Dongfang Shaoting were arranged by him yesterday, he still felt that something was off.","Was it a bit too aggressive?","They were quite old, yet their acting was quite convincing.","\"I also think this is an excellent idea. I have heard that your esteemed nation's Third Princess is not yet married; I am willing to confer upon her the title of Noble Consort.\"","Wang Nie bent over, clutching his chest as his heart cramped with pain.","The Third Princess was only sixteen, and you are over fifty!","What was the use of being a Noble Consort? To become a widow when you die?","\"Our Emperor admires County Princess Linghui, which is why he sent me thousands of miles to propose. If the bride is not her, I fear His Majesty will be greatly disappointed.\"","Song Jinzhao gave a light chuckle and asked in return, \"It seems your Emperor has never even met me. I wonder where this so-called admiration comes from?\"","Wang Nie replied, \"After Prince Wei returned to Yandu, he recounted the County Princess's heroic bearing to His Majesty. Our Emperor was filled with admiration and thus ordered me to come and propose.\"","The civil and military officials collectively rolled their eyes.","Filled with admiration?","More like filled with dread.","That was why he couldn't wait to send you over to take her back.","Once she arrived in Shuobei, whether she could even keep her life would be another matter entirely.","Song Jinzhao nodded, putting on a show of understanding.","\"I see. To fall in love and send someone to propose based solely on the words of others, isn't your Emperor a bit too frivolous and casual?\"","Wang Nie stumbled back two steps. Perhaps because he had spent the entire previous night vomiting, his chest was not only aching, but his head was also starting to spin.","Song Jinzhao continued, \"There are hundreds, if not thousands, of women like me in the storybooks of the capital. If your Emperor were to read them, wouldn't he fall in love with mere paper characters?\"","Thud! Under the amused gazes of the crowd, Wang Nie's head spun and his vision blurred. His body swayed slightly before he collapsed backward.","If it hadn't been for the carpets covering the floor, blood would likely have been drawn.","No one expected him to faint, and for a moment, everyone froze.","Recovering his wits, Xiao Chengjing hastily stood up and shouted to Zhao Yande, \"Summon the imperial physician, quickly!\"","Song Jinzhao could not be married off, but nothing could be allowed to happen to Shuobei's chief envoy either.","If he really died here, even if it didn't spark a war, it would still cost them dearly.","With a single glance, Song Jinzhao could tell that Wang Nie had fainted from dehydration. An ordinary person wouldn't be able to recover from the pill he took yesterday for at least three days."]},{"number":378,"title":"Chapter 378: King Qi Regains Consciousness Then Falls into a Coma Again","paragraphs":["After the imperial physician's diagnosis, it was determined that Wang Nie was suffering from dehydration that damaged his stomach, along with a surge of blood and qi caused by extreme anger. He needed to be carried back for a proper rest.","Thus, the matter of the marriage alliance was temporarily put on hold.","When the man was carried into the Huitong Envoy Guest House, Qi Xiong instantly flew into a rage.","\"What did you do? Minister Wang is the envoy sent by our Shuobei Kingdom to your Dongzhao Kingdom to propose a marriage alliance. How could you beat him?\"","The Imperial Guards placed the stretcher on the ground.","\"We didn't beat him. He fainted because his own constitution is too weak. Yandu is thousands of miles away from the capital; next time you send an envoy, please find someone with a robust physique.\"","Watching the Imperial Guards flick their sleeves and leave, Qi Xiong grabbed the official who had accompanied Wang Nie into the palace, his tone angry and anxious.","\"What exactly happened? Did the Emperor of Dongzhao agree to the marriage alliance?\"","The official cried foul with a bitter face, recounting the matter from beginning to end without missing a single word.","\"Not only did they refuse, but they also humiliated us in return. Minister Wang fainted from their infuriating words.\"","Anger completely twisted Qi Xiong's face into that of a bear, his thick black eyebrows furrowing uglier than caterpillars.","\"Preposterous! We haven't fought them in a few years and their courage has grown. How dare they look down upon our Shuobei Kingdom.\"","\"I will immediately write a memorial to inform the Emperor. We absolutely cannot let this go easily this time.\"","Inside the Prince of Qi's Manor, Xiao Rongche was lying miserably on the edge of the bed, vomiting.","The sour-smelling food residue was mixed with threads of bright red blood.","Gu Jupu stood beside him with a hunched back, jumping with anxiety.","\"Your Highness, the blood stasis in your body has not yet dissipated. You must not get angry at this time, otherwise, once your condition worsens, I fear you might contract consumption.\"","His vision was pitch black. Xiao Rongche wept as he uncomfortably touched his left eye with his hand.","\"Why can't my eyes see? I could still see shadows yesterday.\"","His voice grew louder as he shouted, his fist smashing against the wooden board of the bedframe, each strike heavier than the last.","Gu Jupu stood by helplessly, wanting to pull him back but not daring to.","\"Your Highness has been overthinking and harboring pent-up frustrations. Coupled with your extreme emotional agitation yesterday, it caused an excess of liver fire, which worsened the condition of your eyes.\"","Unable to accept this, Xiao Rongche roared at Gu Jupu, \"Heal my eyes immediately! Right now!\"","Gu Jupu knelt down and kowtowed, \"This humble minister's medical skills are shallow. I beg Your Highness the Prince of Qi for forgiveness.\"","Xiao Rongche shook his head in disbelief, constantly muttering the word \"Impossible.\"","\"It was clearly promised that my left eye would be saved. How can I not see?\"","\"Go find Song Jinzhao! Bring her to me—\" His hoarse voice choked halfway through the roar.","Under the terrified gazes of the crowd, the lofty Xiao Rongche fell from the bed, his body crashing into the puddle of vomit.","\"Your Highness!\" The servants rushed forward to turn him over, but he had already lost consciousness.","Gu Jupu knelt on the ground, his body turning icy cold, the fingers resting on his thighs trembling.","Song Jinzhao had just come out of the palace. Before her front foot even crossed the threshold, the guards from the Prince of Qi's Manor rode frantically to the gate of the County Princess's Manor, even taking a tumble as they dismounted.","His face was covered in a mess of snot and tears, terrified that if Xiao Rongche died, he would be buried with him.","\"County Princess, please hurry over and take a look. My Highness is dying.\"","Song Jinzhao furrowed her brows slightly, a look of displeasure appearing on her face.","\"Is Court Envoy Gu not there?\"","The guard wailed, \"It was Court Envoy Gu who ordered this servant to come find you.\"","Less than half an hour later, Song Jinzhao walked into Xiao Rongche's courtyard. Before she even entered the door, she heard crying.","The Princess Consort and the concubines filled the entire room, two of them even holding children.","Is he dead and they are mourning?","Seeing Song Jinzhao enter, the pale-faced Gu Jupu immediately rushed up to plead for help.","\"County Princess, please quickly take a look at His Highness the Prince of Qi. No matter how I apply the acupuncture needles, he won't wake up.\"","Hearing this sentence, the Princess Consort of Qi, who was wiping her tears, seemed to have triggered an alarm. She rushed up like the wind, grabbed Song Jinzhao's arm, and was about to kneel.","\"County Princess Linghui, nothing can happen to His Highness.\"","Song Jinzhao glanced at Gu Jupu. Is the situation really this serious?","He seemed fine yesterday.","After a very careful examination, Song Jinzhao withdrew her hand from taking his pulse.","The situation was more serious than she had expected.","If this continued, not only would he have a short life, but sudden death was possible at any moment.","\"How did the Prince of Qi get so angry?\"","Gu Jupu replied, \"His Highness's left eye has also gone completely blind.\"","Hearing this, Song Jinzhao looked calmly at Xiao Rongche.","This outcome was bound to happen sooner or later. What made matters worse was that he had fallen into despair after being given hope, causing his emotions to completely collapse."]},{"number":379,"title":"Chapter 379: Fatherly Love Is Nothing Before Imperial Power","paragraphs":["After Song Jinzhao finished the acupuncture and wrote a prescription, she pulled Gu Jupu aside to whisper some advice before leaving.","\"The Prince of Qi is arrogant and proud; he absolutely will not accept the fact that he has gone blind. Coupled with his emotional agitation and internal stagnation, his mental state will deteriorate over time. You had better report his condition to the Emperor immediately, lest you suffer the consequences in the end.\"","Gu Jupu let out a deep, exhausted sigh.","\"I understand what the County Princess means. I will go to the palace later and report the truth to the Emperor.\"","Illness of the heart requires medicine of the heart. No one can save the Prince of Qi in his current state unless he comes to terms with it himself.","That afternoon, after Gu Jupu informed the Emperor of the Prince of Qi's condition, the Emperor remained silent for a long time.","Just when Gu Jupu thought he would erupt in anger, Xiao Chengjing merely said in a calm tone, \"Arrange for an imperial physician from the Imperial Hospital to reside in the Prince of Qi's manor and do your best to treat his illness. As for his sickness of the heart, it is up to him.\"","Having slapped his own face time and again, and now acting like a lunatic while causing trouble, Xiao Chengjing's already meager paternal love had been just about exhausted.","\"I obey the decree.\"","After Gu Jupu left, Xiao Chengjing ordered Zhao Yande, \"Summon Fan Guanshan for an audience.\"","Fan Guanshan, who was patrolling the Meridian Gate, was called to the Imperial Study.","Xiao Chengjing commanded in a deep voice, \"Once Wang Nie wakes up, go to the Huitong Guesthouse. Tell him about the Prince of Qi's condition word for word. Try to make it sound as severe as possible, and take the opportunity to give him a warning.\"","Fan Guanshan looked at Xiao Chengjing with hesitation on his face.","\"His Highness the Prince of Qi was injured by Qi Xiong, the captain of the guards of this marriage proposal delegation. May I ask if Your Majesty intends to hold this person accountable for his crime?\"","The other party was merely a minister, while the Prince of Qi was of royal blood.","Now, with one completely unharmed and the other severely injured and hard to cure, they should pursue the matter no matter what. Otherwise, the Shuobei Kingdom would think they were weak, easy to bully, and afraid of them.","Xiao Chengjing shook his head. \"Refusing the marriage alliance has already angered the Shuobei Kingdom. If we pursue this matter, it will inevitably be going too far. That is why I am sending you to give Wang Nie a warning.\"","Fan Guanshan felt a heavy weight in his chest. Despite this, he had to bow his head and comply, \"I obey the decree.\"","Gong Linjue had swindled the potatoes away with nothing but empty promises. Not only were the Prince of Qi's eyes uncured, but his physical health had also worsened. No matter how one calculated it, the Dongzhao Kingdom was on the losing end.","He truly hoped that one day, the people of the Dongzhao Kingdom would no longer have to swallow their anger and suffer grievances.","The rumors among the commoners shifted from marrying a foreign princess to marrying off their own County Princess. For a time, the people did not quite understand the severity of the matter.","The people arranged by Qingshuang began to quietly mingle in the crowds and exert their influence.","\"Last time, when the Prince of Wei from the Shuobei Kingdom came to our Dongzhao Kingdom, none of the military officials in the court were his match. Only the County Princess of Linghui could defeat him. If the two countries ever go to war, who else could be a match for the Prince of Wei from Shuobei?\"","\"The County Princess of Linghui is highly skilled in martial arts and is a divine doctor. She can even build waterwheels, and she was the one who presented potatoes to the Emperor. If we send her for the marriage alliance, what if she invents something else one day? Wouldn't all the benefits go to the Shuobei Kingdom?\"","A small number of well-informed commoners chimed in, \"I heard that during the morning assembly today, the Emperor and the officials disagreed with sending the County Princess of Linghui for the marriage alliance. Some say that the Shuobei Kingdom is targeting the County Princess this time, aiming to take her to Yandu and kill her.\"","An auntie carrying a basket to buy groceries was so frightened that she covered her mouth, her eyes widening as if they were about to pop out.","\"How can this be allowed? They are here for revenge!\"","A man furrowed his brows. \"It is revenge. Who asked the County Princess of Linghui to defeat the Prince of Wei from the Shuobei Kingdom?\"","The rumors spread faster and faster. With no one to stop them, they only needed a slight push to spread rapidly.","In a short time, all the commoners felt that Song Jinzhao could not be married off to the Shuobei Kingdom.","Coupled with the previous misunderstandings, many people insisted that the Shuobei Kingdom should marry a princess over to them. This way, the interests of the Dongzhao Kingdom would not be harmed, and the two countries could still form a marriage alliance to ensure lasting peace.","Wang Nie was unconscious for half a day, but Xiao Rongche was unconscious for two whole days before waking up.","After learning of his condition from his attendants, he clamored for an audience with the Emperor, wanting Xiao Chengjing to back him up.","But he could not even make it out the front gates of the Prince of Qi's manor.","After being stopped by the Imperial Guards guarding the entrance and told that the Emperor did not want to see him, Xiao Rongche fainted for the third time.","The imperial physician, who had just stepped out of his sedan chair, saw this and felt his world spin.","With so many people in the Imperial Hospital, why did they have to choose him? It was simply too unlucky!"]},{"number":380,"title":"Chapter 380: News from the Southwest","paragraphs":["Inside the County Princess's manor, Qingshuang hurried into Song Jinzhao's study, clutching a letter in her hand.","\"County Princess, a letter from the southwest has arrived. After Huo Chong returned to Ningzhou, he secretly made a trip to Panzhou. Our trackers discovered that the owner of the residence he visited is Zeng Qing, the former commander-in-chief of the Yuecheng Army.\"","\"How is the investigation into Gu Zhongxun going?\" Song Jinzhao closed the ledger and set it aside.","After two years of large-scale expansion, the monthly revenue from her hundreds of shops had reached tens of thousands of taels.","Half of this came from the profits of the perfume shops, with the wives and daughters of high-ranking officials and nobles in the capital serving as their primary customers.","Besides making money, these shops occasionally provided her with gossip and information from the inner courtyards.","Qingshuang took another letter from her robes and handed it to Song Jinzhao. It was a full half-knuckle thicker than the previous one.","\"All the information on Gu Zhongxun is in there, his temperament, background, and personal preferences.\"","\"It also contains the background details of everyone in the Gu family, including their relatives, friends, and colleagues.\"","Ever since she conceived the idea of expanding her influence into the southwest, Song Jinzhao had arranged for people to open shops there, selling food completely different from what was found in the capital.","On the surface, they were merchants; in secret, they gathered intelligence.","Song Jinzhao flipped through the pages one by one. Her expression turned slightly surprised when she read about Gu Zhongxun's background.","\"I didn't expect him to come from a peasant family.\"","Qingshuang nodded. \"Back then, Gu Zhongxun did not rank high in the palace examination, only placing in the third tier. Coupled with his lack of background, he was directly assigned to serve as a county magistrate in a small, remote border town in the southwest.\"","\"Having been an official for forty years, he climbed step by step from a county magistrate to the Provincial Administration Commissioner of the southwest. It is safe to say that no official in the royal court understands the southwest better than he does.\"","Looking up as she reached the third page, Song Jinzhao asked, \"After serving as a county magistrate for six years, he was transferred to be a prefect for another six years. His political achievements are quite impressive. Did he never think of transferring out?\"","Qingshuang nodded slightly. \"There was one time.\"","\"After he spent six years as a prefect, the late Emperor wanted to transfer him back to the capital. However, the official sent to replace him was killed by horse bandits on the way. The imperial court couldn't find a suitable candidate in time, so they ordered him to stay for another three years. Later, when the current Emperor ascended the throne, the matter was never brought up again.\"","\"As time passed, seeing no hope of a transfer, Gu Zhongxun simply settled down in the southwest. Aside from the people in the foreign tribe settlements, the rest of the commoners in the southwest deeply trust and respect him.\"","Song Jinzhao tapped her fingers rhythmically on the desk.","Forty years was longer than the current Emperor's reign. Separated by such vast distances, the Emperor's title likely held less weight in the southwest than the name Gu Zhongxun.","After pondering for a moment, Song Jinzhao continued flipping through the letter.","With two sons, one a civil official and the other a military officer, both serving in the southwest, he had clearly established his family's foundation there.","When Song Jinzhao noticed the age of Gu Zhongxun's only daughter, Gu Baozhu, she could not help but voice her surprise.","\"Gu Zhongxun is sixty-six this year. How is his daughter only fifteen? Didn't he refrain from taking concubines?\"","Qingshuang smiled, the corners of her lips curling up. She had the exact same reaction when she first found out.","\"Gu Baozhu is the child of Gu Zhongxun and his wife's old age. Even the sons of her two older brothers are two years older than her.\"","\"Because she is their only daughter, she is deeply doted on and is the apple of the Gu family's eye.\"","Song Jinzhao blinked in disbelief.","Gu Zhongxun's wife was sixty-three this year, which meant she gave birth to Gu Baozhu at the age of forty-eight.","That wasn't just being an older mother; that was extremely advanced maternal age.","\"How is the health of Gu Zhongxun and his wife?\"","Qingshuang replied, \"I heard it's very good. After going to the southwest, Gu Zhongxun began practicing martial arts. Although he only knows a few basic moves, it's enough to keep him fit and healthy.\"","\"His wife is the daughter of a military general. She has practiced martial arts since childhood and is actually more skilled than Gu Zhongxun.\"","Song Jinzhao nodded in realization. \"That makes sense.\"","After reviewing all the information, Song Jinzhao generally felt that there were no major issues with Gu Zhongxun.","The only person requiring attention was Gu Zhongxun's eldest son, Gu Gaoyuan.","If he intended for his son to succeed him as the Provincial Administration Commissioner of the southwest, this man would undoubtedly become Qiming's biggest competitor."]},{"number":381,"title":"Chapter 381: Choose Between Marrying a Royal Woman or Marrying Off a Princess","paragraphs":["Rumors in the city spread like wildfire, and everyone was waiting for news.","After patiently waiting in peace for a few days, Xiao Chengjing summoned the Minister of Rites, Kang Zhibo, into the palace.","\"Wang Nie has almost fully recovered. Go to the Huitong Guest House and tell them to choose one: either take a daughter from the imperial clan, or we marry off a princess to them.\"","Kang Zhibo lowered his voice with a distressed look. \"What if they refuse to choose either?\"","Xiao Chengjing's face turned cold. \"Then tell them to get the hell out. The Dongzhao Kingdom doesn't have extra free rice to feed them. Regardless, there is no way Princess Linghui is marrying into the Shuobei Kingdom.\"","Kang Zhibo clenched his jaw and bowed his head deeply in a salute.","\"I understand, Your Majesty. I will go negotiate right away.\"","Inside the Huitong Guest House, Wang Nie leaned back in his chair, frustrated and powerless, racking his brains.","Dongzhao's attitude during the morning assembly that day had been far too unyielding. For a moment, he had no idea how to complete the mission He Mingyuan had assigned to him.","Seeing his distress, Qi Xiong, who stood nearby cradling his sword, tried to comfort him. \"Minister Wang, there is no need to worry. I have already sent a messenger riding whip and spur back to Yandu. I believe it won't be long before His Majesty issues an edict.\"","Wang Nie sighed heavily and shot Qi Xiong a glance, a hint of complaint in his voice.","\"No matter how fast, it will still take two months. You heard what Fan Guanshan said when he came over the other day; Prince Qi's body is ruined. Tell me, why couldn't you have gone a little easier on him? Even if he is blind, he is still a prince.\"","Qi Xiong tightened his grip on his weapon and glanced down.","\"The situation was urgent at the time. I was too busy saving you to hold back. I truly didn't expect Xiao Rongche to be so useless that a light kick would cost him half his life.\"","Wang Nie sighed again.","\"The Emperor of Dongzhao refused to let Song Jinzhao enter a marriage alliance. Originally, we were in the right. But now that Prince Qi is severely injured, the situation will be entirely different once word gets out.\"","\"The time for war has not yet come, so this marriage alliance must be settled one way or another.\"","Not long after the two finished speaking, Cao Mo led Kang Zhibo into the courtyard.","\"Seeing that Lord Wang is in good spirits puts me and His Majesty at ease.\" The pleasantries arrived before the man himself even stepped up.","As fellow Ministers of Rites, Wang Nie knew exactly what kind of person the other man was.","Annoyed, Wang Nie propped his forehead with his hand.","\"May I ask what brings Minister Kang here today? Since I woke up, my energy has been far worse than before. This is the only time of day I feel somewhat alert, but I still get drowsy after sitting for just a little while.\"","Kang Zhibo's mouth twitched, a flash of coldness crossing his eyes.","Energy far worse than before? He could fool a ghost with that nonsense.","\"Is that so? I heard from Lord Cao that you've had an excellent appetite these past two days, demanding eight dishes and a soup for every meal. I thought you had fully recovered—unlike our Prince Qi, who cannot even keep water down.\"","Wang Nie looked at the ground, blinking rapidly, in desperate need of a subject change.","\"My head is throbbing a bit, and I need to take a short nap. If Lord Kang has business, please make it quick.\"","A servant brought over a chair, and Kang Zhibo unceremoniously sat down.","\"I have come on His Majesty's orders to ask you: for the marriage alliance, does your kingdom intend to choose a daughter of the imperial clan, or will you have a princess marry over?\"","Wang Nie replied, \"I cannot make that decision. I have already dispatched a letter overnight to Yandu and must wait for my Emperor's decree.\"","Kang Zhibo nodded slowly, his expression meaningful.","\"From the capital to Yandu, a round trip takes at least two months. If the Chief Envoy does not plan to leave, I ask that you remain inside the Huitong Guest House and minimize your outings during this period.\"","Displeased, Qi Xiong gripped his sword.","\"Are you trying to imprison us? Is this the Dongzhao Kingdom's way of treating guests?\"","Kang Zhibo shook his head decisively and began to explain in an earnest tone.","\"Of course not. It is just that rumors are rampant in the capital about how you severely injured Prince Qi. Furthermore, Princess Linghui holds great prestige among the common people, and they are unwilling to see her marry far away into Shuobei.\"","\"If you were to go out, it is inevitable that you would be targeted. I am simply looking out for your own good.\"","Qi Xiong radiated a chilling aura. He wanted to lash out but could only hold it in, his face darker than the bottom of a pot.","Once Kang Zhibo and his entourage left, he kicked and shattered the doorframe.","\"They push us too far! The day the Shuobei army conquers this capital, I will kill them all. I'll slice them into a thousand pieces!\"","Being a civil official, Wang Nie repeatedly pressed his hands down to calm him.","\"Keep your voice down! This is the capital, not Yandu. There are countless spies outside; be careful someone doesn't hear you.\"","Qi Xiong slammed his palm against a pillar.","\"Let them hear! You think I'm afraid of them? Even if you gave them ten times the courage, they wouldn't dare kill us.\"","Wang Nie closed his eyes in sheer exhaustion.","Simple-minded and all brawn. If he had known better, he would have brought someone else with him."]},{"number":382,"title":"Chapter 382: Good News from Oushi Nian's Return to Beijing","paragraphs":["The blazing sun hung high in the sky. Ou Shinian, the Minister of Works, had finally returned from Mingzhou after being away from the capital for nearly a year.","He lifted the carriage curtain and looked up at the characters for \"Capital City\" carved into the city wall. All the exhaustion in his body vanished in an instant, leaving only the bittersweet feeling of being so close to home.","\"Do not return to the manor yet. Head to the palace immediately.\"","The maritime expedition had yielded significant results, and he had to report to the Emperor at once.","\"Yes, My Lord.\" The driver nodded in compliance, immediately pulling the reins to drive the carriage into the city.","In the imperial palace, Xiao Chengjing, who had been in a foul mood for months, finally received some good news.","\"Is this true? Can that ship truly travel a thousand miles a day?\"","Ou Shinian smiled and cupped his hands in a respectful salute. \"To answer Your Majesty, this humble subject personally led the boatmen and the naval forces on a sea trial for a month. During that time, we encountered tsunamis and torrential rains three times, but we remained safe and sound, and the ship never capsized.\"","\"We also verified the locations of six islands provided by the commoners of Mingzhou, though they were all in the coastal waters. However, this humble subject believes that as long as we send more men to travel further, sooner or later, we will find the origin place of potatoes. We might even find more varieties of high-yield crops.\"","The more Xiao Chengjing listened, the more delighted he became, pacing back and forth in his excitement.","\"Excellent! After so many days, We have finally heard a piece of good news.\"","Standing in place, Ou Shinian froze for a moment.","What did that mean?","Could it be that there had been a lot of bad news lately?","After receiving a round of praise, Ou Shinian left the Imperial Study with a glowing, red face.","It was only after returning home that he learned what had transpired in the capital during his absence.","\"It hasn't even been a year, how could so many things have happened?\"","Prince Qi had gone blind in both eyes and was severely injured by the marriage-seeking envoy delegation from the Shuobei Kingdom.","The two countries had been at war for so many years, and neither side had ever brought up the word \"marriage alliance.\"","And the target of their proposal was County Princess Linghui. This was as obvious as Sima Zhao's ill intent; they were clearly harboring nothing but malicious schemes.","Eldest Young Master Ou: \"Father, did you not hear any news at all while you were in Mingzhou?\"","Ou Shinian looked utterly bitter.","\"When I left the capital, I knew something had happened in the southwest, but I never expected the Emperor to send Prince Qi.\"","\"Mingzhou is so far away. I was busy from morning to night every day and had to go out to sea from time to time. I truly had no energy to care about anything else.\"","Madam Ou tugged at Ou Shinian's loose sleeves with an aching heart; he had lost a significant amount of weight compared to when he left.","\"You have suffered, My Lord.\"","Ou Shinian waved his hand to show he was fine. \"No matter how hard it is, serving the imperial court is worth it. So, the Emperor did not agree to the marriage alliance?\"","Eldest Young Master Ou: \"A marriage alliance is acceptable, but the bride cannot be County Princess Linghui. Right now, everyone is waiting for word from the Shuobei Kingdom.\"","Ou Shinian breathed a sigh of relief. \"That is good. They can marry off anyone, but not County Princess Linghui.\"","Song Jinzhao was incredibly talented. If it were not for her ideas, the ocean-faring galleons could never have been built so quickly. Such a talent absolutely could not be married off to the Shuobei Kingdom.","Inside the Huitong Envoy Hostel, Wang Nie, who was still feigning illness, did not step out of his room all day.","Qi Xiong carried some bar snacks in his hands, his expression tense, his footsteps moving so fast they were practically a blur.","He shoved open Wang Nie's door, startling the man sitting on the daybed.","\"Can't you knock before coming in?\" Wang Nie glared at Qi Xiong with annoyance.","Qi Xiong casually placed the food box on the table.","Lately, the meals prepared by the envoy hostel had become increasingly bland, with the staff constantly claiming that a sick person should eat light food. Left with no choice, he had to go out and buy food.","\"My Lord, while buying food at the tavern today, I overheard something that I felt necessary to tell you.\"","Seeing his grave expression, Wang Nie could not help but press, \"What is it?\"","Qi Xiong tugged at his clothes uncomfortably.","He had walked too fast just now, and his back was covered in sweat, causing his innermost layer of clothing to stick to his skin.","\"The Dongzhao Kingdom has built incredibly powerful ships to go out to sea, saying they are looking for the origin place of potatoes. I heard there are also landmasses across the sea with plenty of treasures.\"","Wang Nie furrowed his brows in disbelief. \"More landmasses? Who did you hear this from?\"","Qi Xiong: \"From the youngest son of Dongzhao's Minister of Works, Ou Shinian. I eavesdropped on him at the tavern.\"","\"Ou Shinian just returned to the capital yesterday, specifically for the matter of building ships to go out to sea. According to Ou Shinian's youngest son, they might even find crops with higher yields than potatoes.\"","Wang Nie pondered for a moment before instructing Qi Xiong: \"Find two clever men to go out and gather intelligence. Start with Ou Shinian's youngest son and try to coax more information out of him.\"","Qi Xiong: \"That will be easy. I heard them say they are going out to drink at a brothel tonight. Once they are drunk, we can coax anything out of them.\""]},{"number":383,"title":"Chapter 383: A Message from Yan Capital","paragraphs":["At midnight, two petite men secretly crawled in through the dog hole at the base of the wall.","The moment Wang Nie's door was knocked upon, Qi Xiong immediately opened it from the inside.","What did you find out?","The man got drunk and spilled everything, the two eagerly scrambled to speak.","Seeing Wang Nie sitting on the couch with his coat draped over his shoulders, they immediately ran over to report to him, According to Second Young Master Ou, the ships built by the Dongzhao Kingdom can travel four hundred miles a day at sea.","Ever since County Princess Linghui discovered potatoes, they have indeed been searching for a new continent. Word has it that it won't be long before the imperial court sends people out to sea again, not only to search for treasures but also to expand the territory of their Dongzhao Kingdom...","Wang Nie clenched his fist and slammed it hard on the table. The lamplight flickered, casting dancing shadows across the faces of the four men.","It's this Song Jinzhao again. No wonder the Emperor insists on marrying her and bringing her back. If this person doesn't die, who knows what kind of chaos she will stir up in the future.","Qi Xiong tightened his grip on the sword hanging at his waist, a dark mist gradually rising in his eyes.","Do you need this subordinate to kill her?","Wang Nie glanced at Qi Xiong with a look reserved for idiots.","Even Prince Wei cannot defeat her, how could you possibly kill her?","Qi Xiong blinked, released the hilt of his sword with his right hand, and stepped aside.","He had forgotten for a moment.","He was no match for Gong Linjue, which meant he certainly couldn't defeat Song Jinzhao.","Wang Nie thought it over and over, finally getting up from the couch and walking to the desk in the inner room to pull out some paper and grind ink.","After half a cup of tea's time, he handed the written letter to Qi Xiong.","Send someone out of the city with this first thing tomorrow morning. They must travel day and night without stopping. It would be best if it arrives in Yandu at the same time as the previous two letters.","Qi Xiong took the letter with both hands and nodded solemnly in compliance.","A month and a half later.","Panting heavily, horses galloped into Yandu as if they were flying. The first thing He Mingyuan saw was Qi Xiong's memorial.","After reading the last word on the paper, his face had darkened to a shade blacker than ink.","Without a war in five years, the Dongzhao Kingdom was growing increasingly bold.","Not only did they refuse the marriage alliance, but they also beat up the envoy he had sent to propose.","It seemed that the preparations to attack the Dongzhao Kingdom would have to be moved up.","Summon Prince Wei.","Just as Gong Linjue stepped into the palace, the first letter Wang Nie wrote after waking up was delivered.","The paper, still carrying the scent of ink, was tossed in front of him. As it fluttered down, Gong Linjue reached out and caught it.","After reading it, he chuckled softly, then raised his head to look at He Mingyuan.","Xiao Rongche is not only stupid but also extremely reckless. There is no evidence, and the Emperor of Dongzhao wants to protect his son. Your Majesty need not take this matter to heart.","He Mingyuan held his chin high with an expression of cold indifference.","Even if people died, I wouldn't worry. This trivial matter is nothing. Xiao Chengjing refused to marry off Song Jinzhao. What do you make of this?","The trace of a smile on Gong Linjue's lips gradually vanished.","It is unexpected, yet entirely expected. Everyone can see Song Jinzhao's value. If we immediately dispatch troops for a feigned attack, perhaps the Emperor of Dongzhao will compromise.","The hall remained quiet for a long time. If one listened closely, they could hear the rhythmic tapping of He Mingyuan's fingers against the dragon desk.","A feigned attack wastes resources and effort. Just mobilizing troops to the border would consume a massive amount of rations. If they don't fall for it, and a real war breaks out, now is not the best time.","Since Song Jinzhao won't be marrying anyone in the next few years, we will wait a few years. When the time is ripe for war, we will propose again. If the Dongzhao Kingdom refuses, we can use that as an excuse to deploy our troops. If they agree, we will kill Song Jinzhao and then start the war. Either way, it works to our advantage.","Gong Linjue cupped his hands in a respectful salute. Your Majesty is wise."]},{"number":384,"title":"Chapter 384: Marriage by Proxy","paragraphs":["As soon as he finished speaking, another letter was delivered.","After reading it, He Mingyuan sat in his chair, lost in thought for a long time.","Unaware of the letter's contents, Gong Linjue could only stand where he was and wait.","Three consecutive letters. It seemed the diplomatic marriage envoy had encountered quite a few incidents in the capital.","He Mingyuan spoke, \"I remember that Prince Chuan recently brought back a young daughter from the common folk, and her mother was a brothel woman.\"","Gong Linjue paused for a second before reacting and replying, \"That is indeed true. The girl's name is He Shuwan, and she is fifteen this year.\"","Aloeswood incense curled upward within the hall, creating a heavy, suffocating atmosphere.","He Mingyuan asked faintly, \"Has anyone seen her?\"","Gong Linjue shook his head, a suspicion forming in his mind.","\"Prince Chuan finds it disgraceful. Ever since he brought her back, she has been locked up in the manor and has never stepped outside.\"","He Mingyuan's next words confirmed his guess.","\"Since no one has seen her, then we shall swap her out. Lianyan is about the same age. I leave this matter to you. Tell Prince Chuan that an imperial decree will arrive at his manor in a few days. The one marrying into the Dongzhao Kingdom will be his youngest daughter, He Shuwan.\"","\"Rather than sending her to the imperial palace to be a noble consort, I believe Prince Ying's manor is a much more suitable place.\"","Gong Linjue completely understood He Mingyuan's intentions.","Lianyan was a hidden spy trained by the Thousand Mechanisms Guard. Sending her to the Dongzhao Kingdom meant she would be far more than just a simple princess bride.","\"This subject will see to it immediately.\"","In less than three days, the carriage carrying the princess bride departed from Yandu.","On the very day Wang Nie received the imperial decree, he immediately went to seek an audience with Xiao Chengjing.","In the grand hall, Wang Nie stood tall with his chest out, speaking with righteous conviction, \"Respected Emperor of the Dongzhao Kingdom, my Emperor was deeply disappointed to hear that the County Princess Linghui is unwilling to enter this marriage. However, for the sake of harmony between our two nations, we are willing to marry Princess Shuwan to your esteemed country's Second Prince as his consort, thereby forging a lasting bond between our nations.\"","The civil and military officials all turned to look at Wang Nie in unison, their eyes filled with astonishment.","The Shuobei Kingdom actually agreed to marry a princess over? They had assumed the other party would choose a girl from the imperial clan.","Xiao Chengjing frowned in confusion. \"Your country's Third Princess does not seem to be Princess Shuwan.\"","Wang Nie calmly curled his lips into a smile.","\"Princess Shuwan is the youngest daughter of my Shuobei Kingdom's Prince Chuan. Her surname is He, and her name is Shuwan. My Emperor specially bestowed upon her the title of Princess Shuwan. Her Highness's carriage is already on its way as we speak.\"","Everyone suddenly understood.","So she was actually a commandery princess.","Seeing that Dongfang Shaoting and the others remained silent, as if silently agreeing to the matter, Xiao Rongyan hastily stepped forward.","\"Imperial Father, your son already has a primary consort. I am afraid I cannot marry Princess Shuwan.\"","Taking an enemy nation's princess as a primary consort would be equivalent to telling the whole world that he could never become the emperor.","Xiao Chengjing narrowed his eyes at Wang Nie.","\"Our Dongzhao Kingdom does not have the custom of having two primary consorts of equal standing. If Princess Shuwan wishes to marry him, I am afraid she can only be a secondary consort.\"","Choosing Prince Ying over himself—was this because they thought he was too old?","To everyone's surprise, Wang Nie agreed without hesitation.","\"As long as our two nations can forge an eternal alliance, a secondary consort is fine as well.\"","\"...\"","For a moment, no one spoke a word.","The Shuobei Kingdom had repeatedly made concessions, and suddenly, no one could find a reason to refuse.","Xiao Rongyan furrowed his brows tightly, looking at the Emperor with a pleading expression.","He truly did not want to marry her.","Even as a secondary consort, she was still an enemy nation's princess. He wouldn't be able to hit or scold her; marrying her would be incredibly troublesome.","Xiao Chengjing acted as if he didn't see Xiao Rongyan's pleading gaze, agreeing to the matter without much consideration.","\"As long as your Shuobei Kingdom does not feel wronged, I could ask for nothing more.\"","\"Draft an imperial decree: Today, Princess Shuwan of the Shuobei Kingdom comes from afar to foster peace and secure diplomatic relations between our two nations. We are exceedingly pleased, and hereby bestow this woman in marriage to Prince Ying, Xiao Rongyan, as his secondary consort. They are to be married immediately upon the princess's arrival in the capital. The Ministry of Rites shall prepare all related matters without error!\"","The civil and military officials all knelt and shouted loudly, \"We obey the decree! Long live the Emperor, long live, long, long live!\"","\"Your son obeys the decree and thanks Imperial Father for the marriage bestowal,\" Xiao Rongyan knelt on the ground expressionlessly, as if his heart had died.","Wang Nie swept his gaze over everyone present. In the moment he lowered his eyes, he couldn't help but secretly curl his lips into a smirk.","Once they found out that Princess Shuwan's biological mother was a brothel woman, he wondered if they would still be able to smile."]},{"number":385,"title":"Chapter 385: He Must Marry Her Even If He Dies of Anger","paragraphs":["Xiao Rongyan threw a massive tantrum after returning to the estate, but ultimately had to accept this outcome.","Side Consort Li Qinyun stood outside the room, eavesdropping.","Although they would both be side consorts, the other woman was a princess, thousands of times more noble than her. Once she entered the estate, she would undoubtedly suppress Li Qinyun completely.","\"Your Ladyship, the Princess Consort is heading this way.\"","The maid turned her head toward the entrance. Upon seeing the Princess Consort of Ying approaching with her entourage, she hurriedly tugged at Li Qinyun's sleeve to warn her.","Li Qinyun took a step back, pretending she had just arrived.","When she walked up to them, the Princess Consort of Ying shot her a cold glance.","\"I have important matters to discuss with His Highness. Side Consort Li, you may step down.\"","Li Qinyun clenched her jaw and lowered her head in aggrieved submission.","She only raised her head after the door was closed, her eyes full of grievance.","The maid supporting her comforted her in a low voice, \"Don't be sad, Your Ladyship. Princess Shuwan's entry into the estate is most disadvantageous to the Princess Consort. When they start fighting, you can just sit back and watch the show.\"","Her sharp nails snagged a thread in her silk handkerchief. In Li Qinyun's eyes, there was not only sorrow but also deep resentment.","\"I have endured for so many years, and now there is yet another person stepping on my head. Even His Highness does not treat me as well as he used to.\"","She pressed the back of her hand against her delicate, beautiful face.","Her skin was as smooth as jade, just like before, but it emanated an icy chill, as if the coldness was seeping from her very bones.","\"In the end, I cannot compete with their family backgrounds and statuses. I am afraid I am going to lose this game of chess.\"","After walking down the steps, Li Qinyun looked up at the sky. A desolate smile curled the corners of her lips, as if she were mocking herself, or perhaps regretting her choices.","Inside the room, the floor was a mess of shattered objects. The Princess Consort of Ying could barely find a place to step.","\"Your Highness, someone from the Ministry of Rites just came to discuss the wedding procedures with me. I wonder which courtyard you would like Princess Shuwan to stay in?\"","As the primary wife, no matter how dissatisfied she was, she could only endure it.","With a loud bang, another heavy blow landed. Xiao Rongyan almost cracked the table with his palm.","\"Do you need to ask me about such a trivial matter? Just arrange any random courtyard for her.\"","Her pale lips pressed into a thin line.","Courtyards varied in quality, and the other party was a princess. If she was dissatisfied with the courtyard, the blame would ultimately fall on the Princess Consort.","\"There are two courtyards in the estate that meet the regulations for a side consort: Tinglan Courtyard and Ningshuang Courtyard. Which one does Your Highness think is suitable?\"","Tinglan Courtyard was close to the front hall; it had a good location and its decorations were luxurious yet elegant.","Ningshuang Courtyard was close to the back wall of the estate. It was remote, and although it was spacious, it had been unoccupied for a long time.","She wanted to assign the latter but didn't dare, while assigning the former left her unwilling.","Therefore, upon hearing Xiao Rongyan throwing a temper tantrum in his room, she hurried over. It would be best if she could get him to assign Ningshuang Courtyard to the princess of the Shuobei Kingdom.","Without a second thought, Xiao Rongyan frowned and blurted out, \"Arrange Ningshuang Courtyard for her.\"","The Princess Consort of Ying suppressed the joy in her heart and nodded obediently, \"Yes.\"","After saying that, she spoke again, \"Just now, Her Majesty the Empress sent someone with a message, asking me to enter the palace tomorrow. It is probably regarding the political marriage. Does Your Highness have any instructions?\"","Xiao Rongyan closed his eyes wearily. After a moment of silence, he opened them again, his eyes revealing a sense of despondency.","\"Tomorrow, I will go into the palace with you to pay respects to my mother.\"","Inside the County Princess's Estate.","Hearing that the Shuobei Kingdom was sending a princess for a political marriage, Song Jinzhao raised her eyebrows in surprise.","\"This is not the Shuobei Kingdom's style. Marrying off a princess? They probably want to send a spy over. Send someone to investigate Princess Shuwan's background thoroughly, and plant a mole inside the Ying Prince's Estate.\"","As soon as she finished speaking, a carrier pigeon landed on the windowsill of the room.","Qingshuang walked over to check. There was a wisp of pale yellow down under the pigeon's wing.","\"It's a carrier pigeon from the Shuobei Kingdom.\" She untied the letter from the pigeon's leg and handed it to Song Jinzhao.","Upon opening it, the small slip of paper was completely blank; there was nothing on it.","Song Jinzhao held the paper over the candle flame to roast it for a moment, and the handwriting slowly revealed itself.","\"Grew up with her mother in a brothel from a young age. At fourteen, she was taken back to the estate by Prince Chu'an. She has never been shown to the public, and her appearance is unknown.\"","These short three sentences were all the information they could gather.","Qingshuang took the note and froze halfway through reading it.","Grew up in a brothel? Isn't this a bit...","\"County Princess, do you think others know about Princess Shuwan's origins?\"","Song Jinzhao's expression remained relatively calm.","\"They definitely don't know, otherwise they wouldn't have agreed so readily.\"","Qingshuang asked, \"Does this news need to be spread?\"","Song Jinzhao shook her head.","\"No matter what her status is, the Emperor would agree. The imperial edict has already been issued, so at most people will just curse about it. There's no need to say anything.\"","Qingshuang placed the note in the fire to burn it. \"If the Prince of Ying finds out about Princess Shuwan's background, he will probably die of anger.\"","Song Jinzhao replied, \"Even if he dies of anger, he still has to marry her.\""]},{"number":386,"title":"Chapter 386: Persuasion of Imperial Consort Rong","paragraphs":["The next day, Prince Ying and his wife entered the palace to pay their respects. Noble Consort Rong dismissed everyone else, keeping only the two of them behind to talk.","\"I heard that the officials from the Ministry of Rites visited yesterday. Do you plan to have the princess of Shuobei Kingdom stay in the Ningshuang Courtyard?\"","Prince Ying and his wife both froze, not expecting her to ask about this matter.","The empty bedchamber inexplicably induced a sense of panic.","Princess Consort Ying nervously clutched her skirt, remaining utterly silent in hopes that Xiao Rongyan would answer.","Xiao Rongyan, whose resentment had yet to fade, had no scruples in front of Noble Consort Rong and immediately began to complain.","\"I do not want to marry her at all. Even looking at her for one more second annoys me.\"","Hearing him say this, Noble Consort Rong's face instantly darkened.","She opened her rouged lips and immediately began to scold him.","\"You bastard! No matter how reluctant you are, she is still the princess sent by Shuobei Kingdom for a political marriage. If people find out that you are mistreating her, imagine the gossip it will cause. Your imperial father alone would not spare you.\"","Xiao Rongyan raised his voice in dissatisfaction: \"A woman must obey her husband after marriage. Once she enters my manor, she is my secondary consort. Shuobei Kingdom is separated from us by thousands of mountains and rivers, and Prince Chu'an's daughter is not even a true princess. Who would still care about her?\"","Noble Consort Rong let out a heavy, cold snort, frustrated by his failure to meet her expectations.","\"Whether she is a commandery princess or an imperial princess, He Shuwan came for a political marriage and represents Shuobei Kingdom. The Emperor does not want to go to war with Shuobei. You absolutely must not give anyone cause for gossip, otherwise Prince Qi's fate today will be your fate tomorrow.\"","Princess Consort Ying drew her knees together, gradually feeling a bit cold.","After a moment of silence, Xiao Rongyan began to argue back: \"Shuobei Kingdom has killed so many of our soldiers. If I treat He Shuwan too well, the military officials in the court will definitely say that I am pandering to foreigners for glory and am weak and easily bullied. When that happens, who will stand on my side?\"","Noble Consort Rong shot a cold glance at Princess Consort Ying. \"The affairs of the princely manor are complex. Since Prince Ying is here, you may go back first.\"","She had originally intended to instruct them separately, but who would have thought they would come together.","Her presence was truly somewhat of an obstacle; many things were inconvenient to say.","Princess Consort Ying first glanced at Xiao Rongyan. Seeing him remain silent in tacit agreement, she had no choice but to rise and take her leave.","The moment the doors of the hall closed, Noble Consort Rong immediately stood up, walked over to Xiao Rongyan, and tapped him with her index finger.","\"Without the support of the courtiers, how have you become increasingly stupid, like a headless fly!\"","\"Right now, none of the courtiers are taking sides; they are just waiting for the seven princes in the palace to grow up. The attitudes of those military officials are completely unimportant now. They will not help you anyway.\"","As if his tail had been stepped on, Xiao Rongyan stood up angrily and flared up at Noble Consort Rong, his face turning red.","\"According to what Imperial Mother says, I should just wait for my seven younger brothers to grow up and do nothing. When that time comes, what will the throne have to do with me?\"","Having her exquisite makeup sprayed with saliva, Noble Consort Rong closed her eyes, feeling completely drained of energy.","She tempered her anger and spoke slowly: \"How can you still not understand at this point? The Emperor does not favor you and Prince Qi that much, otherwise he would not have gone to the trouble of having so many sons.\"","\"Not to mention arranging adoptive mothers of noble status for them, especially the Fifth Prince raised by the Empress. When he grows up, your chances of winning will only become smaller and smaller.\"","Xiao Rongyan clenched his fists. He wanted to speak but had nothing to say, so he could only sulk in silence.","Seeing him in this state, Noble Consort Rong also felt a pang of heartache.","She reached out and pressed on Xiao Rongyan's shoulders to make him sit down, then stared into his eyes with a serious expression and said: \"Marrying the princess of Shuobei Kingdom is beneficial to you.\"","\"First, it will make the common people feel that this peace was bought by your marriage to the princess, allowing you to win over the hearts of the people.\"","When she reached the second point, Noble Consort Rong's voice noticeably dropped, becoming as soft as a mosquito's buzz, almost inaudible.","\"Second, you can use the power of Shuobei Kingdom to help you obtain the throne. If no one in the court will help you, you must find others to help you.\"","Xiao Rongyan's pupils suddenly shrank, staring at Noble Consort Rong in disbelief.","\"You want me to collude with a foreign country? This is the grave crime of treason!\"","Noble Consort Rong put on a stern face and said: \"I told you to use them, not to commit treason.\"","Xiao Rongyan's teeth chattered, and his lips trembled continuously.","\"What is the difference? If I want them to help me, I have to pay a price. This is inviting a wolf into the house.\"","Noble Consort Rong spoke with righteous indignation, as if she never felt she was in the wrong at all.","\"Those who achieve great things do not bother about trifles. This is exactly how your imperial father obtained his throne. Back then, if he had not leaked military intelligence to Shuobei Kingdom, causing Marquis Wuying to be defeated in battle, the person sitting on the throne today would not be Xiao Chengjing.\"","\"So what if it is inviting a wolf into the house? Whether it is wealth or territory, as long as you can become the Emperor, just give them some. Have you never learned to endure present hardships for future ambitions? At worst, you can just take it back later.\"","Xiao Rongyan stared blankly at his mother, even his breathing coming to a halt.","Imperial Father's throne was obtained like this?","At this moment, his mind was buzzing, as if a kettle had exploded."]},{"number":387,"title":"Chapter 387: What My Dad Can Do, I Can Do Too","paragraphs":["Seeing him remain silent for a long time, Noble Consort Rong pressed down hard on his shoulders and shook him back and forth, trying to snap him out of it.","\"Marrying Princess Shuwan is a godsend. Not only must you marry her, but you must also treat her well so that she will stand by your side and help you.\"","Xiao Rongyan slowly came back to his senses, staring blankly at Noble Consort Rong.","\"Mother, where did you hear that Imperial Father leaked military intelligence?\"","Noble Consort Rong furrowed her brows in agitation, having no desire to answer this question at all.","\"Where I heard it from is not important. What matters is that he succeeded.\"","Xiao Rongyan's knees gave way, and he collapsed to the ground.","He shook his head, his mind a tangled mess, completely unable to sort out his thoughts.","\"Let me think, let me think,\" he muttered subconsciously, speaking as much to Noble Consort Rong as to himself.","Seeing him in this state, Noble Consort Rong released him, frustrated by his lack of resolve, her brow creased with intense dissatisfaction.","It was already afternoon by the time Xiao Rongyan returned to his manor. Princess Consort Ying, who had been waiting for two hours, immediately came forward to greet him, only to have the door shut in her face.","Looking at the study door that Xiao Rongyan had closed himself, Princess Consort Ying blinked in bewilderment.","She stared at the door, her face full of confusion.","What was going on? He looked as if he had lost his soul.","Inside the study, Xiao Rongyan sat in his chair for the entire afternoon.","He replayed all the significant events he had experienced from childhood to adulthood, especially all the efforts he had made since coming of age to compete with Prince Qi for the position of Crown Prince.","Finally, thinking about how the power in his hands had been completely diluted in just two short years, how his status in the court had plummeted, and how he now had seven more younger brothers vying for the throne, the anger in his heart only grew.","Noble Consort Rong's words involuntarily swirled in his mind.","Xiao Rongyan thought it over and over, deducing the two paths of doing it versus not doing it hundreds of times in his head, before finally reaching a conclusion.","Noble Consort Rong was right.","If he did not use the Shuobei Kingdom, it would be almost impossible for him to obtain the throne.","At the thought that his own father's throne had not been obtained honorably either, Xiao Rongyan gradually convinced himself.","As the thought emerged, the expression on his face began to change.","From his initial apprehension to a final, resolute greed.","He stood up and looked around, as if this place were the Hall of Supreme Harmony, envisioning himself draped in the imperial yellow robe, ascending the steps one by one to sit upon the golden dragon throne.","After coming out of the study, the first thing Xiao Rongyan said to Princess Consort Ying was, \"Change the residence to Tinglan Courtyard.\"","Princess Consort Ying moved her lips but ultimately said nothing.","It was her mother-in-law's intention; she could not and dared not object.","It was early autumn when Princess Shuwan's imperial carriage arrived in the capital.","According to Xiao Chengjing's decree, the marriage was to take place immediately upon her arrival.","The carriage, adorned with red silk, stopped at the entrance of the Ying Prince's Manor, surrounded by commoners who had come to watch the spectacle.","Tens of thousands of copper coins were scattered, clinking and clattering for half a quarter of an hour, as Xiao Rongyan, wearing his wedding attire and a gentle expression, led He Shuwan into the manor.","Watching the two walk side by side through the main entrance, the fake-smiling Princess Consort Ying had already cursed them a thousand times in her heart.","The grand wedding ceremony was almost on par with that of a primary consort—where did that leave her, the actual Princess Consort?","Outside the crowd, at the base of the corner wall, Li Qinyun's face was pale, her heart dying over and over again.","She couldn't fight for the position of Princess Consort, and now even as a secondary consort, she was going to be suppressed by someone else. Her future status in the manor would likely be even more difficult.","Forced to show respect due to imperial prestige, and also wanting to see this Princess Shuwan who had come for the political marriage, Song Jinzhao still brought a modest gift and brought Song Qiming along.","Surprisingly, not only did she come, but Prince Qi, Xiao Rongche, had also arrived.","At the empty tables where no one had yet taken a seat, he was the only one sitting in a chair, his left eye staring blankly into the void, lost in unknown thoughts."]},{"number":388,"title":"Chapter 388: Mediocrities Scrapping, Trading Taunts","paragraphs":["To show his high regard and royal favor, Xiao Rongyan gave He Shuwan a grand wedding ceremony that far exceeded the standard for a side consort.","After welcoming her into the estate, the two first bowed toward the imperial palace to thank the Emperor for his grace, and then bowed to each other.","Standing to the side, Princess Consort Ying nearly ground her back teeth to dust.","Aside from not bowing to heaven and earth, and the wedding attire not being true red, everything else was identical to her own wedding. This was a blatant slap in the face.","On the other side, Xiao Rongche sat at an empty table with only two servants attending him.","The festive drumming and music echoed endlessly in his ears. Accompanied by the laughter and endless congratulations of the crowd, the sounds were like needles piercing his eardrums and stabbing into his heart.","They used to be on equal footing, but now he was blind and plagued by illness, while Xiao Rongyan was joyfully celebrating his wedding. How could one not feel hatred?","In the crowd, Song Jinzhao looked He Shuwan up and down.","The round fan couldn't completely obscure her face; from her side profile alone, it was clear that Princess Shuwan was a true beauty.","After the bowing ceremony concluded, two maidservants escorted the bride into the bridal chamber, while Xiao Rongyan stayed behind to entertain the guests.","On the men's side of the banquet, Song Qiming had just taken his seat when he saw Xiao Rongyan holding a wine cup and walking toward Xiao Rongche.","In an instant, the gazes of everyone around were drawn to them.","As far as they were concerned, it was impossible for Prince Qi to come and offer congratulations.","But not only had he come, he was also being avoided and isolated by everyone. It was truly humiliating.","Since Imperial Brother cannot see, there was really no need for you to come offer congratulations in person. Drink this cup of wedding wine and go back, lest it gets too dark and you take a fall.","The surroundings instantly fell dead silent.","Was this genuine concern or pure mockery?","Prince Qi had already been reduced to this state, yet Prince Ying still had to mock him. Wasn't this going a bit too far?","Xiao Rongche expressionlessly felt for his wine cup and drank it down. Imperial Father ordered you to marry the Princess of Shuobei. I naturally must congratulate you.","At the next table, Wang Nie and Qi Xiong, who were sitting together, frowned.","These words sounded strange and made people uncomfortable.","Xiao Rongyan looked at the other man's wine-soaked sleeve and gave a cold snort.","He bent down, leaned close to Xiao Rongche's ear, and whispered a single sentence.","That is still better than becoming a piece of trash, you short-lived ghost.","The wine cup fell to the ground. Xiao Rongche turned his lifeless eyes toward the direction of the voice, his freezing fingers trembling.","Do you think you are any better off? An abandoned person will never sit on that throne.","A dark shadow crossed Xiao Rongyan's eyes, and his voice floated lightly from his throat.","Whether I can sit there or not is not for you to say, but you certainly never will.","Across the aisle, Song Jinzhao vaguely caught their entire conversation in her ears.","Still fighting even at this point. They were all idiots.","And Prince Qi, coming over to drink despite being so ill. No matter how she looked at it, it seemed strange.","What was his purpose?","The wedding banquet would go on for a long time. Having no intention of staying longer, Song Jinzhao exchanged a few pleasantries with Princess Consort Ying and prepared to leave.","On the other side, faced with Xiao Rongyan's toast, Song Qiming pretended to take a sip from the rim of his cup.","After the man walked away and he saw Song Jinzhao stand up, he hurriedly followed her out.","Sister, can we go back now?","If it weren't an imperial decree marriage and the Prince Ying estate hadn't specifically sent an invitation, he really wouldn't have wanted to come.","Song Jinzhao glanced back at Xiao Rongche, who was still sitting in his chair.","I feel like there's a good show to watch. Let's get on the carriage and change our outfits first.","Song Qiming followed Song Jinzhao in confusion.","What kind of good show required a change of clothes?","After the carriage turned a corner, it stopped by the roadside. Song Qiming, having taken off his outer robe, stepped down from the vehicle.","Not long after, Song Jinzhao, dressed in light clothes and having removed her hairpins and jewelry, jumped out of the carriage with clean, crisp movements.","Watching the carriage gradually move away, Song Jinzhao secured the hidden sleeve-arrows on her wrists and led Song Qiming toward the alleyway."]},{"number":389,"title":"Chapter 389: King Qi wants to kill Wang Nie and Qi Xiong; we must stop him.","paragraphs":["The night was hazy. The guests, having finished their drinks, emerged and were picked up one by one by sedans and carriages.","Wang Nie, clutching his head, was helped into a sedan chair by his servants. Even Qi Xiong, who had always been a heavy drinker, was so intoxicated that he looked as if he would pass out the very next second.","On the roof opposite Prince Ying's mansion, a sister and brother lay on their stomachs behind the semi-circular tiles, peeking out.","Song Qiming raised an eyebrow in confusion.","\"They hadn't even had two cups when I left. How did they get this drunk in such a short time?\"","Song Jinzhao's calm gaze swept over the two men's faces, a profound look flashing in the depths of her eyes.","\"If you were an envoy drinking at Prince Wei's mansion, would you get this drunk?\"","Song Qiming shook his head without hesitation. \"Of course not.\"","As soon as he said that, realization dawned on him. He looked at Song Jinzhao in astonishment. \"Is there a problem with them?\"","No wonder they were so drunk in such a short time. Without anyone forcing them to drink, there was no need to fake being drunk. Could they have been drugged?","Just as the sedan bearers lifted the chairs to leave, two servants helped Prince Qi out of the doors.","Xiao Rongche, who was blind, stood motionless in place.","The attendants on his left and right watched the sedans gradually disappear into the darkness and whispered a few words into Xiao Rongche's ear.","\"Your Highness, they have left.\"","Digging his nails hard into his palms, Xiao Rongche took a slight step forward. The carriage parked at the mansion's entrance immediately drove over.","Watching the three people leave one after another, and considering how Prince Qi's group had stood there watching them depart, Song Jinzhao turned and jumped down from the roof.","The instigators who caused Xiao Rongche's condition to worsen were Qi Xiong and Wang Nie. Could it be that he wanted revenge?","After moving away from Prince Ying's mansion, the guests gradually dispersed.","Seeing the sedans and the carriage separated by only one intersection, Song Jinzhao became even more certain that Xiao Rongche's targets were Wang Nie and Qi Xiong.","The waning moon hanging high in the sky was gradually obscured by dark clouds, making the night even darker, leaving only the candlelight from the lanterns shining.","Suddenly, a gust of cold wind blew through the street, letting out a howling sound.","Amidst the flickering candlelight, four masked assassins rushed out from the alleys on both sides of the street.","The snow-white flash of blades swept past the sedan bearers' eyes. Caught off guard, four of the eight men were instantly hacked to death.","Behind a pillar, Song Qiming covered his mouth, unable to hide the shock in his eyes.","To make a move against the envoys of the Shuobei Kingdom on the day Princess Shuwan married Prince Ying, Prince Qi was too audacious.","\"Help!\" The remaining four sedan bearers fled in a panic, but before they could run a few steps, they were pierced through the heart from behind.","All eight sedan bearers lost their lives. The four masked assassins split into two teams and dragged the unconscious Wang Nie and Qi Xiong out of the sedan chairs.","Despite such a huge commotion, the two men had no reaction at all. They had undoubtedly been drugged.","\"Sister, what do we do now? Should we save them?\" Song Qiming turned his head with a conflicted expression and asked Song Jinzhao.","Wang Nie and Qi Xiong could die, but dying in the capital would have too great an impact and would very likely lead to an early war.","Facing the enemy without certainty, regardless of whether the Dongzhao Kingdom could win, they would pay a heavy price.","On the right, Prince Qi's carriage was approaching. Song Jinzhao stared at it with a dark expression.","\"Wait a little longer.\"","After the carriage stopped, Xiao Rongche was helped down from it.","\"Your Highness, they are already unconscious.\"","Xiao Rongche expressionlessly opened his hand, and the servant supporting him immediately placed a sword in his grasp.","Then, they dragged Wang Nie and Qi Xiong in front of Xiao Rongche.","\"Your Highness can make your move now.\"","The words drifted with the wind, carrying a chill.","Xiao Rongche raised his foot and kicked forward. After confirming the distance, he gripped the sword in his hand and prepared to thrust it forward.","Song Qiming instinctively wanted to rush out and save them.","But Song Jinzhao's arrow was faster than him.","A sharp metallic clang rang out, and the sword in Xiao Rongche's hand was instantly sent flying.","\"Who is it!\" The four masked assassins immediately raised their swords and faced the direction the arrow had come from.","Xiao Rongche was tightly protected behind the two subordinates he had brought.","\"Except for Prince Qi and those two from Shuobei Kingdom, silence all the rest,\" Song Jinzhao said, her voice lowered so deeply it sounded like a man's.","Xiao Rongche could not die, otherwise the Emperor would definitely investigate thoroughly.","As long as the three most important people were fine, the impact of this incident would not be significant.","\"Who are you?\" Before the man's words could finish falling, his throat was pierced by Song Jinzhao's arrow.","Song Qiming picked up a sword from the ground and charged at them.","The opponents were no match for the sister and brother at all. In just a few blinks of an eye, all of their throats were slit.","The sounds of fighting disappeared. Unaware of the battle's outcome, Xiao Rongche tentatively called out, \"Where is everyone? Are they all dead?\"","Song Qiming walked up to his side, covered his mouth, and said faintly, \"They are all dead, and you are next.\"","The gloomy voice sounded like the grim reapers jumping straight out of the underworld.","Xiao Rongche retreated repeatedly in terror, screaming at the top of his lungs, \"Who are you? I am a prince, you cannot kill me!\"","\"Somebody, come quickly!\"","Watching him run around blindly like a headless fly, Song Qiming glared at him wearily.","Assassinating envoys without regard for the big picture, and he still dared to call himself a prince? Killing him a hundred times wouldn't be too much.","The screams would soon attract people. With a dark expression, Song Jinzhao kicked Xiao Rongche squarely in the knee, then grabbed Song Qiming and swiftly vanished from the spot."]},{"number":390,"title":"Chapter 390: The Capital Prefect Who Got Up in the Middle of the Night","paragraphs":["The first to arrive was the capital's night watchman.","Approaching and seeing the ground littered with corpses, he scrambled frantically down the street, running and screaming at the top of his lungs, \"Murder! Murder!\"","Hearing someone approaching, Xiao Rongche, unaware that Song Jinzhao and the others had already left, immediately shouted toward the sound.","\"I am a prince! Save me, and I guarantee you a lifetime of wealth and glory!\"","His face filled with terror, the night watchman fled without looking back, as if he had not heard a thing.","Running to the next intersection, he collided right into the patrolling bailiffs of the Jingzhao Prefecture.","The watchman rushed over and hugged a bailiff's thigh, the flab on his face trembling violently.","\"Officers, there are dead people ahead! So many dead people!\"","Xiao Rongche was still crying for help. The bailiffs vigilantly gripped their swords and charged forward.","At the foot of the Emperor, who would dare to commit murder?","The leading bailiff recognized Xiao Rongche at a glance.","He gasped, his eyes widening as he scanned the corpses on the ground.","When he saw Wang Nie and Qi Xiong, his blood ran cold, and he froze in place like a statue.","The envoys of the Shuobei Kingdom had been murdered. The sky was falling!","After calming down, he walked over to Xiao Rongche on weak legs. Seeing that the prince was uninjured, he finally breathed a sigh of relief and cupped his hands in greeting.","\"This humble one, Lin Jingshan, head bailiff of the Jingzhao Prefecture, greets His Highness Prince Qi. Please forgive me for arriving late to your rescue.\"","Hearing that they were from the Jingzhao Prefecture, Xiao Rongche immediately waved his arms and demanded loudly, \"Where are the assassins? Have they all been killed?\"","Lin Jingshan hesitantly looked around, especially at the bodies lying on the ground.","\"There are no other survivors around besides Your Highness. Who were the assassins, and how many were there in total?\"","Before he even finished speaking, one of the bailiffs inspecting the bodies shouted to Lin Jingshan, \"Head Bailiff, these two are still alive.\"","Lin Jingshan snapped his head around and realized the survivors mentioned were the envoys of the Shuobei Kingdom.","In an instant, his heart leaped to his throat. He rushed over to check their breathing and found they were indeed still alive.","\"Head Bailiff Lin, they do not have a single wound on them, but they just will not wake up. It is like they are drunk.\"","With their breaths, a strong stench of alcohol wafted out. Their faces were flushed red, exactly as if they were dead drunk.","Lin Jingshan furrowed his brows and said sternly, \"Take them back to the prefecture office first, and fetch a doctor.\"","The rest of the delegation was at the Huitong Guesthouse. With such an incident occurring, they needed the Prefecture Governor to make the call on what to do next.","Jiang Dongsheng, the Governor of Jingzhao Prefecture, had just taken off his clothes and was preparing for bed when his door was pounded loudly.","Madam Jiang sleepily opened her eyes. \"What is wrong? Why all the commotion?\"","Jiang Dongsheng helplessly picked up his outer robe and draped it over his shoulders.","\"It is nothing, go back to sleep. There has probably been a case.\"","When he opened the door, an incoming hand nearly slapped him right in the face.","Jiang Dongsheng glared and roared at the person, spitting all over his face.","\"What are you doing! Do you have a death wish?\"","The bailiff hastily explained, \"My Lord, someone assassinated the envoys of the Shuobei Kingdom and Prince Qi in the city. More than a dozen people are dead on the street.\"","The surroundings suddenly fell dead silent; even the wind seemed to stop.","\"What!\" he exploded with a shout so loud that a tile slipped from the eaves and shattered into pieces on the ground.","Without even putting on his trousers, Jiang Dongsheng dashed outside with only his outer robe draped over him.","He babbled rapidly, his voice quacking non-stop like a drake.","\"How is Prince Qi?\"","\"Are the envoys alright?\"","\"Who are the assassins? Have they been caught?\"","\"...\"","The cold wind of early autumn slipped into his clothes; it was still rather chilly in the middle of the night.","Running alongside him, the bailiff answered, \"Prince Qi is unharmed, and the envoys are fine too. It is just that one is terrified and the other two are unconscious. Head Bailiff Lin has already sent for a doctor.\"","\"The assassins have not been caught. By the time we got there, they had already fled.\"","Cold sweat poured out, quickly soaking his back and making him shiver with a dreadful chill.","Jiang Dongsheng sprinted all the way to the front hall of the prefecture office in one breath. Seeing two people lying on the floor and Prince Qi sitting in a chair from a distance, his heart instantly leaped to his throat.","He rushed over, his eyes scanning like a machine, looking as though he wanted to strip them naked to check for injuries.","Prince Qi looked fine, just a little pale in the face.","He then looked down at the two men lying on the ground, his heart pounding like a drum, feeling as if it would burst out of his chest the very next second.","\"Are you sure they are just drunk? Why are they not waking up?\"","Lin Jingshan's expression was somewhat hesitant.","\"This subordinate has already checked. They are indeed uninjured. As for why they are not waking up...\"","He thought for a moment before continuing, \"Perhaps they could not hold their liquor and got too drunk, or they might have been drugged. I have already sent for a doctor, and he will be here shortly.\"","In his chair, having calmed down, Xiao Rongche could not help but slightly furrow his brows upon hearing this.","The assassins who ruined his plans halfway had fled, so the blame could be pushed onto them.","But if the drugging was discovered, it would pull up the radish and bring out the mud—it was highly likely the investigation would lead right back to him.","\"Today is the wedding of the Princess of Shuobei and Prince Ying. These two drank quite a lot at the wedding banquet, so they must just be too drunk.\"","Hearing Prince Qi say this, Jiang Dongsheng's hanging heart finally settled down a bit.","He straightened his posture and ordered his subordinates, \"In this vital capital region, right at the foot of the Emperor, who has the audacity to assassinate His Highness Prince Qi and the Shuobei Kingdom delegation?\"","\"Dispatch all bailiffs immediately to search through the night. We must bring these assassins to justice.\"","Lin Jingshan firmly clasped his hands together and replied with absolute certainty, \"Your subordinate obeys.\"","With that, he turned and led his men out of the prefecture office."]},{"number":391,"title":"Chapter 391: No 300 Taels of Silver Buried Here","paragraphs":["At the entrance of the County Princess's estate, Song Qiming, who had been waiting for quite some time, saw the yamen runners passing by with lanterns and immediately walked out from the gates, feigning confusion.","He called out sternly to stop them, \"In the dead of night, what are you all doing?\"","Hearing the voice, Lin Jingshan thought they had disturbed the peace of the estate and hurriedly ran over to explain.","\"To answer Your Excellency, an assassination attempt was just made on Prince Qi and the envoys of Shuobei on Central Street. I am currently leading my men to search the city for the assassins.\"","Song Qiming raised his bright eyes, his gaze full of disbelief, while he deliberately flattened the corners of his mouth.","\"Who would dare to make a move right under the Emperor's nose? How are Prince Qi and the Shuobei envoys? Are they injured?\"","Lin Jingshan replied, \"Prince Qi is fine, but the two envoys have been in a deep sleep. A physician has already been called to see them.\"","Song Qiming furrowed his brows in feigned worry. \"Nothing must happen to the Shuobei envoys, otherwise there might be a catastrophe. I will have my older sister go take a look.\"","Lin Jingshan widened his eyes in pleasant surprise. \"If the County Princess could go, that would naturally be for the best. My lord would be at ease.\"","Song Qiming gave a slight nod and ran inside to call for her.","Not long after, Song Jinzhao walked out, having changed her clothes and draped an outer robe over her shoulders. Her dark hair was entirely pinned up with a single hairpin. Her face was completely devoid of makeup, without even a touch of rouge on her lips, making her look exactly as if she had just been roused from her bed.","The two boarded a carriage and sped toward the government office.","On the other side, a yamen runner hurriedly arrived with a gray-haired physician.","Worried that the drugging would be exposed, Prince Qi immediately clutched his head.","\"My head aches terribly. Examine me first.\"","Jiang Dongsheng hurriedly directed, \"Treat His Highness Prince Qi first. If it is serious, we will need to summon an imperial physician.\"","The physician rubbed his sleepy eyelids, opened his medicine chest, and began to take Xiao Rongche's pulse.","After a long while, he released his hand with slight hesitation, his gaze lingering on Xiao Rongche's eyes.","His body bore severe, unhealed injuries; stagnant blood was attacking his heart, and his constitution was frail. He feared the prince did not have many years left to live.","Afraid of being blamed if he spoke the truth, the elderly physician with trembling fingers tried his best to downplay the condition.","\"Your Highness's severe injuries have not healed, and you just suffered a great fright. The instability of your mind has caused the headache. You need a good rest and just a few doses of a soothing prescription.\"","Not wanting the physician to stay, Xiao Rongche swayed as he stood up. \"The imperial physicians from the palace won't arrive at my estate until tomorrow. You will come back with me first.\"","Seeing that he was going to take the man away, Jiang Dongsheng hurriedly stepped forward to stop him.","\"Your Highness, please let the physician examine the two envoys first. They still haven't woken up.\"","Xiao Rongche waved his arm impatiently, feigning a look of angry agony.","\"What could happen from being drunk? I am in pain and exhausted right now. Send someone to escort me back to my estate immediately. As for them, just find another physician.\"","The sleeping drug slipped into the wine would wear off in three hours. If he stalled for more time until they woke up, no one would be able to trace it.","Even if suspicions arose, they could completely pass it off as a drunken stupor.","Seeing him lose his temper, Jiang Dongsheng was put in a very difficult position.","Prince Qi had a grudge against the Shuobei envoys. He was likely hoping they would die and was deliberately taking the physician away.","\"Your Highness, how about a quick examination first? These two cannot meet with any mishaps in Dongzhao.\"","Xiao Rongche kicked out in the direction of the voice, roaring furiously, \"They can't have a mishap, but I can?! I am definitely taking this physician with me. Whether you find another one is up to you, Lord Jiang.\"","The shoe brushed past Jiang Dongsheng's calf. It didn't hurt, but it struck fear into his heart.","Even if the other party was currently blind, destitute, and out of favor, he was still a prince. How could a mere prefect like him dare to oppose him?","Jiang Dongsheng helplessly cupped his hands in concession. \"This humble official will have someone escort Your Highness back to your estate at once.\"","He would definitely have to call for another physician, but first, he needed to send this person away.","Xiao Rongche, believing he had achieved his goal, left in Jiang Dongsheng's sedan chair. Right on his heels, the carriage from the estate arrived.","When the yamen runner announced that County Princess Linghui had arrived, Jiang Dongsheng dashed out as if he had found a lifesaver.","\"This humble official pays his respects to the County Princess.\"","Song Jinzhao showed a trace of worry on her face and said, \"Lord Jiang, there is no need for formalities. I heard that Prince Qi and the envoys were attacked by assassins and remain unconscious. I couldn't set my mind at ease, so I came to take a look. Where are they?\"","Jiang Dongsheng hurriedly extended his hand to invite her into the front hall.","\"County Princess, you have arrived at the perfect time. Prince Qi complained of a headache and forcibly took the physician away. The two envoys still haven't woken up. Please quickly take a look at them. Is it drunkenness or something else? Could it be internal injuries?\"","The sister and brother exchanged a glance and continued walking inside with a tacit understanding.","They had no intention of telling anyone that they were the ones who had thwarted the assassination.","Ye Liangyu and Fei Yanzhang had been beaten with staffs and demoted for impeaching Prince Qi, and Song Qiming was Ye Liangyu's student. If they directly stated that Prince Qi had sent assassins to kill the envoys, it would be easy for Xiao Rongche to bite back at them.","The Emperor was protective of his own and would definitely favor his son, so this case had to be investigated by the Emperor himself.","As for who thwarted the attempt, they might as well let it remain a mystery."]},{"number":392,"title":"Chapter 392: Exposed: Unconsciousness Caused by Date Rape Drugs","paragraphs":["Song Jinzhao first examined the complexions of Wang Nie and Qi Xiong.","Their breathing is weak. Although their faces are flushed, their lips are pale with a purplish tint.","She peeled back their eyelids to observe their pupillary responses, bringing the candle closer.","Their pupils are significantly dilated and sluggish to react to light. This does not look like a coma caused by drunkenness.","Then, she reached out to check their pulses.","The pulse is deep, slow, and weak. On the surface, it feels as if suppressed by a heavy weight, but underneath it is hollow and rootless. They must have ingested some kind of knockout drug.","She leaned in, using her hand to waft their breath toward her nose to sniff carefully.","Aside from the smell of alcohol, there is a trace of a bitter, sour, and putrid scent. It should be the smell of the drug.","Jiang Dongsheng's heart beat faster and faster as he listened.","So, before being assassinated, they had already been drugged at the Prince Ying's Manor.","Thoughts raced wildly through his mind, and soon, Jiang Dongsheng made a decision.","He stammered as he asked Song Jinzhao, So, are they in any danger? If it is a knockout drug, will they wake up after a sleep?","The matter was too grave for him, a mere prefect, to decide. He had to let the Emperor make the call first.","Song Jinzhao nodded. They are not in danger. Judging by their pulses, they should wake up in two hours.","Jiang Dongsheng took a deep breath. His mind was a jumbled mess, yet he forced himself to forge a way forward.","I ask the County Princess to keep the matter of the drug a secret for now. I will immediately enter the palace to report to His Majesty, and let him decide everything.","Having said that, he quickly ran out the door.","The clattering hooves disappeared into the dark night, as if his pants were on fire.","In the Emperor's bedchamber, Xiao Chengjing had gone to sleep early, pleased that the marriage alliance matters were finally settled.","The door was suddenly knocked from the outside. Zhao Yande, who was sitting on the floor keeping the night watch, jolted awake in fright, feeling as if he had fallen off a cliff in a dream.","Still shaken, he straightened his hat, stood up, walked to the door, and opened it a crack.","Knocking so loudly! If you wake the Emperor, it will cost you your miserable life.","The little eunuch said in a panic, Eunuch Zhao, something terrible has happened! The Prince of Qi and the envoys from Shuobei were assassinated! Lord Jiang of the Jingzhao Prefecture has entered the palace overnight and demands to see His Majesty.","His whisk fell to the ground. Zhao Yande stood with his mouth half-open, his eyes bulging out.","What is all this noise? Inside the room, the awakened Xiao Chengjing looked entirely displeased as he roared fiercely toward the door.","Zhao Yande hastily picked up his whisk from the floor, turned, and ran to the bedside. Reporting to Your Majesty, the Prince of Qi and the Shuobei envoys have been assassinated! Lord Jiang, the Prefect of Jingzhao, is outside requesting an audience.","Xiao Chengjing, who was just about to lie back down to sleep, suddenly widened his eyes. In an instant, all his drowsiness vanished.","Who is so bold as to assassinate a prince and foreign envoys right here in the capital? Are the Prince of Qi and the envoys injured? Send Jiang Dongsheng in immediately!","By the time Jiang Dongsheng was brought from outside the palace gates to the Imperial Study, Xiao Chengjing had already donned his dragon robes and was sitting solemnly on the dragon throne.","His dark-ringed eyes looked as if they could devour a man alive.","Are the Prince of Qi and the envoys injured? What exactly happened? Tell me everything in full detail.","Jiang Dongsheng fell to both knees, his eyes full of self-reproach and agony, looking as if he were about to cry.","Replying to Your Majesty, just an hour and a half ago...","Jiang Dongsheng explained everything clearly and in minute detail, including the Prince of Qi's attitude afterward and Song Jinzhao's diagnosis that the two envoys had been drugged.","The Imperial Study was terrifyingly quiet. Xiao Chengjing's breathing fell upon Jiang Dongsheng's ears like the sound of a sharpening blade, threatening to slice his flesh off piece by piece.","He did not know how long he knelt there. Just as his knees were about to lose all feeling, Xiao Chengjing finally spoke.","The gloomy voice struck heavily against Jiang Dongsheng's heart. He clenched his fists tightly to keep his body from trembling so violently.","The wedding wine was too strong. The two envoys from Shuobei passed out from intoxication. It has nothing to do with any knockout drug.","On their way back, they ran into a notorious bandit. The bandit wanted to silence them but was coincidentally stumbled upon by the Prince of Qi. The manor guards fought to the death and severely injured the bandit. What you are hunting tonight is a thief, not an assassin. This is the official story for tonight's events.","Jiang Dongsheng swallowed hard, instantly understanding Xiao Chengjing's intention.","He forcefully kowtowed, pressing his forehead against the ground, and said in a trembling tone, This humble subject understands Your Majesty's intent. I will go and handle it immediately."]},{"number":393,"title":"Chapter 393: Secret Investigation, Results Are All the Same","paragraphs":["After Jiang Dongsheng left, no one in the imperial study dared to breathe loudly.","Zhao Yande stood motionless by the desk, terrified that Xiao Chengjing's wrath would be taken out on a servant like him.","Just as everyone wondered when this oppressive atmosphere would end, Xiao Chengjing suddenly spoke, his voice like a deep, dark pool harboring hidden murderous intent.","\"Have Fan Guanshan come see me.\"","\"Yes, Your Majesty,\" Zhao Yande nodded hastily and hurried out.","Not long after, Fan Guanshan strode swiftly into the imperial study, bringing a chill from the outside with him.","He dropped to one knee with a thud. \"Your humble servant greets Your Majesty.\"","Being summoned this late at night could not mean anything good.","Xiao Chengjing explained the cause and effect of the situation in a few brief sentences before getting straight to the point.","\"Take your men to the Prince Ying Manor immediately and find out who administered the drug. I want to know who is trying to kill the envoy of Shuobei, and what their motive is.\"","Fan Guanshan calmly cupped his hands in obeisance. \"I obey Your Majesty's command.\"","With that said, not wishing to linger in the imperial study a moment longer, he immediately turned and left to lead his men to the Prince Ying Manor.","Xiao Chengjing's current expression was simply too terrifying, like a volcano ready to erupt at any moment, capable of claiming lives if one was not careful.","Jiang Dongsheng rushed back to the government office as if he had wings.","He relayed Xiao Chengjing's words verbatim to Song Jinzhao, then added with profound significance, \"County Princess, you should understand His Majesty's intentions. Everything is for the greater good.\"","Song Jinzhao twitched the corners of her mouth, but not a trace of warmth reached her eyes.","\"I understand His Majesty's intentions. There is no cure for drunkenness, and in the middle of the night, it is time for this County Princess to return and rest.\"","Jiang Dongsheng hurriedly escorted Song Jinzhao and Song Qiming out of the office.","After the carriage curtain fell, the expressions on the siblings' faces instantly cooled.","Song Qiming asked in disbelief, \"Sister, is this matter just going to end like this? Assassinating an envoy is a matter of paramount importance! Does the Emperor really intend to smooth things over and cover it up? What if Prince Qi strikes again?\"","\"Even if the envoy leaves, Princess Shuwan is still here. Prince Qi has gone mad; he could cause trouble at any moment.\"","Song Jinzhao leaned against the carriage wall, reaching up to pinch the bridge of her nose, feeling a bit drowsy.","\"The incident happened in the capital, and the Emperor cannot afford the consequences of such a disaster. It is not that he will not investigate, but rather that he cannot do so openly.\"","Song Qiming furrowed his brows in frustration. \"I am just afraid the Emperor will not trace it back to Prince Qi.\"","Song Jinzhao said faintly, \"Every action leaves a trace. As long as he wants to investigate, he will definitely find out. However, how he ultimately deals with it is another matter entirely.\"","Song Qiming choked on his words. Thinking of all the times the Emperor had previously shielded Xiao Rongche, his spirit instantly deflated.","He sighed softly, his tone filled with utter helplessness.","\"That is true. Even if it is traced back to Prince Qi, he probably will not be severely punished. A few light reprimands and the matter will pass.\"","As the carriage passed an intersection, it suddenly stopped. Qingshuang turned her head and lifted the curtain.","\"County Princess, the Imperial Guards are approaching. The one leading them looks like Commander Fan.\"","Song Jinzhao sat up and leaned out to look. She saw a group of Imperial Guards on horseback swiftly crossing the intersection ahead.","The two men at the front carried lanterns discreetly, the dim light barely illuminating anything in the distance.","The faint yellow glow cast upon the leader's face. After clearly seeing his features, Song Jinzhao had a guess in her heart.","\"It is Fan Guanshan. Heading in this direction, they must be going to the Prince Ying Manor.\"","Having the Imperial Guards investigate was exactly Xiao Chengjing's style.","Song Qiming asked, \"Sister, should we send someone to follow them and take a look?\" They needed to know how the situation was developing, after all.","Song Jinzhao shook her head.","\"The Emperor is investigating privately because he does not want anyone to know about this. If Fan Guanshan discovers someone tailing them, it will inevitably arouse suspicion.\"","\"Return to the manor. We do not need to concern ourselves with this matter anymore. The results will reveal themselves in due time.\"","Feeling somewhat reluctant, Song Qiming let the carriage curtain fall. On the way back, his brows remained tightly furrowed."]},{"number":394,"title":"Chapter 394: Xiao Rongyan: I Didn't Plant the Drug","paragraphs":["To show his favor, Prince Ying Xiao Rongyan exerted all his strength on their wedding night.","He had finally managed to close his eyes for a brief rest when the door to the Tinglan Courtyard was knocked on so hard it nearly collapsed.","\"Your Highness, Commander Fan is here and urgently requests to see you.\"","Xiao Rongyan's eyes snapped open, a sudden chill creeping up his spine.","Lying in bed, He Shuwan slowly opened her eyes. Her fingers gently stroked Xiao Rongyan's chest, her voice as enchanting as spring water and sweeter than honey.","\"Your Highness~\" Her voice was melodious, capturing his very soul.","Xiao Rongyan's chest trembled with a sudden thrill. He hurriedly pressed down on He Shuwan's delicate hand, his voice slightly breathless.","\"Go to sleep first. I will come back to accompany you in a while.\"","If this continued, he would be completely drained.","This princess from the Shuobei Kingdom was even more clingy than Side Consort Li. Her irresistible tricks made it impossible to stop.","He Shuwan wrapped her arms around Xiao Rongyan's arm with a look of disappointment.","Pouting, she said, \"Your Highness, you must come back. Today is our wedding night, and no one is allowed to take you away.\"","Xiao Rongyan swallowed hard, unable to resist touching He Shuwan's cheek.","\"Don't worry, I will definitely return.\"","Had he known He Shuwan was this beautiful and alluring, he wouldn't have been so reluctant in the beginning.","But this was even better.","Having a beauty in his arms while also forming a connection with the Shuobei Kingdom was killing two birds with one stone. Ultimately, he was the one who benefited.","After Xiao Rongyan left the room, the expression on He Shuwan's face, who was sitting on the bed, gradually changed.","She got up, walked to the window, and opened it just a crack.","She saw a servant hurriedly leading Xiao Rongyan out of the courtyard, as if something serious had happened.","Her gaze swept over the servants standing at the courtyard gate, and He Shuwan couldn't help but narrow her eyes.","She had to find a way to dismiss these people, otherwise it would be inconvenient to carry out her plans.","In the front hall, Xiao Rongyan looked puzzled as he signaled all the servants to leave.","\"What exactly has happened to warrant Commander Fan coming here so late in the night?\"","Fan Guanshan spoke in a firm tone, \"Prince Qi and the envoy of the Shuobei Kingdom were assassinated on their way back. Someone drugged their wine. The Emperor has ordered me to investigate, and I ask for Your Highness's cooperation.\"","Xiao Rongyan's eyes widened. Seeing Fan Guanshan staring at him with a suspicious gaze, he quickly reacted, holding out his hands to show his innocence.","\"The drugging has absolutely nothing to do with me. Today is my wedding banquet.\"","Fan Guanshan replied, \"No one is saying it has anything to do with Your Highness until the matter is fully investigated. Who was the maid serving wine to the Shuobei envoy today? Please summon her here.\"","Xiao Rongyan took a deep breath, all romantic thoughts completely vanishing from his mind, replaced by a chilling realization.","He called the butler over and said, \"Who served the table of the Shuobei envoy today? Bring everyone who had contact with the wine here.\"","Involving the assassination of a prince and an envoy, this had to be thoroughly investigated. He absolutely could not take the blame for this.","Soon, the butler brought over two servants, one male and one female.","One was the servant responsible for pouring wine at the table, and the other was the maid who carried the wine from the kitchen to the table.","Fan Guanshan's sharp gaze swept over the two.","Compared to the male servant kneeling on the left, the maid looked much more terrified, her hands trembling beneath her sleeves.","\"Men, take them away.\"","Seeing that Fan Guanshan was taking them away without asking a single question, both of them instantly panicked.","They opened their mouths to cry out their innocence, but the Imperial Guards who grabbed them clamped hands over their mouths. Their muffled cries were forced back down their throats, nearly choking them.","Hearing the sound of the door opening, He Shuwan opened her eyes, pretending to have been woken up.","Seeing Xiao Rongyan's grim expression, she asked with a coquettish tone of concern, \"Your Highness looks so unwell, has something happened?\"","Thinking of the excuse Fan Guanshan had just provided, Xiao Rongyan held He Shuwan's hand with a hint of worry.","\"Wang Nie and Qi Xiong were assassinated by notorious bandits on their way back, and my eldest brother ran into it. Royal Father is furious and dispatched the Imperial Guards to search the city. Commander Fan came to warn us, lest the thieves hide inside the Prince Ying Manor.\"","He Shuwan paused for a moment, then covered her mouth in feigned surprise.","\"What kind of bandit is so formidable that even Qi Xiong is no match for him?\"","Xiao Rongyan didn't want He Shuwan to ask any more questions, so he pulled her into his arms and lay down.","\"Wang Nie and Qi Xiong were too drunk; they didn't even wake up during the assassination. Fortunately, the guards from Prince Qi's Manor and the Capital Prefecture arrived in time. A few sedan bearers died, but everyone else is fine. Go to sleep, we still have to enter the palace tomorrow to pay our respects to my mother.\"","He Shuwan didn't believe Xiao Rongyan's explanation. She closed her eyes thoughtfully, pretending to sleep.","Bandits only steal; even if they were caught, they wouldn't easily commit murder, especially when facing multiple people.","Qi Xiong spent his years in the military camp, so his alcohol tolerance couldn't possibly be low. There was no way he should have gotten drunk at a wedding banquet.","There was definitely a problem here. She would have to send someone to ask around tomorrow."]},{"number":395,"title":"Chapter 395: Upon investigating the Prince of Qi, Wang Nie guessed that Xiao Rongche was the one who made the move.","paragraphs":["In the dark and sunless prison cell, thick blood stained the straw on the ground a deep red.","The maid, who had been neatly dressed just moments ago, now lay wretchedly on the floor, her pale, smooth face covered in tears and blood.","Fan Guanshan picked up a stack of confessions from the ground.","To be able to plant a mole in Prince Ying's manor for so many years without being discovered, Prince Qi certainly had some tricks up his sleeve.","He just didn't know if there were others.","Looking up at Fan Guanshan's tall back as he turned to leave, the maid no longer had the strength to hold on. Her head dropped, and she passed out on the ground.","The imperial guards in charge of keeping watch frowned.","\"She cannot die yet. Go get a doctor.\"","As he walked out of the prison, the horizon was already faintly white.","Colorful rays of dawn peeked out from below the horizon, but Fan Guanshan's heart felt exceptionally heavy.","He gripped the confessions tightly and walked toward the imperial palace.","In the imperial study, looking at the fresh confessions, Xiao Chengjing slammed his hand heavily on the desk.","With a ferocious expression, he roared at the air, \"How audacious! When did this rebellious son become like this!\"","Standing below, Fan Guanshan twitched his eyelids.","Wasn't it because you spoiled him.","After calming down, Xiao Chengjing closed his eyes.","\"To avoid affecting diplomatic relations between the two countries, the matter ends here. I will punish Prince Qi myself. The wedding is over, and the envoys of the Shuobei State should be leaving.\"","Fan Guanshan nodded without a word.","The commotion at the Jingzhao Prefecture last night was too great. Everyone in the royal court knew that Prince Qi and the Shuobei envoys were almost assassinated.","The officials who did not know the inside story were all submitting memorials during the morning assembly to reorganize the capital's defenses.","At the same time, Wang Nie and Qi Xiong, lying in the Huitong Guesthouse, were furious.","Qi Xiong pointed his thick finger at Jiang Dongsheng's nose and roared, \"I can drink a thousand cups without getting drunk. How could I be knocked out by a mere pot of wine? There must be a problem here.\"","Sitting in the chair, Wang Nie rubbed his temples, still feeling a bit of a headache.","\"I only had two cups. Was there something wrong with the food and wine?\"","Jiang Dongsheng forced a fake laugh. \"Perhaps the wine of our Dongzhao State is too strong, and you two lords couldn't handle it.\"","Qi Xiong put his hands on his hips, wishing he could punch Jiang Dongsheng in the face.","\"I've drunk the strongest of wines. What exactly are you trying to do?\"","It must be the people of Dongzhao who drugged them, but what was the purpose of setting up this scene?","Jiang Dongsheng kept a smile on his face. \"Yesterday, County Princess Linghui already checked your pulses. You were indeed just too drunk.\"","\"Fortunately, His Highness Prince Qi arrived in time, otherwise the consequences would be unimaginable. Before the thieves are caught, please do not leave the guesthouse to avoid encountering danger again.\"","Qi Xiong puffed out his chest and angrily stepped right up to Jiang Dongsheng's face.","\"A mere thief? You think I'm afraid of him?\"","Jiang Dongsheng twitched the corners of his mouth.","\"The opponent has strong martial arts. More than a dozen guards couldn't defeat him. It is better for you to stay in the guesthouse, Lord.\"","After speaking, he ignored their angry glares, turned around, and left.","As his figure disappeared into the courtyard, Qi Xiong smashed the table with a punch.","After venting his anger, he quickly turned to look at Wang Nie, his eyes full of confusion. \"Lord Wang, what do you think they are trying to do?\"","Wang Nie lowered his hand and took a deep breath.","\"The possibility of it being a thief is very small. Even if we ran into Xiao Rongche, he wouldn't save us.\"","Qi Xiong paced back and forth in the room with his hands behind his back, his eyes suddenly lighting up.","\"Could it be that Xiao Rongche wants to kill us?\"","Wang Nie's expression paused slightly. \"Then why didn't he strike last night?\"","Because they were going to offer congratulations, and Qi Xiong was also going, the eight sedan chair bearers they brought had very weak martial arts. Eliminating them would have been extremely easy. Yet, six of Xiao Rongche's guards also died. No matter how you thought about it, it was strange.","Qi Xiong's thick eyebrows knitted together. \"Could it be that he regretted it halfway through? Xiao Rongche is afraid we will wage war against them.\"","Wang Nie thought for a moment and nodded slightly. \"That is very likely the case.\"","Qi Xiong asked, \"Should we expose this matter?\"","Wang Nie raised his hand in objection.","\"No. The Emperor doesn't plan to attack Dongzhao right now. You and I are completely unharmed, and being here in Dongzhao, no one would believe us.\"","Qi Xiong said unwillingly, \"Then what should we do? Just pretend this never happened? We lost eight men.\"","Wang Nie stood up and touched his neck, his voice sounding incredibly calm.","\"The marriage alliance is already over. We must leave as soon as possible.\" To avoid Xiao Rongche continuing his madness.","In the end, this incident was caused by Prince Wei, yet the two of them were left to clean up the mess.","They got no benefits at all, but suffered plenty.","\"Yes.\" Seeing Wang Nie say this, Qi Xiong, as the captain of the guards, could only agree.","Under Xiao Chengjing's arrangement, the Jingzhao Prefecture soon released news that they had caught the notorious bandit who assassinated Prince Qi and the Shuobei envoys.","Just as the court officials wanted to inquire about the details, the Jingzhao Prefecture beheaded the man that very day.","From capture to execution, the whole process took no more than half an hour.","By the time Wang Nie received the news, the man was already dead.","Not only that, Jiang Dongsheng even put on a show of bringing the severed head over to report back.","\"Lord Wang, Guard Qi, this is the notorious bandit who tried to assassinate you the night before last.\"","Looking at the bloody severed head, Wang Nie vomited on the spot.","\"Get out, and take it away.\"","Not wanting to stay in the capital any longer, Wang Nie entered the palace the next day to bid farewell to Xiao Chengjing.","Eager for them to leave quickly, Xiao Chengjing approved it without the slightest hesitation.","Before leaving, Wang Nie took his men to Prince Ying's manor.","\"The wedding is complete, and this humble official will set off for Shuobei tomorrow. If the princess suffers any grievances in Dongzhao in the future, you can write to the Emperor at any time. You will always be a princess of our Shuobei State.\"","When saying the last sentence, Wang Nie and He Shuwan locked eyes, everything understood without needing to be spoken.","Sitting to the side, Xiao Rongyan smiled and said, \"Rest assured, Minister Wang. Shuwan is my secondary consort, and I will absolutely not let her suffer any grievances.\"","Wang Nie calmly curled the corners of his mouth. \"With Your Highness's words, this official can return and report back on his mission.\"","Xiao Rongyan, satisfied, had someone see Wang Nie out.","The more importance the Shuobei State attached to He Shuwan, the more beneficial it would be for him.","Considering that he might need Shuobei's help in the future, he didn't mind saying a few nice words to them at this time."]},{"number":396,"title":"Chapter 396: Bestow Jinzhou upon the Prince of Qi as a fief","paragraphs":["On the third day after the envoys of the Shuobei Kingdom left the capital.","During the morning court session, Xiao Chengjing sat on the dragon throne, resting his head on his hand, looking somewhat exhausted.","A deep voice rolled from his throat, Read the decree.","Zhao Yande stepped forward confidently and slowly unrolled the bright yellow scroll in his hands.","By the grace of Heaven, the Emperor decrees: Jinzhou is granted to Prince Qi, Xiao Rongche, as his fiefdom. He is to depart for his fiefdom within three days.","This simple sentence plunged the imperial court into a moment of dead silence.","Everyone looked at Xiao Chengjing in disbelief.","It was well known that Prince Qi was not only blind but also physically weaker than an ordinary person; calling him a sickly invalid would not be an exaggeration.","Given the Emperor's previous protection and doting on him, they all thought the Emperor would let Prince Qi stay in the capital permanently to recuperate. Why was he suddenly driving him away to Jinzhou?","Xiao Rongyan stood at the very front of the ranks. Unlike the others, he appeared exceptionally calm at this moment.","Recalling Xiao Rongche's uninvited appearance at the wedding banquet, the maid taken away from his manor by Fan Guanshan, and the lies the Emperor fabricated to hide the truth.","A suspicion gradually formed in his heart.","That maid was a mole planted in his manor by Xiao Rongche; it was he who wanted to kill Wang Nie and Qi Xiong.","His imperial father knew, Fan Guanshan knew, and Jiang Dongsheng knew too, yet they still kept it a secret from the rest of the world.","Xiao Rongyan could not help but look up at the Emperor.","Assassinating the envoys and deliberately provoking a war between the two nations.","Despite such a heinous crime, his imperial father still granted such a prime location like Jinzhou to Xiao Rongche as his fiefdom.","Thinking back on the Emperor's various acts of shielding and protecting Xiao Rongche, Xiao Rongyan felt both angry and stifled.","He was the one who solved the political marriage dilemma for his father and married the princess of the Shuobei Kingdom, yet his father was so protective of Prince Qi.","They were both his sons, so why was it like this?","The more he thought about it, the more he fixated on the unfairness, bitterness welling up and stinging his heart.","In stark contrast to Xiao Rongyan's jealousy, Xiao Rongche had a completely different reaction upon receiving the imperial decree.","I won't go to Jinzhou. I want to stay in the capital. I want to see Imperial Father!","Eunuch Zhao calmly handed the imperial decree to an attendant beside him.","The Emperor asked this servant to pass a message to Your Highness: once you go to Jinzhou, do not cause any more trouble. Behave yourself.","As Xiao Rongche tried to scramble up from the ground, his toe accidentally hit the steps. The pain made him lose his balance, and he fell hard onto the floor.","He roared hysterically, tears spilling from his eyes.","Imperial Father cannot treat me like this! My eyes went blind for the sake of the Dongzhao Kingdom! I did nothing wrong! It's all their fault; they all lied to me!","Seeing him in such a wretched state, Eunuch Zhao felt a twinge of pity in his heart.","Rest assured, Your Highness. Imperial physicians will accompany you to Jinzhou. It will be no different from staying in the capital.","Xiao Rongyan waved his arms agitatedly, driving everyone away.","How could there be no difference?! Imperial Father is exiling me! He wants to abandon me! He is abandoning me—","Roar after roar echoed through Prince Qi's Manor.","Seeing Xiao Rongche beginning to criticize the Emperor, Eunuch Zhao dared not speak any further. After pausing for a moment, he led his people away from Prince Qi's Manor.","In the imperial study, Xiao Chengjing looked at Eunuch Zhao, who had just walked in, and asked, How is Prince Qi?","Eunuch Zhao lowered his head.","Prince Qi does not want to leave the capital. His emotions are somewhat out of control.","Xiao Chengjing placed his wolf-hair brush on the brush rest and spoke faintly.","For the sake of our father-son bond, I have already granted him Jinzhou as his fiefdom. I have done everything I can. Keep a close eye on Prince Qi's Manor. Prince Qi must leave the capital within three days.","If he stays any longer, who knows what kind of disaster he will cause. It is better to drive him out early and completely sever his ambitions.","Eunuch Zhao said submissively, The Emperor has given this much thought; His Highness Prince Qi will understand sooner or later.","Xiao Chengjing sat quietly without uttering a word."]},{"number":397,"title":"Chapter 397: Sending Off the King of Qi","paragraphs":["After suppressing his emotions all day, Song Qiming only dared to vent his frustration upon returning to the County Princess's estate.","\"He has committed so many mistakes; if it were anyone else, they would have been beheaded eight hundred times over. Yet His Majesty still granted him Jinzhou as his fief. This isn't a punishment, it's blatant favoritism!\"","\"Jinzhou collects two hundred thousand strings of cash in taxes a year, which is enough to cover the Jinglei Army's rations and military expenses for an entire year. They always claim the national treasury is empty for everything else, but they show such partiality to Prince Qi. The Dongzhao Kingdom will be finished sooner or later.\"","Worried that his voice might carry outside, Qingshuang silently closed the door.","In the next room, Song Anhao, who had been practicing calligraphy, looked up.","Blinking his eyes in innocent confusion, he said, \"Why is brother acting like this too? When I came back today, Grandpa Dongfang was also angry. His face was completely red from fury.\"","Song Shixue set down the medical records in her hands and asked in confusion, \"Did he curse in front of you?\"","Song Anhao shook his head.","\"No, Ah You and I went to the study to find him and just happened to see it. Brother Yukun was there too.\"","Song Shixue instructed him with a serious expression, \"Remember, never repeat these words to anyone else.\"","Song Anhao nodded obediently. \"I know. Brother Yukun told me the same thing when we were leaving.\"","Back in the other room, looking at the indignant Song Qiming, Song Jinzhao, who hadn't held any expectations to begin with, appeared very calm.","\"The Prefect of Suining is retiring due to illness. After the new year, Cai Qiong will propose to His Majesty that you be transferred to the southwest.\"","Song Qiming's mind instantly cooled down.","He asked uncertainly, \"Will His Majesty agree?\"","Officials dispatched outside the capital after three years in the Hanlin Academy usually started as county magistrates. Unless one had served a full six years in the Hanlin Academy or received an exceptional promotion from the Emperor, they wouldn't be directly appointed as a prefect. And he hadn't even been in the Hanlin Academy for three full years.","Song Jinzhao replied, \"Suining is closest to the territory of the southwestern foreign tribes. This is already the third time the Prefect of Suining has claimed illness to seek retirement. Rumor has it that he is completely bedridden, so the imperial court has no choice but to agree.\"","Song Qiming sat down and took a breath to compose himself.","\"Teacher and Lord Fei's standing before His Majesty is not what it used to be. I am not afraid to go to Suining, but I worry someone in the court will object.\"","Jumping ranks from a secondary sixth-grade official to a secondary fifth-grade one was ultimately somewhat against the rules.","Song Jinzhao spoke slowly and methodically, \"Being the Prefect of Suining is no easy task. If war breaks out in the southwest, that isolated city will be the first to be attacked. Very few people with connections are willing to go there.\"","\"I am a County Princess, so naturally, your status is different from others. No one will say much about an exceptional promotion.\"","Song Qiming let out a deep sigh. \"It's for the best if I leave early. I don't want to stay in this capital anymore.\"","It was incredibly frustrating to be forced to watch things he couldn't stand.","Three days later, outside the city walls.","Xiao Rongyan smiled as he mocked Xiao Rongche, who was sitting in a carriage, \"Take care of your health on your way to Jinzhou, Big Brother. Don't end up on your deathbed without even a single son.\"","Xiao Rongche tightly clenched the hand resting against his chest.","He gritted his teeth and retorted, \"You don't have a son either. The fact that you were made to marry Princess Shuwan proves that Imperial Father gave up on you long ago.\"","The smile on Xiao Rongyan's face instantly faded. \"At least I am not blind. With your short lifespan, Big Brother, I am in no rush compared to you.\"","\"Cough, cough, cough!\" A rush of air surged from his chest to his throat, and Xiao Rongche was so enraged that he covered his mouth, coughing incessantly.","The servant responsible for attending to him immediately climbed into the carriage to check. Seeing blood on his hand, the servant's face turned pale as he shouted outside for an imperial physician.","Seeing this, Xiao Rongyan swallowed hard.","Coughing up blood after just a couple of sentences, has his health really deteriorated this much?","If something happened, Imperial Father would definitely blame him. Thinking of this, Xiao Rongyan turned and walked away, losing all desire to continue mocking Prince Qi.","Anyway, once he arrived in Jinzhou, Xiao Rongche would never be able to oppose him again.","Until the other seven princes grew up, he would be the only adult prince in the capital. There would be no one else."]},{"number":398,"title":"Chapter 398: He Shuwan's Background Exposed","paragraphs":["After Prince Qi left, the capital fell into a brief period of peace.","Following the onset of winter, several snowfalls occurred in succession. The accumulated snow outside the window had not melted despite two consecutive days of sunshine, freezing into a rock-hard layer.","Inside the room, the charcoal fire burned a bright red. Floral tea was brewing on an iron stand, filling the entire room with its fragrance.","Fushun respectfully handed a list to Song Jinzhao.","\"To answer the County Princess, the managers of the various shops have all been properly arranged. They are all veterans who have been with us for two years.\"","Song Jinzhao picked up the list and scanned it; they were all familiar names.","\"With you staying in the capital, I can rest easy. Before the new year, go spend a few more days at the manor. Lanxi will hand over the matters regarding the essential oil and perfume factory to you.\"","Fushun bowed his head and, with a face full of loyalty, promised, \"This servant understands. I will certainly not disappoint the County Princess's expectations.\"","Just as his voice faded, Qingshuang, who had just returned from outside, walked up to Song Jinzhao and whispered, \"County Princess, today the whole city is spreading rumors about Princess Shuwan, especially regarding her biological mother.\"","\"Many commoners are discussing it, saying that Princess Shuwan was no longer a maiden when she married Prince Ying.\"","Song Jinzhao raised her eyes, a trace of surprise flashing through them.","\"Who started the rumor?\"","Qingshuang replied, \"It was the merchant caravan from the Shuobei Kingdom. It seems Gong Linjue is behind it.\"","Song Jinzhao pondered for a few seconds before curling the corners of her lips, though there was no warmth in her eyes.","\"It seems they did this on purpose. As early as when they were selecting a candidate, they wanted to use this to humiliate the Dongzhao Kingdom, even at the cost of exposing their own family scandal.\"","Qingshuang said, \"Prince Chu'an is not highly regarded in the Shuobei Kingdom, so he probably had no say in the matter.\"","Song Jinzhao asked, \"Is there any movement from Prince Ying's estate?\"","Qingshuang replied, \"They must have heard about it by now.\"","An exquisite multi-colored ceramic cup smashed a large hole through the window. The servants passing by the corridor were so frightened that they fell to their knees, not daring to make a sound.","The next second, Xiao Rongyan stormed out of the room in a towering rage, breathing heavily through his nostrils, his dark pupils looking like two bottomless pits.","No man could accept that the woman he married was not pure, let alone coming from a filthy place like a brothel.","Even if Xiao Rongyan wanted to use He Shuwan to get the Shuobei Kingdom to help him seize the throne, he could not stand being made a cuckold.","The door was forcefully pushed open from the outside, revealing He Shuwan sitting on the couch, embroidering a fragrant sachet.","Seeing that it was Xiao Rongyan who had entered, she happily rushed forward, wanting to hug his arm.","\"Your Highness, quickly take a look. Is the sachet your concubine embroidered for you beautiful?\"","Xiao Rongyan, his face dark and gloomy, shook off her hand and said sternly, \"Everyone, get out.\"","The servants attending in the room froze for a moment before all withdrawing from the room.","He Shuwan looked at Xiao Rongyan with feigned innocence, acting as if she were completely unaware and had been wronged.","\"Your Highness, what is wrong?\"","Xiao Rongyan took a step forward, closing in on He Shuwan. His fierce expression frightened her into backing up continuously.","\"There is a widespread rumor in the capital that your mother was a brothel woman. Is it true?\"","He Shuwan blinked, her expression turning slightly panicked.","Tears slid down the corners of her eyes. \"It is true that my mother was a brothel woman, but she was forced into it.\"","In that instant, Xiao Rongyan's heart died. Looking at the stunningly beautiful and gracefully figured woman before him, he only felt a wave of disgust.","He continued to press in disbelief, \"So it is also true that you grew up in a brothel and were only brought back by Prince Chu'an at the age of fifteen?\"","He Shuwan slid to her knees on the floor. Desperately clinging to Xiao Rongyan's hand, she cried and explained, \"Although I grew up in a brothel, my mother always protected me very well. Did Your Highness not know this on our wedding night?\"","Xiao Rongyan's eyes flickered with sudden realization.","Right, the virgin blood was real; she was indeed pure.","But despite this, Xiao Rongyan still could not accept it.","He originally thought he had married a princess, or at the very least someone of a county princess's birth. Who would have thought she grew up in a brothel?","No wonder she was so skilled in bed; it must have been due to what she saw and heard growing up.","Shaking off He Shuwan's hand, Xiao Rongyan took two steps back.","So what if she was pure? Outsiders would still mock him for marrying a brothel princess. How could he face anyone in the future?","His mind felt like a jumbled mess. With lifeless eyes, he turned and walked away.","\"Your Highness—\" He Shuwan stretched out her arms, lying on the floor and crying out, but the sorrow and despair in her voice were all faked.","Everything was developing according to plan. What happened next would depend on her own methods.","Outside the Tinglan Courtyard, watching Xiao Rongyan walk away briskly, the Princess Consort Ying, standing behind the rockery, curled her lips in a smug smile.","Ever since He Shuwan entered the estate, the Prince had constantly favored her, not even taking her, the official Princess Consort, seriously.","Now it was perfect. With a brothel woman for a biological mother and such a lowly status, let's see how she could swagger around in the future.","The rumors in the capital intensified and soon reached the palace.","During the morning court session the next day, everyone was secretly observing Xiao Rongyan.","With his face looking that dark, it had to be true.","In the history of the Dongzhao Kingdom, there had never been a prince whose secondary consort came from a brothel. Under normal circumstances, she would have long been cursed to death by the imperial censors.","But unfortunately, this person was a princess sent for a political marriage from the Shuobei Kingdom, and the marriage was personally bestowed by the Emperor himself. There was nowhere to even reason about it."]},{"number":399,"title":"Chapter 399: Hypocritical Father-Son Affection","paragraphs":["Xiao Chengjing looked at his son, who had his head bowed in silence, and felt a complex mix of emotions in his heart.","Who could have imagined that Prince Chu'an's daughter would have such a background? She was, after all, a commandery princess.","After a distracted court report concluded, Xiao Chengjing quietly had Zhao Yande ask Prince Ying to stay behind.","In the quiet and stifling imperial study, Xiao Chengjing stared at Xiao Rongyan, whose eyes were filled with grievance, and let out a deep sigh.","\"Now that things have come to this and He Shuwan has already married into Prince Ying's manor, if you truly dislike her, just accommodate her properly.\"","\"I have only one demand: for the sake of peace between our two nations, she must remain alive.\"","Xiao Rongyan looked up in distress, his eyes red.","\"Imperial Father, the Kingdom of Shuobei just wants to humiliate us. Otherwise, with so many women in their royal clan, why would they specifically choose He Shuwan to marry over!\"","With the facade torn away, Xiao Chengjing's expression also turned ugly.","\"How could I not know? But now is not a good time to wage war against Shuobei. For the sake of the bigger picture, we can only endure it.\"","His lips trembling slightly, Xiao Rongyan fell silent for a moment before speaking in a choked voice, \"As long as I can share Imperial Father's burdens, your son is willing to endure this humiliation.\"","After saying this, he squeezed his eyes shut, as if he had suffered an immense injustice.","Seeing him so sincere and earnest, Xiao Chengjing was moved and stood up from the dragon throne.","He walked down the steps, grasped Xiao Rongyan's shoulders, and patted them reassuringly.","\"This time, it is Imperial Father who has wronged you. Had I known He Shuwan had such a background, I would never have let her marry you.\"","Xiao Rongyan, who hadn't been this close to his own father since adulthood, felt his entire body stiffen, a tingling sensation washing over his skin.","A bit at a loss, he looked into Xiao Chengjing's eyes.","As their eyes met, the short distance of half a foot seemed to bridge more than a decade, taking them back to his childhood.","The corners of his lips curling up, Xiao Rongyan spoke with genuine emotion, \"As long as Imperial Father holds me in his heart, your son does not feel wronged.\"","Xiao Chengjing's heart stirred slightly. After a half-second pause in his gaze, his grip on his son's arms tightened.","\"Right now, you are the only one Imperial Father can rely on. Do not let me down.\"","Xiao Rongyan nodded vigorously.","\"Your son is willing to share Imperial Father's burdens at all times.\"","Just as he left the imperial study, a palace maid serving Noble Consort Rong called Xiao Rongyan over.","\"I am already aware of the rumors in the capital. What are your thoughts? Have you taken your anger out on Princess Shuwan?\"","Xiao Rongyan lifted his eyelids.","\"What does Mother Consort mean by this? Now that your son has become the laughingstock of the capital's commoners, can I not even question her?\"","Noble Consort Rong waved her hand to dismiss the attendants. When she spoke, her tone was extremely stern.","\"You cannot. Let alone the fact that her birth mother was a brothel woman, even if she herself were a brothel woman, you must not treat her coldly.\"","She walked heavily over to Xiao Rongyan. \"Do not forget what I told you. He Shuwan is your bridge to the Kingdom of Shuobei. You must keep her happy, pamper her until she forgets her roots, and make her willing to help you.\"","Xiao Rongyan closed his eyes, not wanting to listen, feeling immense disgust in his heart.","\"With her background, she is nothing but an abandoned pawn. Her title of princess is just an empty shell. She is merely a tool used by Shuobei to humiliate us. What use could she possibly be?\"","Sharp nails poked hard at Xiao Rongyan's forehead, leaving four or five crescent-shaped marks.","\"If you do not pretend to be completely bewitched by her, will Shuobei lower its guard and step in to help you?\"","\"Even if He Shuwan grew up in a brothel, she is still Prince Chu'an's biological daughter. As long as her blood ties remain unbroken, she has value to be exploited.\"","In the Palace of Eternal Harmony, Noble Consort Rong spoke with Xiao Rongyan for four hours, even keeping him for lunch, and he did not leave until the afternoon.","Upon returning to Prince Ying's manor, Xiao Rongyan sat in his room for a long time. Even when Princess Consort Ying came over, he did not give her a pleasant look.","\"If Your Highness does not wish to see Secondary Consort He, the Ningshuang Courtyard is still empty. She can be moved there.\"","Meeting his gaze, the smile in Princess Consort Ying's eyes slowly faded.","That look wasn't quite right. What did he mean?","\"There is no need. You may withdraw for now.\"","His icy voice was chilling.","Her heartbeat involuntarily quickening, Princess Consort Ying cautiously stood up to leave.","She said with concern, \"It gets cold at night. Your Highness should remember to wear more layers to avoid catching a chill.\"","Xiao Rongyan remained silent, not even sparing her a glance.","Seeing his attitude, Princess Consort Ying's heart began to pound with uncertainty.","Things had already reached this point; could he possibly still like He Shuwan?","Had he stopped minding after just one day? Or did he like her so much that he was willing to endure it?"]},{"number":400,"title":"Chapter 400: Small Gathering","paragraphs":["The gossip surrounding He Shuwan's background circulated the capital for nearly half a month before it finally died down.","As the rumors gradually dissipated, people also stopped mocking Prince Ying behind his back.","With the end of the year approaching, the streets and alleys gradually filled with pedestrians.","Shop assistants were kept off their feet all day long, especially in stores selling fabrics and food, as everyone wanted to wear new clothes and eat well for the New Year.","Compared to the bustling streets, the County Princess's manor seemed much quieter.","Although there was an atmosphere of the approaching New Year, it felt as though something was being suppressed.","On the twentieth of the twelfth lunar month, the day after the imperial court sealed its seals for the holidays, Song Gaoli packed his bags and came to bid farewell to Song Qiming.","Having honed himself under Wu Jianzheng for two and a half years, he now appeared much more composed than before.","\"This time I've asked the court for a three-month family visitation leave. I won't be back until the end of March, so we'll get together then.\"","The day after next, Song Qiming was going to have a small gathering with Dongfang Yukun and the others at Dingfei Restaurant. He had originally invited Song Gaoli, but Gaoli was leaving in a hurry and couldn't make it.","Resting his gaze on Song Gaoli's face, Song Qiming silently sighed in his heart.","By the end of March, he feared he would no longer be in the capital.","Knowing he couldn't tell his good friend everything yet, Song Qiming could only curl his lips into a slightly sorrowful smile.","\"Stay safe on the road, and say hello to the village chief for me.\"","Song Gaoli smiled and nodded. \"Don't worry, I'm traveling with a merchant caravan, and they've hired armed escorts.\"","Having not returned for three years, he was already eager to head home, wishing he could leap straight to Song Family Village immediately.","Two days later, in a private room at Dingfei Restaurant.","Cui Zhengyang dropped shrimp paste into the hot pot while saying to the two of them, \"Minister Ou said that after the metropolitan examination next year, he will transfer me to the Ministry of Works. What are your thoughts? Are you going to stay at the Hanlin Academy or go elsewhere?\"","Given the aptitude and performance of the three of them, they could easily stay in the Hanlin Academy and be promoted.","However, Cui Zhengyang had previously been exposed to the Ministry of Works' shipbuilding affairs and had taken an interest in it, feeling it would be easier for him to make achievements there.","Not long ago, when Ou Shinian returned from Mingzhou, the two had talked a few times, and he made up his mind to go to the Ministry of Works.","Dongfang Yukun first cast a subtle glance at Song Qiming, and seeing him remain silent, spoke up first.","\"I will stay at the Hanlin Academy. A Reader-in-Waiting position will open up soon, and I should be the one to fill it.\"","The Dongfang family didn't want Dongfang Yukun transferred out of the capital, so they wanted him to stay at the Hanlin Academy for a full six years. After that, he would serve as the Education Intendant of Jingzhao Prefecture. Once he reached the required years of service and had achievements, he could directly enter the Six Ministries as a Vice Minister.","This path might not be so smooth for others, as being promoted to Education Intendant usually meant being sent out to a local provincial capital. But for the Dongfang family, it was a minor issue, taking just a few words to arrange.","Cui Zhengyang nodded in understanding and shifted his gaze to Song Qiming.","\"What about you, Qiming? With the County Princess's status, keeping you in the capital shouldn't be a problem either. Why don't you come to the Ministry of Works? Minister Ou has mentioned you to me several times, saying he admires you.\"","Song Qiming smiled gently, pretending to be calm as he continued to pick up food from the pot. The red chili oil dripped onto the table and quickly solidified.","\"Lord Ou doesn't admire me; he admires my older sister.\"","Cui Zhengyang couldn't help but laugh. \"If the County Princess could come, Minister Ou probably wouldn't even spare a glance at me.\"","After eating and drinking his fill, Cui Zhengyang leaned back in his chair, feeling a bit drowsy.","Turning his head and seeing the snow falling heavier outside, he stood up and said, \"My little sister's wedding is set for the twenty-sixth of the twelfth month. Remember to come and have some wedding wine that day. I'll have someone send the invitations to your manors.\"","Cui Zhengyang's sister got engaged to the youngest son of the Vice Minister of Rites last year, and the Cui family moved to the capital this year entirely to arrange the wedding.","Dongfang Yukun's handsome eyes curved into two crescents.","\"You haven't taken a wife yet, but your sister is getting married first. You need to hurry up.\"","Cui Zhengyang just smiled without responding and took his leave."]}]);
